                                                                                                               |\n| --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `postLoginPage` | `string` | The page URL when the client is created | Used with `loginPage`: the page to return to after sign-in. Without `loginPage`, the client returns to the page the user was on. |","table":"table-2"},"30":{"id":"/authentication-28","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option      | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `loginPage` | `string` |         | A page in your app to show before redirecting to Foundry, such as `/login`. When set, the client navigates there instead of redirecting straight to Foundry. |","table":"table-2"},"31":{"id":"/authentication-29","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option       | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useHistory` | `boolean` | `true`  | Navigate within your app, to `loginPage` or back to the original page after sign-in, with `history.replaceState()` instead of `window.location.assign()`, so the page does not reload. |","table":"table-2"},"32":{"id":"/authentication-30","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option               | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `refreshTokenMarker` | `string` |         | An extra value stored with the refresh token. Change it to invalidate stored refresh tokens and make every user sign in again. |","table":"table-2"},"33":{"id":"/authentication-31","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option    | Type           | Default            | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchFn` | `typeof fetch` | `globalThis.fetch` | The `fetch` used for token requests. |","table":"table-2"},"34":{"id":"/authentication-32","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default       | Description                                             |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ctxPath` | `string` | `\"multipass\"` | The path of Foundry's authorization server under `url`. |","table":"table-2"},"35":{"id":"/authentication-33","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"| Option   | Type          | Default | Description                                                                                                                   |\n| -------- | ------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `logger` | `OauthLogger` |         | Receives warnings, such as a failed refresh. Without it, warnings are dropped. Compatible with the `Logger` from `@osdk/api`. |","table":"table-2"},"36":{"id":"/authentication-34","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-users-in-from-a-browser","content":"The fourth argument can also be the older positional form, `useHistory, loginPage, postLoginPage, scopes, fetchFn, ctxPath`. Pass either an options object or positional arguments, not both. `tokenStorage`, `refreshTokenMarker`, and `logger` are only available in the options object."},"37":{"id":"/authentication-35","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"The first time your app needs a token, the client looks for a stored refresh token and uses it if it is valid."},"38":{"id":"/authentication-36","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"Without one, it saves a PKCE verifier and the current URL in `sessionStorage`, then redirects to Foundry's sign-in page."},"39":{"id":"/authentication-37","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"Foundry redirects to `redirectUrl` with an authorization code."},"40":{"id":"/authentication-38","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"On that page, your app asks for a token again. The client exchanges the code, stores the refresh token, and navigates back to the page the user started on."},"41":{"id":"/authentication-39","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"The client refreshes the access token one minute before it expires. You do not schedule refreshes yourself. With `tokenStorage: \"none\"` there is no refresh token, so users sign in again when the access token expires."},"42":{"id":"/authentication-40","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#how-the-flow-works","content":"Concurrent token requests share one sign-in, so several components asking for data at once trigger a single redirect."},"43":{"id":"/authentication-41","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#handle-the-redirect-callback","content":"Render a route at your redirect URL's path that calls `auth.signIn()`. This completes step 4. The React template from `@osdk/create-app` uses this component, which then navigates to `/`; navigate elsewhere if your app needs to:"},"44":{"id":"/authentication-42","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#handle-the-redirect-callback","content":"Register it at the same path as `redirectUrl`:"},"45":{"id":"/authentication-43","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#handle-the-redirect-callback","content":"If the redirect URL in your code, in `.env` files, and on **OAuth & scopes** differ in any character, including the port and a trailing slash, Foundry rejects the sign-in."},"46":{"id":"/authentication-44","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#require-sign-in-before-rendering","content":"The client starts sign-in on the first request, so pages that load OSDK data trigger it automatically. To keep a route from rendering until the user is signed in, check for a token first. `getTokenOrUndefined()` returns the current access token synchronously, or `undefined` if there is none or it has expired:"},"47":{"id":"/authentication-45","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#scopes","content":"Scopes limit what the token can do. Both OAuth clients default to `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write`. Request only what your app needs, and make sure each scope is allowed for your application on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console. A read-only app can drop the two `write` scopes."},"48":{"id":"/authentication-46","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#scopes","content":"The defaults only cover the Ontology. Add the scopes for anything else your app calls: each Platform SDK endpoint lists its required scopes (see Platform SDK setup), and the AI packages need `api:use-language-models-execute` (see AI)."},"49":{"id":"/authentication-47","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#scopes","content":"The public client also requests `offline_access` so Foundry issues a refresh token, unless `tokenStorage` is `\"none\"`. A stored refresh token is only reused when it was issued for the same set of scopes, so changing `scopes` signs users in again."},"50":{"id":"/authentication-48","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#token-storage","content":"| `tokenStorage`   | Refresh token kept      | Trade-off                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"localStorage\"` | Across browser sessions | Fewest sign-ins. Anyone with access to the browser profile stays signed in. |","table":"table-3"},"51":{"id":"/authentication-49","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#token-storage","content":"| `tokenStorage`     | Refresh token kept              | Trade-off                       |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `\"sessionStorage\"` | Until the tab or browser closes | Recommended for shared devices. |","table":"table-3"},"52":{"id":"/authentication-50","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#token-storage","content":"| `tokenStorage` | Refresh token kept | Trade-off                                                                 |\n| -------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"none\"`       | Never              | Users sign in on every page load. No `offline_access` scope is requested. |","table":"table-3"},"53":{"id":"/authentication-51","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#token-storage","content":"The refresh token is stored under the key `@osdk/oauth : refresh : <clientId>`. Access tokens stay in memory."},"54":{"id":"/authentication-52","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-out","content":"`signOut()` revokes the access token with Foundry, deletes the stored refresh token, and emits a `signOut` event. It does not navigate, so redirect the user yourself:"},"55":{"id":"/authentication-53","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#sign-out","content":"`signOut()` throws if nobody is signed in. If revocation fails, it still clears local state but throws instead of emitting `signOut`. The next token request after sign-out starts a new sign-in."},"56":{"id":"/authentication-54","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"The public client emits `signIn`, `refresh`, and `signOut` events. `signIn` and `refresh` carry the new token in `event.detail`:"},"57":{"id":"/authentication-55","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member   | Description                                                             |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auth()` | Resolves to a valid access token, refreshing or signing in when needed. |","table":"table-4"},"58":{"id":"/authentication-56","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member          | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auth.signIn()` | Runs sign-in: refreshes from a stored token, completes a redirect callback, or redirects to Foundry. Resolves to the token object. |","table":"table-4"},"59":{"id":"/authentication-57","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member           | Description                                               |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auth.refresh()` | Refreshes the access token with the stored refresh token. |","table":"table-4"},"60":{"id":"/authentication-58","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member           | Description                                |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `auth.signOut()` | Revokes the token and clears stored state. |","table":"table-4"},"61":{"id":"/authentication-59","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member                       | Description                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `auth.getTokenOrUndefined()` | Returns the current access token, or `undefined` if there is none or it has expired. |","table":"table-4"},"62":{"id":"/authentication-60","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member                                  | Description                                    |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `auth.addEventListener(type, listener)` | Listens for `signIn`, `refresh`, or `signOut`. |","table":"table-4"},"63":{"id":"/authentication-61","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#listen-for-auth-events","content":"| Member                                     | Description         |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `auth.removeEventListener(type, listener)` | Removes a listener. |","table":"table-4"},"64":{"id":"/authentication-62","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"`createConfidentialOauthClient` uses the client credentials grant with a client ID and secret from a confidential application in Developer Console. Requests run as that application's service user, not as a person."},"65":{"id":"/authentication-63","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument   | Type     | Default | Description                               |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `clientId` | `string` |         | The confidential application's client ID. |","table":"table-5"},"66":{"id":"/authentication-64","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument       | Type     | Default | Description        |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------ |\n| `clientSecret` | `string` |         | The client secret. |","table":"table-5"},"67":{"id":"/authentication-65","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument | Type     | Default | Description                         |\n| -------- | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `url`    | `string` |         | The base URL of your Foundry stack. |","table":"table-5"},"68":{"id":"/authentication-66","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument | Type       | Default                                                                                      | Description        |\n| -------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `scopes` | `string[]` | `[\"api:read-data\", \"api:write-data\", \"api:use-ontologies-read\", \"api:use-ontologies-write\"]` | Scopes to request. |","table":"table-5"},"69":{"id":"/authentication-67","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument  | Type           | Default            | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchFn` | `typeof fetch` | `globalThis.fetch` | The `fetch` used for token requests. |","table":"table-5"},"70":{"id":"/authentication-68","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"| Argument  | Type     | Default       | Description                                             |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ctxPath` | `string` | `\"multipass\"` | The path of Foundry's authorization server under `url`. |","table":"table-5"},"71":{"id":"/authentication-69","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"The client requests a new token when the current one expires. There is no refresh token or browser storage. It supports `signIn()`, `signOut()`, `getTokenOrUndefined()`, and `signIn` and `signOut` events, but not `refresh()`."},"72":{"id":"/authentication-70","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#authenticate-a-server-or-service","content":"Never use `createConfidentialOauthClient` in browser code. Anything you ship to a browser, including environment variables inlined by your bundler, is readable by users, and the client secret lets anyone act as your application."},"73":{"id":"/authentication-71","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#public-apps-without-sign-in","content":"`createAuthlessClient()` returns a token provider that sends a fixed public token, for apps that let anyone view data without a Foundry account:"},"74":{"id":"/authentication-72","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#public-apps-without-sign-in","content":"The **React (Public)** template of `@osdk/create-app` sets this up, including the request proxy it relies on. It reads the Foundry URL and Ontology RID from the `osdk-foundryUrl` and `osdk-ontologyRid` `<meta>` tags instead of environment variables, so a Marketplace installation uses its destination's Foundry URL and Ontology."},"75":{"id":"/authentication-73","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#use-an-existing-token","content":"For scripts, tests, and one-off tools, pass a function that returns a token you already have, such as one from an environment variable:"},"76":{"id":"/authentication-74","page_id":"/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/authentication#use-an-existing-token","content":"The client does not refresh a static token. When it expires, requests fail with `401` until you supply a new one."},"77":{"id":"/client","page_id":"/client","type":"page","content":"Create a client","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/client"},"78":{"id":"/client-0","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client","content":"Configure createClient with your Foundry URL, Ontology RID, and token provider, share it through OsdkProvider, and query without React."},"79":{"id":"/client-1","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#createclient","content":"`createClient`"},"80":{"id":"/client-2","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#keep-one-client-per-app","content":"Keep one client per app"},"81":{"id":"/client-3","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#platform-api-only-clients","content":"Platform API only clients"},"82":{"id":"/client-4","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"Provide the client to React"},"83":{"id":"/client-5","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"Use the client without React"},"84":{"id":"/client-6","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"Fetch objects"},"85":{"id":"/client-7","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"Apply an action"},"86":{"id":"/client-8","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#execute-a-function","content":"Execute a function"},"87":{"id":"/client-9","page_id":"/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/client#read-metadata","content":"Read metadata"},"88":{"id":"/client-10","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client","content":"The client from `@osdk/client` sends every OSDK request: it fetches objects, applies actions, and executes functions. Create it once per app, then hand it to `OsdkProvider` for React or call it directly."},"89":{"id":"/client-11","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Argument  | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | The base URL of your Foundry stack, such as `https://example.palantirfoundry.com`. In local development behind a CORS proxy, your dev server's origin. |","table":"table-0"},"90":{"id":"/client-12","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Argument      | Type                        | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ontologyRid` | `string \\| Promise<string>` | The Ontology to query, such as `ri.ontology.main.ontology.<id>`. Usually `$ontologyRid` from your generated SDK. |","table":"table-0"},"91":{"id":"/client-13","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Argument        | Type                    | Description                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tokenProvider` | `() => Promise<string>` | Returns a bearer token for each request. Usually an OAuth client from `@osdk/oauth`. See Authentication. |","table":"table-0"},"92":{"id":"/client-14","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Argument  | Type     | Description                      |\n| --------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `object` | Optional settings, listed below. |","table":"table-0"},"93":{"id":"/client-15","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Argument  | Type           | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchFn` | `typeof fetch` | The `fetch` used for every request. Defaults to the global `fetch`. |","table":"table-0"},"94":{"id":"/client-16","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Option    | Type                     | Default | Description                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `headers` | `Record<string, string>` |         | Extra headers added to every request. |","table":"table-1"},"95":{"id":"/client-17","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Option   | Type     | Default                   | Description                                                                   |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `logger` | `Logger` | A minimal built-in logger | A `Logger`, as defined in `@osdk/api`, that receives the client's log output. |","table":"table-1"},"96":{"id":"/client-18","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"| Option                       | Type             | Default            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` | `string \\| null` | Read from the page | Beta. The Foundry branch to read and write on. When omitted in a browser, the client uses the `foundryBranchRid` query parameter, then the branch meta tag injected by OSDK build tooling. `null` pins the default branch. |","table":"table-1"},"97":{"id":"/client-19","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"`createClient` throws `Invalid ontology RID` when `ontologyRid` is a string that does not start with `ri.`."},"98":{"id":"/client-20","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#createclient","content":"Some generated SDKs omit `$ontologyRid`, because they are built to run on more than one Foundry stack and an embedded RID would only be correct on one. Pass the RID from configuration instead."},"99":{"id":"/client-21","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#keep-one-client-per-app","content":"Create the client at module scope in a single file, such as `src/client.ts`, and import it everywhere. `OsdkProvider` builds its cache from the client instance, so a new instance starts over with an empty cache."},"100":{"id":"/client-22","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#keep-one-client-per-app","content":"Read configuration from your environment instead of hard-coding it. With Vite, use `import.meta.env`:"},"101":{"id":"/client-23","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#keep-one-client-per-app","content":"The React template from `@osdk/create-app` goes one step further: `index.html` renders the env values into `<meta>` tags, such as `<meta name=\"osdk-foundryUrl\" content=\"%VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL%\" />`, and `src/client.ts` reads them at startup. Hosting can then change configuration by rewriting the HTML, without a new JavaScript build:"},"102":{"id":"/client-24","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#platform-api-only-clients","content":"`createPlatformClient(baseUrl, tokenProvider, options?, fetchFn?)` creates a client for Foundry Platform APIs, such as `@osdk/foundry.admin`, without an Ontology. Use it in apps that have no generated SDK. A client from `createClient` also works with the `@osdk/foundry.*` Platform SDK functions, so most apps need only one client. The exception is the AI helpers in `@osdk/aip-core`, such as `foundryModel`, which require a client from `createPlatformClient` (see Chat and streaming):"},"103":{"id":"/client-25","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"Wrap your app's root in `OsdkProvider` from `@osdk/react`. Every `@osdk/react` hook reads the client and its cache from the provider."},"104":{"id":"/client-26","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| Prop     | Type     | Default | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `Client` |         | The client from `createClient`. The provider creates its cache from this instance. |","table":"table-2"},"105":{"id":"/client-27","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| Prop       | Type        | Default | Description |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ------- | ----------- |\n| `children` | `ReactNode` |         | Your app.   |","table":"table-2"},"106":{"id":"/client-28","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| Prop             | Type      | Default                                          | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableDevTools` | `boolean` | `true` when `@osdk/react-devtools` is registered | Turns the OSDK Devtools panel on or off. Has no effect in production builds. |","table":"table-2"},"107":{"id":"/client-29","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| Prop      | Type     | Default | Description                                                               |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `devMode` | `object` |         | Development-only cache behavior, ignored in production builds. See below. |","table":"table-2"},"108":{"id":"/client-30","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| `devMode` field | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actionDelayMs` | `number` | `1000`  | Delays the result of a single (non-batched) action that has an optimistic update, so you can see the optimistic state. Set `0` to turn it off. |","table":"table-3"},"109":{"id":"/client-31","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| `devMode` field | Type                                                           | Default   | Description                                                |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `logLevel`      | `\"trace\" \\| \"debug\" \\| \"info\" \\| \"warn\" \\| \"error\" \\| \"fatal\"` | `\"error\"` | Log level of the cache layer. `\"debug\"` shows its tracing. |","table":"table-3"},"110":{"id":"/client-32","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| `devMode` field   | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `debug.refCounts` | `boolean` | `false` | Logs cache entry reference counts and cleanup, and shortens retention so cleanup happens sooner. |","table":"table-3"},"111":{"id":"/client-33","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"| `devMode` field   | Type      | Default | Description             |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| `debug.cacheKeys` | `boolean` | `false` | Logs cache key lookups. |","table":"table-3"},"112":{"id":"/client-34","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"Put the provider above everything that uses OSDK data, including headers and navigation, and pass it a client created at module scope. `<OsdkProvider client={createClient(...)}>` inside a component creates a new client, and an empty cache, on every render."},"113":{"id":"/client-35","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"A hook rendered outside the provider throws:"},"114":{"id":"/client-36","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"To call the client inside a component, for example in an event handler, read it from the provider with `useOsdkClient`:"},"115":{"id":"/client-37","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#provide-the-client-to-react","content":"For data you render, prefer the hooks, such as `useOsdkObjects` and `useOsdkAction`: they cache results and update when objects change. Direct client calls bypass the cache."},"116":{"id":"/client-38","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"Call `client` with a definition from your SDK. What it returns depends on the definition:"},"117":{"id":"/client-39","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"| You pass                        | You get                                   | Main methods                                                          |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object type, such as `Employee` | An object set of all objects of that type | `where`, `fetchPage`, `fetchOne`, `asyncIter`, `aggregate`, `pivotTo` |","table":"table-4"},"118":{"id":"/client-40","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"| You pass  | You get                                          | Main methods                                         |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interface | An object set over every type that implements it | Object set methods except `fetchOne`; see Interfaces |","table":"table-4"},"119":{"id":"/client-41","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"| You pass                         | You get           | Main methods                      |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Action, such as `modifyEmployee` | An action invoker | `applyAction`, `batchApplyAction` |","table":"table-4"},"120":{"id":"/client-42","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#use-the-client-without-react","content":"| You pass         | You get            | Main methods      |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ----------------- |\n| Function (query) | A function invoker | `executeFunction` |","table":"table-4"},"121":{"id":"/client-43","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"`fetchPage` returns one page with `data`, `nextPageToken`, and `totalCount`. `where` narrows the set and returns a new object set, so you can chain it:"},"122":{"id":"/client-44","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"Without `$select`, the response includes the type's default properties. Select only what you read. `$pageSize` sizes each page; it does not cap the total."},"123":{"id":"/client-45","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"Fetch one object by primary key with `fetchOne`, and follow links from it through `$link`:"},"124":{"id":"/client-46","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"To process every matching object, iterate with `asyncIter`. It fetches page after page from a consistent snapshot, so each object arrives once even if the data changes during the loop. Stream-backed object types have no snapshot guarantee, and iteration throws if the snapshot expires:"},"125":{"id":"/client-47","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#fetch-objects","content":"For counts, sums, and group-bys, use `aggregate` instead of loading every object."},"126":{"id":"/client-48","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"`applyAction` takes the action's parameters and an optional options object. Object parameters accept an object instance or its primary key:"},"127":{"id":"/client-49","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"| Option | Returns     |\n| ------ | ----------- |\n| none   | `undefined` |","table":"table-5"},"128":{"id":"/client-50","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"| Option                   | Returns                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ $returnEdits: true }` | The edits the action made: objects added, modified, and deleted. |","table":"table-5"},"129":{"id":"/client-51","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"| Option                    | Returns                                             |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ $validateOnly: true }` | The validation result, without applying the action. |","table":"table-5"},"130":{"id":"/client-52","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#apply-an-action","content":"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when the parameters fail validation, with the details in `error.validation`. `batchApplyAction` takes an array of parameter objects and applies them in one request."},"131":{"id":"/client-53","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#execute-a-function","content":"Replace `getEmployeeCount` with a function from your SDK. Its parameters and return type come from the function's definition."},"132":{"id":"/client-54","page_id":"/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/client#read-metadata","content":"`client.fetchMetadata(definition)` returns runtime metadata, such as display names and descriptions, for an object type, interface, action, or function:"},"133":{"id":"/concepts/caching","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"page","content":"Caching and reactivity","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching"},"134":{"id":"/concepts/caching-0","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching","content":"How @osdk/react stores objects once, shares them across hooks, deduplicates requests, and updates every view after an action."},"135":{"id":"/concepts/caching-1","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#one-cache-per-provider","content":"One cache per provider"},"136":{"id":"/concepts/caching-2","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"Objects are stored once"},"137":{"id":"/concepts/caching-3","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#read-an-instance-you-already-have","content":"Read an instance you already have"},"138":{"id":"/concepts/caching-4","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"When two hooks share an entry"},"139":{"id":"/concepts/caching-5","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"When hooks fetch"},"140":{"id":"/concepts/caching-6","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#deduplication","content":"Deduplication"},"141":{"id":"/concepts/caching-7","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#retention","content":"Retention"},"142":{"id":"/concepts/caching-8","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"Updates after actions"},"143":{"id":"/concepts/caching-9","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"How lists stay correct"},"144":{"id":"/concepts/caching-10","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#functions","content":"Functions"},"145":{"id":"/concepts/caching-11","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#optimistic-updates","content":"Optimistic updates"},"146":{"id":"/concepts/caching-12","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#real-time-updates","content":"Real-time updates"},"147":{"id":"/concepts/caching-13","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"When you need to invalidate"},"148":{"id":"/concepts/caching-14","page_id":"/concepts/caching","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/caching#practices","content":"Practices"},"149":{"id":"/concepts/caching-15","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching","content":"`@osdk/react` keeps one normalized cache per `OsdkProvider`. This page explains what the cache stores, when hooks hit the network, and how data updates after actions, so you can predict what a component renders."},"150":{"id":"/concepts/caching-16","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#one-cache-per-provider","content":"`OsdkProvider` wraps your `Client` in an `ObservableClient` from `@osdk/client/observable`. Every hook below that provider reads from and writes to the same cache:"},"151":{"id":"/concepts/caching-17","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#one-cache-per-provider","content":"Create the client once, outside any component. A new client creates a new, empty cache. To share one cache with code outside React or across several providers, pass an `ObservableClient` to `OsdkProvider` instead; see Share an observable client."},"152":{"id":"/concepts/caching-18","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"The cache stores each object under its object type and primary key, such as `Employee:12345`. Lists, links, and object sets do not copy objects. They store references to those entries."},"153":{"id":"/concepts/caching-19","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"| Hook            | What the cache stores                      |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `useOsdkObject` | One entry per object type and primary key. |","table":"table-0"},"154":{"id":"/concepts/caching-20","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"| Hook                             | What the cache stores                                               |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet` | The ordered list of references, plus `totalCount` and paging state. |","table":"table-0"},"155":{"id":"/concepts/caching-21","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"| Hook       | What the cache stores                                                             |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useLinks` | References to the linked objects, keyed by source object, link name, and filters. |","table":"table-0"},"156":{"id":"/concepts/caching-22","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"| Hook                 | What the cache stores                                                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useOsdkAggregation` | The aggregation result, keyed by object type, filter, and aggregate definition. |","table":"table-0"},"157":{"id":"/concepts/caching-23","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"| Hook              | What the cache stores                                  |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `useOsdkFunction` | The function result, keyed by function and parameters. |","table":"table-0"},"158":{"id":"/concepts/caching-24","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"Because objects are shared, a change to `Employee:12345` reaches every list, link, and detail view that contains it in the same render:"},"159":{"id":"/concepts/caching-25","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#objects-are-stored-once","content":"All three render the same `Employee` instance for `12345`."},"160":{"id":"/concepts/caching-26","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#read-an-instance-you-already-have","content":"`useOsdkObject(instance)` reads the object from the cache and does not send a request. Use it in a row component to get `isOptimistic` for an object a list already loaded:"},"161":{"id":"/concepts/caching-27","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#read-an-instance-you-already-have","content":"`useOsdkObject(Employee, id)` with a type and primary key does fetch. Calls for the same object type made within 25 ms are batched into one request of up to 100 objects."},"162":{"id":"/concepts/caching-28","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"Two hooks share a cache entry when they ask for the same data. The client canonicalizes options before building the key, so structurally equal options match even if you write them inline or list keys in a different order."},"163":{"id":"/concepts/caching-29","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"| Part of the key          | Not part of the key |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Object type or interface | `pageSize`          |","table":"table-1"},"164":{"id":"/concepts/caching-30","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"| Part of the key | Not part of the key |\n| --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `where`         | `enabled`           |","table":"table-1"},"165":{"id":"/concepts/caching-31","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"| Part of the key | Not part of the key |\n| --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `orderBy`       | `dedupeIntervalMs`  |","table":"table-1"},"166":{"id":"/concepts/caching-32","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"| Part of the key  | Not part of the key |\n| ---------------- | ------------------- |\n| `withProperties` | `autoFetchMore`     |","table":"table-1"},"167":{"id":"/concepts/caching-33","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"| Part of the key                               | Not part of the key |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `$select`, `intersectWith`, `pivotTo`, `rids` |                     |","table":"table-1"},"168":{"id":"/concepts/caching-34","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"For example, these share one entry, and each component sees its own page size:"},"169":{"id":"/concepts/caching-35","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"These are separate entries, because the filters differ:"},"170":{"id":"/concepts/caching-36","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-two-hooks-share-an-entry","content":"Adding `withProperties` creates a separate variant of each object, so derived properties never leak into views that did not request them."},"171":{"id":"/concepts/caching-37","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"The cache serves data immediately and refreshes it in the background. When a hook subscribes, it does three things:"},"172":{"id":"/concepts/caching-38","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"Returns any data already in the cache for its key."},"173":{"id":"/concepts/caching-39","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"Starts a request to revalidate the entry, unless a request for that entry is already in flight or one started within `dedupeIntervalMs`."},"174":{"id":"/concepts/caching-40","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"Updates when the response arrives."},"175":{"id":"/concepts/caching-41","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-hooks-fetch","content":"So a component that mounts onto cached data renders it at once, with `isLoading: true` while the refresh runs. See Loading and errors for how to render that state."},"176":{"id":"/concepts/caching-42","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#deduplication","content":"`dedupeIntervalMs` defaults to `2000` on `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, `useLinks`, `useOsdkAggregation`, and `useOsdkFunction`. If two components mount the same query within that window, the second one reuses the first request."},"177":{"id":"/concepts/caching-43","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#deduplication","content":"When several mounted hooks share an entry, the smallest non-zero `dedupeIntervalMs` among them applies. In-flight requests are always shared, whatever the interval."},"178":{"id":"/concepts/caching-44","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#retention","content":"An entry stays in the cache for about 60 seconds after its last hook unmounts. Navigating away and back within that window renders the cached data while it revalidates. After that, the entry is removed and the next mount starts empty."},"179":{"id":"/concepts/caching-45","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"When you apply an action with `useOsdkAction`, the client requests the action's edits from the server and updates the cache from them. You do not need to invalidate anything."},"180":{"id":"/concepts/caching-46","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"| Edit            | What happens                                                                              |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object modified | The object is refetched. Every list, link, and detail view that references it re-renders. |","table":"table-2"},"181":{"id":"/concepts/caching-47","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"| Edit         | What happens                                                                      |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object added | The object is fetched. Lists of that type whose `where` clause it matches add it. |","table":"table-2"},"182":{"id":"/concepts/caching-48","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"| Edit           | What happens                                                                |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object deleted | The object is removed from the cache and from every list that contained it. |","table":"table-2"},"183":{"id":"/concepts/caching-49","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"| Edit               | What happens                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Any edit to a type | Aggregations over that type refetch. Links to that type re-evaluate. Functions with `dependsOn` that include the type refetch. |","table":"table-2"},"184":{"id":"/concepts/caching-50","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#updates-after-actions","content":"The action's promise resolves after the edited objects are refetched. Aggregation and other type-wide refreshes continue in the background. When an action edits too many objects for the server to list them, the response names only the edited object types: every cached query for those types refetches in the background, and the promise resolves without waiting."},"185":{"id":"/concepts/caching-51","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"For a modified or added object, each list of that type checks the object against its `where` clause in the browser:"},"186":{"id":"/concepts/caching-52","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"If the object matches, the list keeps it or inserts it."},"187":{"id":"/concepts/caching-53","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"If the object no longer matches, the list removes it."},"188":{"id":"/concepts/caching-54","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"If the clause uses a filter the browser cannot evaluate, such as full-text search, the list removes a modified object, does not insert an added one, and refetches from the server with `isLoading: true`. The rest of the list stays in place until the response arrives."},"189":{"id":"/concepts/caching-55","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#how-lists-stay-correct","content":"Lists that follow a link (`pivotTo`) or return a different object type than they start from always refetch from the server when objects of their result type change."},"190":{"id":"/concepts/caching-56","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#functions","content":"Function results are not tied to objects, so the cache cannot know which edits affect them. Declare the dependency with `dependsOn` or `dependsOnObjects`:"},"191":{"id":"/concepts/caching-57","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#functions","content":"| Option                  | Refetches when                  |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `dependsOn: [Employee]` | An action edits any `Employee`. |","table":"table-3"},"192":{"id":"/concepts/caching-58","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#functions","content":"| Option                         | Refetches when                        |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `dependsOnObjects: [employee]` | An action edits that specific object. |","table":"table-3"},"193":{"id":"/concepts/caching-59","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#functions","content":"| Option                          | Refetches when                                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dependsOnObjects: [objectSet]` | An action edits any object of the object set's type. |","table":"table-3"},"194":{"id":"/concepts/caching-60","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#optimistic-updates","content":"Pass `$optimisticUpdate` in the arguments to `applyAction` from `useOsdkAction`. It writes your predicted change to a temporary layer above the server data. Every view shows the predicted change at once and reports `isOptimistic: true`. When the action finishes, the layer is removed and the server's data replaces it. If the action fails, the layer is removed and the views return to the previous data."},"195":{"id":"/concepts/caching-61","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#optimistic-updates","content":"In development, a single (non-batched) action with an optimistic update is delayed by 1000 ms so you can see the optimistic state. Set `devMode={{ actionDelayMs: 0 }}` on `OsdkProvider` to turn the delay off. The delay never applies in production builds."},"196":{"id":"/concepts/caching-62","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#optimistic-updates","content":"See Optimistic updates for the API."},"197":{"id":"/concepts/caching-63","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#real-time-updates","content":"Pass `streamUpdates: true` to `useOsdkObjects` to keep a list current over a WebSocket. Changes made outside your app, by other users or pipelines, arrive without polling. `streamUpdates` cannot be combined with `pivotTo`, because the server does not support subscriptions for link traversal."},"198":{"id":"/concepts/caching-64","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"Automatic updates cover changes that go through `useOsdkAction` in this app. Invalidate manually when data changes another way:"},"199":{"id":"/concepts/caching-65","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"Another system or pipeline edits the data."},"200":{"id":"/concepts/caching-66","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"Your code edits data with `@osdk/client` directly, a REST call, or a background job."},"201":{"id":"/concepts/caching-67","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"A function reads data the cache cannot track."},"202":{"id":"/concepts/caching-68","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#when-you-need-to-invalidate","content":"See Cache invalidation for `invalidateObjects`, `invalidateObjectType`, `invalidateFunction`, and the other methods."},"203":{"id":"/concepts/caching-69","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#practices","content":"**Let actions drive updates.** Do not call `invalidate*` after `applyAction`. The cache already handles the edits."},"204":{"id":"/concepts/caching-70","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#practices","content":"**Keep one source of truth.** Do not copy OSDK data into Redux, TanStack Query, or component state. Copies miss optimistic updates and action edits."},"205":{"id":"/concepts/caching-71","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#practices","content":"**Declare function dependencies.** Prefer `dependsOn` and `dependsOnObjects` over invalidating functions by hand."},"206":{"id":"/concepts/caching-72","page_id":"/concepts/caching","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/caching#practices","content":"**Use the devtools.** The Cache panel shows entries, hits, and misses in a running app."},"207":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"page","content":"Loading and errors","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors"},"208":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-0","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","content":"Render @osdk/react hooks correctly while data loads, refreshes, or fails, and narrow errors to PalantirApiError and ActionValidationError."},"209":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-1","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"Loading is not the same as empty"},"210":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-2","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#keep-rendering-while-loading","content":"Keep rendering while loading"},"211":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-3","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"Loading and error fields by hook"},"212":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-4","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"Narrow API errors"},"213":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-5","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#handle-action-errors","content":"Handle action errors"},"214":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-6","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validation-not-message","content":"`.validation`, not `.message`"},"215":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-7","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validate-before-you-apply","content":"Validate before you apply"},"216":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-8","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#related","content":"Related"},"217":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-9","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","content":"`@osdk/react` hooks can return data and report loading at the same time. This page shows the loading pattern that avoids flashing UI, the error shape of each hook, and how to turn an error into a message the user can act on."},"218":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-10","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"`isLoading` means a request for the hook's data is in flight. It does not mean `data` is missing. The cache serves what it has and refreshes in the background, so `isLoading` is `true` with data present when:"},"219":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-11","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"The component mounts onto data that another component already cached."},"220":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-12","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"An action edits an object and a list must refetch to decide whether the object still belongs in it."},"221":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-13","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"You call `refetch`, or something invalidates the entry."},"222":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-14","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"An optimistic update is applied to a list."},"223":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-15","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"The states you can see are:"},"224":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-16","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"| `data`      | `isLoading` | Meaning                     | Render                     |\n| ----------- | ----------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `undefined` | `true`      | First load, nothing cached. | A placeholder or skeleton. |","table":"table-0"},"225":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-17","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"| `data`  | `isLoading` | Meaning                 | Render                                       |\n| ------- | ----------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Present | `true`      | Refreshing cached data. | The data, with a small refreshing indicator. |","table":"table-0"},"226":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-18","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"| `data`  | `isLoading` | Meaning     | Render    |\n| ------- | ----------- | ----------- | --------- |\n| Present | `false`     | Up to date. | The data. |","table":"table-0"},"227":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-19","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"| `data`      | `isLoading` | Meaning                                     | Render          |\n| ----------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `undefined` | `false`     | The hook is disabled with `enabled: false`. | An empty state. |","table":"table-0"},"228":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-20","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"| `data`      | `isLoading`       | Meaning                                                                                                     | Render     |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `undefined` | `true` or `false` | The first load failed and `error` is set. On `useOsdkObjects` and `useObjectSet`, `isLoading` stays `true`. | The error. |","table":"table-0"},"229":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-21","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-is-not-the-same-as-empty","content":"See Caching and reactivity for when hooks refetch."},"230":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-22","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#keep-rendering-while-loading","content":"Do not return early on `isLoading`. An early return replaces the content with a spinner every time the cache refreshes, which makes the page flash and resets scroll position and focus. The only early return that is safe is the initial state, when there is no data yet:"},"231":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-23","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#keep-rendering-while-loading","content":"The component checks `error` separately from `data`. On `useOsdkObjects` and `useObjectSet`, a refresh can fail after earlier data loaded, so both can be set at once. `useOsdkFunction` and `useOsdkAggregation` clear `data` on failure, and `useLinks` returns an empty `links` array."},"232":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-24","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#keep-rendering-while-loading","content":"Do not write `if (isLoading) return <Spinner />`. Use `if (data == null && isLoading && error == null)` for the initial load, and render an inline indicator for refreshes."},"233":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-25","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"The hooks do not all use the same field names. Check this table before you destructure:"},"234":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-26","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook             | Data   | Loading     | Error                       | Retry       |\n| ---------------- | ------ | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `useOsdkObjects` | `data` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | `refetch()` |","table":"table-1"},"235":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-27","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook           | Data   | Loading     | Error                       | Retry       |\n| -------------- | ------ | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `useObjectSet` | `data` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | `refetch()` |","table":"table-1"},"236":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-28","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook            | Data     | Loading     | Error                       | Retry |\n| --------------- | -------- | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----- |\n| `useOsdkObject` | `object` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | None  |","table":"table-1"},"237":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-29","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook       | Data    | Loading     | Error                       | Retry |\n| ---------- | ------- | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----- |\n| `useLinks` | `links` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | None  |","table":"table-1"},"238":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-30","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook                 | Data   | Loading     | Error                       | Retry       |\n| -------------------- | ------ | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `useOsdkAggregation` | `data` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | `refetch()` |","table":"table-1"},"239":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-31","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook              | Data   | Loading     | Error                       | Retry       |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ----------- | --------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `useOsdkFunction` | `data` | `isLoading` | `error: Error \\| undefined` | `refetch()` |","table":"table-1"},"240":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-32","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook            | Data   | Loading                     | Error                                                 | Retry                    |\n| --------------- | ------ | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `useOsdkAction` | `data` | `isPending`, `isValidating` | `error: { actionValidation?, unknown? } \\| undefined` | Call `applyAction` again |","table":"table-1"},"241":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-33","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"| Hook              | Data       | Loading   | Error                        | Retry |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | --------- | ---------------------------- | ----- |\n| `useOsdkMetadata` | `metadata` | `loading` | `error: string \\| undefined` | None  |","table":"table-1"},"242":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-34","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"Details that differ between hooks:"},"243":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-35","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**`refetch` scope.** On `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, and `useOsdkAggregation`, `refetch` invalidates the whole object type, so every cached object, list, link, aggregation, and `dependsOn` function for that type refetches. On `useOsdkFunction`, it refetches only that function call with those parameters. To refetch more narrowly, use the methods in Cache invalidation."},"244":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-36","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**`useOsdkObject`.** `isLoading` is `false` as soon as `error` is set."},"245":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-37","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**`useObjectSet`.** When the object set changes, `data` keeps the last loaded result until the new set loads."},"246":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-38","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**`useOsdkFunction`.** `isLoading` is `true` only while a request is in flight, so the first render can report `isLoading: false` with no data. Treat `data === undefined && error == null` as the initial state, or check `lastUpdated === 0`."},"247":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-39","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**`useOsdkMetadata`.** It uses `loading`, not `isLoading`, and `error` is the error's message as a string, not an `Error`. It does not retry after a failure."},"248":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-40","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#loading-and-error-fields-by-hook","content":"**Disabled hooks.** With `enabled: false` (or `false` as the last argument to `useOsdkObject`), `isLoading` is `false` and no request is sent."},"249":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-41","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"Errors from Foundry are instances of `PalantirApiError`, which `@osdk/client` exports. `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, `useOsdkObject`, and `useOsdkFunction` pass it through, and type `error` as `Error`, so narrow it with `instanceof`. `useOsdkAggregation` and `useLinks` replace it with a generic `Error`:"},"250":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-42","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field     | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | The server's message, or `Failed to fetch <status> <statusText>`. |","table":"table-2"},"251":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-43","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorCode` | `string \\| undefined` | The error category, such as `PERMISSION_DENIED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, `CONFLICT`, or `TIMEOUT`. |","table":"table-2"},"252":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-44","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                   |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorName` | `string \\| undefined` | The specific error, such as `ObjectNotFound`. |","table":"table-2"},"253":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-45","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field              | Type                  | Description                        |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `errorDescription` | `string \\| undefined` | A longer description of the error. |","table":"table-2"},"254":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-46","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description           |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `statusCode` | `number \\| undefined` | The HTTP status code. |","table":"table-2"},"255":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-47","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                                                                    |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorInstanceId` | `string \\| undefined` | An ID for this occurrence. Include it when you report a problem to your Foundry administrator. |","table":"table-2"},"256":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-48","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"| Field        | Type      | Description                                                         |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `unknown` | Error-specific details, such as the object type that was not found. |","table":"table-2"},"257":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-49","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"Some errors carry only a message:"},"258":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-50","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"When a request fails before reaching Foundry, or the response is not JSON, the error is a `PalantirApiError` with no `errorCode` or `errorName`, and the original error on `cause`. `statusCode` is set if a response arrived."},"259":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-51","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"`useOsdkObject(Employee, id)` for an object that does not exist, or that you cannot see, reports a `PalantirApiError` with the message `Object not found: <id>` and no `errorCode` or `statusCode`."},"260":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-52","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#narrow-api-errors","content":"The client retries requests that fail with `429` or `503` up to three times, with exponential backoff, before the error reaches your hook."},"261":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-53","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#handle-action-errors","content":"`useOsdkAction` splits errors into two kinds:"},"262":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-54","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#handle-action-errors","content":"| Field                    | Set when                                                                                                            | Type                    |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `error.actionValidation` | The server ran the action's validation and it failed: a submission criterion or a parameter constraint was not met. | `ActionValidationError` |","table":"table-3"},"263":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-55","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#handle-action-errors","content":"| Field           | Set when                                                                         | Type      |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `error.unknown` | Anything else, such as a network failure, a permission error, or a server error. | `unknown` |","table":"table-3"},"264":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-56","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#handle-action-errors","content":"`applyAction` also rethrows the error, so always await it in `try`/`catch` or attach `.catch`. Otherwise a failed action becomes an unhandled promise rejection:"},"265":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-57","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validation-not-message","content":"`ActionValidationError.message` is `\"Validation Error: \"` followed by the validation response as JSON. It is useful in logs, not in UI. Read `.validation` instead:"},"266":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-58","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validation-not-message","content":"| Field               | Type                   | Description         |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `validation.result` | `\"VALID\" \\| \"INVALID\"` | The overall result. |","table":"table-4"},"267":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-59","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validation-not-message","content":"| Field                           | Type                                             | Description                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validation.submissionCriteria` | Array of `{ result, configuredFailureMessage? }` | One entry per submission criterion. `configuredFailureMessage` is the message the action's author wrote. |","table":"table-4"},"268":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-60","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validation-not-message","content":"| Field                   | Type                                                                   | Description                                             |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validation.parameters` | Record of parameter ID to `{ result, required, evaluatedConstraints }` | Per-parameter results. Use it to highlight form fields. |","table":"table-4"},"269":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-61","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validate-before-you-apply","content":"`validateAction` runs the same validation without applying the action. An invalid result does not throw: it resolves to the validation response, which the hook also stores as `validationResult`. `validateAction` throws only for other failures, and resolves to `undefined` if a newer validation or an `applyAction` call supersedes it."},"270":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-62","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#validate-before-you-apply","content":"The hook clears `error` when you call `applyAction` or `validateAction` again."},"271":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-63","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#related","content":"Actions: apply, validate, and batch actions."},"272":{"id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors-64","page_id":"/concepts/loading-and-errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/loading-and-errors#related","content":"Troubleshooting: fixes for setup, version, and auth errors."},"273":{"id":"/concepts/ontology","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"page","content":"The Ontology and your SDK","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology"},"274":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-0","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology","content":"How object types, links, actions, functions, interfaces, and object sets map to the generated SDK and to Osdk.Instance values in TypeScript."},"275":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-1","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"Ontology concepts"},"276":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-2","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"Why `client(Employee)`"},"277":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-3","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#object-instances","content":"Object instances"},"278":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-4","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"Metadata fields"},"279":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-5","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#instances-are-immutable","content":"Instances are immutable"},"280":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-6","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#links","content":"Links"},"281":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-7","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"Property value types"},"282":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-8","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#dates-and-timestamps","content":"Dates and timestamps"},"283":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-9","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"Object sets"},"284":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-10","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"285":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-11","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/ontology#related","content":"Related"},"286":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-12","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology","content":"Your generated SDK is a typed description of part of a Foundry Ontology. This page explains what each Ontology concept becomes in TypeScript, so you can read the SDK and the values it returns."},"287":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-13","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept     | What it is                                           | In the generated SDK                                                                             | How you use it                                                |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object type | A schema for real-world entities, such as employees. | A definition, `Employee`, plus the namespace types `Employee.Props` and `Employee.OsdkInstance`. | `client(Employee)` returns an object set of every `Employee`. |","table":"table-0"},"288":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-14","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept  | What it is                       | In the generated SDK                                            | How you use it                               |\n| -------- | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Property | A typed field on an object type. | A key in `Employee.Props`, typed from the property's base type. | Read it on an instance: `employee.fullName`. |","table":"table-0"},"289":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-15","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept     | What it is                                       | In the generated SDK                                        | How you use it                                                 |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Primary key | The property that uniquely identifies an object. | `primaryKeyApiName` and `primaryKeyType` on the definition. | `client(Employee).fetchOne(12345)`, or `employee.$primaryKey`. |","table":"table-0"},"290":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-16","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept   | What it is                               | In the generated SDK         | How you use it                                                              |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Link type | A relationship between two object types. | Entries in `Employee.Links`. | `employee.$link.lead` for a single link, `employee.$link.reports` for many. |","table":"table-0"},"291":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-17","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept     | What it is                        | In the generated SDK            | How you use it                                 |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Action type | A transaction that edits objects. | A definition, `modifyEmployee`. | `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction({ ... })`. |","table":"table-0"},"292":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-18","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept          | What it is                                                     | In the generated SDK                        | How you use it                                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Function (query) | Server-side logic that reads the Ontology and returns a value. | A definition, such as `getEmployeeMetrics`. | `client(getEmployeeMetrics).executeFunction({ ... })`. |","table":"table-0"},"293":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-19","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept   | What it is                                          | In the generated SDK                  | How you use it                                                    |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interface | A shared shape that several object types implement. | A definition with its own properties. | `client(MyInterface).fetchPage()`, then `instance.$as(Employee)`. |","table":"table-0"},"294":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-20","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"| Concept    | What it is                             | In the generated SDK  | How you use it                                     |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object set | A lazy, composable query over objects. | `Employee.ObjectSet`. | `client(Employee).where({ ... }).pivotTo(\"lead\")`. |","table":"table-0"},"295":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-21","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"The generated package does not contain a client. It exports definitions, which are plain metadata. You pass a definition to a client created with `createClient` from `@osdk/client`, and the client does the work:"},"296":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-22","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#ontology-concepts","content":"See Create a client to set up `client`."},"297":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-23","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"The SDK separates the code that knows your Ontology (the generated package) from the code that talks to Foundry (`@osdk/client`). That design has practical effects:"},"298":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-24","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"**Smaller bundles.** Each definition is a small named export. Bundlers drop the ones you do not import, so the SDK's cost scales with what you use, not with the size of the Ontology."},"299":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-25","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"**One runtime.** Several generated SDKs share the same `@osdk/client` code instead of each shipping its own."},"300":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-26","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"**Fixes without regenerating.** A bug fix in `@osdk/client` reaches you through a dependency update. You do not need to regenerate the SDK."},"301":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-27","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"If you want autocomplete across the whole Ontology, import the namespace exports. Tree-shaking still removes what you do not reference:"},"302":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-28","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#why-clientemployee","content":"The generated package also exports `$Actions`, `$Queries`, and `$Interfaces`, and `$ontologyRid` when the SDK was generated for a single Foundry environment."},"303":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-29","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-instances","content":"Every object you fetch, from `@osdk/client` or from `@osdk/react` hooks, is an `Osdk.Instance`. The generated alias `Employee.OsdkInstance` is the same type:"},"304":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-30","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"Fields that start with `$` describe the object rather than hold Ontology data:"},"305":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-31","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field      | Type     | Description                                                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$apiName` | `string` | API name of the type you queried. For an interface query, this is the interface's API name. |","table":"table-1"},"306":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-32","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$objectType` | `string` | API name of the concrete object type, even when you queried an interface. |","table":"table-1"},"307":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-33","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field         | Type             | Description                                              |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$primaryKey` | Primary key type | The object's primary key value. Use it as a React `key`. |","table":"table-1"},"308":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-34","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field    | Type                  | Description                                |\n| -------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `$title` | `string \\| undefined` | Value of the object type's title property. |","table":"table-1"},"309":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-35","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field              | Type              | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `$objectSpecifier` | `ObjectSpecifier` | A string that identifies the object by type and primary key. |","table":"table-1"},"310":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-36","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field   | Type         | Description                       |\n| ------- | ------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| `$link` | Links object | Accessors for the object's links. |","table":"table-1"},"311":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-37","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$as` | Function | Converts between an interface and an object type that implements it. |","table":"table-1"},"312":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-38","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field    | Type     | Description                                             |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$clone` | Function | Returns a copy of the instance with updated properties. |","table":"table-1"},"313":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-39","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#metadata-fields","content":"| Field  | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$rid` | `string` | The object's RID. Present only when you request it with `$includeRid: true`. |","table":"table-1"},"314":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-40","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#instances-are-immutable","content":"Instances are frozen, and their properties are `readonly`. To get a changed copy, call `$clone`:"},"315":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-41","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#instances-are-immutable","content":"`$clone` throws if the update changes the primary key. It does not write anything to Foundry. Use it to build optimistic state for an action, as shown in Optimistic updates. To change data, apply an action."},"316":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-42","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#links","content":"A single-valued link returns an accessor with `fetchOne`. A many-valued link returns an object set:"},"317":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-43","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#links","content":"In React, use `useLinks` instead so linked objects share the cache."},"318":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-44","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"Most properties are optional on the instance (`T | undefined`). Only the primary key and properties the Ontology marks as required are always present."},"319":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-45","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `string`      | `string`         |       |","table":"table-2"},"320":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-46","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `boolean`     | `boolean`        |       |","table":"table-2"},"321":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-47","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type                                 | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `integer`, `short`, `byte`, `float`, `double` | `number`         |       |","table":"table-2"},"322":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-48","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                                                    |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `long`        | `string`         | Strings keep 64-bit precision that `number` cannot hold. |","table":"table-2"},"323":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-49","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                             |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `decimal`     | `string`         | Strings keep arbitrary precision. |","table":"table-2"},"324":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-50","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                                  |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `date`        | `string`         | ISO 8601 date, such as `\"2024-03-15\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"325":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-51","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                                                     |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `timestamp`   | `string`         | ISO 8601 date and time, such as `\"2024-03-15T09:30:00Z\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"326":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-52","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `geopoint`    | `GeoJSON.Point`  |       |","table":"table-2"},"327":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-53","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value  | Notes |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | ----- |\n| `geoshape`    | `GeoJSON.GeoJSON` |       |","table":"table-2"},"328":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-54","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                                                                                |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `attachment`  | `Attachment`     | Has `rid`, `fetchMetadata()`, and `fetchContents()`, which resolves to a `Response`. |","table":"table-2"},"329":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-55","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type    | TypeScript value | Notes                                                                |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mediaReference` | `Media`          | Has `fetchMetadata()`, `fetchContents()`, and `getMediaReference()`. |","table":"table-2"},"330":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-56","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes                                  |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `cipherText`  | `CipherText`     | Call `decrypt()` to get the plaintext. |","table":"table-2"},"331":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-57","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `marking`     | `string`         |       |","table":"table-2"},"332":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-58","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type | TypeScript value | Notes |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----- |\n| `vector`      | `number[]`       |       |","table":"table-2"},"333":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-59","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type                           | TypeScript value     | Notes                                                          |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Numeric, string, and sensor time series | `TimeSeriesProperty` | Has `getFirstPoint()`, `getLastPoint()`, and `getAllPoints()`. |","table":"table-2"},"334":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-60","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#property-value-types","content":"| Ontology type            | TypeScript value        | Notes |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------- | ----- |\n| `geotimeSeriesReference` | `GeotimeSeriesProperty` |       |","table":"table-2"},"335":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-61","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#dates-and-timestamps","content":"The SDK returns dates and timestamps as ISO 8601 strings instead of `Date` objects or a date library's types. This keeps a large date library out of your bundle, lets you use the date library you already have, and avoids parsing values you never read."},"336":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-62","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#dates-and-timestamps","content":"Parse a value when you need date math:"},"337":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-63","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#dates-and-timestamps","content":"To send a date-only value, `@osdk/client` exports helpers that format a `Date` as `YYYY-MM-DD`:"},"338":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-64","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#dates-and-timestamps","content":"`extractDate` returns the date part of an ISO 8601 timestamp string."},"339":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-65","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"An object set describes which objects you want. Building one does not send a request; only fetching does:"},"340":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-66","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method          | Returns    | Description      |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------- |\n| `where(clause)` | Object set | Filters the set. |","table":"table-3"},"341":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-67","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method                                                      | Returns    | Description                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `union(...sets)`, `intersect(...sets)`, `subtract(...sets)` | Object set | Combines sets of the same type. |","table":"table-3"},"342":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-68","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method          | Returns    | Description                        |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `pivotTo(link)` | Object set | Follows a link to the linked type. |","table":"table-3"},"343":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-69","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method                | Returns    | Description                                     |\n| --------------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `withProperties(...)` | Object set | Adds derived properties computed on the server. |","table":"table-3"},"344":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-70","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method               | Returns             | Description                                                  |\n| -------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchPage(options)` | `Promise` of a page | Fetches one page: `data`, `nextPageToken`, and `totalCount`. |","table":"table-3"},"345":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-71","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method                 | Returns                  | Description                            |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchOne(primaryKey)` | `Promise` of an instance | Fetches one object. Object types only. |","table":"table-3"},"346":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-72","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method        | Returns        | Description                              |\n| ------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `asyncIter()` | Async iterator | Iterates over every object across pages. |","table":"table-3"},"347":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-73","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method               | Returns              | Description                        |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `aggregate(options)` | `Promise` of results | Runs an aggregation on the server. |","table":"table-3"},"348":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-74","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"| Method                | Returns      | Description                                   |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `subscribe(listener)` | Subscription | Receives changes to the set over a WebSocket. |","table":"table-3"},"349":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-75","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#object-sets","content":"In React, pass the same filters to `useOsdkObjects` or build a set with `useObjectSet`."},"350":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-76","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#interfaces","content":"An interface lets you query several object types through one shape. Instances from an interface query expose the interface's properties. `$objectType` tells you the concrete type, and `$as` converts to it:"},"351":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-77","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#related","content":"Caching and reactivity: how `@osdk/react` stores these instances."},"352":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-78","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#related","content":"Objects: query objects in React."},"353":{"id":"/concepts/ontology-79","page_id":"/concepts/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/ontology#related","content":"Actions: edit objects."},"354":{"id":"/deploy/branches","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"page","content":"Develop on Foundry branches","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches"},"355":{"id":"/deploy/branches-0","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches","content":"Point your OSDK app at a Foundry global branch with osdk branch sync, @osdk/vite-plugin-branch, and the beta UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH client option."},"356":{"id":"/deploy/branches-1","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"357":{"id":"/deploy/branches-2","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"Set up a new app"},"358":{"id":"/deploy/branches-3","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#add-to-an-existing-app","content":"Add to an existing app"},"359":{"id":"/deploy/branches-4","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-packages","content":"Install the packages"},"360":{"id":"/deploy/branches-5","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#sync-the-sdk-on-install","content":"Sync the SDK on install"},"361":{"id":"/deploy/branches-6","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#register-the-vite-plugin","content":"Register the Vite plugin"},"362":{"id":"/deploy/branches-7","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"Install the branch's SDK"},"363":{"id":"/deploy/branches-8","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"Inject the branch with Vite"},"364":{"id":"/deploy/branches-9","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"Choose the branch in the client"},"365":{"id":"/deploy/branches-10","page_id":"/deploy/branches","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/branches#generate-an-sdk-on-a-branch","content":"Generate an SDK on a branch"},"366":{"id":"/deploy/branches-11","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches","content":"Develop against Ontology changes on a Foundry global branch before they merge, using the SDK versions generated for that branch and sending every request to it. Three pieces work together: `osdk branch sync` installs the branch's SDK, `@osdk/vite-plugin-branch` tells the client which branch you are on, and the client sends that branch with its requests."},"367":{"id":"/deploy/branches-12","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches","content":"Branch support is beta. The client option is named `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH`, and `@osdk/create-app` only sets it up behind `--unstableFeatures`. Names and behavior can change in any release."},"368":{"id":"/deploy/branches-13","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"| Piece                 | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Branched SDK versions | An SDK generated on a branch is published as a prerelease under the npm dist tag `<branch>-latest`. Its `package.json` records the branch RID in `osdk.branch`, and the SDK exports it as `$branch`. |","table":"table-0"},"369":{"id":"/deploy/branches-14","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"| Piece              | What it does                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk branch sync` | Reads your git branch and installs the matching SDK version: the branch's prerelease on a branch, the stable `latest` on `main`. |","table":"table-0"},"370":{"id":"/deploy/branches-15","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"| Piece                      | What it does                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/vite-plugin-branch` | Injects the current branch into your app's HTML, and reloads the page when you switch git branches. |","table":"table-0"},"371":{"id":"/deploy/branches-16","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"| Piece          | What it does                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/client` | Reads the injected branch when you create the client, then reads and writes objects, actions, and queries on that branch. |","table":"table-0"},"372":{"id":"/deploy/branches-17","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#how-it-works","content":"Both the CLI and the plugin take the branch from `git branch --show-current`, so use the same name for your git branch and the Foundry branch you develop against."},"373":{"id":"/deploy/branches-18","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"Pass `--unstableFeatures` to `@osdk/create-app`:"},"374":{"id":"/deploy/branches-19","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"For an app with an SDK, this adds three things to the generated project:"},"375":{"id":"/deploy/branches-20","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"`@osdk/cli` as a dev dependency."},"376":{"id":"/deploy/branches-21","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"A `postinstall` script that runs `./node_modules/.bin/osdk branch sync`, so every install picks the SDK for your branch."},"377":{"id":"/deploy/branches-22","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#set-up-a-new-app","content":"`@osdk/vite-plugin-branch`, registered in `vite.config.ts` for the React and Vue 2.x templates. The Expo template instead passes `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH: $branch` to `createClient`."},"378":{"id":"/deploy/branches-23","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-packages","content":"Install `@osdk/vite-plugin-branch` at the same version as `@osdk/client`. It supports Vite 6, 7, and 8."},"379":{"id":"/deploy/branches-24","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#register-the-vite-plugin","content":"`branchPlugin()` takes no options."},"380":{"id":"/deploy/branches-25","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"For each dependency in your root `package.json` whose installed `package.json` has an `osdk` block, the command reads the package's npm dist tags and picks a target:"},"381":{"id":"/deploy/branches-26","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| You are on | Installed SDK | Target                                                                                |\n| ---------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A branch   | Any           | The `<branch>-latest` dist tag, if one is published. Otherwise the SDK is left alone. |","table":"table-1"},"382":{"id":"/deploy/branches-27","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| You are on                             | Installed SDK         | Target                 |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `main`, `master`, or a detached `HEAD` | Generated on a branch | The `latest` dist tag. |","table":"table-1"},"383":{"id":"/deploy/branches-28","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| You are on                             | Installed SDK     | Target      |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------- |\n| `main`, `master`, or a detached `HEAD` | Generated on main | Left alone. |","table":"table-1"},"384":{"id":"/deploy/branches-29","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"It installs every SDK whose declared version differs from its target in one `npm install <pkg>@<version> --save-exact`, so your `package.json` pins exact versions. It always runs `npm`, and only looks at `dependencies`, not `devDependencies`."},"385":{"id":"/deploy/branches-30","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| Option                | Description                                            |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--branchName <name>` | Sync to this branch instead of the current git branch. |","table":"table-2"},"386":{"id":"/deploy/branches-31","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| Option                 | Description         |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `--packageName <name>` | Sync only this SDK. |","table":"table-2"},"387":{"id":"/deploy/branches-32","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"| Option     | Description                                                     |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dryRun` | Print `Would install <pkg>@<version>` lines without installing. |","table":"table-2"},"388":{"id":"/deploy/branches-33","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#install-the-branchs-sdk","content":"The command reads dist tags from your registry, so it needs the same `.npmrc` and `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` as a normal install. A `401` from the registry fails with `Not authorized to read <pkg>`. See Installation."},"389":{"id":"/deploy/branches-34","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"`branchPlugin()` adds a meta tag to the `<head>` of your HTML:"},"390":{"id":"/deploy/branches-35","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"It decides the value in this order:"},"391":{"id":"/deploy/branches-36","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"| Condition                                                       | Value       |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `FOUNDRY_BRANCH_RID` is set in the environment or a `.env` file | That value. |","table":"table-3"},"392":{"id":"/deploy/branches-37","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"| Condition                            | Value                                  |\n| ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| The git branch is `main` or `master` | Empty, which means the default branch. |","table":"table-3"},"393":{"id":"/deploy/branches-38","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"| Condition            | Value            |\n| -------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Any other git branch | The branch name. |","table":"table-3"},"394":{"id":"/deploy/branches-39","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"| Condition                                                              | Value                                                                                      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| No branch: detached `HEAD`, or not a git repository, during `vite dev` | `ri.branch..branch.unknown`. Requests fail instead of silently reading the default branch. |","table":"table-3"},"395":{"id":"/deploy/branches-40","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"| Condition                     | Value                                  |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| No branch during `vite build` | Empty, which means the default branch. |","table":"table-3"},"396":{"id":"/deploy/branches-41","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"`FOUNDRY_BRANCH_RID` has no `VITE_` prefix, so Vite does not expose it to your client code. Use it to pin a branch RID, or to build for a branch in CI where HEAD is detached:"},"397":{"id":"/deploy/branches-42","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"The dev server logs the branch it uses, such as `Using Foundry branch \"my-feature\".` While it runs, it checks the git branch every second and reloads open pages when it changes, so you do not restart the server. Reloading needs HMR, which is on by default."},"398":{"id":"/deploy/branches-43","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#inject-the-branch-with-vite","content":"A production build fixes the branch at build time. Rebuild to deploy for another branch."},"399":{"id":"/deploy/branches-44","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"`createClient` resolves the branch once, when you create the client:"},"400":{"id":"/deploy/branches-45","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"The `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` option, when you pass it. `null` forces the default branch."},"401":{"id":"/deploy/branches-46","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"The `foundryBranchRid` query parameter in the page URL, such as `?foundryBranchRid=ri.branch..branch.<id>`. This lets a page that embeds your app in an iframe choose the branch."},"402":{"id":"/deploy/branches-47","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"The `osdk-foundry-branch-rid` meta tag from the Vite plugin."},"403":{"id":"/deploy/branches-48","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"A blank query parameter or meta tag is skipped, and a blank `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` acts like `null`. Outside a browser, only the option applies."},"404":{"id":"/deploy/branches-49","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"| Option                       | Type             | Default     | Description                                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` | `string \\| null` | `undefined` | Beta. The branch for every request. `undefined` reads the query parameter, then the meta tag. `null` ignores both and uses the default branch. |","table":"table-4"},"405":{"id":"/deploy/branches-50","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"To pin a client to the branch your SDK was generated on, pass the SDK's `$branch` export. It is `undefined` for SDKs generated on main, which keeps the default lookup:"},"406":{"id":"/deploy/branches-51","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#choose-the-branch-in-the-client","content":"In Node.js scripts there is no meta tag, so pass the branch explicitly:"},"407":{"id":"/deploy/branches-52","page_id":"/deploy/branches","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/branches#generate-an-sdk-on-a-branch","content":"To generate SDK files locally from a branch's Ontology, pass the branch RID to `osdk unstable typescript generate --branch`. See Generate an SDK."},"408":{"id":"/deploy/cli","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"page","content":"CLI reference","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli"},"409":{"id":"/deploy/cli-0","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli","content":"Every @osdk/cli command and flag for deploying sites and widget sets, managing versions, syncing branched SDKs, and generating SDKs locally."},"410":{"id":"/deploy/cli-1","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"Run the CLI"},"411":{"id":"/deploy/cli-2","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#global-options","content":"Global options"},"412":{"id":"/deploy/cli-3","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"413":{"id":"/deploy/cli-4","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"Tokens"},"414":{"id":"/deploy/cli-5","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"`osdk site`"},"415":{"id":"/deploy/cli-6","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"`osdk site deploy`"},"416":{"id":"/deploy/cli-7","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"`osdk site version`"},"417":{"id":"/deploy/cli-8","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"Site errors"},"418":{"id":"/deploy/cli-9","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"`osdk widgetset`"},"419":{"id":"/deploy/cli-10","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-deploy","content":"`osdk widgetset deploy`"},"420":{"id":"/deploy/cli-11","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-version","content":"`osdk widgetset version`"},"421":{"id":"/deploy/cli-12","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"`osdk branch sync`"},"422":{"id":"/deploy/cli-13","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"`osdk unstable typescript generate`"},"423":{"id":"/deploy/cli-14","page_id":"/deploy/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-auth-login","content":"`osdk unstable auth login`"},"424":{"id":"/deploy/cli-15","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli","content":"`@osdk/cli` deploys your app to Foundry website hosting, manages its versions, publishes widget sets, keeps branched SDKs in sync, and generates SDKs from an Ontology. This page lists every command and flag."},"425":{"id":"/deploy/cli-16","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"Run it with `npx`, or install it as a dev dependency to get the `osdk` binary:"},"426":{"id":"/deploy/cli-17","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command            | Description                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site deploy` | Upload a new version of your site and, by default, make it live. |","table":"table-0"},"427":{"id":"/deploy/cli-18","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command             | Description                                      |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `osdk site version` | List, get, set, unset, and delete site versions. |","table":"table-0"},"428":{"id":"/deploy/cli-19","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command                 | Description                       |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset deploy` | Publish a new widget set version. |","table":"table-0"},"429":{"id":"/deploy/cli-20","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command                  | Description                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version` | List, inspect, and delete widget set versions. |","table":"table-0"},"430":{"id":"/deploy/cli-21","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command            | Description                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk branch sync` | Install the SDK versions published for your current branch. |","table":"table-0"},"431":{"id":"/deploy/cli-22","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command                             | Description                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk unstable typescript generate` | Generate SDK source files from an Ontology. Unstable. |","table":"table-0"},"432":{"id":"/deploy/cli-23","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"| Command                    | Description                                        |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk unstable auth login` | Test an OAuth sign-in from the terminal. Unstable. |","table":"table-0"},"433":{"id":"/deploy/cli-24","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#run-the-cli","content":"`osdk experimental` is an alias for `osdk unstable`. Commands under it can change or be removed in any release."},"434":{"id":"/deploy/cli-25","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#global-options","content":"| Option            | Type  | Description                                                                     |\n| ----------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--verbose`, `-v` | count | Debug logging. Pass `-vv` for trace logging, which includes every HTTP request. |","table":"table-1"},"435":{"id":"/deploy/cli-26","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#global-options","content":"| Option   | Type    | Description                                                                                 |\n| -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--help` | boolean | Print the commands and options available at that level, such as `osdk site version --help`. |","table":"table-1"},"436":{"id":"/deploy/cli-27","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#global-options","content":"Each option also accepts its kebab-case form: `--foundryUrl` and `--foundry-url` are the same option."},"437":{"id":"/deploy/cli-28","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"Options come from three places. The first one set wins:"},"438":{"id":"/deploy/cli-29","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"The command-line flag."},"439":{"id":"/deploy/cli-30","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"An environment variable named `OSDK_` plus the option in upper snake case, such as `OSDK_FOUNDRY_URL`, `OSDK_APPLICATION`, or `OSDK_DIRECTORY`."},"440":{"id":"/deploy/cli-31","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"`foundry.config.json`, for the options it covers."},"441":{"id":"/deploy/cli-32","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#configuration","content":"The CLI looks for `foundry.config.json` in the current directory and then each parent, and uses the first one it finds. A file holds either a `site` block or a `widgetSet` block, not both. The full schema is in Host on Foundry."},"442":{"id":"/deploy/cli-33","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"Every `site` and `widgetset` command needs a Foundry token. The CLI uses the first of:"},"443":{"id":"/deploy/cli-34","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"`--token <token>`"},"444":{"id":"/deploy/cli-35","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"`--tokenFile <path>`, a file whose contents are the token"},"445":{"id":"/deploy/cli-36","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"The `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` environment variable"},"446":{"id":"/deploy/cli-37","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"The `FOUNDRY_SDK_AUTH_TOKEN` environment variable, which is deprecated and logs a warning"},"447":{"id":"/deploy/cli-38","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#tokens","content":"`--token` and `--tokenFile` cannot be used together. The token must be a JWT. Without one, the command exits with `No token found.`"},"448":{"id":"/deploy/cli-39","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"Manages the website hosted for a Developer Console application. Run it with a subcommand: `deploy` or `version`."},"449":{"id":"/deploy/cli-40","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"These options apply to every `site` subcommand:"},"450":{"id":"/deploy/cli-41","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default            | Description                                                                                 |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--application` | `string` | `site.application` | The application RID, such as `ri.third-party-applications.main.application.<id>`. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"451":{"id":"/deploy/cli-42","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default      | Description                                                  |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `string` | `foundryUrl` | The Foundry stack URL. Must start with `https://`. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"452":{"id":"/deploy/cli-43","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--token` | `string` |         | A Foundry token. Conflicts with `--tokenFile`. |","table":"table-2"},"453":{"id":"/deploy/cli-44","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--tokenFile` | `string` |         | A path to a file containing a Foundry token. Conflicts with `--token`. |","table":"table-2"},"454":{"id":"/deploy/cli-45","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"Zips the contents of a directory, uploads it as a new site version, and makes that version live."},"455":{"id":"/deploy/cli-46","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default          | Description                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--directory` | `string` | `site.directory` | The directory to upload, usually your build output. Required. Everything in it is zipped, with the directory itself as the root. |","table":"table-3"},"456":{"id":"/deploy/cli-47","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option      | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                                               |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--version` | `string` |         | The version to create. Must be valid SemVer. Conflicts with `--autoVersion`; when `site.autoVersion` is set in the config file, `--version` overrides it. |","table":"table-3"},"457":{"id":"/deploy/cli-48","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option          | Type                               | Default                 | Description                                                                 |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--autoVersion` | `\"git-describe\" \\| \"package-json\"` | `site.autoVersion.type` | Compute the version instead of passing `--version`. See Automatic versions. |","table":"table-3"},"458":{"id":"/deploy/cli-49","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default                      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--gitTagPrefix` | `string` | `site.autoVersion.tagPrefix` | With `git-describe`, match only tags that start with this prefix, and strip it from the version. Without it, every tag matches and a leading `v` is stripped. Only valid with `git-describe`. |","table":"table-3"},"459":{"id":"/deploy/cli-50","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option         | Type      | Default                         | Description                                                                       |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--uploadOnly` | `boolean` | `site.uploadOnly`, else `false` | Upload the version without making it live. The CLI prints a preview link instead. |","table":"table-3"},"460":{"id":"/deploy/cli-51","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option       | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--snapshot` | `boolean` | `false` | Upload a snapshot version with automatic retention. The CLI never makes a snapshot live. Cannot be combined with `--uploadOnly`. |","table":"table-3"},"461":{"id":"/deploy/cli-52","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default | Description                                                        |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--snapshotId` | `string` |         | An alias to attach to the snapshot version. Requires `--snapshot`. |","table":"table-3"},"462":{"id":"/deploy/cli-53","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-deploy","content":"You must pass `--version` or `--autoVersion`, or set `site.autoVersion` in `foundry.config.json`. When the deploy succeeds, the CLI prints the live URL, `https://<subdomain>`. With `--uploadOnly`, it prints `https://<subdomain>/.system/preview?previewVersion=<version>` instead."},"463":{"id":"/deploy/cli-54","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"Manages existing versions. Run it with a subcommand."},"464":{"id":"/deploy/cli-55","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Command                  | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site version list` | Lists every version that is valid SemVer, newest first, and marks the live one `(deployed)`. |","table":"table-4"},"465":{"id":"/deploy/cli-56","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Command                 | Description                                             |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site version get` | Prints the live version, or `No live site version set`. |","table":"table-4"},"466":{"id":"/deploy/cli-57","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Command                           | Description                                                                                       |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site version set <version>` | Makes `<version>` live. Use it to roll back or to publish a version uploaded with `--uploadOnly`. |","table":"table-4"},"467":{"id":"/deploy/cli-58","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Command                   | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site version unset` | Clears the live version after a confirmation prompt. The site is unreachable until you set a version again. |","table":"table-4"},"468":{"id":"/deploy/cli-59","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Command                              | Description                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk site version delete <version>` | Deletes a version after a confirmation prompt. You cannot delete the live version, and deletion cannot be undone. |","table":"table-4"},"469":{"id":"/deploy/cli-60","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-site-version","content":"| Option        | Applies to        | Type      | Description                   |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | --------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--yes`, `-y` | `unset`, `delete` | `boolean` | Skip the confirmation prompt. |","table":"table-5"},"470":{"id":"/deploy/cli-61","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"The CLI turns Foundry errors into these messages:"},"471":{"id":"/deploy/cli-62","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                           | Cause                                           | What to do                                 |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `The site version already exists` | A version with that number was uploaded before. | Use a new version. Versions are immutable. |","table":"table-6"},"472":{"id":"/deploy/cli-63","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                                                         | Cause                      | What to do                                                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `The site version is invalid and must be a valid SemVer string` | The version is not SemVer. | Fix `--version`, or the tag or `package.json` version that `--autoVersion` reads. |","table":"table-6"},"473":{"id":"/deploy/cli-64","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                               | Cause                                                            | What to do                                           |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `The site contains too many versions` | The application reached its version limit, shown in the message. | Delete old versions with `osdk site version delete`. |","table":"table-6"},"474":{"id":"/deploy/cli-65","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                                 | Cause                                           | What to do                               |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `The .zip file contains too many files` | The build output has more files than the limit. | Reduce the number of files in the build. |","table":"table-6"},"475":{"id":"/deploy/cli-66","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                                               | Cause                            | What to do                 |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `The .zip file contains a file ... that is too large` | One file exceeds the size limit. | Shrink or split that file. |","table":"table-6"},"476":{"id":"/deploy/cli-67","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                                                                               | Cause                                 | What to do                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `The website version is being scanned for vulnerabilities and cannot be deployed yet` | Foundry is still scanning the upload. | Deploy with `--uploadOnly`, then make the version live after the scan, with `osdk site version set` or from **Website hosting** in Developer Console. |","table":"table-6"},"477":{"id":"/deploy/cli-68","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                                                    | Cause                                 | What to do                      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `The site version to delete is live and cannot be deleted` | You tried to delete the live version. | Set another version live first. |","table":"table-6"},"478":{"id":"/deploy/cli-69","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"| Message                               | Cause                       | What to do                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `The site version could not be found` | The version does not exist. | Check `osdk site version list`. |","table":"table-6"},"479":{"id":"/deploy/cli-70","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#site-errors","content":"A `401` means the token is invalid or expired; a `403` means it lacks the permission or scopes for the request."},"480":{"id":"/deploy/cli-71","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"Publishes and manages widget sets for Workshop custom widgets. Run it with a subcommand: `deploy` or `version`. Publish a widget set covers the build and the manifest."},"481":{"id":"/deploy/cli-72","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"These options apply to every `widgetset` subcommand:"},"482":{"id":"/deploy/cli-73","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default         | Description                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--widgetSet` | `string` | `widgetSet.rid` | The widget set RID. Required. |","table":"table-7"},"483":{"id":"/deploy/cli-74","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default      | Description                                                  |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `string` | `foundryUrl` | The Foundry stack URL. Must start with `https://`. Required. |","table":"table-7"},"484":{"id":"/deploy/cli-75","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--token` | `string` |         | A Foundry token. Conflicts with `--tokenFile`. |","table":"table-7"},"485":{"id":"/deploy/cli-76","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--tokenFile` | `string` |         | A path to a file containing a Foundry token. Conflicts with `--token`. |","table":"table-7"},"486":{"id":"/deploy/cli-77","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-deploy","content":"Zips a directory and publishes it as a new widget set version. The version comes from the manifest at `.palantir/widgets.config.json` inside the directory; there is no version flag."},"487":{"id":"/deploy/cli-78","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-deploy","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default               | Description                        |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `--directory` | `string` | `widgetSet.directory` | The directory to upload. Required. |","table":"table-8"},"488":{"id":"/deploy/cli-79","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-deploy","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default                | Description                                                                                            |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--repository` | `string` | `widgetSet.repository` | A code repository RID to publish through. The repository must be authorized to publish the widget set. |","table":"table-8"},"489":{"id":"/deploy/cli-80","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-deploy","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default                | Description                     |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `--branchName` | `string` | The current git branch | The git branch to publish from. |","table":"table-8"},"490":{"id":"/deploy/cli-81","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-version","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version list` | Lists published versions for the current git branch. Accepts `--branchName`. |","table":"table-9"},"491":{"id":"/deploy/cli-82","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-version","content":"| Command                                 | Description                        |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version info <version>` | Prints the details of one version. |","table":"table-9"},"492":{"id":"/deploy/cli-83","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-widgetset-version","content":"| Command                                   | Description                                                                      |\n| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version delete <version>` | Deletes a version after a confirmation prompt. `--yes` or `-y` skips the prompt. |","table":"table-9"},"493":{"id":"/deploy/cli-84","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"Installs the version of each generated SDK that matches your current branch: the newest prerelease published for that branch, or, on `main`, the stable `latest` release for any SDK currently installed from a branch. Develop on Foundry branches explains the workflow."},"494":{"id":"/deploy/cli-85","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default                | Description                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--branchName` | `string` | The current git branch | The branch to sync to, used as given. Without it, the current git branch is used, and `main`, `master`, or a detached `HEAD` mean the default branch. |","table":"table-10"},"495":{"id":"/deploy/cli-86","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--packageName` | `string` |         | Sync only this SDK instead of every SDK found. |","table":"table-10"},"496":{"id":"/deploy/cli-87","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"| Option     | Type      | Default | Description                                              |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dryRun` | `boolean` | `false` | Print what would be installed without changing anything. |","table":"table-10"},"497":{"id":"/deploy/cli-88","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-branch-sync","content":"`osdk unstable branch sync` is the same command under its earlier name."},"498":{"id":"/deploy/cli-89","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"Generates SDK source files from an Ontology, either by signing in to Foundry or from a saved Ontology metadata file. Generate an SDK shows when to use it."},"499":{"id":"/deploy/cli-90","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option     | Type     | Default | Description                                   |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `--outDir` | `string` |         | Where to write the generated files. Required. |","table":"table-11"},"500":{"id":"/deploy/cli-91","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option      | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--version` | `string` |         | The SDK version: `dev` or a SemVer string. Written into the generated SDK's user agent string, and used as the package version with `--asPackage`. Required. |","table":"table-11"},"501":{"id":"/deploy/cli-92","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option         | Type     | Default | Description                                                                 |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `string` |         | Load the Ontology from this stack. Requires `--clientId`. Alias: `--stack`. |","table":"table-11"},"502":{"id":"/deploy/cli-93","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option       | Type     | Default | Description                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--clientId` | `string` |         | The OAuth client ID to sign in with. Requires `--foundryUrl`. |","table":"table-11"},"503":{"id":"/deploy/cli-94","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default | Description                                                                           |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--ontologyRid` | `string` |         | With `--foundryUrl`, use this Ontology. Needed when the client can see more than one. |","table":"table-11"},"504":{"id":"/deploy/cli-95","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option     | Type     | Default | Description                                                            |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--branch` | `string` |         | With `--foundryUrl`, the Foundry branch RID to load the Ontology from. |","table":"table-11"},"505":{"id":"/deploy/cli-96","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option                | Type     | Default | Description                                                                       |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--ontologyWritePath` | `string` |         | With `--foundryUrl`, also save the loaded Ontology metadata as JSON at this path. |","table":"table-11"},"506":{"id":"/deploy/cli-97","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--ontologyPath` | `string` |         | Generate from an Ontology metadata JSON file instead of Foundry. Conflicts with `--foundryUrl` and `--clientId`. |","table":"table-11"},"507":{"id":"/deploy/cli-98","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option          | Type                     | Default      | Description                                         |\n| --------------- | ------------------------ | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--packageType` | `\"commonjs\" \\| \"module\"` | `\"commonjs\"` | The module format of the project you generate into. |","table":"table-11"},"508":{"id":"/deploy/cli-99","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option    | Type      | Default | Description                          |\n| --------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `--clean` | `boolean` |         | Delete `--outDir` before generating. |","table":"table-11"},"509":{"id":"/deploy/cli-100","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option                    | Type      | Default | Description                                                              |\n| ------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--skipPackageJsonUpdate` | `boolean` | `false` | Do not add `@osdk/api` and `@osdk/client` to the nearest `package.json`. |","table":"table-11"},"510":{"id":"/deploy/cli-101","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option              | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--externalObjects` | `string` |         | Import these object types from another generated SDK instead of generating them, as `ApiName:@scope/package` pairs separated by commas. |","table":"table-11"},"511":{"id":"/deploy/cli-102","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option                 | Type     | Default | Description               |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------- |\n| `--externalInterfaces` | `string` |         | The same, for interfaces. |","table":"table-11"},"512":{"id":"/deploy/cli-103","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option                           | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--experimentalOntologyMetadata` | `boolean` | `false` | Also write the raw Ontology metadata to `experimental/ontology-metadata.json` in `--outDir`. With `--asPackage`, it is also exported as `./experimental/ontology-metadata`. May change or be removed. |","table":"table-11"},"513":{"id":"/deploy/cli-104","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option        | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                       |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--asPackage` | `boolean` |         | Generate a standalone package with its own `package.json`. Requires `--packageName` and `--beta`. |","table":"table-11"},"514":{"id":"/deploy/cli-105","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default | Description                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `--packageName` | `string` |         | The package name when using `--asPackage`. |","table":"table-11"},"515":{"id":"/deploy/cli-106","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option   | Type      | Default | Description                  |\n| -------- | --------- | ------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `--beta` | `boolean` |         | Required with `--asPackage`. |","table":"table-11"},"516":{"id":"/deploy/cli-107","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"| Option       | Type      | Default | Description                                                                 |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--internal` | `boolean` | `false` | For the `osdk-ts` repository only. Writes `workspace:` dependency versions. |","table":"table-11"},"517":{"id":"/deploy/cli-108","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-typescript-generate","content":"Pass either `--ontologyPath`, or `--foundryUrl` and `--clientId`."},"518":{"id":"/deploy/cli-109","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-auth-login","content":"Runs the OAuth authorization code flow in your browser, to check that a client ID and redirect URL work. It does not save or print the token."},"519":{"id":"/deploy/cli-110","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-auth-login","content":"| Option         | Type     | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `string` | The Foundry stack URL. Required. Alias: `--baseUrl`. |","table":"table-12"},"520":{"id":"/deploy/cli-111","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-auth-login","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--clientId` | `string` | The OAuth client ID. Required. Alias: `--applicationId`. |","table":"table-12"},"521":{"id":"/deploy/cli-112","page_id":"/deploy/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/cli#osdk-unstable-auth-login","content":"The CLI listens on port 8080 and uses `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` as the redirect URL, so that URL must be allowed on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console and port 8080 must be free. It requests the `offline_access`, `api:read-data`, and `api:use-ontologies-read` scopes. `osdk unstable typescript generate --foundryUrl` uses the same sign-in."},"522":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"page","content":"Generate an SDK","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk"},"523":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-0","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk","content":"Generate your Ontology SDK in Developer Console or locally with osdk unstable typescript generate or @osdk/foundry-sdk-generator, and update it when the Ontology changes."},"524":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-1","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-a-method","content":"Choose a method"},"525":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-2","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-in-developer-console","content":"Generate in Developer Console"},"526":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-3","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-the-resources","content":"Choose the resources"},"527":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-4","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-a-version","content":"Generate a version"},"528":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-5","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#install-it","content":"Install it"},"529":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-6","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"What the package exports"},"530":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-7","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"Update the SDK when the Ontology changes"},"531":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-8","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"Generate locally"},"532":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-9","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"Build a package with `@osdk/foundry-sdk-generator`"},"533":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-10","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk","content":"Your generated SDK holds typed definitions for the object types, links, actions, functions, and interfaces your app uses. Generate it in Developer Console and install it from your Foundry npm registry, or generate it yourself from the command line."},"534":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-11","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-a-method","content":"| Method            | Output                                            | Use it when                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Developer Console | A versioned npm package in your Foundry registry. | Almost always. Apps from `@osdk/create-app` expect it. |","table":"table-0"},"535":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-12","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-a-method","content":"| Method                              | Output                                               | Use it when                                                                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `osdk unstable typescript generate` | TypeScript source files in a folder of your project. | You want the SDK in your repository, or you work offline from a saved Ontology file. |","table":"table-0"},"536":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-13","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-a-method","content":"| Method                        | Output                                                 | Use it when                                      |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/foundry-sdk-generator` | A built npm package directory you can pack or publish. | You publish SDK packages from your own pipeline. |","table":"table-0"},"537":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-14","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#choose-the-resources","content":"In your application in Developer Console, add the object types, link types, actions, functions, and interfaces your app uses to the application's SDK. Only those resources are generated."},"538":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-15","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-a-version","content":"On **SDK versions**, generate a new version with the **npm** package type and the latest generator. The install instructions show the package name, such as `@my-app/sdk`, and your registry URL."},"539":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-16","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#install-it","content":"Point your SDK's npm scope at the Foundry registry in `.npmrc`, then install:"},"540":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-17","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#install-it","content":"Installation covers the `.npmrc` lines, the token, and the other packages you need."},"541":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-18","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"| Export                           | Description                          |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Object types, such as `Employee` | Pass to `client(Employee)` to query. |","table":"table-1"},"542":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-19","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"| Export                            | Description                                        |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Actions, such as `modifyEmployee` | Pass to `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction(...)`. |","table":"table-1"},"543":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-20","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"| Export                   | Description                         |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| Functions and interfaces | Pass to `client(...)` the same way. |","table":"table-1"},"544":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-21","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"| Export         | Description                           |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `$ontologyRid` | The Ontology RID, for `createClient`. |","table":"table-1"},"545":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-22","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#what-the-package-exports","content":"| Export    | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$branch` | The Foundry branch RID the SDK was generated on, or `undefined` for main. See Develop on Foundry branches. |","table":"table-1"},"546":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-23","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"The SDK is a snapshot of the Ontology when you generated it. When you add a resource to the SDK, or a property, parameter, or link you use changes:"},"547":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-24","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"Generate a new version in Developer Console."},"548":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-25","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"Install it:"},"549":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-26","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"Run your type checker. Renamed or removed properties and parameters show up as type errors where your code uses them."},"550":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-27","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#update-the-sdk-when-the-ontology-changes","content":"The SDK has a peer dependency on the `@osdk/client` version that generated it. If npm reports a peer conflict, align `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/api`, and `@osdk/react` as described in Version compatibility. On a Foundry branch, `osdk branch sync` picks the branch's SDK version instead of `latest`."},"551":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-28","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"`osdk unstable typescript generate` from `@osdk/cli` writes the SDK as TypeScript source files into your project. It is unstable: flags and output can change in any release."},"552":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-29","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"The CLI opens your browser to sign in, with `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` as the redirect URL, so allow that URL on **OAuth & scopes** and keep port 8080 free. It generates every object type, action, function, and interface the client can see in the Ontology, except functions that return Ontology edits. If the client can see more than one Ontology, pass `--ontologyRid`. Pass `--branch <branch RID>` to read a branch's Ontology."},"553":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-30","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"`--ontologyWritePath` saves the loaded metadata so you can regenerate later without signing in."},"554":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-31","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"`--ontologyPath` takes an Ontology metadata file written by `--ontologyWritePath`."},"555":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-32","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"Import from the generated folder instead of a package:"},"556":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-33","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"Unless you pass `--skipPackageJsonUpdate`, the command also edits the nearest `package.json` above `--outDir`: it adds `@osdk/api` and `@osdk/client` as peer dependencies and `@osdk/api` as a dev dependency, and sets any existing `@osdk/api` and `@osdk/client` entries to the versions the CLI was built with. Install `@osdk/client` as a regular dependency of your app yourself."},"557":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-34","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#generate-locally","content":"All flags are in the CLI reference."},"558":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-35","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"`@osdk/foundry-sdk-generator` loads the resources you name from Foundry and writes a compiled npm package with ESM, CommonJS, and bundled type definitions."},"559":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-36","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"The package is written to `<outputDir>/<packageName>`, here `./out/@my-app/sdk`, with a `peerDependencies` entry for `@osdk/client`. Pack or publish it from there with npm."},"560":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-37","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------- |\n| `--authToken` | `string` | A Foundry token. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"561":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-38","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option              | Type     | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--foundryHostname` | `string` | Your stack, such as `example.palantirfoundry.com`. A full `https://` URL also works. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"562":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-39","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--ontology` | `string` | The Ontology RID or API name. |","table":"table-2"},"563":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-40","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option          | Type     | Description                     |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `--packageName` | `string` | The npm package name. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"564":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-41","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option             | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--packageVersion` | `string` | The package version. Must be SemVer. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"565":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-42","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--outputDir` | `string` | The directory to write the package under. Required. |","table":"table-2"},"566":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-43","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option          | Type       | Description            |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `--objectTypes` | `string[]` | Object type API names. |","table":"table-2"},"567":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-44","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option        | Type       | Description                                           |\n| ------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--linkTypes` | `string[]` | Links to include, as `ObjectTypeApiName.linkApiName`. |","table":"table-2"},"568":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-45","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option          | Type       | Description            |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `--actionTypes` | `string[]` | Action type API names. |","table":"table-2"},"569":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-46","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option         | Type       | Description                                                                            |\n| -------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--queryTypes` | `string[]` | Function API names. Add `:<version>` to pin a version, such as `countEmployees:1.2.0`. |","table":"table-2"},"570":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-47","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option             | Type       | Description          |\n| ------------------ | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| `--interfaceTypes` | `string[]` | Interface API names. |","table":"table-2"},"571":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-48","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option     | Type       | Description                       |\n| ---------- | ---------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `--agents` | `string[]` | AIP Agents, as `apiName:version`. |","table":"table-2"},"572":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-49","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"| Option                           | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| -------------------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--experimentalOntologyMetadata` | `boolean` | Also export the raw metadata at `./experimental/ontology-metadata`. Experimental. |","table":"table-2"},"573":{"id":"/deploy/generate-sdk-50","page_id":"/deploy/generate-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/generate-sdk#build-a-package-with-osdkfoundry-sdk-generator","content":"Each list flag takes space-separated values. The generator includes only what you list: an object type's links are left out unless you pass them in `--linkTypes`, and generation fails if a requested resource is missing."},"574":{"id":"/deploy/hosting","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"page","content":"Host on Foundry","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting"},"575":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-0","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting","content":"Build your OSDK app with Vite and deploy it to Foundry website hosting with osdk site deploy, foundry.config.json, versions, previews, and rollbacks."},"576":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-1","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"577":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-2","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#deploy-your-app","content":"Deploy your app"},"578":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-3","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#add-foundryconfigjson","content":"Add `foundry.config.json`"},"579":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-4","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#set-the-production-redirect-url","content":"Set the production redirect URL"},"580":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-5","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#build","content":"Build"},"581":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-6","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#deploy","content":"Deploy"},"582":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-7","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"`foundry.config.json`"},"583":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-8","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"Automatic versions"},"584":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-9","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#preview-before-going-live","content":"Preview before going live"},"585":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-10","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#roll-back","content":"Roll back"},"586":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-11","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#clean-up-old-versions","content":"Clean up old versions"},"587":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-12","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/hosting#host-somewhere-else","content":"Host somewhere else"},"588":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-13","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting","content":"Foundry website hosting serves your app's static build from a subdomain of your Foundry stack. You upload each build as a version with `@osdk/cli`, and one version at a time is live. This page covers configuring production, deploying, and managing versions; the CLI reference lists every flag."},"589":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-14","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#before-you-start","content":"| You need                                                        | Where to get it                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| An application in Developer Console with website hosting set up | Developer Console. Note the subdomain, such as `https://myapp.example.palantirfoundry.com`. |","table":"table-0"},"590":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-15","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#before-you-start","content":"| You need            | Where to get it                                                                    |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| The application RID | The application's Developer Console URL, `/workspace/developer-console/app/<rid>`. |","table":"table-0"},"591":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-16","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#before-you-start","content":"| You need        | Where to get it                                       |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| A Foundry token | Set it as `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`. The CLI accepts only JWTs. |","table":"table-0"},"592":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-17","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#before-you-start","content":"| You need       | Where to get it                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| A static build | Any framework works. Apps from `@osdk/create-app` build to `./dist` with Vite. |","table":"table-0"},"593":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-18","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#add-foundryconfigjson","content":"Apps from `@osdk/create-app` already have this file. Otherwise, create it in your project root:"},"594":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-19","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#add-foundryconfigjson","content":"The CLI reads it from the current directory or the nearest parent, so you do not repeat these values on every command. All fields are described in `foundry.config.json`."},"595":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-20","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#set-the-production-redirect-url","content":"After sign-in, Foundry sends users back to your app's redirect URL, which must point at the hosted subdomain in production. In an app from `@osdk/create-app`, set it in `.env.production`:"},"596":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-21","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#set-the-production-redirect-url","content":"If you skipped the production URL when you created the app, the redirect line is commented out with a placeholder. Then add the same URL as a redirect URL on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console. The two must match exactly. See Authentication."},"597":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-22","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#set-the-production-redirect-url","content":"The React template includes a test that fails while any of these variables is missing or still a placeholder:"},"598":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-23","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#build","content":"In the React templates from `@osdk/create-app` this runs `tsc && vite build` (`vue-tsc && vite build` for Vue, `expo export -p web` for Expo). Vite builds in `production` mode, reads `.env.production`, and writes to `./dist`. Your Vite config must define `process.env.NODE_ENV`; see Use OSDK with Vite."},"599":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-24","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#deploy","content":"The CLI computes the version, zips `./dist`, uploads it, makes it live, and prints the site URL. To set the version yourself, pass `--version 1.2.0`."},"600":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-25","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field        | Type     | Required | Description                                        |\n| ------------ | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundryUrl` | `string` | Yes      | The Foundry stack URL. Must start with `https://`. |","table":"table-1"},"601":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-26","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field              | Type     | Required | Description                            |\n| ------------------ | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `site.application` | `string` | Yes      | The Developer Console application RID. |","table":"table-1"},"602":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-27","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field            | Type     | Required | Description                                                 |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `site.directory` | `string` | Yes      | The directory to upload, relative to where you run the CLI. |","table":"table-1"},"603":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-28","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field              | Type     | Required | Description                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `site.autoVersion` | `object` | No       | How to compute versions. `{ \"type\": \"git-describe\", \"tagPrefix\"?: string }` or `{ \"type\": \"package-json\" }`. |","table":"table-1"},"604":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-29","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field             | Type      | Required | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `site.uploadOnly` | `boolean` | No       | Upload new versions without making them live. Defaults to `false`. |","table":"table-1"},"605":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-30","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#foundryconfigjson","content":"The file must not contain other top-level fields. A `widgetSet` block, used by widget sets, cannot share a file with `site`. Command-line flags and `OSDK_*` environment variables override the file; see Configuration."},"606":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-31","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"Every version must be valid SemVer and unique: Foundry rejects a version that already exists. Pass `--version`, or let the CLI compute it."},"607":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-32","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| `autoVersion.type` | Version comes from                                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `git-describe`     | `git describe --tags --first-parent --dirty`, limited to tags starting with `tagPrefix` when it is set. |","table":"table-2"},"608":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-33","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| `autoVersion.type` | Version comes from                                 |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `package-json`     | The `version` field of the nearest `package.json`. |","table":"table-2"},"609":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-34","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"With `git-describe`, the CLI strips `tagPrefix` from the result, or a leading `v` when there is no prefix. The result depends on where you are relative to the newest tag:"},"610":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-35","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| Repository state     | Example tag | Version |\n| -------------------- | ----------- | ------- |\n| On the tagged commit | `v1.2.0`    | `1.2.0` |","table":"table-3"},"611":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-36","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| Repository state            | Example tag | Version            |\n| --------------------------- | ----------- | ------------------ |\n| Three commits after the tag | `v1.2.0`    | `1.2.0-3-g1a2b3c4` |","table":"table-3"},"612":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-37","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| Repository state    | Example tag | Version       |\n| ------------------- | ----------- | ------------- |\n| Uncommitted changes | `v1.2.0`    | `1.2.0-dirty` |","table":"table-3"},"613":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-38","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"| Repository state     | Example tag    | Version |\n| -------------------- | -------------- | ------- |\n| Tag prefix `my-app@` | `my-app@1.2.0` | `1.2.0` |","table":"table-3"},"614":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-39","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"The deploy fails if git is missing, the directory is not a git repository, no tag matches, or the result is not SemVer. In CI, check out tags as well as commits, or `git describe` finds no tag."},"615":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-40","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#automatic-versions","content":"To use the version in `package.json`, bump it before each deploy:"},"616":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-41","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#preview-before-going-live","content":"Upload a version without making it live with `--uploadOnly`, or set `site.uploadOnly` to `true` to make that the default:"},"617":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-42","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#preview-before-going-live","content":"The CLI prints a preview link, `https://<subdomain>/.system/preview?previewVersion=<version>`. When it looks right, make it live:"},"618":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-43","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#preview-before-going-live","content":"Use the same flow when Foundry reports that a version is still being scanned for vulnerabilities: upload with `--uploadOnly`, wait for the scan, then set the version live with the CLI or from **Website hosting** in Developer Console."},"619":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-44","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#roll-back","content":"To roll back, set an earlier uploaded version live:"},"620":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-45","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#roll-back","content":"`list` shows each version, newest first, and marks the live one. `osdk site version get` prints only the live version."},"621":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-46","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#clean-up-old-versions","content":"An application has a version limit. When you reach it, deploys fail with `The site contains too many versions`. Delete versions you no longer need:"},"622":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-47","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#clean-up-old-versions","content":"You cannot delete the live version. To take the site offline, clear the live version with `osdk site version unset`; the site is unreachable until you set one again."},"623":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-48","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#host-somewhere-else","content":"The build is static files, so any web server or CDN can host it. Foundry website hosting sets up cross-origin access to your stack for you; elsewhere you configure it yourself:"},"624":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-49","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#host-somewhere-else","content":"| Requirement                            | Why                                                                                                   |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Your stack allows your origin for CORS | The browser calls Foundry APIs directly from your origin. Ask your Foundry administrator to allow it. |","table":"table-4"},"625":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-50","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#host-somewhere-else","content":"| Requirement                               | Why                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| The redirect URL is on **OAuth & scopes** | Foundry only redirects to listed URLs. Use your origin plus `/auth/callback`, and set the same value in `.env.production`. |","table":"table-4"},"626":{"id":"/deploy/hosting-51","page_id":"/deploy/hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/hosting#host-somewhere-else","content":"| Requirement                                      | Why                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| The server returns your app for `/auth/callback` | Sign-in lands on that path. A server that returns `404` for paths without a file breaks sign-in, so serve `index.html` for unknown paths. |","table":"table-4"},"627":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"page","content":"Integration testing","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing"},"628":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-0","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing","content":"Run OSDK code against a local Ontology server with @osdk/integration-testing, seed it with objects and links, and stub functions in Vitest."},"629":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-1","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"630":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-2","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"631":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-3","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#install","content":"Install"},"632":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-4","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"Foundry CLI"},"633":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-5","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"Get the Ontology metadata"},"634":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-6","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#write-a-test","content":"Write a test"},"635":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-7","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#create-a-fixture","content":"Create a fixture"},"636":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-8","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#build-the-seed-data","content":"Build the seed data"},"637":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-9","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#test-against-the-local-server","content":"Test against the local server"},"638":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-10","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#run-the-tests","content":"Run the tests"},"639":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-11","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#change-data-inside-a-test","content":"Change data inside a test"},"640":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-12","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#api-reference","content":"API reference"},"641":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-13","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"`createIntegrationServer(config)`"},"642":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-14","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"`SeedClient`"},"643":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-15","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#integrationclient","content":"`IntegrationClient`"},"644":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-16","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/deploy/integration-testing#other-exports","content":"Other exports"},"645":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-17","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing","content":"`@osdk/integration-testing` starts a local Ontology server from the Foundry CLI, fills it with seed objects and links, and gives you a real `Client` connected to it. Use it to test code that queries objects, filters, and follows links end to end, without a Foundry stack. To test React components with mocks instead, see Testing."},"646":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-18","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing","content":"`@osdk/integration-testing` is a `0.x` package and depends on the experimental `--experimentalOntologyMetadata` generator flag. Its API may change between releases."},"647":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-19","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#how-it-works","content":"| Piece                     | What it does                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createIntegrationServer` | Writes your Ontology metadata to a temporary `.test-run-*` directory and runs `foundry start ontology` from the Foundry CLI. |","table":"table-0"},"648":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-20","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#how-it-works","content":"| Piece       | What it does                                                                                                   |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Seed client | Writes objects and links to the local server. Each call replaces the server's data with the seed built so far. |","table":"table-0"},"649":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-21","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#how-it-works","content":"| Piece              | What it does                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Integration client | A `Client` from `@osdk/client` pointed at the local server. Object and interface calls, such as `fetchPage`, `where`, and `pivotTo`, run against the seeded data. |","table":"table-0"},"650":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-22","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#how-it-works","content":"| Piece          | What it does                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Function stubs | The local Ontology cannot run functions, so the integration client sends function calls to an in-memory mock from `@osdk/unit-testing`. Register results with `whenQuery`. |","table":"table-0"},"651":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-23","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#requirements","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                               |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Node.js     | The package starts a subprocess and reads files, so tests run in Node, not a browser. |","table":"table-1"},"652":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-24","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#requirements","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                            |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Foundry CLI | The `foundry` binary, version `0.224.0` or later, on your `PATH`. Pass `foundryCliPath` to use a binary elsewhere. |","table":"table-1"},"653":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-25","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#requirements","content":"| Requirement       | Details                                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Ontology metadata | The full Ontology metadata your SDK was generated from, as JSON. See Get the Ontology metadata. |","table":"table-1"},"654":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-26","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#requirements","content":"| Requirement          | Details                                                      |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/seed-helpers` | A peer dependency, `>=0.25.0 <1.0.0`, that builds seed data. |","table":"table-1"},"655":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-27","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#install","content":"`@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` are peer dependencies as well; install them as described in Installation."},"656":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-28","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"On install, a postinstall script checks for the Foundry CLI:"},"657":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-29","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"If `foundry` is installed and recent enough, it does nothing."},"658":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-30","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"If it is too old, the install fails and asks you to run `foundry update self`."},"659":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-31","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"If it is missing, it downloads the installer from your Foundry stack and runs it. If that fails, the install continues with a warning, and creating a client fails until the CLI is installed."},"660":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-32","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"To find your stack and authenticate the download, the script reads, in order:"},"661":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-33","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"| Value        | Sources                                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry host | `FOUNDRY_EXTERNAL_HOST` or `FOUNDRY_HOSTNAME`, then the host of the git remote `origin`. |","table":"table-2"},"662":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-34","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"| Value | Sources                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Token | `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` when `FOUNDRY_HOSTNAME`, `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`, and `FOUNDRY_USERNAME` are all set, otherwise the credentials in the git remote URL. Foundry CI and Code Workspaces provide their own token automatically. |","table":"table-2"},"663":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-35","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#foundry-cli","content":"Set the three variables before installing on a machine whose git remote does not point at Foundry:"},"664":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-36","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"`createIntegrationServer` needs the Ontology metadata as an `OntologyFullMetadata` object. The SDK generator writes it when you generate locally with the experimental `--experimentalOntologyMetadata` flag:"},"665":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-37","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"The metadata lands in `experimental/ontology-metadata.json` inside `--outDir`. An SDK package generated with the flag, such as one built with `--asPackage` or published from Developer Console, also exports it as the `./experimental/ontology-metadata` subpath, which the examples below import. If you generate source files instead, import `../src/generatedNoCheck/experimental/ontology-metadata.json` with `resolveJsonModule` enabled. For the other generate options, see Generate your SDK."},"666":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-38","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#write-a-test","content":"This example uses Vitest. One server starts per Vitest worker, and every test resets the seed before it runs."},"667":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-39","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#create-a-fixture","content":"`test.extend` creates the server, seed client, and integration client once per worker and passes them to each test. `stop()` runs in `finally`, so a server that fails to start does not leave its process or `.test-run-*` directory behind."},"668":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-40","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#build-the-seed-data","content":"`createSeedWithMetadata` from `@osdk/seed-helpers` builds seed data without a server, and returns it with whatever your function returns. `create` returns a reference with the object's properties, `$apiName`, and `$primaryKey`; `link` connects two references by link name."},"669":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-41","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#build-the-seed-data","content":"`create` throws when an object of that type with the same primary key already exists, and when the properties do not match the metadata. A non-primary-key property set to `undefined` is allowed, even when the metadata marks it required, and is left empty."},"670":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-42","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#test-against-the-local-server","content":"Reset the seed before each test so tests do not see each other's writes, and clear function stubs after each one."},"671":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-43","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#test-against-the-local-server","content":"Replace `countEmployees` with a function from your SDK. A stub matches only calls whose parameters deep-equal the second argument of `whenQuery`, or calls with no parameters when you omit it: `client.whenQuery(fn, params).thenReturn(result)`. Use `thenThrow(error)` to make the call fail."},"672":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-44","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#run-the-tests","content":"Starting the Ontology server can take a while on the first run. If the fixture times out, raise Vitest's `hookTimeout` and `testTimeout`. Each server's `.test-run-*` directory is removed when it stops; add `.test-run-*` to `.gitignore` in case a run is killed first."},"673":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-45","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#change-data-inside-a-test","content":"Each seed client method updates the seed and writes it to the server before it resolves, so a test can set up extra data right before it queries:"},"674":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-46","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"Returns a `Promise<IntegrationServer>`. Creating the server writes the metadata to disk; `start()` launches the CLI."},"675":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-47","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| Option     | Type                   | Default | Description                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `OntologyFullMetadata` |         | The Ontology metadata to serve. Required. Interfaces that object types implement but the metadata does not include are dropped, with a warning. |","table":"table-3"},"676":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-48","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default             | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `foundryCliPath` | `string` | `foundry` on `PATH` | Path to the Foundry CLI binary. |","table":"table-3"},"677":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-49","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default               | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `projectPath` | `string` | The working directory | An existing directory to create the server's `.test-run-*` directory in. Servers that share a `projectPath` stay isolated. |","table":"table-3"},"678":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-50","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| `IntegrationServer` member | Description                                                     |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `start()`                  | Starts the Ontology service and resolves once it reports ready. |","table":"table-4"},"679":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-51","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| `IntegrationServer` member | Description                                                         |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stop()`                   | Stops the service and deletes the server's `.test-run-*` directory. |","table":"table-4"},"680":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-52","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| `IntegrationServer` member | Description                                              |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getOntologyUrl()`         | The local server's URL, or `undefined` before it starts. |","table":"table-4"},"681":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-53","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| `IntegrationServer` member | Description                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getClient()`              | Resolves to the `IntegrationClient` for this server. Repeated calls return the same client. |","table":"table-4"},"682":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-54","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"| `IntegrationServer` member | Description                                                                               |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getSeedClient()`          | Resolves to the `SeedClient` for this server. Repeated calls return the same seed client. |","table":"table-4"},"683":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-55","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#createintegrationserverconfig","content":"`getClient()` and `getSeedClient()` throw an error containing `Ontology server is not ready` when called before `start()` resolves."},"684":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-56","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"Every method applies the full seed to the server before it resolves."},"685":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-57","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member     | Description                                                                             |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seed(fn)` | Calls `fn` with a `SeedBuilder`, applies the result, and resolves to what `fn` returns. |","table":"table-5"},"686":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-58","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member         | Description                                                                 |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seed(output)` | Adds a `SeedOutput`, such as `baseSeed.output`, to the seed and applies it. |","table":"table-5"},"687":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-59","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member         | Description                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `set(output?)` | Replaces the whole seed with `output` and applies it. With no argument, clears all data. |","table":"table-5"},"688":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-60","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member           | Description                                  |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `addAll(output)` | Merges a `SeedOutput` into the current seed. |","table":"table-5"},"689":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-61","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member                | Description                                                                                |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `create(type, props)` | Creates an object and resolves to its reference. Throws if the primary key already exists. |","table":"table-5"},"690":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-62","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member               | Description                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `update(ref, props)` | Merges `props` into the object, leaving omitted properties unchanged. A property set to `undefined` is cleared. Creates the object if it does not exist. |","table":"table-5"},"691":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-63","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member        | Description                                            |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `delete(ref)` | Removes the object. Does nothing if it does not exist. |","table":"table-5"},"692":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-64","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member                           | Description                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `link(source, linkName, target)` | Links `source` to one reference, or an array for many-valued links. Re-adding a link does nothing. |","table":"table-5"},"693":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-65","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member                             | Description                                         |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `unlink(source, linkName, target)` | Removes matching links. Does nothing if none exist. |","table":"table-5"},"694":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-66","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#seedclient","content":"| Member                  | Description                                                                                            |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ref(type, primaryKey)` | Returns the reference for an object already in the seed, or `undefined`. Does not write to the server. |","table":"table-5"},"695":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-67","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#integrationclient","content":"A `Client` from `@osdk/client` with two extra members:"},"696":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-68","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#integrationclient","content":"| Member                      | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `whenQuery(query, params?)` | Starts a function stub. Finish it with `.thenReturn(result)` or `.thenThrow(error)`. |","table":"table-6"},"697":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-69","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#integrationclient","content":"| Member         | Description                  |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `clearStubs()` | Removes every function stub. |","table":"table-6"},"698":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-70","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#other-exports","content":"| Export                            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `createIntegrationClient(config)` | Creates an `IntegrationClient` for a server that is already running, with `baseUrl` and `metadata`, and optionally `caCertPath` for the server's certificate. Without `caCertPath`, the client skips TLS certificate checks. Throws if the Foundry CLI is not installed. |","table":"table-7"},"699":{"id":"/deploy/integration-testing-71","page_id":"/deploy/integration-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/deploy/integration-testing#other-exports","content":"| Export                     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `checkFoundryCliVersion()` | Resolves to `{ type: \"installed\", version }`, `{ type: \"version-incompatible\", version }`, `{ type: \"version-error\" }`, or `{ type: \"not-found\" }`. Use it to skip integration tests on machines without the CLI, for example with `describe.runIf`. |","table":"table-7"},"700":{"id":"/faq","page_id":"/faq","type":"page","content":"FAQ","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Help"],"tags":[],"url":"/faq"},"701":{"id":"/faq-0","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Short answers about @osdk/react versus React Query, using OSDK without React or on a server, package versions, dates, templates, and changelogs."},"702":{"id":"/faq-1","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Short answers to common questions about the OSDK TypeScript and React SDKs. Each answer links to the page that covers the topic in full."},"703":{"id":"/faq-2","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"React Query and SWR cache responses by a key you choose. `@osdk/react` knows the Ontology, so it caches objects themselves:"},"704":{"id":"/faq-3","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Each object is stored once by type and primary key, and every list, link, and detail view that contains it updates together."},"705":{"id":"/faq-4","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Actions report which objects they added, modified, or deleted, and the cache applies those edits without manual invalidation."},"706":{"id":"/faq-5","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Optimistic updates roll back automatically if the action fails."},"707":{"id":"/faq-6","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`streamUpdates: true` keeps lists live over a WebSocket."},"708":{"id":"/faq-7","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Use `@osdk/react` for Foundry data and keep React Query or SWR for other APIs. They work side by side, but do not copy OSDK data into another cache. See Caching and reactivity."},"709":{"id":"/faq-8","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Yes. `@osdk/client` has no UI dependency and works in any browser or JavaScript runtime with `fetch`. Create a client with `createClient` and call `client(Employee).fetchPage()`, `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction()`, and so on. See Use the client without React."},"710":{"id":"/faq-9","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"For the normalized cache outside React, `createObservableClient` from `@osdk/client/observable` is the same engine `OsdkProvider` uses."},"711":{"id":"/faq-10","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` are released together with one version number. Install the same version of all three, and keep prereleases together. Your generated SDK has a peer dependency on `@osdk/client`, so generate a new SDK version when you upgrade the client across many versions."},"712":{"id":"/faq-11","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`@osdk/react-components`, `@osdk/react-devtools`, and `@osdk/oauth` have their own version numbers. Upgrade them alongside the three core packages. See Version compatibility."},"713":{"id":"/faq-12","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Date and timestamp properties are ISO 8601 strings, such as `\"2024-03-15\"` and `\"2024-03-15T09:30:00Z\"`. Bundling a date library would add weight to every app, often duplicating a library you already use, and parsing every value costs time even when you never read it. Parse values with `Date` or your date library when you need date math. See Dates and timestamps."},"714":{"id":"/faq-13","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Yes, with `@osdk/client` and a confidential OAuth client. `createConfidentialOauthClient` from `@osdk/oauth` uses the client credentials grant, so requests act as the application's service user, not a signed-in person:"},"715":{"id":"/faq-14","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Keep the client secret on the server; never ship it to a browser. `@osdk/react` is for browser apps. See Authenticate a server or service."},"716":{"id":"/faq-15","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Yes. `@osdk/create-app` has React, Vue, and Expo templates, plus a React template for public apps without sign-in. Choose one at the prompt, or pass it directly:"},"717":{"id":"/faq-16","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"The Vue template uses `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/oauth` directly. `@osdk/react` and its components are React-only."},"718":{"id":"/faq-17","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Both come from your application in Developer Console:"},"719":{"id":"/faq-18","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"| Value     | Where to find it             |\n| --------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Client ID | The **OAuth & scopes** page. |","table":"table-0"},"720":{"id":"/faq-19","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"| Value        | Where to find it                                                                                                                |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Ontology RID | The **Ontology SDK** page. Your generated SDK also exports it as `$ontologyRid` when it was generated for a single environment. |","table":"table-0"},"721":{"id":"/faq-20","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"| Value        | Where to find it                                                                       |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Redirect URL | Also on **OAuth & scopes**. The value in your app must match one listed there exactly. |","table":"table-0"},"722":{"id":"/faq-21","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Apps created with `@osdk/create-app` store these in `.env.development` and `.env.production` as `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_ONTOLOGY_RID`, and `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`."},"723":{"id":"/faq-22","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"The generated SDK exports definitions, and the client does the work. Importing definitions by name lets your bundler drop the parts of the Ontology you do not use, and lets several SDKs share one `@osdk/client`. See Why `client(Employee)`."},"724":{"id":"/faq-23","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Each package has a `CHANGELOG.md` on GitHub and in its npm package:"},"725":{"id":"/faq-24","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`@osdk/react` changelog"},"726":{"id":"/faq-25","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`@osdk/client` changelog"},"727":{"id":"/faq-26","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"`@osdk/react-components` changelog"},"728":{"id":"/faq-27","page_id":"/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/faq","content":"Locally, open `node_modules/@osdk/react/CHANGELOG.md` to read the notes for the version you have installed."},"729":{"id":"/frameworks/expo","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"page","content":"Expo and React Native","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Frameworks"],"tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo"},"730":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-0","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo","content":"Build an iOS, Android, and web app on OSDK with the create-app Expo template, sign in with expo-auth-session, and query objects from React Native screens."},"731":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-1","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"Create an Expo app"},"732":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-2","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"What the template generates"},"733":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-3","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#sign-in","content":"Sign in"},"734":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-4","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#store-the-token","content":"Store the token"},"735":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-5","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#run-the-authorization-flow","content":"Run the authorization flow"},"736":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-6","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"Register redirect URLs"},"737":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-7","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#query-objects","content":"Query objects"},"738":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-8","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#use-osdkreact-hooks","content":"Use `@osdk/react` hooks"},"739":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-9","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"Metro configuration"},"740":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-10","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/expo#deploy-the-web-build","content":"Deploy the web build"},"741":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-11","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo","content":"The `expo` template of `@osdk/create-app` gives you an Expo Router app that signs in to Foundry and calls `@osdk/client` on iOS, Android, and the web. Sign-in works differently from the browser templates, so read Sign in before you configure redirect URLs."},"742":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-12","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"Run `@osdk/create-app` with the `expo` template:"},"743":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-13","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"The CLI asks for your Foundry URL, application RID, OAuth client ID, and SDK package. Quickstart lists every prompt and its flag. The Expo template supports SDK version 2.x only. It ignores the scopes you enter: `app/(tabs)/login.tsx` hardcodes `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write`, so edit that list instead."},"744":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-14","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"Answer **No** to the CORS proxy prompt, or pass `--corsProxy false`. The Expo template has no proxy server, but a **Yes** still sets `EXPO_PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_API_URL` to `http://localhost:8080` in `.env.development`, so every request goes to the Expo dev server instead of Foundry."},"745":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-15","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"Then install and start the app:"},"746":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-16","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"`FOUNDRY_TOKEN` must be able to read your SDK's npm registry; see Installation."},"747":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-17","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script         | Runs                     | Use it to                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dev`, `start` | `expo start --port 8080` | Start the dev server, then press `i`, `a`, or `w` to open iOS, Android, or web. |","table":"table-0"},"748":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-18","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script | Runs               | Use it to                         |\n| ------ | ------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| `ios`  | `expo start --ios` | Start and open the iOS simulator. |","table":"table-0"},"749":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-19","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script    | Runs                   | Use it to                            |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `android` | `expo start --android` | Start and open the Android emulator. |","table":"table-0"},"750":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-20","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script | Runs                           | Use it to                     |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `web`  | `expo start --web --port 8080` | Start and open the web build. |","table":"table-0"},"751":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-21","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script  | Runs                 | Use it to                                    |\n| ------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `build` | `expo export -p web` | Export the web build to `dist/` for hosting. |","table":"table-0"},"752":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-22","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script | Runs                           | Use it to  |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | ---------- |\n| `test` | `vitest run --passWithNoTests` | Run tests. |","table":"table-0"},"753":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-23","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#create-an-expo-app","content":"| Script          | Runs                              | Use it to                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reset-project` | `node ./scripts/reset-project.js` | Move `app/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `constants/`, and `scripts/`, including the Login screen, to `app-example/`, and create a minimal `app/`. |","table":"table-0"},"754":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-24","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.development\" />"},"755":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-25","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.production\" />"},"756":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-26","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"757":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-27","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"app.json\" />"},"758":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-28","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"759":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-29","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"metro.config.js\" />"},"760":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-30","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"761":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-31","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"_layout.tsx\" />"},"762":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-32","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"_layout.tsx\" />"},"763":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-33","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"explore.tsx\" />"},"764":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-34","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"index.tsx\" />"},"765":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-35","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"login.tsx\" />"},"766":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-36","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"Auth.ts\" />"},"767":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-37","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"768":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-38","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"osdkConst.ts\" />"},"769":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-39","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                                  | Purpose                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.env.development`, `.env.production` | `EXPO_PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_API_URL`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, and `EXPO_PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_ONTOLOGY_RID`. Expo inlines `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables into the bundle. |","table":"table-1"},"770":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-40","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                                                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry/osdkConst.ts` | Reads those variables and throws `Missing environment variable` if one is unset. |","table":"table-1"},"771":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-41","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File              | Purpose                                                                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `foundry/Auth.ts` | Holds the access token in memory and exposes `getValidAuthToken` as the client's token provider. |","table":"table-1"},"772":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-42","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                | Purpose                               |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry/client.ts` | Creates `client` with `createClient`. |","table":"table-1"},"773":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-43","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                                                |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `app/(tabs)/login.tsx` | The **Login** tab, which runs the OAuth flow with `expo-auth-session`. |","table":"table-1"},"774":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-44","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `app/(tabs)/index.tsx` | The **Home** tab. On web it also completes the sign-in popup. |","table":"table-1"},"775":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-45","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                     | Purpose                                                     |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `app/(tabs)/explore.tsx` | Lists the object types, actions, and functions in your SDK. |","table":"table-1"},"776":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-46","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File              | Purpose                                                        |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metro.config.js` | Lets Metro resolve the OSDK packages. See Metro configuration. |","table":"table-1"},"777":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-47","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File       | Purpose                                                                    |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `app.json` | Expo config, including the URL `scheme` used for native sign-in redirects. |","table":"table-1"},"778":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-48","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#what-the-template-generates","content":"The generated `.env` files also contain `EXPO_PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`. The Expo template does not read it: the redirect URL comes from `makeRedirectUri`, described below."},"779":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-49","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#sign-in","content":"The browser templates use `createPublicOauthClient` from `@osdk/oauth`, which signs in by navigating the page to Foundry and back. A native app cannot do that, so the Expo template runs the same authorization code flow with PKCE through `expo-auth-session` instead, which opens Foundry's sign-in page in a system browser session and returns the code to the app."},"780":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-50","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#store-the-token","content":"`foundry/Auth.ts` keeps the token response in a module variable. `getValidAuthToken` is the token provider you pass to `createClient`; it throws until the user has signed in:"},"781":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-51","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#store-the-token","content":"The token lives only in memory. The template neither refreshes nor persists it, so the user signs in again when the app restarts or the access token expires."},"782":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-52","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#run-the-authorization-flow","content":"The **Login** tab points `useAuthRequest` at Foundry's authorize and token endpoints under `/multipass/api/oauth2`, then exchanges the returned code for a token. This version adds error handling to the generated screen:"},"783":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-53","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#run-the-authorization-flow","content":"Request only the scopes your app needs, and allow each of them for your application on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console."},"784":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-54","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#run-the-authorization-flow","content":"On web, `promptAsync` opens Foundry in a popup. Foundry redirects the popup to your app's root URL, where `app/(tabs)/index.tsx` calls `WebBrowser.maybeCompleteAuthSession()` from `expo-web-browser`. That call hands the result back to the original window and closes the popup. Keep it in whichever screen renders at the redirect path."},"785":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-55","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"`makeRedirectUri({ path: \"\" })` returns a different URL on each platform, and each one must be registered exactly on **OAuth & scopes**:"},"786":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-56","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"| Where the app runs     | Redirect URL                                           |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Web, local development | `http://localhost:8080`, with no `/auth/callback` path |","table":"table-2"},"787":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-57","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"| Where the app runs     | Redirect URL                                                                          |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Web, hosted on Foundry | Your site's root URL, such as `https://<subdomain>.<your-domain>.palantirfoundry.com` |","table":"table-2"},"788":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-58","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"| Where the app runs | Redirect URL                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| iOS and Android    | In a development or standalone build, a URL with the `scheme` from `app.json`; in Expo Go, an `exp://<ip>:<port>` URL. The template's scheme is `my-app`; change it to one unique to your app. |","table":"table-2"},"789":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-59","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#register-redirect-urls","content":"To see the exact value on a device, render or log `redirectUri` from the **Login** screen and copy it into Developer Console."},"790":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-60","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#query-objects","content":"Call the client from a screen once the user has signed in. Keep the list on screen while it reloads:"},"791":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-61","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#query-objects","content":"A request made before sign-in fails with `No valid auth token`. Send users to the **Login** tab first, as the template does by making it the initial route. The rest of the client API is the same as on the web; see Use the client without React."},"792":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-62","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#use-osdkreact-hooks","content":"`@osdk/react` does not touch the DOM, so its hooks work in React Native screens. The template lists `@osdk/react` in `package.json` but does not use it, and pins it to `^0.7.0`, a release line from before `@osdk/react` shared a version number with `@osdk/client`. Install the same version as your `@osdk/client` first, for example:"},"793":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-63","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#use-osdkreact-hooks","content":"Version compatibility explains the rule. `react-dom`, a peer dependency of `@osdk/react`, is already in the template for the web build. Then wrap the root layout in `OsdkProvider`:"},"794":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-64","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#use-osdkreact-hooks","content":"The generated layout also loads fonts, controls the splash screen, and sets a theme; keep those and add `OsdkProvider` around the `Stack`. Screens can now use the hooks:"},"795":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-65","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#use-osdkreact-hooks","content":"Hooks fetch as soon as a screen mounts, so mount data screens only after sign-in. Everything else about the hooks is covered under Query objects and Apply actions. `@osdk/react-components` renders HTML, so it works in the web build only."},"796":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-66","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"`metro.config.js` makes three changes to Expo's default Metro config:"},"797":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-67","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"**Enables package exports** (`resolver.unstable_enablePackageExports: true`), because the OSDK packages publish their entry points, such as `@osdk/client/observable`, through the `exports` field."},"798":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-68","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"**Resolves `@osdk` packages with the `browser`, `require`, and `import` conditions**, so Metro picks their browser builds on every platform."},"799":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-69","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"**Loads `.env.development` with `dotenv`** and adds `react-native-svg-transformer` for `.svg` imports."},"800":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-70","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#metro-configuration","content":"Keep the first two if you replace the file. The template adds no polyfills."},"801":{"id":"/frameworks/expo-71","page_id":"/frameworks/expo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/expo#deploy-the-web-build","content":"`npm run build` exports the web build to `dist/`, which `foundry.config.json` points at. Register your site's root URL as a redirect URL first, then follow Hosting. Publishing to the App Store or Google Play uses Expo's own build tooling and is not covered by the template."},"802":{"id":"/frameworks/node","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"page","content":"Node.js","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Frameworks"],"tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node"},"803":{"id":"/frameworks/node-0","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node","content":"Use @osdk/client in Node.js scripts, servers, and serverless functions, with service-user or token auth, custom fetch, and a bulk-edit example."},"804":{"id":"/frameworks/node-1","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"805":{"id":"/frameworks/node-2","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#install","content":"Install"},"806":{"id":"/frameworks/node-3","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#authenticate","content":"Authenticate"},"807":{"id":"/frameworks/node-4","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#create-the-client","content":"Create the client"},"808":{"id":"/frameworks/node-5","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables"},"809":{"id":"/frameworks/node-6","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"Page through every object and apply an action"},"810":{"id":"/frameworks/node-7","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#apply-in-batches","content":"Apply in batches"},"811":{"id":"/frameworks/node-8","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#use-a-custom-fetch","content":"Use a custom `fetch`"},"812":{"id":"/frameworks/node-9","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#logging","content":"Logging"},"813":{"id":"/frameworks/node-10","page_id":"/frameworks/node","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/node#servers-and-serverless-functions","content":"Servers and serverless functions"},"814":{"id":"/frameworks/node-11","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node","content":"`@osdk/client` runs in Node.js without a browser or bundler, so you can query the Ontology and apply actions from scripts, backend services, scheduled jobs, and serverless functions. This page covers what changes outside the browser: authentication, module format, `fetch`, and configuration."},"815":{"id":"/frameworks/node-12","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#requirements","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                          |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Node.js     | A version with a global `fetch`: Node 18 or later. The client and `@osdk/oauth` use `globalThis.fetch` unless you pass your own. |","table":"table-0"},"816":{"id":"/frameworks/node-13","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#requirements","content":"| Requirement   | Details                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Module format | `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/api`, `@osdk/oauth`, and generated SDKs ship both ESM and CommonJS builds. The samples on this page use top-level `await`, which needs ESM: set `\"type\": \"module\"` in `package.json` or use `.mjs` and `.mts` files. |","table":"table-0"},"817":{"id":"/frameworks/node-14","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#requirements","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| TypeScript  | Set `\"module\": \"NodeNext\"` (or `\"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\"` if you bundle). Older `node` resolution ignores package `exports` and cannot find subpaths such as `@osdk/client/unstable-do-not-use`. With `NodeNext`, relative imports need a `.js` extension, as in `./client.js`. |","table":"table-0"},"818":{"id":"/frameworks/node-15","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#requirements","content":"Subscriptions work in Node without a polyfill: `@osdk/client` depends on `ws` and uses it for WebSocket connections in Node."},"819":{"id":"/frameworks/node-16","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#install","content":"Install the client, the OAuth helpers, and your generated SDK. The SDK comes from your Foundry npm registry, so set up `.npmrc` first as described in Installation."},"820":{"id":"/frameworks/node-17","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#install","content":"`@osdk/react` is not needed in Node."},"821":{"id":"/frameworks/node-18","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#authenticate","content":"A Node process has no browser to run the sign-in redirect, so `createPublicOauthClient` does not apply. Use one of these instead:"},"822":{"id":"/frameworks/node-19","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#authenticate","content":"| Token provider                                     | Requests run as                                                     | Use it for                                                                                                          |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createConfidentialOauthClient` from `@osdk/oauth` | The service user of a confidential application in Developer Console | Servers, scheduled jobs, CI, and serverless functions. The client fetches a new token when the current one expires. |","table":"table-1"},"823":{"id":"/frameworks/node-20","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#authenticate","content":"| Token provider                                   | Requests run as                                           | Use it for                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| A function that returns a token you already have | Whoever owns the token, such as you with a personal token | One-off scripts and local tools. The token is not refreshed; requests fail with `401` once it expires. |","table":"table-1"},"824":{"id":"/frameworks/node-21","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#authenticate","content":"Both options, and the scopes the confidential client requests, are covered on Authentication."},"825":{"id":"/frameworks/node-22","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#create-the-client","content":"Read the Foundry URL and credentials from environment variables and create one client at module scope. Other modules import it."},"826":{"id":"/frameworks/node-23","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#create-the-client","content":"`createClient` takes the same arguments in Node as in the browser; see Create a client for every option. Only an explicit `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` sets the branch in Node, because there is no page URL or meta tag to read it from."},"827":{"id":"/frameworks/node-24","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"The OSDK packages do not read environment variables themselves. These names are a convention used on this page:"},"828":{"id":"/frameworks/node-25","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"| Variable      | Used for                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `FOUNDRY_URL` | The base URL of your Foundry stack, such as `https://example.palantirfoundry.com`. |","table":"table-2"},"829":{"id":"/frameworks/node-26","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"| Variable            | Used for                                  |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID` | The confidential application's client ID. |","table":"table-2"},"830":{"id":"/frameworks/node-27","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                | Used for                                      |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `FOUNDRY_CLIENT_SECRET` | The confidential application's client secret. |","table":"table-2"},"831":{"id":"/frameworks/node-28","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"| Variable        | Used for                                       |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` | A bearer token, for the existing-token option. |","table":"table-2"},"832":{"id":"/frameworks/node-29","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#environment-variables","content":"Keep secrets out of source control. Locally, put them in a `.env` file that git ignores and load it with `node --env-file=.env` (Node 20.6 and later). In production, use your platform's secret store."},"833":{"id":"/frameworks/node-30","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"This script finds every `Employee` whose department is `Eng` and renames the department to `Engineering` with the `modifyEmployee` action. Pass `--dry-run` to validate each edit without applying it."},"834":{"id":"/frameworks/node-31","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"Run it with a TypeScript runner such as `tsx`, or compile it with `tsc` first:"},"835":{"id":"/frameworks/node-32","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"How it works:"},"836":{"id":"/frameworks/node-33","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"`asyncIter` fetches page after page until every matching object has loaded. It reads from a consistent snapshot, so each object arrives once even when data changes during the loop. Page size is chosen by the client; `asyncIter` has no `$pageSize` option."},"837":{"id":"/frameworks/node-34","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"The script collects primary keys first and applies the action afterwards. A long-running loop can outlive the snapshot, and `asyncIter` throws when the snapshot expires, so keep slow work out of the iteration."},"838":{"id":"/frameworks/node-35","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"Object parameters such as `employee` accept a primary key or a loaded object."},"839":{"id":"/frameworks/node-36","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when validation fails, with details in `error.validation`. Other request failures, such as a missing permission, throw `PalantirApiError` from `@osdk/client`. Catching per object lets the rest of the run continue."},"840":{"id":"/frameworks/node-37","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#page-through-every-object-and-apply-an-action","content":"With `{ $validateOnly: true }`, `applyAction` returns the validation result instead of applying the action. Its `result` is `\"VALID\"` or `\"INVALID\"`."},"841":{"id":"/frameworks/node-38","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#apply-in-batches","content":"`batchApplyAction` applies an array of parameter objects in one request, which is faster than one request per object. It does not support `$validateOnly`. Send the edits in chunks:"},"842":{"id":"/frameworks/node-39","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#apply-in-batches","content":"Pass `{ $returnEdits: true }` as the second argument to get the objects each batch added and modified."},"843":{"id":"/frameworks/node-40","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#use-a-custom-fetch","content":"Pass a `fetch` implementation as the fifth argument of `createClient`, and as the `fetchFn` argument of `createConfidentialOauthClient` so token requests use it too. A common reason is a stack whose TLS certificate is signed by a private certificate authority. With `undici`:"},"844":{"id":"/frameworks/node-41","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#use-a-custom-fetch","content":"Passing `undefined` for the scopes keeps the default scopes."},"845":{"id":"/frameworks/node-42","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#logging","content":"By default the client prints errors to the console. Pass a `logger` to route its output elsewhere. The `Logger` interface from `@osdk/api` matches pino, so a pino logger works as-is:"},"846":{"id":"/frameworks/node-43","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#servers-and-serverless-functions","content":"Create the client once at module scope, not per request. The token provider caches its access token in memory, so reusing the client avoids a token request for every call. In serverless functions, warm invocations reuse the module and its client."},"847":{"id":"/frameworks/node-44","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#servers-and-serverless-functions","content":"A confidential client acts as one service user for every request. To run a request as the user who called your server, create a client per request with that user's token, and do not share it across users."},"848":{"id":"/frameworks/node-45","page_id":"/frameworks/node","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/node#servers-and-serverless-functions","content":"Never ship the client secret to a browser. Keep `createConfidentialOauthClient` in server code only."},"849":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"page","content":"TypeScript library","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Frameworks"],"tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library"},"850":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-0","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library","content":"Scaffold a standalone TypeScript package with the create-app typescript-library template, and add OSDK code that apps can share."},"851":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-1","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#when-to-use-it","content":"When to use it"},"852":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-2","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#create-the-library","content":"Create the library"},"853":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-3","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"Project structure"},"854":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-4","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"Scripts"},"855":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-5","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"Add OSDK code"},"856":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-6","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library","content":"The `typescript-library` template of `@osdk/create-app` creates a TypeScript package that builds ESM and type declarations with `tsc`, tests with Vitest, and lints with Ultracite. Use it to start a package of shared code, such as Ontology helpers that several of your OSDK apps import."},"857":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-7","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library","content":"This template is beta and hidden from the CLI's framework list. Select it with `--template typescript-library`. It contains no OSDK code or dependencies; you add those yourself."},"858":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-8","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#when-to-use-it","content":"| You want to                                                        | Use           |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------- |\n| Share functions, types, or object-set helpers between several apps | This template |","table":"table-0"},"859":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-9","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#when-to-use-it","content":"| You want to         | Use                                                     |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Build a browser app | The `react`, `vue`, or `expo` template. See Quickstart. |","table":"table-0"},"860":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-10","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#when-to-use-it","content":"| You want to                                  | Use                                |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Run a script, server, or serverless function | A plain Node project. See Node.js. |","table":"table-0"},"861":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-11","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#create-the-library","content":"Run `@osdk/create-app` with the template, and pass `--skipOsdk` to skip the SDK prompts. `--skipOsdk` only works with an explicit `--sdkVersion 2.x`:"},"862":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-12","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#create-the-library","content":"The CLI still asks for a Foundry URL, application RID, client ID, application URL, CORS proxy, and scopes, and writes `.env.development`, `.env.production`, `.npmrc`, and `foundry.config.json` from them. The library does not read the `.env` files or `foundry.config.json`; delete them if you do not need them. Keep `.npmrc` if you will install your SDK from the Foundry registry. It holds only the token line, so add your SDK's `@scope:registry=` line as described in Installation."},"863":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-13","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#create-the-library","content":"Then install and build:"},"864":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-14","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"AGENTS.md\" />"},"865":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-15","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"oxfmt.config.ts\" />"},"866":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-16","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"oxlint.config.ts\" />"},"867":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-17","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"868":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-18","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"tsconfig.json\" />"},"869":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-19","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"CLAUDE.md\" />"},"870":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-20","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"settings.json\" />"},"871":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-21","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"extensions.json\" />"},"872":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-22","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"index.ts\" />"},"873":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-23","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"<File name=\"index.test.ts\" />"},"874":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-24","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/index.ts` | The package entry point. Everything it exports is the library's public API. The template exports a sample `greet` function. |","table":"table-1"},"875":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-25","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/__tests__/` | Vitest tests. `tsconfig.json` excludes them from the build. |","table":"table-1"},"876":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-26","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `package.json` | An ESM package (`\"type\": \"module\"`) whose `exports`, `main`, and `types` point at `dist/`. Only `dist/` is published. |","table":"table-1"},"877":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-27","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File            | Purpose                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tsconfig.json` | Strict settings that compile `src/` to `dist/` with declaration files, declaration maps, and source maps. Targets ES2022. |","table":"table-1"},"878":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-28","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File                                  | Purpose                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `oxlint.config.ts`, `oxfmt.config.ts` | The Ultracite presets for oxlint and oxfmt. Lint warns on function expressions and prefers named function declarations. |","table":"table-1"},"879":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-29","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File                    | Purpose                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/` | Coding standards for AI agents. `.claude/settings.json` runs `npx ultracite fix` after every file edit Claude Code makes. |","table":"table-1"},"880":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-30","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#project-structure","content":"| File                      | Purpose                       |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `.vscode/extensions.json` | Recommends the Oxc extension. |","table":"table-1"},"881":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-31","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script  | Runs  | Does                                                           |\n| ------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build` | `tsc` | Type-checks and emits JavaScript and `.d.ts` files to `dist/`. |","table":"table-2"},"882":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-32","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script  | Runs          | Does                      |\n| ------- | ------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `clean` | `rm -rf dist` | Deletes the build output. |","table":"table-2"},"883":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-33","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script | Runs         | Does                 |\n| ------ | ------------ | -------------------- |\n| `test` | `vitest run` | Runs the tests once. |","table":"table-2"},"884":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-34","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script       | Runs     | Does                          |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `test:watch` | `vitest` | Runs the tests in watch mode. |","table":"table-2"},"885":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-35","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script | Runs              | Does                              |\n| ------ | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `lint` | `ultracite check` | Checks formatting and lint rules. |","table":"table-2"},"886":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-36","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script | Runs            | Does                              |\n| ------ | --------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `fix`  | `ultracite fix` | Fixes formatting and lint issues. |","table":"table-2"},"887":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-37","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"| Script   | Runs      | Does                |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------- |\n| `format` | `oxfmt .` | Formats every file. |","table":"table-2"},"888":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-38","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#scripts","content":"The generated `README.md` mentions `npm run check`. The script is named `lint`."},"889":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-39","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"Install `@osdk/client` and your SDK. Your SDK comes from your Foundry npm registry, so set up `.npmrc` first as described in Installation:"},"890":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-40","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"Also list both in `peerDependencies`, so an app that installs your library provides them. The app and your library then share one `@osdk/client` and one copy of the SDK. Your generated SDK already declares `@osdk/client` as a peer."},"891":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-41","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"Take the `Client` as a parameter instead of creating one in the library. The app keeps a single client with its own authentication, and your functions use it:"},"892":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-42","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"Export it from the entry point:"},"893":{"id":"/frameworks/typescript-library-43","page_id":"/frameworks/typescript-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/typescript-library#add-osdk-code","content":"`tsc` does not rewrite import paths. Write relative imports with the `.js` extension, as above, so `dist/` also loads in Node.js without a bundler. Create a client lists the client methods you can call."},"894":{"id":"/frameworks/vue","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"page","content":"Vue","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Frameworks"],"tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue"},"895":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-0","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue","content":"Build a Vue app on OSDK with the create-app Vue template, set up sign-in, and query objects and apply actions from components with @osdk/client."},"896":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-1","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#create-a-vue-app","content":"Create a Vue app"},"897":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-2","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"What the template generates"},"898":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-3","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#set-up-the-client-and-sign-in","content":"Set up the client and sign-in"},"899":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-4","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#query-objects-in-a-component","content":"Query objects in a component"},"900":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-5","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#refetch-when-inputs-change","content":"Refetch when inputs change"},"901":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-6","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#apply-an-action","content":"Apply an action"},"902":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-7","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"Reactivity tips"},"903":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-8","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#keep-lists-live-with-the-observable-client","content":"Keep lists live with the observable client"},"904":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-9","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/frameworks/vue#deploy","content":"Deploy"},"905":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-10","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue","content":"Use `@osdk/client` directly from Vue components: there is no Vue-specific OSDK package. The `vue` template of `@osdk/create-app` gives you a Vite app with sign-in, routing, and a configured client."},"906":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-11","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#create-a-vue-app","content":"Run `@osdk/create-app` with the `vue` template:"},"907":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-12","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#create-a-vue-app","content":"The CLI asks for your Foundry URL, application RID, OAuth client ID, and SDK package, the same prompts as the React template. Quickstart lists every prompt and its flag. The template uses SDK version 2.x unless you pass `--sdkVersion 1.x`."},"908":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-13","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#create-a-vue-app","content":"Then install and start the dev server:"},"909":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-14","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#create-a-vue-app","content":"Open `http://localhost:8080`. `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` must be able to read your SDK's npm registry; see Installation."},"910":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-15","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.development\" />"},"911":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-16","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.production\" />"},"912":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-17","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"913":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-18","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"914":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-19","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"915":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-20","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"916":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-21","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"917":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-22","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"AuthCallback.vue\" />"},"918":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-23","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"919":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-24","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"env.test.ts\" />"},"920":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-25","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"Home.vue\" />"},"921":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-26","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"main.ts\" />"},"922":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-27","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"router.ts\" />"},"923":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-28","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"Header.vue\" />"},"924":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-29","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"NextSteps.vue\" />"},"925":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-30","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"<File name=\"Osdk.vue\" />"},"926":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-31","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                                  | Purpose                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.env.development`, `.env.production` | `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`, and `VITE_FOUNDRY_ONTOLOGY_RID` for each mode. |","table":"table-0"},"927":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-32","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File         | Purpose                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `index.html` | Copies the env values into `<meta>` tags such as `osdk-foundryUrl` and `osdk-clientId`. |","table":"table-0"},"928":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-33","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File            | Purpose                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/client.ts` | Reads the meta tags, creates `auth` with `createPublicOauthClient`, and exports `client` from `createClient`. |","table":"table-0"},"929":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-34","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File            | Purpose                                                                 |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/router.ts` | A `vue-router` router with `/` and the redirect route `/auth/callback`. |","table":"table-0"},"930":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-35","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                        |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/AuthCallback.vue` | Completes sign-in when Foundry redirects back. |","table":"table-0"},"931":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-36","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File              | Purpose                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/env.test.ts` | Fails the test run when `.env.production` is missing a value or still has a `<placeholder>`. It runs only when `VERIFY_ENV_PRODUCTION=true`. |","table":"table-0"},"932":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-37","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                  |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite.config.ts` | Serves on port `8080`, defines `process.env.NODE_ENV`, and adds the optional CORS proxy. |","table":"table-0"},"933":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-38","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                         |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json` | Settings for deploying to Foundry. See Hosting. |","table":"table-0"},"934":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-39","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"The generated `package.json` depends on `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/oauth`, `@osdk/foundry`, your SDK, `vue`, and `vue-router`, and has these scripts:"},"935":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-40","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| Script | Runs   |\n| ------ | ------ |\n| `dev`  | `vite` |","table":"table-1"},"936":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-41","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| Script  | Runs                                                                          |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build` | `vue-tsc && vite build`, which type-checks `.vue` files, then writes `dist/`. |","table":"table-1"},"937":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-42","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| Script | Runs         |\n| ------ | ------------ |\n| `test` | `vitest run` |","table":"table-1"},"938":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-43","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"| Script    | Runs           |\n| --------- | -------------- |\n| `preview` | `vite preview` |","table":"table-1"},"939":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-44","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#what-the-template-generates","content":"`vite.config.ts` aliases `vue` to `vue/dist/vue.esm-bundler`, the build that includes the template compiler, because `src/main.ts` mounts the root component from a template string (`\"<router-view />\"`). Keep the alias, or change `main.ts` to mount a compiled `.vue` component instead."},"940":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-45","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#set-up-the-client-and-sign-in","content":"`src/client.ts` exports one `auth` and one `client` for the whole app. It reads its configuration from the `<meta>` tags in `index.html`, so you can change values per environment without touching code:"},"941":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-46","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#set-up-the-client-and-sign-in","content":"The generated file also throws when a tag still holds an unreplaced `%VITE_...%` value, which means the variable is missing from your `.env` file."},"942":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-47","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#set-up-the-client-and-sign-in","content":"The first request starts sign-in. Foundry redirects back to `/auth/callback`, where `AuthCallback.vue` exchanges the code and returns to `/`:"},"943":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-48","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#set-up-the-client-and-sign-in","content":"`VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL` must exactly match a redirect URL on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console. Authentication covers scopes, token storage, and sign-out, all of which work the same in Vue."},"944":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-49","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#query-objects-in-a-component","content":"Call the client from `<script setup>` and keep the result in a `shallowRef`. This component loads the first page of engineers and keeps the list on screen while it reloads:"},"945":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-50","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#query-objects-in-a-component","content":"Every method on the client, including `fetchOne`, `asyncIter`, `aggregate`, and `$link`, works the same in Vue. See Use the client without React for the full API."},"946":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-51","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#refetch-when-inputs-change","content":"Use `watch` with `immediate: true` to load data from reactive inputs, such as a filter bound to a `<select>`. Mark each run as stale in `onCleanup`, so a slow response for an old value cannot overwrite a newer one:"},"947":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-52","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#apply-an-action","content":"Put the action in its own component. Await `applyAction` inside `try`/`catch`, and emit an event on success so the parent reloads; the client does not update objects you already fetched:"},"948":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-53","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#apply-an-action","content":"In `EmployeeList.vue`, render `<PromoteButton :employee=\"employee\" @promoted=\"load\" />` inside each `<li>`. Validation failures throw `ActionValidationError`; Apply an action shows how to read them."},"949":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-54","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"**Store results in `shallowRef`.** OSDK objects are frozen. Vue does not wrap frozen objects in reactive proxies, so changes are never detected inside them anyway. Replace the whole value when new data arrives."},"950":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-55","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"**Never mutate an object to update the UI.** Assigning to `employee.jobTitle` throws in strict mode. Apply an action, then fetch again."},"951":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-56","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"**Key lists by `$primaryKey`.** It is unique within an object type and stable across fetches."},"952":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-57","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"**Create the client once.** Import `client` from `src/client.ts` in every component. Do not call `createClient` inside `setup`."},"953":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-58","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#reactivity-tips","content":"**Do not reach for `@osdk/react`.** Its hooks need React. For a shared cache in Vue, use the observable client below."},"954":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-59","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#keep-lists-live-with-the-observable-client","content":"`createObservableClient` from `@osdk/client/observable` is the cache that powers `@osdk/react`. It deduplicates requests, shares objects between subscribers, and refetches affected lists after an action you apply through it. Wrap it in a composable:"},"955":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-60","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#keep-lists-live-with-the-observable-client","content":"`watchEffect` resubscribes when `department()` changes and unsubscribes when the component unmounts. Call `useEmployees(() => props.department)` from `<script setup>`."},"956":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-61","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#keep-lists-live-with-the-observable-client","content":"Apply actions through `observableClient.applyAction(modifyEmployee, { ... })` instead of `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction(...)`. Before it resolves, the objects the action edited are fetched again. Subscribed lists of the edited types then refetch in the background, so the component updates without a manual reload. It throws like `applyAction`, so await it in `try`/`catch`."},"957":{"id":"/frameworks/vue-62","page_id":"/frameworks/vue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/frameworks/vue#deploy","content":"`npm run build` writes the app to `dist/`, which `foundry.config.json` already points at. Before you build for production, set `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL` in `.env.production` to your hosted app's `/auth/callback` and add that URL on **OAuth & scopes**. Hosting covers uploading the build to Foundry."},"958":{"id":"/guides/vite","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"page","content":"Use OSDK with Vite","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite"},"959":{"id":"/guides/vite-0","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite","content":"Configure Vite for OSDK apps, including the process.env fix, a local CORS proxy to Foundry, and the OSDK Devtools plugin."},"960":{"id":"/guides/vite-1","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#define-processenvnode_env","content":"Define `process.env.NODE_ENV`"},"961":{"id":"/guides/vite-2","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#proxy-foundry-requests-in-development","content":"Proxy Foundry requests in development"},"962":{"id":"/guides/vite-3","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#proxy-the-api-paths","content":"Proxy the API paths"},"963":{"id":"/guides/vite-4","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#point-the-client-at-the-dev-server","content":"Point the client at the dev server"},"964":{"id":"/guides/vite-5","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#allow-the-redirect-url","content":"Allow the redirect URL"},"965":{"id":"/guides/vite-6","page_id":"/guides/vite","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/vite#add-osdk-devtools","content":"Add OSDK Devtools"},"966":{"id":"/guides/vite-7","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite","content":"Vite is the default bundler for apps created with `@osdk/create-app`. This page covers the Vite settings an OSDK app needs and why."},"967":{"id":"/guides/vite-8","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite","content":"The React template in `@osdk/create-app` already includes these settings in its generated `vite.config.ts`. Read on if you add OSDK to an existing Vite app or want to know what the generated config does."},"968":{"id":"/guides/vite-9","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#define-processenvnode_env","content":"OSDK packages read `process.env.NODE_ENV` to decide how much to log and to strip development-only code from production builds. Vite does not replace `process.env` by default, so the browser throws:"},"969":{"id":"/guides/vite-10","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#define-processenvnode_env","content":"Tell Vite to replace `process.env.NODE_ENV` with the current mode:"},"970":{"id":"/guides/vite-11","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#define-processenvnode_env","content":"`vite dev` runs in `development` mode and `vite build` in `production` mode, so production bundles get `\"production\"`."},"971":{"id":"/guides/vite-12","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#proxy-foundry-requests-in-development","content":"The browser blocks requests from `http://localhost:8080` to your Foundry stack unless the stack allows that origin for CORS. If you cannot get localhost allowed, proxy the requests through the Vite dev server instead. `@osdk/create-app` generates this setup when you answer yes to the CORS proxy prompt or pass `--corsProxy true`:"},"972":{"id":"/guides/vite-13","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#proxy-the-api-paths","content":"Forward `/api` and `/multipass/api` to your Foundry URL:"},"973":{"id":"/guides/vite-14","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#point-the-client-at-the-dev-server","content":"Set the Foundry URL that the client uses to the dev server's origin, so requests go through the proxy:"},"974":{"id":"/guides/vite-15","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#point-the-client-at-the-dev-server","content":"Pass that URL to both `createPublicOauthClient` and `createClient`. The OAuth calls under `/multipass/api` and the data calls under `/api` then reach Foundry through the proxy."},"975":{"id":"/guides/vite-16","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#allow-the-redirect-url","content":"Add `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` as a redirect URL on the OAuth client in Developer Console."},"976":{"id":"/guides/vite-17","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#allow-the-redirect-url","content":"The proxy runs only under `vite dev`. Production builds call Foundry directly, so keep the real Foundry URL in `.env.production`. Once your stack allows `http://localhost:8080` for CORS, you can remove the proxy and set `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL` back to the Foundry URL."},"977":{"id":"/guides/vite-18","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#add-osdk-devtools","content":"`@osdk/react-devtools` ships a Vite plugin that injects an inspection panel into your app during `vite dev` and does nothing in production builds:"},"978":{"id":"/guides/vite-19","page_id":"/guides/vite","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/vite#add-osdk-devtools","content":"See OSDK Devtools for installation, options, and the panel tabs."},"979":{"id":"/installation","page_id":"/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation"},"980":{"id":"/installation-0","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"Add @osdk/client, @osdk/oauth, @osdk/react, and your generated SDK to an existing app, with the npm registry setup and version rules they need."},"981":{"id":"/installation-1","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"982":{"id":"/installation-2","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#install","content":"Install"},"983":{"id":"/installation-3","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#point-your-sdks-scope-at-the-foundry-registry","content":"Point your SDK's scope at the Foundry registry"},"984":{"id":"/installation-4","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#install-the-client-packages-and-your-sdk","content":"Install the client packages and your SDK"},"985":{"id":"/installation-5","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#add-the-react-packages","content":"Add the React packages"},"986":{"id":"/installation-6","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#create-the-client","content":"Create the client"},"987":{"id":"/installation-7","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"Version compatibility"},"988":{"id":"/installation-8","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#optional-peers-for-platform-apis","content":"Optional peers for Platform APIs"},"989":{"id":"/installation-9","page_id":"/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation#bundler-setup","content":"Bundler setup"},"990":{"id":"/installation-10","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"Add OSDK to an app you already have by installing the client packages and your generated SDK from your Foundry npm registry. To start from a new project with everything configured, use the Quickstart instead."},"991":{"id":"/installation-11","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#before-you-start","content":"Generate an SDK for your application in Developer Console with the **npm** package type, and note three values from its install instructions:"},"992":{"id":"/installation-12","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example       |\n| ---------------- | ------------- |\n| SDK package name | `@my-app/sdk` |","table":"table-0"},"993":{"id":"/installation-13","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| npm registry URL | `https://example.palantirfoundry.com/artifacts/api/repositories/ri.artifacts.main.repository.<id>/contents/release/npm` |","table":"table-0"},"994":{"id":"/installation-14","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#before-you-start","content":"| Value         | Example                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry token | A token that can read that registry. Keep it out of source control. |","table":"table-0"},"995":{"id":"/installation-15","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#point-your-sdks-scope-at-the-foundry-registry","content":"The generated SDK is not on the public npm registry. Add two lines to `.npmrc` in your project root: one maps your SDK's scope to the Foundry registry, and one authenticates every request to Foundry's artifacts API with a token from the environment."},"996":{"id":"/installation-16","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#point-your-sdks-scope-at-the-foundry-registry","content":"Replace `example.palantirfoundry.com` with your Foundry host, `@my-app` with your SDK's scope, and the registry URL with yours. Keep the trailing `/` on the registry URL, which pnpm requires. This is the same file `@osdk/create-app` writes."},"997":{"id":"/installation-17","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#point-your-sdks-scope-at-the-foundry-registry","content":"Export the token before you install, and set it as a secret in CI:"},"998":{"id":"/installation-18","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#install-the-client-packages-and-your-sdk","content":"| Package        | Why you need it                                               |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/client` | `createClient` and the runtime that runs queries and actions. |","table":"table-1"},"999":{"id":"/installation-19","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#install-the-client-packages-and-your-sdk","content":"| Package     | Why you need it                          |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/api` | Types shared by the client and your SDK. |","table":"table-1"},"1000":{"id":"/installation-20","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#install-the-client-packages-and-your-sdk","content":"| Package       | Why you need it                                           |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/oauth` | Token providers for signing users in. See Authentication. |","table":"table-1"},"1001":{"id":"/installation-21","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#install-the-client-packages-and-your-sdk","content":"| Package       | Why you need it                        |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `@my-app/sdk` | Your Ontology's generated definitions. |","table":"table-1"},"1002":{"id":"/installation-22","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#add-the-react-packages","content":"Skip this step if you do not use React."},"1003":{"id":"/installation-23","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#add-the-react-packages","content":"`@osdk/react` supports React 17, 18, and 19. For prebuilt components, also install `@osdk/react-components`; its setup is on Components prerequisites."},"1004":{"id":"/installation-24","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#create-the-client","content":"Create one client for your app and wrap your React tree in `OsdkProvider`. Create a client walks through both."},"1005":{"id":"/installation-25","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"`@osdk/client`, `@osdk/api`, and `@osdk/react` are released together and share a version number. `@osdk/react` imports its cache runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, which is tied to the exact release line, so a mismatch fails at build time even when npm's peer ranges are satisfied."},"1006":{"id":"/installation-26","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"**Install the same version of all three.** If `@osdk/react` is `2.83.0`, use `@osdk/client@2.83.0` and `@osdk/api@2.83.0`."},"1007":{"id":"/installation-27","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"**Keep prereleases together.** A prerelease `@osdk/react`, such as `-beta.3`, needs the same prerelease of `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api`. Pairing it with stable releases breaks."},"1008":{"id":"/installation-28","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"**Upgrade them in one command.** Bump the three packages together, and include `@osdk/react-components` if you use it:"},"1009":{"id":"/installation-29","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"**Your generated SDK has a peer dependency on `@osdk/client`.** It is set to the client version that generated it, so install an `@osdk/client` that satisfies the SDK's peer range. When you upgrade the client across many versions, generate a new SDK version too."},"1010":{"id":"/installation-30","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"A version mismatch usually shows up as one of these errors:"},"1011":{"id":"/installation-31","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"| Error                                                                             | Cause                                                                                                                            | Fix                                                                                 |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"<name>\" is not exported by @osdk/client/.../observable.js` (or `@osdk/api/...`) | `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` is on a different release line than `@osdk/react`, often a prerelease paired with stable versions. | Install the exact `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` versions that match `@osdk/react`. |","table":"table-2"},"1012":{"id":"/installation-32","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"| Error                                                      | Cause                                                                                                                                                    | Fix                                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| npm or pnpm peer warning for `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` | The declared peer ranges allow newer `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` releases than `@osdk/react` was built with, and, since `2.87.0`, warn on older ones. | Pin the matching versions instead of ignoring the warning. |","table":"table-2"},"1013":{"id":"/installation-33","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"Before `2.15.0`, `@osdk/react` was versioned separately (`0.x`). To find the `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` versions it was built against:"},"1014":{"id":"/installation-34","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"Open `node_modules/@osdk/react/CHANGELOG.md`."},"1015":{"id":"/installation-35","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"Find the heading for your installed `@osdk/react` version."},"1016":{"id":"/installation-36","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"If that entry has an **Updated dependencies** section, install the exact `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` versions it lists."},"1017":{"id":"/installation-37","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"If it does not, walk back to the closest earlier entry that does, and use those versions."},"1018":{"id":"/installation-38","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"Upgrading to `2.15.0` or later is simpler: from then on the three versions match."},"1019":{"id":"/installation-39","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#version-compatibility","content":"If npm reports a peer conflict for OSDK packages after you have aligned versions, tell it to reuse your direct dependency versions with `overrides`:"},"1020":{"id":"/installation-40","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#optional-peers-for-platform-apis","content":"Hooks from `@osdk/react/platform-apis`, such as `useCurrentFoundryUser`, `useFoundryUser`, and `useMarkings`, call Foundry Platform APIs through two optional peer dependencies. Install them only if you import from that entry point:"},"1021":{"id":"/installation-41","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#optional-peers-for-platform-apis","content":"Without them, a build that imports `@osdk/react/platform-apis` fails with `Rollup failed to resolve import \"@osdk/foundry.admin\"` (or `@osdk/foundry.core`). See Platform APIs."},"1022":{"id":"/installation-42","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation#bundler-setup","content":"OSDK packages read `process.env.NODE_ENV`, which Vite does not define by default. Without it the browser throws `ReferenceError: process is not defined`. Use OSDK with Vite shows the `define` setting and a local CORS proxy to Foundry."},"1023":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"page","content":"Import existing types","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import"},"1024":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import","content":"Convert an existing Foundry ontology's metadata into TypeScript with @osdk/maker-import, and reference those types from your ontology-as-code definitions."},"1025":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#install","content":"Install"},"1026":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"Get the ontology metadata"},"1027":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"Generate the modules"},"1028":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-imported-types","content":"Use imported types"},"1029":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"What is converted"},"1030":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-it-from-code","content":"Use it from code"},"1031":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/import#share-types-between-ontology-as-code-projects","content":"Share types between ontology-as-code projects"},"1032":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import","content":"`@osdk/maker-import` turns the metadata of an ontology that already exists in Foundry into TypeScript modules. Import those modules into your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file to link to, implement, or reuse existing types without redefining them."},"1033":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import","content":"Imported types are references, not definitions: maker writes them to the IR's `importedOntology` section, and your ontology does not create or change them."},"1034":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"`maker-import` reads an `OntologyFullMetadata` JSON file, the response of the Foundry endpoint `GET /api/v2/ontologies/{ontology}/fullMetadata`. Two ways to get it:"},"1035":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"**From the OSDK CLI.** `osdk unstable typescript generate` with `--foundryUrl`, `--clientId`, and `--ontologyWritePath ontology-full-metadata.json` signs you in, fetches the metadata, and writes it to that path while it generates an SDK."},"1036":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#get-the-ontology-metadata","content":"**From the API.** Call the endpoint with a token that can read the ontology, and save the response."},"1037":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default | Description                                     |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `-i`, `--input` | `string` |         | Required. The `OntologyFullMetadata` JSON file. |","table":"table-0"},"1038":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default               | Description           |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--output` | `string` | `./generated-imports` | The output directory. |","table":"table-0"},"1039":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"The output has one module per type and an `index.ts` that re-exports them all:"},"1040":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"<File name=\"index.ts\" />"},"1041":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#generate-the-modules","content":"Each export is named after the type's API name, without its namespace, in camelCase: `Employee` becomes `employee` and `modify-employee` becomes `modifyEmployee`. When two types share a short name, both use the full API name instead, such as `comExampleEmployee`, and any remaining clash gets a numeric suffix. Each run deletes and rewrites the four `codegen` folders."},"1042":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-imported-types","content":"Each export is a proxy. The first time your ontology reads one of its properties, maker records the type as imported, along with the shared property types its properties use. Exports you never touch stay out of the IR."},"1043":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-imported-types","content":"The generated modules are TypeScript files that import each other with `.js` extensions, so Node cannot load them as they are. Compile the output directory with `tsc` as an ES module project before you run maker, or publish it as a compiled package. The example above imports the compiled `./imports/index.js`."},"1044":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-imported-types","content":"An interface link constraint or an interface action type constraint cannot start from an imported interface. Define them only on interfaces in your own ontology."},"1045":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"| Metadata              | Converted to         | Notes                                          |\n| --------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Shared property types | `SharedPropertyType` | API name, display name, description, and type. |","table":"table-1"},"1046":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"| Metadata   | Converted to    | Notes                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interfaces | `InterfaceType` | Properties, including interface-defined properties, links, and the interfaces they extend. Status is always active, and action type constraints are not included. |","table":"table-1"},"1047":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"| Metadata     | Converted to | Notes                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object types | `ObjectType` | Properties, primary key, title, description, visibility, and shared property types. Status is active or experimental. `pluralDisplayName` is the display name with `s` added. |","table":"table-1"},"1048":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"| Metadata     | Converted to | Notes                                                                   |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Action types | `ActionType` | Parameters only, with no logic rules. Status is active or experimental. |","table":"table-1"},"1049":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"| Metadata   | Converted to  | Notes                                                     |\n| ---------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Link types | Not converted | Define links to imported object types yourself, as above. |","table":"table-1"},"1050":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"Marking properties are imported with the marking input name `not-applicable`, because the existing type already owns its marking configuration."},"1051":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"`maker-import` throws on types it cannot represent, naming the type:"},"1052":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"Property types other than the primitive, geospatial, media, attachment, marking, struct, array, vector, and geotime series types. A marking property must have a `markingType`."},"1053":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"Struct fields that are arrays or structs, and struct main values that are arrays."},"1054":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"Vector properties that support more than one search similarity function, or whose embedding model is missing settings."},"1055":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#what-is-converted","content":"Vector action parameters, and action parameter types with no maker equivalent."},"1056":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-it-from-code","content":"The package also exports the conversion functions:"},"1057":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-it-from-code","content":"| Function                                | Returns              | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `convertOntologyFullMetadata(metadata)` | `OntologyDefinition` | Converts the metadata to maker's in-memory form, keyed by entity kind and API name, without writing files. |","table":"table-2"},"1058":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#use-it-from-code","content":"| Function                                     | Returns | Description                                                    |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `writeImportedOntology(metadata, outputDir)` | `void`  | Converts the metadata and writes the modules, as the CLI does. |","table":"table-2"},"1059":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/import-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/import#share-types-between-ontology-as-code-projects","content":"To reuse types from another ontology-as-code project instead of from Foundry, compile that project with `maker --outputDir`. Maker writes the same module layout, plus `link-types` and `value-types` folders, and its `index.ts` records the package's namespace and version when it loads, so a consuming project can list it with `maker --dependencies <file>`. As with `maker-import` output, compile or publish the modules before you import them."},"1060":{"id":"/ontology-as-code","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"page","content":"Ontology as code","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code"},"1061":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code","content":"Define object types, links, actions, and interfaces in TypeScript with @osdk/maker, compile them to Ontology IR, and develop against them locally."},"1062":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#packages","content":"Packages"},"1063":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1064":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#install","content":"Install"},"1065":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"Project layout"},"1066":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"Write an ontology"},"1067":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"API names and namespaces"},"1068":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"`maker` CLI"},"1069":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1070":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code","content":"Ontology as code lets you define Ontology types in TypeScript files that live next to your app. `@osdk/maker` validates the definitions and compiles them into an Ontology intermediate representation (IR) file, and `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` turns that IR into a generated SDK and a mock Foundry server for local development."},"1071":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code","content":"Every ontology-as-code package is pre-1.0 and treated as experimental. Definitions, CLI flags, and the IR format can change in any release. Pin exact versions and read the changelog before you upgrade."},"1072":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#packages","content":"| Package       | What it does                                                                                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/maker` | The `define*` functions you write your ontology with, and the `maker` CLI that compiles it to IR. |","table":"table-0"},"1073":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#packages","content":"| Package                 | What it does                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` | A Vite plugin that compiles the ontology on every change, generates an SDK from it, and serves a mock Foundry API from the dev server. See Local development. |","table":"table-0"},"1074":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#packages","content":"| Package              | What it does                                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/maker-import` | Converts the metadata of an existing Foundry ontology into TypeScript files you can reference from your definitions. See Import existing types. |","table":"table-0"},"1075":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#packages","content":"| Package                                     | What it does                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/seed-helpers`, `@osdk/seed-compiler` | Build seed objects and links for the local Ontology server. See Local development. |","table":"table-0"},"1076":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#how-it-works","content":"**Define.** You write object types, links, actions, interfaces, shared property types, and value types in `.ontology/ontology.mts`. Each `define*` call validates its input and registers the type."},"1077":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#how-it-works","content":"**Compile.** The `maker` CLI imports that file and writes the IR to `ontology.json`, plus `value-types.json` when you define value types."},"1078":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#how-it-works","content":"**Develop locally.** In a Vite app, `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` runs `maker` on every change, converts the IR to Ontology metadata, generates an SDK into `.osdk/src`, and answers OSDK requests from the dev server with seeded data."},"1079":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#how-it-works","content":"**Ship.** The IR file is the artifact. None of these packages uploads or installs it into a Foundry stack."},"1080":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#install","content":"`@osdk/maker` installs a `maker` binary. For local development, also install the Vite plugin; see Local development."},"1081":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#install","content":"The CLI loads your ontology file with Node's own `import()`, so a `.mts` or `.ts` entry file needs a Node.js version that strips TypeScript types natively: 22.18 or later, or 23.6 or later. On older versions, write the file as `.mjs`."},"1082":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"ontology.mts\" />"},"1083":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"seed.ts\" />"},"1084":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"ontology-schema-lock.json\" />"},"1085":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"1086":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1087":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"| Path                     | Purpose                                                         |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.ontology/ontology.mts` | Your definitions. The Vite plugin reads exactly this file name. |","table":"table-1"},"1088":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"| Path                | Purpose                                       |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `.ontology/seed.ts` | Mock data for the Vite plugin's local server. |","table":"table-1"},"1089":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"| Path                                  | Purpose                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `.ontology/ontology-schema-lock.json` | Written by `maker --write-locks` once an interface opts into schema migrations. Commit it. |","table":"table-1"},"1090":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#project-layout","content":"| Path        | Purpose                                                    |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.osdk/src` | The SDK the Vite plugin generates. Do not edit it by hand. |","table":"table-1"},"1091":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"The ontology file is a module whose top-level `define*` calls register types as they run. Export each result so other files, such as a seed file or another ontology, can import it."},"1092":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"This file defines the `Employee` and `Office` object types, the links between them, a `Worker` interface, and a `modifyEmployee` action:"},"1093":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"In the SDK generated from this file, `Employee` has the links `office` and `lead` (one object each) and `reports` (many), `Office` has `occupants`, and the action is `modifyEmployee`: action API names must be lowercase and hyphenated, and the SDK generator converts them to camelCase. The `leadId` and `officeId` properties are the foreign keys the links join on."},"1094":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"Compile it:"},"1095":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#write-an-ontology","content":"Each `define*` function throws when its input is invalid, for example when a title or primary key property is missing, an API name breaks the naming rules, or two types share an API name. `maker` reports the first error and exits with code 1; run it with `-v` to print the stack trace."},"1096":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"`--apiNamespace com.example` prefixes the API names of the object types, interfaces, shared property types, and action types you define, so `Employee` becomes `com.example.Employee`. Pass names without the prefix in your definitions. Link type API names are not prefixed, and value types are prefixed only when you set `namespacePrefix: true`."},"1097":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"| Name        | Rule                                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Object type | Starts with a letter, then letters and digits, with optional `.`-separated segments, at most 100 characters. |","table":"table-2"},"1098":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"| Name                | Rule                                                                         |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Property, link side | Starts with a letter, then letters, digits, and `_`, at most 100 characters. |","table":"table-2"},"1099":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"| Name        | Rule                                                               |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Action type | Lowercase letters and digits, in segments separated by `-` or `.`. |","table":"table-2"},"1100":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"| Name      | Rule                                                                                                                                               |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Link type | Converted to a lowercase, hyphenated ID (`officeOccupants` and `office_occupants` both become `office-occupants`), which must start with a letter. |","table":"table-2"},"1101":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#api-names-and-namespaces","content":"| Name                                                 | Rule                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object types, interfaces, properties, and link sides | Cannot be a reserved word: `ontology`, `object`, `property`, `link`, `relation`, `rid`, `primaryKey`, `typeId`, or `ontologyObject`, in any case. |","table":"table-2"},"1102":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option          | Type     | Default                 | Description                |\n| --------------- | -------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `-i`, `--input` | `string` | `.ontology/ontology.ts` | The ontology file to load. |","table":"table-3"},"1103":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default         | Description            |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--output` | `string` | `ontology.json` | Where to write the IR. |","table":"table-3"},"1104":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option               | Type     | Default            | Description                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | -------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--valueTypesOutput` | `string` | `value-types.json` | Where to write value types. Written only when the ontology defines or imports value types. |","table":"table-3"},"1105":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--apiNamespace` | `string` | `\"\"`    | Prefix for API names, such as `com.example`. A trailing `.` is added for you. Must match `^[a-z0-9-]+(\\.[a-z0-9-]+)*\\.$`. |","table":"table-3"},"1106":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option              | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-d`, `--outputDir` | `string` |         | Also write each defined type as a TypeScript module under `<dir>/codegen`, with an `index.ts` that re-exports them. Other ontologies can import this output; see Import existing types. |","table":"table-3"},"1107":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default | Description                                                                        |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dependencies` | `string` |         | Write the namespaces and versions of imported ontology packages to this JSON file. |","table":"table-3"},"1108":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option                   | Type      | Default | Description                                                                 |\n| ------------------------ | --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--generateCodeSnippets` | `boolean` | `false` | Write OSDK usage snippets for each object type, action type, and interface. |","table":"table-3"},"1109":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option                     | Type     | Default | Description                                 |\n| -------------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `--codeSnippetPackageName` | `string` | `\"\"`    | The SDK package name shown in the snippets. |","table":"table-3"},"1110":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option             | Type     | Default | Description                  |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `--codeSnippetDir` | `string` | `./`    | Where to write the snippets. |","table":"table-3"},"1111":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-50","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option            | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--randomnessKey` | `string` |         | A UUID recorded in the IR to keep generated entities unique. Rejected if it is not a UUID. |","table":"table-3"},"1112":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-51","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option       | Type     | Default                                       | Description                    |\n| ------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `--lockfile` | `string` | `ontology-schema-lock.json` next to the input | The interface schema lockfile. |","table":"table-3"},"1113":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-52","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option         | Type      | Default | Description                                                    |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--writeLocks` | `boolean` |         | Update the lockfile instead of failing when it is out of date. |","table":"table-3"},"1114":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-53","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option        | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                             |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-y`, `--yes` | `boolean` |         | Accept detected schema migration finalizations and deletions without a prompt. Requires `--writeLocks`. |","table":"table-3"},"1115":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-54","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#maker-cli","content":"| Option            | Type    | Default | Description                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-v`, `--verbose` | `count` |         | `-v` logs debug output and stack traces; `-vv` logs trace output. |","table":"table-3"},"1116":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-55","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#next-steps","content":"Properties, primary keys, value types, and datasources."},"1117":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-56","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#next-steps","content":"Relate object types and define the actions that edit them."},"1118":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-57","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#next-steps","content":"Share properties and contracts across object types."},"1119":{"id":"/ontology-as-code-58","page_id":"/ontology-as-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code#next-steps","content":"Generate an SDK and run a mock Foundry API with Vite."},"1120":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"page","content":"Interfaces and shared properties","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces"},"1121":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","content":"Define shared property types and interfaces with @osdk/maker, implement them on object types, and add interface links, actions, and schema migrations."},"1122":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"Shared property types"},"1123":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#refer-to-a-shared-property-type-defined-elsewhere","content":"Refer to a shared property type defined elsewhere"},"1124":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"Define an interface"},"1125":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#implement-an-interface","content":"Implement an interface"},"1126":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"Interface links"},"1127":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"Interface actions"},"1128":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#action-type-constraints","content":"Action type constraints"},"1129":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"Schema migrations"},"1130":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#the-lockfile","content":"The lockfile"},"1131":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#create-the-lockfile","content":"Create the lockfile"},"1132":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#end-a-transition","content":"End a transition"},"1133":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","content":"A shared property type is a property definition that several object types reuse. An interface is a contract of properties and links that object types implement, so code can work with any object that is a `Worker` without knowing its concrete type. Define both with `@osdk/maker` in your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file."},"1134":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"`type`, `array`, `reducers`, `description`, `visibility`, `nullability`, `typeClasses`, and `baseFormatter` work as they do on object type properties. The other options:"},"1135":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The API name, without the namespace. |","table":"table-0"},"1136":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default   | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | `apiName` | The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1137":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option    | Type            | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | --------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `aliases` | `Array<string>` |         | Other names to find the property by in search. |","table":"table-0"},"1138":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option      | Type                                       | Default | Description                             |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `valueType` | `OntologyIrValueTypeReferenceWithMetadata` |         | A reference to an installed value type. |","table":"table-0"},"1139":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option          | Type                              | Default | Description                     |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `gothamMapping` | `SharedPropertyTypeGothamMapping` |         | A mapping to a Gotham property. |","table":"table-0"},"1140":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model. |","table":"table-0"},"1141":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#shared-property-types","content":"To back an object type's property with a shared property type, set `sharedPropertyType` on the property and keep `type` and `array` the same as the shared property type's:"},"1142":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#refer-to-a-shared-property-type-defined-elsewhere","content":"`importSharedPropertyType` refers to a shared property type that another ontology defines. Maker records it as an imported type, and `typeHint` tells the SDK generator its type:"},"1143":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#refer-to-a-shared-property-type-defined-elsewhere","content":"The full API name is `<packageName>.<apiName>`, here `com.example.finance.costCenter`. `packageName` must be lowercase and cannot end with `.`. To import many types from an existing ontology at once, use `@osdk/maker-import`."},"1144":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"`Worker` inherits `name` from `Party`, so an object type that implements `Worker` must provide `name` and `jobTitle`, and may provide `email` and `hourlyRate`."},"1145":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The API name, without the namespace. |","table":"table-1"},"1146":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default   | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | `apiName` | The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-1"},"1147":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default       | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` | `displayName` | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-1"},"1148":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option | Type                                        | Default | Description                            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `{ locator: BlueprintIcon; color: string }` |         | A Blueprint icon name and a hex color. |","table":"table-1"},"1149":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option       | Type                                | Default | Description                                   |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `properties` | `Record<string, InterfaceProperty>` |         | The properties, keyed by API name. See below. |","table":"table-1"},"1150":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option    | Type                                    | Default | Description                                                                                      |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `extends` | `InterfaceType \\| Array<InterfaceType>` |         | Interfaces whose properties this interface inherits. Pass the values `defineInterface` returned. |","table":"table-1"},"1151":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option   | Type                                                                                                                                 | Default              | Description             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `status` | `{ type: \"active\" } \\| { type: \"experimental\" } \\| { type: \"example\" } \\| { type: \"deprecated\"; message: string; deadline: string }` | `{ type: \"active\" }` | The interface's status. |","table":"table-1"},"1152":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option       | Type      | Default | Description                              |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `searchable` | `boolean` | `true`  | Whether the interface appears in search. |","table":"table-1"},"1153":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model. |","table":"table-1"},"1154":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Option             | Type                                 | Default | Description                                         |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `schemaMigrations` | `{ transitions: Array<Transition> }` |         | Opts into schema migrations. See Schema migrations. |","table":"table-1"},"1155":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"Each entry in `properties` takes one of three forms:"},"1156":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Form                   | Example | Required to implement |\n| ---------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| A shared property type | `name`  | Yes                   |","table":"table-2"},"1157":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Form                               | Example                                          | Required to implement |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| A shared property type with a flag | `{ sharedPropertyType: email, required: false }` | As set                |","table":"table-2"},"1158":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"| Form                          | Example                                                                                             | Required to implement      |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| An interface-defined property | `{ type: \"string\", required?: boolean, displayName?, description?, array?, primaryKeyConstraint? }` | `required`, default `true` |","table":"table-2"},"1159":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"When you use a shared property type, its key must be the shared property type's API name: `properties: { name }` works, and `properties: { fullName: name }` throws. `primaryKeyConstraint` is `\"MUST_BE_PK\"`, `\"CANNOT_BE_PK\"`, or `\"NO_RESTRICTION\"`."},"1160":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#define-an-interface","content":"Locally generated SDKs include only the shared-property-type properties of an interface. Interface-defined properties are in the IR but not in the SDK that `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` generates. See Local development."},"1161":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#implement-an-interface","content":"List the interface in the object type's `implementsInterfaces`, and map each interface property to one of the object's properties:"},"1162":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#implement-an-interface","content":"`defineObject` throws if a required interface property, including one inherited through `extends`, is not mapped, if a mapping names an interface property that does not exist, or if the object property's type differs from the interface property's type."},"1163":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"`defineInterfaceLinkConstraint` adds a link to an interface. Every object type that implements the interface must provide the link when `required` is `true`."},"1164":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                            |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The link's API name on the `from` interface. |","table":"table-3"},"1165":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option | Type            | Default | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------ | --------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `from` | `InterfaceType` |         | Required. The interface the link belongs to. It must be defined in this ontology, not imported. |","table":"table-3"},"1166":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option              | Type                      | Default | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toOne` or `toMany` | `InterfaceType \\| string` |         | Required, exactly one. The target interface, or its API name. |","table":"table-3"},"1167":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default   | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | `apiName` | The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1168":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default       | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` | `displayName` | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1169":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-links","content":"| Option     | Type      | Default | Description                                              |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `required` | `boolean` | `true`  | Whether implementing object types must provide the link. |","table":"table-3"},"1170":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"These helpers generate action types that work on any object that implements an interface. The create, modify, and delete helpers take the object action helper options, with `interfaceType` in place of `objectType`. The link helpers take different options, described below."},"1171":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-50","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"| Helper                              | Default API name                                                         | What it does                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defineCreateInterfaceObjectAction` | `create-<interface>`, or `create-<interface>-<object>` with `objectType` | Creates an object that implements the interface. Without `objectType`, the user picks the object type in an `objectTypeParameter` parameter. |","table":"table-4"},"1172":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-51","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"| Helper                              | Default API name                                                         | What it does                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defineModifyInterfaceObjectAction` | `modify-<interface>`, or `modify-<interface>-<object>` with `objectType` | Modifies an object through the interface's properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1173":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-52","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"| Helper                              | Default API name                      | What it does                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defineDeleteInterfaceObjectAction` | `delete-interface-object-<interface>` | Deletes an object that implements the interface. |","table":"table-4"},"1174":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-53","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"| Helper                            | Default API name                          | What it does                                |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `defineCreateInterfaceLinkAction` | Derived from the interface and link names | Adds an interface link between two objects. |","table":"table-4"},"1175":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-54","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"| Helper                            | Default API name                          | What it does               |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `defineDeleteInterfaceLinkAction` | Derived from the interface and link names | Removes an interface link. |","table":"table-4"},"1176":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-55","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#interface-actions","content":"The link actions take the value `defineInterfaceLinkConstraint` returned as `interfaceLink`, or the link's API name together with `from`. Use `sourceParameter` and `targetParameter` to rename their two parameters."},"1177":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-56","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#action-type-constraints","content":"`defineInterfaceActionTypeConstraint` declares an action that implementing object types provide, with the parameters it must accept:"},"1178":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-57","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#action-type-constraints","content":"The interface must be defined in this ontology, and the constraint's API name must be unique on it."},"1179":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-58","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"Interface schema migrations are in beta in Foundry and may not be available on your enrollment."},"1180":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-59","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"Changing a published interface can break the object types that implement it. A schema migration announces a change and gives implementers a grace period before it is enforced. Adding `schemaMigrations` to an interface also turns on compatibility checks, so maker rejects breaking changes that are not staged as a migration. Every interface in an `extends` hierarchy must opt in together."},"1181":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-60","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"The only migration is `addRequiredProperty`, which makes an optional property required. While the migration is active, the property stays `required: false`:"},"1182":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-61","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"A transition groups migrations that are finalized or deleted together:"},"1183":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-62","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"| Field | Type     | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | A stable ID, unique on the interface. 1 to 150 characters: a letter or digit, then letters, digits, `_`, or `-`. |","table":"table-5"},"1184":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-63","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"| Field   | Type     | Description              |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------ |\n| `title` | `string` | A summary of the change. |","table":"table-5"},"1185":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-64","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------- |\n| `description` | `string` | Optional details. |","table":"table-5"},"1186":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-65","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"| Field         | Type                                                                               | Description                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gracePeriod` | `{ type: \"afterInstall\"; days: number } \\| { type: \"deadline\"; deadline: string }` | How long implementers have to comply. `afterInstall` allows 7 to 180 days and suits Marketplace-distributed ontologies. `deadline` is an ISO 8601 UTC date-time, and installing after it fails. |","table":"table-5"},"1187":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-66","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"| Field          | Type                                                       | Description                       |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `instructions` | `Array<{ type: \"addRequiredProperty\"; property: string }>` | The migrations in the transition. |","table":"table-5"},"1188":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-67","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#schema-migrations","content":"Use `schemaMigrations: { transitions: [] }` to turn on compatibility checks without a migration."},"1189":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-68","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#the-lockfile","content":"Maker tracks opted-in interfaces in `ontology-schema-lock.json`, next to the ontology file. Commit it."},"1190":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-69","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#create-the-lockfile","content":"Without `--write-locks`, maker fails when an interface has opted in and no lockfile exists, or when the lockfile is out of date."},"1191":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces-70","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/interfaces#end-a-transition","content":"After the grace period, remove the transition and update the schema in the same change: set the property to `required: true` to **finalize**, or leave it optional to **delete** the transition. Then run `maker --write-locks` again. Maker compares the schema with the lockfile, asks you to confirm `FINALIZE` or `DELETE`, and rejects a schema that matches neither. Pass `--yes` to confirm without a prompt."},"1192":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"page","content":"Links and actions","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions"},"1193":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","content":"Relate object types with defineLink and define action types with the create, modify, and delete helpers from @osdk/maker."},"1194":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"Link types"},"1195":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"One-to-many"},"1196":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#many-to-many","content":"Many-to-many"},"1197":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#intermediary","content":"Intermediary"},"1198":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"Link options"},"1199":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#status","content":"Status"},"1200":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"Action types"},"1201":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"Helper options"},"1202":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"Configure parameters"},"1203":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"Conditions"},"1204":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#who-can-submit","content":"Who can submit"},"1205":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"Set properties without a parameter"},"1206":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#form-sections","content":"Form sections"},"1207":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#define-an-action-from-rules","content":"Define an action from rules"},"1208":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","content":"Link types connect object types, so that an `Employee` can reach its `Office`. Action types describe the edits users can make, such as changing an employee's job title. Define both with `@osdk/maker` in your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file."},"1209":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"`defineLink` supports three kinds of link, chosen by the keys you pass:"},"1210":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"| Kind        | Keys                                      | Joined on                                         |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| One-to-many | `one`, `toMany`, `manyForeignKeyProperty` | A foreign key property on the \"many\" object type. |","table":"table-0"},"1211":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"| Kind         | Keys             | Joined on                            |\n| ------------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Many-to-many | `many`, `toMany` | A link dataset of primary key pairs. |","table":"table-0"},"1212":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"| Kind         | Keys                                       | Joined on                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Intermediary | `many`, `toMany`, `intermediaryObjectType` | An object type that sits between the two, joined by two one-to-many links. |","table":"table-0"},"1213":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-types","content":"`defineLink` records the link without looking up its object types, so a link can refer to an object type that is defined later in the file. Maker checks the link when it compiles the ontology."},"1214":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"Each side's `metadata.apiName` is the name of the link as seen from that side's object type. The `one` side's name leads to many objects, and the `toMany` side's name leads to one:"},"1215":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"These two links give the generated SDK the following link names:"},"1216":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"| Object type | Link        | Leads to                                                              |\n| ----------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Office`    | `occupants` | Many `Employee` objects whose `officeId` is the office's primary key. |","table":"table-1"},"1217":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"| Object type | Link     | Leads to                              |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `Employee`  | `office` | The one `Office` named by `officeId`. |","table":"table-1"},"1218":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"| Object type | Link      | Leads to                                                               |\n| ----------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Employee`  | `reports` | Many `Employee` objects whose `leadId` is this employee's primary key. |","table":"table-1"},"1219":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"| Object type | Link   | Leads to                              |\n| ----------- | ------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `Employee`  | `lead` | The one `Employee` named by `leadId`. |","table":"table-1"},"1220":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#one-to-many","content":"`manyForeignKeyProperty` must be a property of the `toMany` object type, with the same type as the `one` object type's primary key. Set `cardinality: \"OneToOne\"` when each object on the `one` side links to at most one object on the `toMany` side; the default is `\"OneToMany\"`."},"1221":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#many-to-many","content":"Maker backs a many-to-many link with a dataset named `link-<apiName>` that has one column per primary key. When both object types use the same primary key name, the columns get `_from` and `_to` suffixes."},"1222":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#intermediary","content":"An intermediary link connects two object types through a third. Define the intermediary object type and a one-to-many link from each side to it, then pass those links as `linkToIntermediary`:"},"1223":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. Converted to a lowercase, hyphenated link type ID. Not prefixed by `--apiNamespace`. |","table":"table-2"},"1224":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option                  | Type                   | Default | Description                                                                                                       |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `one`, `many`, `toMany` | `{ object, metadata }` |         | The two sides. `object` is a definition from `defineObject`, an imported object type, or an object type API name. |","table":"table-2"},"1225":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option                   | Type     | Default | Description                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manyForeignKeyProperty` | `string` |         | One-to-many only. The foreign key property on the `toMany` object type. |","table":"table-2"},"1226":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option        | Type                        | Default       | Description       |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | ------------- | ----------------- |\n| `cardinality` | `\"OneToMany\" \\| \"OneToOne\"` | `\"OneToMany\"` | One-to-many only. |","table":"table-2"},"1227":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option                   | Type                             | Default | Description        |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------ |\n| `intermediaryObjectType` | `ObjectTypeDefinition \\| string` |         | Intermediary only. |","table":"table-2"},"1228":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-2"},"1229":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option   | Type         | Default    | Description |\n| -------- | ------------ | ---------- | ----------- |\n| `status` | `LinkStatus` | `\"active\"` | See Status. |","table":"table-2"},"1230":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option         | Type      | Default | Description                      |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `editsEnabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether users can edit the link. |","table":"table-2"},"1231":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description                        |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model for the link. |","table":"table-2"},"1232":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"Each side's `metadata`:"},"1233":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                              |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The link name on this side's object type. Starts with a letter, then letters, digits, and `_`. |","table":"table-3"},"1234":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default                                     | Description                         |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | `apiName` with its first letter capitalized | The singular name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1235":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option              | Type     | Default                                                        | Description                       |\n| ------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `pluralDisplayName` | `string` | `apiName` capitalized, with an `s` added unless it ends in `s` | The plural name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1236":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option       | Type                                  | Default    | Description                             |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `visibility` | `\"PROMINENT\" \\| \"NORMAL\" \\| \"HIDDEN\"` | `\"NORMAL\"` | How prominently Foundry shows the link. |","table":"table-3"},"1237":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option             | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `groupDisplayName` | `string` | `\"\"`    | A group to show the link under. |","table":"table-3"},"1238":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#link-options","content":"| Option        | Type                                    | Default | Description   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------- |\n| `typeClasses` | `Array<{ kind: string; name: string }>` | `[]`    | Type classes. |","table":"table-3"},"1239":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#status","content":"A link's `status` is `\"active\"`, `\"experimental\"`, `\"example\"`, or `{ type: \"deprecated\", message, deadline, replacedBy? }`. It must agree with the object types it connects: if either side is deprecated, the link must be deprecated, and if either side is experimental or example, the link must be experimental or example."},"1240":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"Most actions create, change, or delete one object. The helpers below generate an action type from an object type: one parameter per property, the logic rule, and a default parameter order."},"1241":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Helper                     | Default API name         | Parameters                                | Rule            |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `defineCreateObjectAction` | `create-object-<object>` | Every property, including the primary key | Adds an object. |","table":"table-4"},"1242":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Helper                     | Default API name         | Parameters                                                            | Rule                                                                               |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defineModifyObjectAction` | `modify-object-<object>` | `objectToModifyParameter`, then every property except the primary key | Modifies the chosen object. Each parameter defaults to the object's current value. |","table":"table-4"},"1243":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-50","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Helper                             | Default API name            | Parameters                                                                    | Rule                                                                                               |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defineCreateOrModifyObjectAction` | `create-or-modify-<object>` | `objectToCreateOrModifyParameter`, then every property except the primary key | Modifies the chosen object, or creates one. Each parameter defaults to the object's current value. |","table":"table-4"},"1244":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-51","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Helper                     | Default API name         | Parameters                | Rule                       |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `defineDeleteObjectAction` | `delete-object-<object>` | `objectToDeleteParameter` | Deletes the chosen object. |","table":"table-4"},"1245":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-52","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"`<object>` is the object type's API name in lowercase with hyphens, so `Employee` gives `modify-object-employee`. Parameters skip vector properties, properties in `excludedProperties`, and properties set by `nonParameterMappings`; all three also skip properties backed by a `derived` datasource. For interfaces, see Interface actions."},"1246":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-53","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"Action API names must contain lowercase letters and digits in segments separated by `-` or `.`. The SDK generator converts them to camelCase, so `modify-employee` is `modifyEmployee` in your generated SDK."},"1247":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-54","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"The parameter IDs of the chosen object are exported as constants:"},"1248":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-55","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Constant                  | Value                       |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `MODIFY_OBJECT_PARAMETER` | `\"objectToModifyParameter\"` |","table":"table-5"},"1249":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-56","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Constant                            | Value                               |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `CREATE_OR_MODIFY_OBJECT_PARAMETER` | `\"objectToCreateOrModifyParameter\"` |","table":"table-5"},"1250":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-57","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Constant                  | Value                       |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `DELETE_OBJECT_PARAMETER` | `\"objectToDeleteParameter\"` |","table":"table-5"},"1251":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-58","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Constant                            | Value                   |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `CREATE_INTERFACE_OBJECT_PARAMETER` | `\"objectTypeParameter\"` |","table":"table-5"},"1252":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-59","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#action-types","content":"| Constant                            | Value                                |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `MODIFY_INTERFACE_OBJECT_PARAMETER` | `\"interfaceObjectToModifyParameter\"` |","table":"table-5"},"1253":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-60","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option       | Type                   | Default | Description                          |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `objectType` | `ObjectTypeDefinition` |         | Required. The object type to act on. |","table":"table-6"},"1254":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-61","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default             | Description            |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` | See the table above | The action's API name. |","table":"table-6"},"1255":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-62","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default                                                                             | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | `Create`, `Modify`, `Create or Modify`, or `Delete`, then the object's display name | The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-6"},"1256":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-63","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-6"},"1257":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-64","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option   | Type                                                    | Default    | Description          |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| `status` | `\"active\" \\| \"experimental\" \\| \"example\" \\| deprecated` | `\"active\"` | The action's status. |","table":"table-6"},"1258":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-65","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type            | Default | Description                             |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `excludedProperties` | `Array<string>` |         | Properties that do not get a parameter. |","table":"table-6"},"1259":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-66","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option                   | Type                                     | Default | Description                                       |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterConfiguration` | `Record<string, ParameterConfiguration>` |         | Per-parameter settings. See Configure parameters. |","table":"table-6"},"1260":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-67","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option                 | Type                           | Default | Description                                                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `nonParameterMappings` | `Record<string, MappingValue>` |         | Properties set without a parameter. See Set properties without a parameter. |","table":"table-6"},"1261":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-68","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option                  | Type                                     | Default | Description                                                             |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actionLevelValidation` | `Array<{ condition; displayMetadata? }>` |         | Conditions that must all pass to submit the action. See Who can submit. |","table":"table-6"},"1262":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-69","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option              | Type            | Default                                                          | Description                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterOrdering` | `Array<string>` | Configured parameters first, then properties in definition order | The form's parameter order. Must list every parameter; the chosen-object parameter is added first if you leave it out. |","table":"table-6"},"1263":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-70","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option     | Type                   | Default | Description                                             |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sections` | `Array<ActionSection>` |         | Group parameters into form sections. See Form sections. |","table":"table-6"},"1264":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-71","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option          | Type                | Default | Description                |\n| --------------- | ------------------- | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `defaultFormat` | `\"FORM\" \\| \"TABLE\"` |         | The form's default layout. |","table":"table-6"},"1265":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-72","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type      | Default | Description                                      |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enableLayoutSwitch` | `boolean` |         | Let users switch between form and table layouts. |","table":"table-6"},"1266":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-73","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type                                                   | Default | Description                    |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `tableConfiguration` | `{ columnWidthByParameterRid; enableFileImport; ... }` |         | Settings for the table layout. |","table":"table-6"},"1267":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-74","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type                                                                                          | Default | Description                                                |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `submissionMetadata` | `{ successMessage: string; submitButtonDisplayMetadata?; undoButtonConfiguration?: boolean }` |         | The submit button and the message shown after it succeeds. |","table":"table-6"},"1268":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-75","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option | Type                                        | Default | Description        |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------ |\n| `icon` | `{ locator: BlueprintIcon; color: string }` |         | The action's icon. |","table":"table-6"},"1269":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-76","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model for the action. |","table":"table-6"},"1270":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-77","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"`defineDeleteObjectAction` reads only `objectType`, `apiName`, `displayName`, `description`, `status`, `actionLevelValidation`, `icon`, `permission`, and `parameterConfiguration.objectToDeleteParameter`."},"1271":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-78","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"`parameterConfiguration` is keyed by parameter ID, which for property parameters is the property's API name. A key that is not a property adds a new parameter, and needs `customParameterType`."},"1272":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-79","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | The parameter's label. Defaults to the property's display name. |","table":"table-7"},"1273":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-80","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `description` | `string` | Help text under the parameter. |","table":"table-7"},"1274":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-81","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option     | Type                                                        | Description                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `required` | `boolean \\| { listLength: { min?: number; max?: number } }` | Whether a value is required. Defaults to `true` when the property sets `nullability.noNulls`, and for arrays to a minimum length of 1 when it sets `noEmptyCollections`. |","table":"table-7"},"1275":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-82","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option          | Type            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedValues` | `AllowedValues` | The values the parameter accepts, such as `{ type: \"oneOf\", oneOf }`, `{ type: \"range\", min?, max? }`, or `{ type: \"text\", minLength?, maxLength?, regex? }`. Defaults to what the property type allows. |","table":"table-7"},"1276":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-83","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option         | Type                         | Description        |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `defaultValue` | `OntologyIrParameterPrefill` | A prefilled value. |","table":"table-7"},"1277":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-84","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option              | Type                                   | Description               |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `defaultVisibility` | `\"editable\" \\| \"disabled\" \\| \"hidden\"` | How the parameter starts. |","table":"table-7"},"1278":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-85","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                 | Type                         | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `conditionalOverrides` | `Array<ConditionalOverride>` | Change the visibility, whether a value is required, the default, or the allowed values when a condition passes. |","table":"table-7"},"1279":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-86","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option       | Type                  | Description                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `renderHint` | `ParameterRenderHint` | Which input control to use. |","table":"table-7"},"1280":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-87","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                   | Type                                       | Description                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `structFieldValidations` | `Record<string, StructFieldConfiguration>` | For struct parameters, per-field settings, including `defaultValue`. Set a field's `defaultValue` to `null` to turn off the default that modify helpers infer. |","table":"table-7"},"1281":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-88","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                | Type                  | Description                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `customParameterType` | `ActionParameterType` | The type of a parameter that is not a property, such as `\"string\"` or `\"booleanList\"`. |","table":"table-7"},"1282":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-89","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"A conditional override is one of:"},"1283":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-90","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                   | Effect when `condition` passes                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"visibility\", condition, then? }` | Sets visibility to `then`: `\"editable\"`, `\"disabled\"`, or `\"hidden\"`. |","table":"table-8"},"1284":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-91","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                 | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"disabled\", condition, then? }` | Disables the parameter.        |","table":"table-8"},"1285":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-92","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                          | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"required\", condition }` | Makes the parameter required.  |","table":"table-8"},"1286":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-93","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                            | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"defaultValue\", condition, defaultValue }` | Uses a different default.      |","table":"table-8"},"1287":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-94","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                        | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"constraint\", condition, constraint }` | Uses different allowed values. |","table":"table-8"},"1288":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-95","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"Validation rules and overrides take a `ConditionDefinition`:"},"1289":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-96","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                 | Passes when                                                                          |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"group\", name }` | The user is in the group chosen for the input `name` when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-9"},"1290":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-97","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                                     | Passes when                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"parameter\", parameterId, matches }` | The parameter's value equals `matches`, such as `{ type: \"staticValue\", staticValue: { type: \"string\", string: \"Engineering\" } }`. |","table":"table-9"},"1291":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-98","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"and\" \\| \"or\", conditions }` | All or any of `conditions` pass. |","table":"table-9"},"1292":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-99","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#who-can-submit","content":"`actionLevelValidation` is a list of rules that must all pass before a user can submit. `displayMetadata.failureMessage` is shown when a rule fails."},"1293":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-100","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#who-can-submit","content":"This action can only be submitted by members of the HR group, shows `skills` only when the department is Engineering, limits `department` to two values, and records who made the edit:"},"1294":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-101","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"`nonParameterMappings` sets a property from something other than user input. The property gets no parameter."},"1295":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-102","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                     | Sets the property to                       |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"currentUser\" }` | The ID of the user who submits the action. |","table":"table-10"},"1296":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-103","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                     | Sets the property to              |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"currentTime\" }` | The time the action is submitted. |","table":"table-10"},"1297":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-104","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                       | Sets the property to                                            |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"uuid\", linkId? }` | A new UUID. Properties that share a `linkId` get the same UUID. |","table":"table-10"},"1298":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-105","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                                  | Sets the property to |\n| -------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"staticValue\", staticValue }` | A fixed value.       |","table":"table-10"},"1299":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-106","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                                  | Sets the property to                                        |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"parameterId\", parameterId }` | The value of another parameter, such as a custom parameter. |","table":"table-10"},"1300":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-107","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#form-sections","content":"Each entry in `sections` has an `id`, a `displayName`, and the `parameters` it holds, plus optional `description`, `defaultVisibility` (`\"visible\"` or `\"hidden\"`), `columnCount` (`1` or `2`), `showTitleBar`, `collapsedByDefault`, `style` (`\"box\"` or `\"minimal\"`), and `conditionalOverrides`."},"1301":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-108","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#define-an-action-from-rules","content":"`defineAction` takes the parameters and logic rules directly, for actions the helpers do not cover. The rules use the Ontology IR rule types, such as `addObjectRule`, `modifyObjectRule`, `deleteObjectRule`, `addOrModifyObjectRuleV2`, and `addInterfaceRule`."},"1302":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-109","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#define-an-action-from-rules","content":"`defineAction` throws when there are no rules, when parameter IDs repeat, when a rule or section references a parameter that is not defined, or when a parameter condition refers to the same parameter or to one that comes later in the parameter order."},"1303":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"page","content":"Local development","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development"},"1304":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"Use @osdk/vite-plugin-oac to compile your ontology, generate an SDK, and serve a seeded mock Foundry API from the Vite dev server."},"1305":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1306":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"1307":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#install","content":"Install"},"1308":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Configure Vite"},"1309":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"Seed data"},"1310":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"Connect your app"},"1311":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"Limitations"},"1312":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"Seed data for the local Ontology server"},"1313":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"`@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` lets you build an app against your ontology-as-code definitions before they exist in Foundry. On every change to `.ontology/`, it compiles the ontology again, regenerates an SDK into `.osdk/src`, and answers OSDK requests from the Vite dev server with data from a seed file."},"1314":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"In current releases, the step in `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` that converts the IR to Ontology metadata reads a `blockData` key, but `@osdk/maker` writes the IR under `ontology`. The conversion fails with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'interfaceTypes')`, so no SDK is generated and the mock serves no types. Check the changelog for a fix before you adopt the plugin."},"1315":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                    | Tool                                            | Output                                      |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| 1. Compile the ontology | `pnpm exec maker -i <ontologyDir>/ontology.mts` | `node_modules/.osdk/.oac/.ontology.ir.json` |","table":"table-0"},"1316":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                                   | Tool                                    | Output                                   |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Convert the IR to Ontology metadata | `@osdk/generator-converters.ontologyir` | `node_modules/.osdk/.oac/.ontology.json` |","table":"table-0"},"1317":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step               | Tool                                          | Output                                       |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| 3. Generate an SDK | `pnpm exec osdk unstable typescript generate` | `.osdk/src`, then `pnpm exec tsc` in `.osdk` |","table":"table-0"},"1318":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                                | Tool         | Output                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 4. Start the mock (dev server only) | `@osdk/faux` | Ontology metadata and `seed.ts` data, served from the dev server |","table":"table-0"},"1319":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"The plugin writes the SDK to a temporary directory first, then copies only the files whose contents changed into `.osdk/src` and deletes files that are no longer generated."},"1320":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Command             | What runs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite` (dev server) | All four steps before the server starts, then all four again on every add, change, or delete under the ontology directory. After each successful run, the browser does a full reload. Failures are logged, and the server keeps running. |","table":"table-1"},"1321":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Command      | What runs                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite build` | Steps 1 to 3 in the `buildStart` hook. The build fails if any step fails. No mock server. |","table":"table-1"},"1322":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**pnpm.** The plugin runs `maker`, `osdk`, and `tsc` with `pnpm exec`, so pnpm must be on your `PATH` and each binary must be installed in your project."},"1323":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**Vite** and a Node.js version that can import `.mts` files natively: 22.18 or later, or 23.6 or later."},"1324":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**A `tsconfig.json` in `.osdk`.** After generating, the plugin runs `tsc` with `.osdk` as the working directory and fails if it exits with an error."},"1325":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#install","content":"The app itself needs `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api`, which the generated SDK imports, plus `@osdk/react` if you use React. `@osdk/faux` is only needed for the seed file's types."},"1326":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Add `ontologyAsCode` to your Vite config:"},"1327":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Pass `ontologyDir` as an absolute path: the plugin ignores a changed file unless its path starts with `ontologyDir`, and Vite's watcher reports absolute paths. The `resolve.alias` entry is one way to import the generated SDK as `@my-app/sdk`; add a matching `paths` entry to your app's `tsconfig.json` so TypeScript resolves it too."},"1328":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ontologyDir` | `string` |         | Required. The directory that holds `ontology.mts` and `seed.ts`. Created if it does not exist. |","table":"table-2"},"1329":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option        | Type                                     | Default  | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `loggerLevel` | `\"debug\" \\| \"info\" \\| \"warn\" \\| \"error\"` | `\"info\"` | The lowest level the plugin logs. Messages are prefixed with `[osdk]`. |","table":"table-2"},"1330":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option          | Type                                        | Default | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hooks.preSeed` | `(ontology: FauxOntology) => Promise<void>` |         | Runs after the plugin registers the generated metadata with the mock and before it applies the seed. Errors are logged and ignored. |","table":"table-2"},"1331":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Create `.osdk/tsconfig.json` for the `tsc` step. The generated code uses ES module imports with `.js` extensions:"},"1332":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Add `.osdk/src` to `.gitignore`, or commit it so the app builds without running the plugin. Do not edit it by hand."},"1333":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"The mock starts empty. The plugin loads `seed.ts` from the ontology directory after every regeneration and calls its default export with the mock's `FauxFoundry`. The file is required: without it, each regeneration logs an error and the browser does not reload."},"1334":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"`registerObject` takes the object's API name in `__apiName`, its primary key in `__primaryKey`, and property values in their wire format, such as ISO 8601 strings for dates. `registerLink(source, linkName, target, reverseLinkName)` takes both sides' link names and sets the foreign key for you, so this seed sets Ada's `officeId` to `\"lon\"` and her `leadId` to `2`."},"1335":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"Every regeneration rebuilds the mock from the seed, so edits made through actions last only until the next change to `.ontology/`."},"1336":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"The mock answers on the dev server's own origin, and passes any request it does not handle on to Vite. Create the client with the dev server's origin, the mock's Ontology RID, and the token the mock accepts:"},"1337":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value                    | Why                                       |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `window.location.origin` | The mock runs inside the Vite dev server. |","table":"table-3"},"1338":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value                                                            | Why                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ri.ontology.main.ontology.00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000` | The RID of the mock's only ontology. Do not use the generated SDK's `$ontologyRid`; a locally generated SDK sets it to a placeholder. |","table":"table-3"},"1339":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value             | Why                                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"myAccessToken\"` | The mock rejects any other bearer token with `401`. |","table":"table-3"},"1340":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"From there, use the client as you would against Foundry. With `@osdk/react`, pass it to `OsdkProvider` and query the generated types:"},"1341":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"See Create a client for `OsdkProvider`, and Load objects for the hooks."},"1342":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"The mock is an approximation of Foundry built from the generated metadata."},"1343":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area    | Behavior                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Actions | Create, modify, and delete object rules work. Add and delete link rules are only partly supported. Interface create, modify, and delete rules throw `not implemented`. |","table":"table-4"},"1344":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area                 | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Numeric primary keys | The mock accepts an object parameter only as a string, while the client sends the primary key as it is. Modify and delete actions on object types with numeric primary keys, such as `employeeId`, fail validation with `INVALID`. Use string primary keys for types you edit locally. |","table":"table-4"},"1345":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area       | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interfaces | Only shared-property-type properties reach the generated SDK and the mock, every interface property is optional, and object types do not record which interfaces they implement. Interface-defined properties are missing. |","table":"table-4"},"1346":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area      | Behavior                                                                  |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Functions | The generated metadata has no queries, so there are no functions to call. |","table":"table-4"},"1347":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area              | Behavior                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Schema migrations | The plugin runs `maker` without `--write-locks`. If an interface uses schema migrations, commit an up-to-date `ontology-schema-lock.json` or compilation fails. |","table":"table-4"},"1348":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"`@osdk/seed-helpers` and `@osdk/seed-compiler` build seed data for a different local server: the Ontology server that `@osdk/integration-testing` starts, which loads seed JSON into SQLite. They do not seed the Vite plugin's mock. To use them in tests, see Integration testing."},"1349":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"`seed-compiler` merges a directory of seed files into one JSON file:"},"1350":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option       | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--metadata` | Required. The `ontology-metadata.json` that the SDK generator writes with `--experimentalOntologyMetadata`. |","table":"table-5"},"1351":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option       | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--seed-dir` | Required. A directory of seed files. Every top-level `.mts` file whose name does not start with `$` is loaded, in file name order. |","table":"table-5"},"1352":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option           | Description                               |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--output` | Required. Where to write the merged JSON. |","table":"table-5"},"1353":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"Each seed file default-exports the result of `createSeedWithMetadata` from `@osdk/seed-helpers`, or its `output`. All files are merged through one builder, so primary keys must be unique across the whole directory, and a link can reference objects created in any file:"},"1354":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"page","content":"Object types","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types"},"1355":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","content":"Define object types with defineObject from @osdk/maker, including property types, primary keys, titles, value types, and datasources."},"1356":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"Define an object type"},"1357":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#primary-key-and-title","content":"Primary key and title"},"1358":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"Properties"},"1359":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"Property types"},"1360":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#struct-properties","content":"Struct properties"},"1361":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"Value types"},"1362":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#status","content":"Status"},"1363":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"Datasources"},"1364":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"Property security"},"1365":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"Derived properties"},"1366":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","content":"An object type describes one kind of thing in your ontology, such as an employee or an office: its properties, which property identifies each object, and where its data comes from. Define one with `defineObject` from `@osdk/maker` in your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file."},"1367":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"`defineObject` registers the type and returns its definition with the namespaced API name, so `employee.apiName` is `com.example.Employee` when you compile with `--apiNamespace com.example`. Pass the returned value wherever another definition needs the object type, such as a link or an action."},"1368":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The API name, without the namespace. |","table":"table-0"},"1369":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` |         | Required. The singular name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1370":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option              | Type     | Default | Description                                 |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `pluralDisplayName` | `string` |         | Required. The plural name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1371":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                      | Type     | Default | Description                                                |\n| --------------------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `primaryKeyPropertyApiName` | `string` |         | Required. The property whose value identifies each object. |","table":"table-0"},"1372":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                 | Type     | Default | Description                                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `titlePropertyApiName` | `string` |         | Required. The property shown as each object's title. |","table":"table-0"},"1373":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option       | Type                                 | Default | Description                                        |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `properties` | `Record<string, PropertyDefinition>` |         | The properties, keyed by API name. See Properties. |","table":"table-0"},"1374":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1375":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option | Type                                        | Default | Description                            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `{ locator: BlueprintIcon; color: string }` |         | A Blueprint icon name and a hex color. |","table":"table-0"},"1376":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option       | Type                                  | Default | Description                             |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `visibility` | `\"PROMINENT\" \\| \"NORMAL\" \\| \"HIDDEN\"` |         | How prominently Foundry shows the type. |","table":"table-0"},"1377":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option   | Type               | Default    | Description |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------- | ----------- |\n| `status` | `ObjectTypeStatus` | `\"active\"` | See Status. |","table":"table-0"},"1378":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                 | Type                             | Default | Description                                     |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `implementsInterfaces` | `Array<InterfaceImplementation>` |         | Interfaces the type implements. See Interfaces. |","table":"table-0"},"1379":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option        | Type                          | Default   | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `datasources` | `Array<DatasourceDefinition>` | A dataset | Where property values come from. See Datasources. |","table":"table-0"},"1380":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option         | Type      | Default | Description                                  |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `editsEnabled` | `boolean` |         | Whether users can edit objects of this type. |","table":"table-0"},"1381":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option               | Type                                                         | Default | Description                         |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `editsHistoryConfig` | `{ enabled: boolean; storeAllPreviousProperties?: boolean }` |         | Whether to keep a history of edits. |","table":"table-0"},"1382":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option    | Type            | Default | Description                                |\n| --------- | --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `aliases` | `Array<string>` |         | Other names to find the type by in search. |","table":"table-0"},"1383":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                          | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `includeEmptyBackingDatasource` | `boolean` |         | Ask `@osdk/maker-experimental` to package an empty backing dataset. Only valid when every datasource is `dataset` or `derived`. The `maker` CLI ignores it. |","table":"table-0"},"1384":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description                        |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model for the type. |","table":"table-0"},"1385":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#primary-key-and-title","content":"The primary key and title must both name properties of the object type, and `defineObject` throws if either is missing."},"1386":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#primary-key-and-title","content":"**Primary key.** Must be a primitive type, such as `string` or `integer`, and cannot be `editOnly`. Every object needs a unique value."},"1387":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#primary-key-and-title","content":"**Title.** Must be a primitive type, or a struct whose `mainValue` is primitive."},"1388":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"Each entry in `properties` maps an API name to a property definition. Only `type` is required. Property API names start with a letter and contain letters, digits, and `_`."},"1389":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option | Type               | Default | Description                   |\n| ------ | ------------------ | ------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `type` | `PropertyTypeType` |         | Required. See Property types. |","table":"table-1"},"1390":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default                                        | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | The API name with its first letter capitalized | The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-1"},"1391":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-1"},"1392":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option  | Type      | Default | Description                       |\n| ------- | --------- | ------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `array` | `boolean` | `false` | Store a list of values of `type`. |","table":"table-1"},"1393":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option     | Type                                                                      | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `reducers` | `Array<{ direction: \"ascending\" \\| \"descending\"; structField?: string }>` |         | For arrays, how to reduce the list to one value for display. |","table":"table-1"},"1394":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option      | Type                         | Default | Description                                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `valueType` | `ValueTypeDefinitionVersion` |         | A value type from `defineValueType`. Its constraints apply to the property. See Value types. |","table":"table-1"},"1395":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option               | Type                 | Default | Description                                                                                                                                  |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sharedPropertyType` | `SharedPropertyType` |         | Back the property with a shared property type. A shared property type can back only one property per object type. See Shared property types. |","table":"table-1"},"1396":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option        | Type                                                | Default | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `nullability` | `{ noNulls: boolean; noEmptyCollections: boolean }` |         | Disallow nulls or empty lists. Generated actions make the parameter required when `noNulls` is set. |","table":"table-1"},"1397":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option       | Type                                  | Default    | Description                                 |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `visibility` | `\"PROMINENT\" \\| \"NORMAL\" \\| \"HIDDEN\"` | `\"NORMAL\"` | How prominently Foundry shows the property. |","table":"table-1"},"1398":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option   | Type               | Default | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `ObjectTypeStatus` |         | The property's status. Must match the object's status unless the object is active. |","table":"table-1"},"1399":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option     | Type      | Default | Description                                                                   |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `editOnly` | `boolean` |         | The property has no datasource column and only holds values written by edits. |","table":"table-1"},"1400":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option             | Type      | Default                     | Description                         |\n| ------------------ | --------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `indexedForSearch` | `boolean` | `true`, except `attachment` | Whether the property is searchable. |","table":"table-1"},"1401":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option        | Type                                    | Default                                  | Description                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `typeClasses` | `Array<{ kind: string; name: string }>` | `SELECTABLE` and `SORTABLE` render hints | Type classes. `struct`, `geoshape`, `mediaReference`, `geotimeSeries`, `attachment`, and `vector` properties cannot have render hints. |","table":"table-1"},"1402":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option          | Type                      | Default | Description                             |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `baseFormatter` | `OntologyIrBaseFormatter` |         | How Foundry formats values for display. |","table":"table-1"},"1403":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"| Option                        | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ----------------------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `includeEmptyBackingMediaSet` | `boolean` |         | For `mediaReference` properties, ask `@osdk/maker-experimental` to package an empty media set. The `maker` CLI ignores it. |","table":"table-1"},"1404":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"`type` takes a string for most types and an object for types with options."},"1405":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-50","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type    | Value       | Notes |\n| ------- | ----------- | ----- |\n| Boolean | `\"boolean\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1406":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-51","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type     | Value                                      | Notes |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----- |\n| Integers | `\"byte\"`, `\"short\"`, `\"integer\"`, `\"long\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1407":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-52","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type     | Value                              | Notes                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Decimals | `\"float\"`, `\"double\"`, `\"decimal\"` | `{ type: \"decimal\", precision?: number, scale?: number }` sets precision and scale, which default to 5 and 2. |","table":"table-2"},"1408":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-53","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value      | Notes                                                     |\n| ------ | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| String | `\"string\"` | `{ type: \"string\", ... }` sets search options; see below. |","table":"table-2"},"1409":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-54","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type          | Value                   | Notes |\n| ------------- | ----------------------- | ----- |\n| Date and time | `\"date\"`, `\"timestamp\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1410":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-55","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type       | Value          | Notes |\n| ---------- | -------------- | ----- |\n| Attachment | `\"attachment\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1411":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-56","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type       | Value                      | Notes |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | ----- |\n| Geospatial | `\"geopoint\"`, `\"geoshape\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1412":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-57","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type  | Value              | Notes                                                             |\n| ----- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Media | `\"mediaReference\"` | Each `mediaReference` property gets its own media set datasource. |","table":"table-2"},"1413":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-58","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type        | Value             | Notes |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | ----- |\n| Time series | `\"geotimeSeries\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1414":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-59","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type    | Value                                                                                    | Notes                                                                                  |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Marking | `{ type: \"marking\", markingType: \"MANDATORY\" \\| \"CBAC\", markingInputGroupName: string }` | `markingInputGroupName` names the marking input chosen when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-2"},"1415":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-60","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value                                              | Notes                  |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Struct | `{ type: \"struct\", structDefinition, mainValue? }` | See Struct properties. |","table":"table-2"},"1416":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-61","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value                                                                                       | Notes                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Vector | `{ type: \"vector\", dimension: number, supportsSearchWith, embeddingModel?, quantization? }` | `supportsSearchWith` is `\"COSINE_SIMILARITY\"`, `\"DOT_PRODUCT\"`, or `\"EUCLIDEAN_DISTANCE\"`. `dimension` must be an integer of at least 1, and a vector property cannot be an array. |","table":"table-2"},"1417":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-62","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"The object form of `string` accepts `isLongText`, `supportsEfficientLeadingWildcard`, `supportsExactMatching`, `supportsFullTextRegex`, `supportsPhonetic`, `enableAsciiFolding`, and `analyzerOverride`:"},"1418":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-63","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#struct-properties","content":"A struct property groups named fields into one value. Each field is a type name, or an object with `fieldType` and `displayMetadata`. Fields cannot be structs, markings, or vectors. `mainValue` names the field or fields that represent the struct when it is shown as a single value, such as a title."},"1419":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-64","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"A value type is a reusable, versioned type with constraints, such as \"a string that looks like an email address\". Define it with `defineValueType`, then reference it from a property with `valueType`. Value types are written to `value-types.json` as well as the IR."},"1420":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-65","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The value type's API name. |","table":"table-3"},"1421":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-66","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                          |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `displayName` | `string` |         | Required. The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1422":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-67","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `version` | `string` |         | Required. A semantic version. You can define several versions of the same API name; each version must be unique. |","table":"table-3"},"1423":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-68","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option | Type                     | Default | Description                                  |\n| ------ | ------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `type` | `{ type, constraints? }` |         | Required. The base type and its constraints. |","table":"table-3"},"1424":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-69","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1425":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-70","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option   | Type                                                                                         | Default    | Description          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| `status` | `\"active\" \\| { type: \"deprecated\"; message: string; deadline: string; replacedBy?: string }` | `\"active\"` | Deprecate a version. |","table":"table-3"},"1426":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-71","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option            | Type      | Default | Description                                |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `namespacePrefix` | `boolean` | `false` | Prefix the API name with `--apiNamespace`. |","table":"table-3"},"1427":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-72","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"`type.type` is a type name (`boolean`, `binary`, `byte`, `short`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `double`, `decimal`, `string`, `date`, or `timestamp`) or an object for a composite type: `{ type: \"array\", elementType }`, `{ type: \"map\", keyType, valueType }`, `{ type: \"optional\", wrappedType }`, or `{ type: \"struct\", fields: [{ identifier, baseType }] }`. Each entry in `constraints` has a `constraint` for that base type and an optional `failureMessage`. String constraints are `regex`, `oneOf`, `length`, `isUuid`, and `isRid`:"},"1428":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-73","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#status","content":"`status` is `\"active\"`, `\"experimental\"`, `\"example\"`, or `{ type: \"deprecated\", message, deadline }`, where `deadline` is an ISO 8601 date or date-time. An experimental, example, or deprecated object type can only contain properties with the same status, and a link to it must have a matching status. See Link status."},"1429":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-74","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"`datasources` says where property values come from. Without it, a dataset backs every property. Give an object type one base datasource (`dataset`, `stream`, `restrictedView`, or `direct`) plus any number of `derived` datasources; `defineObject` throws if you list more than one `dataset`, `stream`, or `restrictedView`. Properties not mapped by a `derived` datasource come from the base datasource."},"1430":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-75","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`      | Options                                            | Description                     |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `\"dataset\"` | `objectSecurityPolicy?`, `propertySecurityGroups?` | A dataset backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1431":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-76","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`     | Options            | Description                                                                                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"stream\"` | `retentionPeriod?` | A stream backs the properties. `retentionPeriod` is an ISO 8601 duration, such as `\"P90D\"`. |","table":"table-4"},"1432":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-77","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`             | Options | Description                             |\n| ------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `\"restrictedView\"` |         | A restricted view backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1433":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-78","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`     | Options                                            | Description                           |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `\"direct\"` | `objectSecurityPolicy?`, `propertySecurityGroups?` | A direct source backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1434":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-79","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`      | Options                             | Description                                                      |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"derived\"` | `linkDefinition`, `propertyMapping` | Properties computed from linked objects. See Derived properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1435":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-80","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"On `dataset` and `direct` datasources, `propertySecurityGroups` restricts who can read a set of properties, and `objectSecurityPolicy` restricts who can read the objects. Each takes a `name`, an optional `granularPolicy` condition, and optional `appliedMarkings` and `assumedMarkings` maps from a marking input name to `\"CBAC\"` or `\"MANDATORY\"`."},"1436":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-81","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"A `granularPolicy` condition is one of:"},"1437":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-82","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                 | Passes when                                                                          |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"group\", name }` | The user is in the group chosen for the input `name` when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-5"},"1438":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-83","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                                  |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"groupProperty\", property }` | The user is in a group listed in `property`. |","table":"table-5"},"1439":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-84","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                               | Passes when                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"markingProperty\", property }` | The user satisfies the markings in the marking property `property`. |","table":"table-5"},"1440":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-85","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"and\" \\| \"or\", conditions }` | All or any of `conditions` pass. |","table":"table-5"},"1441":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-86","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"A `derived` datasource computes properties from objects reached through one or more links. `linkDefinition` lists the links to follow in order, and `propertyMapping` maps each derived property to either a property on the linked object or an aggregation."},"1442":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-87","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation         | Derived property must be | Description                   |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"count\" }` | Any                      | The number of linked objects. |","table":"table-6"},"1443":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-88","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                          | Derived property must be | Description                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"sum\" \\| \"avg\", property }` | Numeric                  | The sum or average of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1444":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-89","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                          | Derived property must be | Description                                  |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"min\" \\| \"max\", property }` | Primitive                | The smallest or largest value of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1445":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-90","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                                                          | Derived property must be | Description                                  |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"approximateCardinality\" \\| \"exactCardinality\", property }` | Primitive                | The number of distinct values of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1446":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-91","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                                                | Derived property must be | Description                                      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"collectList\" \\| \"collectSet\", property, limit }` | An array                 | Up to `limit` values of `property`, at most 100. |","table":"table-6"},"1447":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-92","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"Aggregations skip linked objects where the property is null. Generated create, modify, and create-or-modify actions leave derived properties out of their parameters."},"1448":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-93","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"The link must be defined before the object that uses it. When the object is not defined yet, refer to it from the link by its API name:"},"1449":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-94","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"When you compile with `--apiNamespace`, the string reference must include the namespace, such as `\"com.example.Office\"`."},"1450":{"id":"/overview","page_id":"/overview","type":"page","content":"What is OSDK","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/overview"},"1451":{"id":"/overview-0","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview","content":"The Ontology SDK gives TypeScript apps a typed client for your Foundry Ontology's objects, links, actions, functions, and interfaces."},"1452":{"id":"/overview-1","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1453":{"id":"/overview-2","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#packages","content":"Packages"},"1454":{"id":"/overview-3","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"A first query"},"1455":{"id":"/overview-4","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"Why use `@osdk/react`"},"1456":{"id":"/overview-5","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1457":{"id":"/overview-6","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview","content":"The Ontology SDK (OSDK) lets you read and write your Foundry Ontology from TypeScript with types generated from your own object types, actions, and functions. Use it in browser apps, Node.js services, and scripts, and add `@osdk/react` to get cached, reactive hooks in React."},"1458":{"id":"/overview-7","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"You pick the Ontology resources your app needs in Developer Console, and Foundry generates an npm package for them, such as `@my-app/sdk`. The generated package contains typed definitions only. The runtime that sends requests, pages results, and applies actions lives in `@osdk/client`, and you pass definitions to it:"},"1459":{"id":"/overview-8","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export     | How you use it                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object type      | `Employee`, `Office` | `client(Employee).where(...).fetchPage()`, or `useOsdkObjects(Employee)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1460":{"id":"/overview-9","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export       | How you use it                                             |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Link type        | `$link` on each object | `employee.$link.office.fetchOne()`, or `useLinks` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1461":{"id":"/overview-10","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export | How you use it                                                                         |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Action type      | `modifyEmployee` | `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction(...)`, or `useOsdkAction(modifyEmployee)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1462":{"id":"/overview-11","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export                | How you use it                                                       |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Function (query) | A function definition per query | `client(fn).executeFunction(...)`, or `useOsdkFunction(fn)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1463":{"id":"/overview-12","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export             | How you use it                                                                     |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interface        | One definition per interface | `client(MyInterface).fetchPage()` returns objects of every type that implements it |","table":"table-0"},"1464":{"id":"/overview-13","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"Because the SDK holds metadata rather than generated implementation code, its size grows with the number of types you include, unused definitions tree-shake away, and fixes to the client ship as a dependency bump without regenerating your SDK. The generated package also exports namespaces such as `$Objects`, `$Actions`, and `$Queries`, so `import * as Sdk from \"@my-app/sdk\"` gives you autocomplete over everything in it."},"1465":{"id":"/overview-14","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"Dates and timestamps arrive as ISO 8601 strings. OSDK does not bundle a date library, so parse them with the one your app already uses."},"1466":{"id":"/overview-15","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package        | Role                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/client` | The runtime. `createClient` returns the `client` you call with definitions to fetch objects, follow links, apply actions, and execute functions. |","table":"table-1"},"1467":{"id":"/overview-16","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package     | Role                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/api` | Shared type definitions that `@osdk/client` and generated SDKs both depend on. Install it alongside `@osdk/client`. |","table":"table-1"},"1468":{"id":"/overview-17","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                       | Role                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Generated SDK (`@my-app/sdk`) | Your Ontology's object types, interfaces, actions, and functions, generated in Developer Console and installed from your Foundry npm registry. |","table":"table-1"},"1469":{"id":"/overview-18","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package       | Role                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/oauth` | Token providers: `createPublicOauthClient` for browser apps, `createConfidentialOauthClient` for servers, `createAuthlessClient` for public apps. |","table":"table-1"},"1470":{"id":"/overview-19","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package       | Role                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react` | `OsdkProvider` and hooks such as `useOsdkObjects`, `useOsdkObject`, `useLinks`, `useOsdkAction`, and `useOsdkFunction`, backed by a normalized cache. |","table":"table-1"},"1471":{"id":"/overview-20","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                  | Role                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | Ontology-aware React components, such as `ObjectTable`, `FilterList`, and `ActionForm`, built on `@osdk/react`. |","table":"table-1"},"1472":{"id":"/overview-21","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package            | Role                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/create-app` | A CLI that scaffolds a React, Vue, or Expo app with authentication, client setup, and your SDK already wired in. |","table":"table-1"},"1473":{"id":"/overview-22","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                | Role                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-devtools` | A development panel and Vite plugin for inspecting the queries, cache entries, and actions of a running `@osdk/react` app. |","table":"table-1"},"1474":{"id":"/overview-23","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"Create a client once, then pass it a definition from your SDK. `createClient` takes the Foundry URL, your Ontology RID, and a token provider, here the OAuth client from `@osdk/oauth`:"},"1475":{"id":"/overview-24","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"In React, wrap your app in `OsdkProvider` with the same client, and read the data with a hook. The hook loads the page, caches it, and re-renders the component when the objects change:"},"1476":{"id":"/overview-25","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"See Create a client for `OsdkProvider` setup and the full `createClient` reference."},"1477":{"id":"/overview-26","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"You can call `@osdk/client` from any data layer, including TanStack Query. `@osdk/react` adds behavior that a generic request cache cannot reproduce because it understands Ontology objects:"},"1478":{"id":"/overview-27","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Normalized object cache.** Each object, such as `Employee:42`, is stored once. When it changes, every list, link, and detail view that contains it re-renders with the new values."},"1479":{"id":"/overview-28","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Deduplicated requests.** Components that ask for the same objects with the same options share one cache entry and one request."},"1480":{"id":"/overview-29","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Updates after actions.** An action's response lists the objects it added, modified, and deleted. The cache reloads those objects and re-evaluates affected lists against their `where` clauses, with no manual invalidation."},"1481":{"id":"/overview-30","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Optimistic updates with rollback.** Pass `$optimisticUpdate` to `applyAction` to show the expected result immediately. If the action fails, the cache restores the previous state."},"1482":{"id":"/overview-31","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Live data.** `streamUpdates: true` keeps a list current over a WebSocket subscription instead of polling."},"1483":{"id":"/overview-32","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Function dependencies.** `useOsdkFunction` reruns a function when objects it depends on change, using `dependsOn` for object types or `dependsOnObjects` for specific instances."},"1484":{"id":"/overview-33","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"Use `@osdk/react` for Ontology data and keep a general-purpose library such as TanStack Query for non-Foundry APIs. The two work side by side. Caching explains how the cache stores and shares entries."},"1485":{"id":"/overview-34","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Scaffold a React app with `@osdk/create-app` and run your first query and action."},"1486":{"id":"/overview-35","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Add OSDK packages and your generated SDK to an existing app."},"1487":{"id":"/overview-36","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Fetch lists and single objects with `useOsdkObjects` and `useOsdkObject`."},"1488":{"id":"/overview-37","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Build with Ontology-aware tables, filters, and action forms."},"1489":{"id":"/quickstart","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/quickstart"},"1490":{"id":"/quickstart-0","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Scaffold a React app with @osdk/create-app, sign in to Foundry, and run your first OSDK query and action."},"1491":{"id":"/quickstart-1","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"1492":{"id":"/quickstart-2","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#create-the-app","content":"Create the app"},"1493":{"id":"/quickstart-3","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Run the CLI"},"1494":{"id":"/quickstart-4","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"Install dependencies"},"1495":{"id":"/quickstart-5","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#start-the-dev-server","content":"Start the dev server"},"1496":{"id":"/quickstart-6","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"What the CLI generates"},"1497":{"id":"/quickstart-7","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Run your first query"},"1498":{"id":"/quickstart-8","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"Apply your first action"},"1499":{"id":"/quickstart-9","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1500":{"id":"/quickstart-10","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Use `@osdk/create-app` to generate a React and Vite app that already handles sign-in, creates an OSDK client, and installs your generated SDK. By the end of this page you have a local app that lists `Employee` objects and applies the `modifyEmployee` action."},"1501":{"id":"/quickstart-11","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"To add OSDK to an app you already have, see Installation instead."},"1502":{"id":"/quickstart-12","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"You need Node.js and an application in Foundry Developer Console. The CLI asks for these values, so collect them first:"},"1503":{"id":"/quickstart-13","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value       | Example                               | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry URL | `https://example.palantirfoundry.com` | The URL of your Foundry stack.        |","table":"table-0"},"1504":{"id":"/quickstart-14","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value           | Example                                                   | Where to find it in Developer Console                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Application RID | `ri.third-party-applications.main.application.1c66b352-…` | The application's Developer Console URL, `/workspace/developer-console/app/<rid>`. |","table":"table-0"},"1505":{"id":"/quickstart-15","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value           | Example                            | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| OAuth client ID | `2650385ab6c5e0df3b44aff776b00a42` | **OAuth & scopes**.                   |","table":"table-0"},"1506":{"id":"/quickstart-16","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value        | Example                                | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Ontology RID | `ri.ontology.main.ontology.1df1ce4c-…` | **Ontology SDK**.                     |","table":"table-0"},"1507":{"id":"/quickstart-17","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example       | Where to find it in Developer Console                                               |\n| ---------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| SDK package name | `@my-app/sdk` | The npm install instructions of a generated SDK version. Must match `@<scope>/sdk`. |","table":"table-0"},"1508":{"id":"/quickstart-18","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example                                                                                                | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| npm registry URL | `https://example.palantirfoundry.com/artifacts/api/repositories/<repository-rid>/contents/release/npm` | The SDK's npm install instructions.   |","table":"table-0"},"1509":{"id":"/quickstart-19","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"In Developer Console, also:"},"1510":{"id":"/quickstart-20","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Add the object types, link types, actions, and functions your app uses to the application's SDK, then generate a new version on **SDK versions** with the **npm** package type and the latest generator. Generate a new version whenever you change the resources."},"1511":{"id":"/quickstart-21","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"On **OAuth & scopes**, add `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` as a redirect URL. The generated app runs on port 8080 and handles the sign-in redirect at that path."},"1512":{"id":"/quickstart-22","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Get a Foundry token with access to the SDK's npm registry. The generated `.npmrc` reads it from the `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` environment variable when you install packages."},"1513":{"id":"/quickstart-23","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Run `@osdk/create-app` and pass the project directory name:"},"1514":{"id":"/quickstart-24","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"`npm create @osdk/app@latest` runs the same CLI. The prompts, in order:"},"1515":{"id":"/quickstart-25","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                   | Default       | Flag                   |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Project name (letters, digits, `-`, `_`) | `my-osdk-app` | positional `[project]` |","table":"table-1"},"1516":{"id":"/quickstart-26","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                         | Default | Flag         |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| Framework: React, React (Public), Expo, or Vue |         | `--template` |","table":"table-1"},"1517":{"id":"/quickstart-27","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                   | Default | Flag           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------- |\n| Foundry URL (must start with `https://`) |         | `--foundryUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1518":{"id":"/quickstart-28","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                           | Default | Flag                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Do you know your production URL? |         | `--applicationUrl` or `--skipApplicationUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1519":{"id":"/quickstart-29","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt          | Default | Flag            |\n| --------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| Application RID |         | `--application` |","table":"table-1"},"1520":{"id":"/quickstart-30","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt          | Default | Flag         |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| OAuth client ID |         | `--clientId` |","table":"table-1"},"1521":{"id":"/quickstart-31","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                              | Default | Flag                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Will you use an OSDK? (No means Platform APIs only) |         | `--skipOsdk` (also pass `--sdkVersion 2.x`) |","table":"table-1"},"1522":{"id":"/quickstart-32","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Default | Flag         |\n| ------------ | ------- | ------------ |\n| Ontology RID |         | `--ontology` |","table":"table-1"},"1523":{"id":"/quickstart-33","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Default | Flag            |\n| ---------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| SDK package name |         | `--osdkPackage` |","table":"table-1"},"1524":{"id":"/quickstart-34","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Default | Flag                |\n| ---------------- | ------- | ------------------- |\n| npm registry URL |         | `--osdkRegistryUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1525":{"id":"/quickstart-35","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                      | Default | Flag          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------- |\n| Include a CORS proxy for local development? | No      | `--corsProxy` |","table":"table-1"},"1526":{"id":"/quickstart-36","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Default                                                                         | Flag       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| OAuth scopes | `api:read-data api:write-data api:use-ontologies-read api:use-ontologies-write` | `--scopes` |","table":"table-1"},"1527":{"id":"/quickstart-37","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Choose **React** for this guide. Answer **Yes** to the CORS proxy unless your Foundry administrator has allowed `http://localhost:8080` as a CORS origin."},"1528":{"id":"/quickstart-38","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"To skip every prompt, pass all values as flags:"},"1529":{"id":"/quickstart-39","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"Export your token so npm can reach your SDK's registry, then install:"},"1530":{"id":"/quickstart-40","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"A `401` or `404` for `@my-app/sdk` means `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` is missing, expired, or lacks access to the registry."},"1531":{"id":"/quickstart-41","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#start-the-dev-server","content":"Open `http://localhost:8080` to see the starter page. The app does not sign you in until it makes its first OSDK request. Once you add the component in Run your first query, it sends you to Foundry to sign in, Foundry redirects back to `/auth/callback`, and the app returns you to the home page. If Foundry reports an invalid redirect URL, add `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console."},"1532":{"id":"/quickstart-42","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.development\" />"},"1533":{"id":"/quickstart-43","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.production\" />"},"1534":{"id":"/quickstart-44","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"1535":{"id":"/quickstart-45","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"1536":{"id":"/quickstart-46","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1537":{"id":"/quickstart-47","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"1538":{"id":"/quickstart-48","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1539":{"id":"/quickstart-49","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"resources.json\" />"},"1540":{"id":"/quickstart-50","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"AuthCallback.tsx\" />"},"1541":{"id":"/quickstart-51","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"1542":{"id":"/quickstart-52","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"env.test.ts\" />"},"1543":{"id":"/quickstart-53","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Home.tsx\" />"},"1544":{"id":"/quickstart-54","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1545":{"id":"/quickstart-55","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"router.tsx\" />"},"1546":{"id":"/quickstart-56","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"ErrorBoundary.tsx\" />"},"1547":{"id":"/quickstart-57","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Header.tsx\" />"},"1548":{"id":"/quickstart-58","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Loading.tsx\" />"},"1549":{"id":"/quickstart-59","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"NextSteps.tsx\" />"},"1550":{"id":"/quickstart-60","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Osdk.tsx\" />"},"1551":{"id":"/quickstart-61","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                                  | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `.env.development`, `.env.production` | `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`, and `VITE_FOUNDRY_ONTOLOGY_RID` for each mode. With the CORS proxy, the development API URL is `http://localhost:8080`. With `--skipApplicationUrl`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL` in `.env.production` is commented out; fill it in before you deploy. |","table":"table-2"},"1552":{"id":"/quickstart-62","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File         | Purpose                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `index.html` | Copies the env values into `<meta>` tags such as `osdk-foundryUrl` and `osdk-clientId`, so you can change configuration without rebuilding JavaScript. |","table":"table-2"},"1553":{"id":"/quickstart-63","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File            | Purpose                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/client.ts` | Reads the meta tags, creates `auth` with `createPublicOauthClient`, and exports `client` from `createClient`. |","table":"table-2"},"1554":{"id":"/quickstart-64","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                     |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.tsx` | Renders the router inside `<OsdkProvider client={client}>`. |","table":"table-2"},"1555":{"id":"/quickstart-65","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/router.tsx` | Maps `/` to `Home` and `/auth/callback` to `AuthCallback`. |","table":"table-2"},"1556":{"id":"/quickstart-66","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                                                    |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/AuthCallback.tsx` | Calls `auth.signIn()` to finish the OAuth redirect, then navigates to `/`. |","table":"table-2"},"1557":{"id":"/quickstart-67","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite.config.ts` | Serves on port 8080, proxies `/api` and `/multipass/api` to Foundry when you chose the CORS proxy, and defines `process.env.NODE_ENV`. See Use OSDK with Vite. |","table":"table-2"},"1558":{"id":"/quickstart-68","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File     | Purpose                                                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.npmrc` | Points your SDK's npm scope at the Foundry registry and authenticates with `${FOUNDRY_TOKEN}`. |","table":"table-2"},"1559":{"id":"/quickstart-69","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json` | Deployment settings for Foundry website hosting with `@osdk/cli`. Delete it if you host elsewhere. |","table":"table-2"},"1560":{"id":"/quickstart-70","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File              | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/env.test.ts` | A test that checks `.env.production` sets `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, and `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`. It runs only when `VERIFY_ENV_PRODUCTION=true`. |","table":"table-2"},"1561":{"id":"/quickstart-71","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"The generated `src/client.ts` looks like this:"},"1562":{"id":"/quickstart-72","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"Authentication explains the sign-in flow and the callback route. Create a client covers `createClient` and `OsdkProvider`."},"1563":{"id":"/quickstart-73","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Create a component that lists employees with `useOsdkObjects`. Replace `Employee`, `department`, and `fullName` with an object type and properties from your SDK:"},"1564":{"id":"/quickstart-74","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Render it from `src/Home.tsx`:"},"1565":{"id":"/quickstart-75","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"The list keeps rendering while it loads and reloads, so show the loading indicator next to the data instead of in place of it. See Load objects for filters, pagination, and live updates."},"1566":{"id":"/quickstart-76","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"Add a button that applies `modifyEmployee`. `useOsdkAction` tracks the pending state and the last error, and `applyAction` rethrows, so attach a `catch`:"},"1567":{"id":"/quickstart-77","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"When the action succeeds, the list updates without a refetch call: the action response tells the cache which objects changed. See Apply actions for validation, batches, and optimistic updates."},"1568":{"id":"/quickstart-78","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Filter, sort, paginate, and stream updates with `useOsdkObjects`."},"1569":{"id":"/quickstart-79","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Validate parameters and show optimistic results."},"1570":{"id":"/quickstart-80","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Drop in `ObjectTable`, `FilterList`, and `ActionForm`."},"1571":{"id":"/quickstart-81","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Inspect your app's queries and cache while you develop."},"1572":{"id":"/troubleshooting","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Help"],"tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting"},"1573":{"id":"/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting","content":"Fixes for common OSDK errors, including a missing OsdkProvider, mismatched package versions, CORS, auth failures, and Vite build issues."},"1574":{"id":"/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"`No OsdkProvider found. Did you forget to wrap your component tree with <OsdkProvider>?`"},"1575":{"id":"/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"`\"<name>\" is not exported by @osdk/client/…/observable.js`"},"1576":{"id":"/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"Peer dependency warnings for `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api`"},"1577":{"id":"/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"`Rollup failed to resolve import \"@osdk/foundry.admin\"`"},"1578":{"id":"/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#referenceerror-process-is-not-defined","content":"`ReferenceError: process is not defined`"},"1579":{"id":"/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"CORS errors in local development"},"1580":{"id":"/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"`401 Unauthorized`"},"1581":{"id":"/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"`403 Forbidden` or `PERMISSION_DENIED`"},"1582":{"id":"/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#invalid-ontology-rid","content":"`Invalid ontology RID`"},"1583":{"id":"/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#meta-tag-osdk-clientid-contains-placeholder-value","content":"`Meta tag osdk-clientId contains placeholder value`"},"1584":{"id":"/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#rendered-more-hooks-than-during-the-previous-render","content":"`Rendered more hooks than during the previous render`"},"1585":{"id":"/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#actions-take-about-a-second-in-development","content":"Actions take about a second in development"},"1586":{"id":"/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#data-does-not-update-after-a-change-made-elsewhere","content":"Data does not update after a change made elsewhere"},"1587":{"id":"/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"Deprecation warnings for `@osdk/react/experimental`"},"1588":{"id":"/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"The devtools panel does not appear"},"1589":{"id":"/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting","content":"Find the error message or symptom you see, then apply the fix. Each section names the cause first."},"1590":{"id":"/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"A component called an `@osdk/react` hook, or used the client from `useOsdkClient`, outside an `OsdkProvider`. Outside a provider, every hook gets a placeholder client that throws this error."},"1591":{"id":"/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"Render `OsdkProvider` once at the root, above every component that uses OSDK hooks:"},"1592":{"id":"/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"If only some components fail, they render outside the provider, for example in a header or a portal mounted next to `<App />`. Move `OsdkProvider` up so it wraps them."},"1593":{"id":"/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"In tests, wrap the component under test in a provider. See Testing."},"1594":{"id":"/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"You might also see the same error for `unstable-do-not-use.js` or a path in `@osdk/api`. `@osdk/react` imports its runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, and your installed `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` comes from a different release than your `@osdk/react`."},"1595":{"id":"/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"`@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` share one version number. Install the same version of all three, and keep prereleases together:"},"1596":{"id":"/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"Check what is installed with `npm ls @osdk/api @osdk/client @osdk/react`. Do not delete the failing import or downgrade one package on its own. See Version compatibility."},"1597":{"id":"/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"The peer ranges that `@osdk/react` declares allow newer `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` minor versions than it was built with, and before 2.87.0 they also allowed older ones. Pin `@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` to the same version instead of ignoring the warning."},"1598":{"id":"/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"If the warning comes from your generated SDK, the SDK was built against a newer `@osdk/client` than you have. Upgrade the three OSDK packages, or generate a new SDK version. If npm still cannot resolve peers, use `overrides` as shown in Installation."},"1599":{"id":"/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"The same error can name `@osdk/foundry.core`. You import from `@osdk/react/platform-apis`, which depends on two optional peer packages that are not installed."},"1600":{"id":"/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"Install them:"},"1601":{"id":"/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"If you do not use the platform API hooks, remove the imports from `@osdk/react/platform-apis` instead. See Platform APIs."},"1602":{"id":"/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#referenceerror-process-is-not-defined","content":"OSDK packages read `process.env.NODE_ENV`, and Vite does not replace it by default. Add `\"process.env.NODE_ENV\": JSON.stringify(mode)` to `define` in your Vite config. See Use OSDK with Vite for the full config."},"1603":{"id":"/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"The browser console shows an error like `Access to fetch at 'https://<your-stack>/api/...' from origin 'http://localhost:8080' has been blocked by CORS policy`. Your Foundry environment does not allow requests from your dev server's origin."},"1604":{"id":"/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"Fix it in one of two ways:"},"1605":{"id":"/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"**Allow the origin.** Ask your Foundry administrator to allow `http://localhost:8080` for CORS on your environment."},"1606":{"id":"/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"**Proxy through Vite.** Forward `/api` and `/multipass/api` to Foundry from the dev server, and set `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL=http://localhost:8080`. Requests then go to your own origin, so CORS does not apply. See Proxy Foundry requests in development."},"1607":{"id":"/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"Apps created with `@osdk/create-app` include the proxy when you answer yes to the CORS proxy prompt or pass `--corsProxy`. The proxy runs only under `vite dev`, so keep the real Foundry URL in `.env.production`."},"1608":{"id":"/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"The request had no valid token. Check, in order:"},"1609":{"id":"/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Client ID.** The client ID passed to `createPublicOauthClient` matches the one on your application's **OAuth & scopes** page in Developer Console."},"1610":{"id":"/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Redirect URL.** The redirect URL matches one listed on the same page exactly, including protocol, port, and path, such as `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback`."},"1611":{"id":"/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Callback route.** Your app renders a route at the redirect path, so the OAuth client can complete sign-in."},"1612":{"id":"/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Token provider.** The client receives the OAuth client as its token provider: `createClient(foundryUrl, ontologyRid, auth)`."},"1613":{"id":"/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"To detect an expired session in UI code, check `error.statusCode === 401` on a `PalantirApiError`. See Loading and errors."},"1614":{"id":"/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"The token is valid but cannot do what you asked. Common causes:"},"1615":{"id":"/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**Missing scopes.** The OAuth client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write` by default. Other APIs need more. For example, the user and marking hooks in `@osdk/react/platform-apis` need `api:admin-read`. Add the scope to the application in Developer Console, then request it:"},"1616":{"id":"/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"Changing `scopes` signs users in again so the new token carries them. See Scopes."},"1617":{"id":"/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**Resources outside the application's scope.** The object type, action, or function is not included in the application's Ontology SDK resources in Developer Console."},"1618":{"id":"/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**User permissions.** The signed-in user cannot see the data or apply the action. Requests made with a public OAuth client act as the signed-in user and never exceed that user's access."},"1619":{"id":"/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"A `NOT_FOUND` error, such as `ObjectNotFound`, can also mean the user lacks access to an object that exists."},"1620":{"id":"/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#invalid-ontology-rid","content":"`createClient` throws this when its second argument does not start with `ri.`. The value is often empty, an API name, or a placeholder from an env file. Pass the full Ontology RID, such as `ri.ontology.main.ontology.<uuid>`. Find it on the **Ontology SDK** page of your application in Developer Console, or import `$ontologyRid` from your generated SDK."},"1621":{"id":"/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#meta-tag-osdk-clientid-contains-placeholder-value","content":"Apps created with `@osdk/create-app` read their configuration from `<meta>` tags that Vite fills in from `.env` files. This error means a variable, such as `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, is not set for the current mode. Add it to `.env.development` or `.env.production` and restart the dev server."},"1622":{"id":"/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rendered-more-hooks-than-during-the-previous-render","content":"A component called an `@osdk/react` hook conditionally. Call every hook on every render, and use `enabled` to skip the request:"},"1623":{"id":"/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#actions-take-about-a-second-in-development","content":"In development, single (non-batched) actions that have an `$optimisticUpdate` wait 1000 ms after the server responds so you can see the optimistic state. The console logs `[@osdk/client] Applied a 1000ms dev-mode delay…` the first time it happens. Production builds never delay. To turn it off in development:"},"1624":{"id":"/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#data-does-not-update-after-a-change-made-elsewhere","content":"The cache updates itself after actions you apply through `useOsdkAction`. It cannot see changes made by other systems, by `@osdk/client` calls outside the hooks, or by REST calls. Invalidate the affected data, or use `streamUpdates: true` on lists that must stay live. See Caching and reactivity and Cache invalidation."},"1625":{"id":"/troubleshooting-52","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"The hooks from `@osdk/react/experimental` are now exported from `@osdk/react`, and `OsdkProvider2` is now `OsdkProvider`. Change the imports:"},"1626":{"id":"/troubleshooting-53","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"The `experimental` entry point will be removed in a future major version."},"1627":{"id":"/troubleshooting-54","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom   | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| No panel. | Confirm `osdkDevTools()` from `@osdk/react-devtools/vite` is in your Vite `plugins` and you run `vite dev`. Pass `osdkDevTools({ verbose: true })` and look for `Injected devtools into HTML` in the terminal. |","table":"table-0"},"1628":{"id":"/troubleshooting-55","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom              | Fix                                                                                                                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Panel shows no data. | The screen must read data through `@osdk/react` hooks under `OsdkProvider`. The panel does not see raw `fetch` calls. |","table":"table-0"},"1629":{"id":"/troubleshooting-56","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom                              | Fix                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Component inspection is unavailable. | Something loaded React before the devtools script. Remove scripts in `index.html` that load React first. |","table":"table-0"},"1630":{"id":"/troubleshooting-57","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"See the devtools troubleshooting table for more."},"1631":{"id":"/widgets","page_id":"/widgets","type":"page","content":"Custom widgets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets"},"1632":{"id":"/widgets-0","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets","content":"Build React or plain TypeScript widgets that run inside Foundry UIs such as Workshop, exchange parameters and events with the host, and call the OSDK."},"1633":{"id":"/widgets-1","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1634":{"id":"/widgets-2","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#packages","content":"Packages"},"1635":{"id":"/widgets-3","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"Create a widget set project"},"1636":{"id":"/widgets-4","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"Run the CLI"},"1637":{"id":"/widgets-5","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#install-dependencies","content":"Install dependencies"},"1638":{"id":"/widgets-6","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#start-developer-mode","content":"Start developer mode"},"1639":{"id":"/widgets-7","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"Project layout"},"1640":{"id":"/widgets-8","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#run-locally","content":"Run locally"},"1641":{"id":"/widgets-9","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#start-the-dev-server","content":"Start the dev server"},"1642":{"id":"/widgets-10","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"Open the setup URL"},"1643":{"id":"/widgets-11","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"Edit your code"},"1644":{"id":"/widgets-12","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"Code Workspaces"},"1645":{"id":"/widgets-13","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"Use the OSDK in a widget"},"1646":{"id":"/widgets-14","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"Build a widget without React"},"1647":{"id":"/widgets-15","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1648":{"id":"/widgets-16","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets","content":"A custom widget is a web page you build with Vite that Foundry embeds inside a host UI such as Workshop. The host passes values into the widget as parameters, the widget sends events back to update them, and the widget can read and write your Ontology through the OSDK."},"1649":{"id":"/widgets-17","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"Widgets ship in a **widget set**, a Foundry resource with a RID such as `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. One project builds one widget set, and each HTML entrypoint in its Vite config becomes one widget in the set. You deploy the set as numbered versions, and the host loads the scripts and stylesheets that the version's manifest lists."},"1650":{"id":"/widgets-18","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"Each widget declares its contract in a config file built with `defineConfig`: an ID and name, the parameters the host can set, and the events the widget can emit. At build time, `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` turns those configs into the manifest at `.palantir/widgets.config.json`, which tells Foundry what to show in the widget's setup panel. See Parameters and events."},"1651":{"id":"/widgets-19","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"At runtime the host injects `window.__PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__` into the widget's page, and the two sides exchange typed messages through it:"},"1652":{"id":"/widgets-20","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message        | Direction      | Payload                   | When                                                          |\n| -------------- | -------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.ready` | Widget to host | `{ apiVersion: \"1.0.0\" }` | The widget is listening and wants its first parameter values. |","table":"table-0"},"1653":{"id":"/widgets-21","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message                  | Direction      | Payload                                            | When                                             |\n| ------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `host.update-parameters` | Host to widget | `{ parameters }`, one async value per parameter ID | Parameter values or their loading states change. |","table":"table-0"},"1654":{"id":"/widgets-22","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message             | Direction      | Payload                         | When                                         |\n| ------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.emit-event` | Widget to host | `{ eventId, parameterUpdates }` | The widget fires one of its declared events. |","table":"table-0"},"1655":{"id":"/widgets-23","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message         | Direction      | Payload                                               | When                               |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `widget.resize` | Widget to host | `{ width, height }` of the document body's border box | The widget's content changes size. |","table":"table-0"},"1656":{"id":"/widgets-24","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message         | Direction      | Payload | When                                                                            |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.reload` | Widget to host | `{}`    | The widget needs a full reload, such as a Vite full-page reload in development. |","table":"table-0"},"1657":{"id":"/widgets-25","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message            | Direction      | Payload       | When                                                         |\n| ------------------ | -------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `host.set-hotkeys` | Host to widget | `{ hotkeys }` | The host tells the widget which key combinations to forward. |","table":"table-0"},"1658":{"id":"/widgets-26","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message         | Direction      | Payload      | When                                                              |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.hotkey` | Widget to host | `{ hotkey }` | The user pressed one of those key combinations inside the widget. |","table":"table-0"},"1659":{"id":"/widgets-27","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message          | Direction      | Payload     | When                      |\n| ---------------- | -------------- | ----------- | ------------------------- |\n| `host.set-theme` | Host to widget | `{ theme }` | The host's theme changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1660":{"id":"/widgets-28","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"`FoundryWidget` from `@osdk/widget.client-react` sends `widget.ready`, `widget.resize`, and `widget.reload` for you and exposes the rest through a hook. See React widgets."},"1661":{"id":"/widgets-29","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package            | Use it for                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/widget.api` | The contract itself: message, manifest, and parameter value types, `BrowserPermission`, and `MANIFEST_FILE_LOCATION`. `@osdk/widget.client` re-exports the parts you need, so you rarely import it directly. |","table":"table-1"},"1662":{"id":"/widgets-30","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package               | Use it for                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/widget.client` | `defineConfig` for widget configs, `createFoundryWidgetClient` for widgets without React, and `createFoundryWidgetTokenProvider` for OSDK clients inside a widget. |","table":"table-1"},"1663":{"id":"/widgets-31","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package                     | Use it for                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/widget.client-react` | The `FoundryWidget` provider and the `useFoundryWidgetContext` hook. Supports React 18 and 19. |","table":"table-1"},"1664":{"id":"/widgets-32","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package                    | Use it for                                                                                               |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` | Generates the manifest during `vite build` and runs developer mode during `vite`. Supports Vite 6 and 7. |","table":"table-1"},"1665":{"id":"/widgets-33","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package               | Use it for                                                                      |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/create-widget` | A CLI that scaffolds a React widget set project with all of the above wired in. |","table":"table-1"},"1666":{"id":"/widgets-34","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package     | Use it for                                                                                                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/cli` | `osdk widgetset deploy` and `osdk widgetset version` for publishing and managing versions. See Build and publish. |","table":"table-1"},"1667":{"id":"/widgets-35","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"Before you start, you need:"},"1668":{"id":"/widgets-36","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"A widget set in Foundry and its RID, `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`."},"1669":{"id":"/widgets-37","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"A Foundry token in the `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` environment variable. Developer mode, `osdk widgetset deploy`, and installing your SDK package from Foundry's npm registry all read it."},"1670":{"id":"/widgets-38","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"To call the Ontology, the name of your widget set's SDK package, such as `@my-app/sdk`, and the URL of the npm registry that hosts it. The registry URL has the form `https://<stack>/artifacts/api/repositories/ri.artifacts.main.repository.<id>/contents/release/npm`."},"1671":{"id":"/widgets-39","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"`npm create @osdk/widget@latest` runs the same CLI. It prompts for each value you do not pass as a flag:"},"1672":{"id":"/widgets-40","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Flag                   | Accepted values                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Project name | positional `[project]` | Letters, digits, `-`, and `_`. Defaults to `my-osdk-widget`. |","table":"table-2"},"1673":{"id":"/widgets-41","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                            | Flag          | Accepted values                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Overwrite the existing directory? | `--overwrite` | Asked only if the directory exists. `--overwrite` removes its files; `--no-overwrite` keeps them and writes over matching paths. |","table":"table-2"},"1674":{"id":"/widgets-42","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt    | Flag         | Accepted values                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Framework | `--template` | `widget-react`, listed as **OSDK React**: React, Vite, and Blueprint. |","table":"table-2"},"1675":{"id":"/widgets-43","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Flag           | Accepted values                                                                                |\n| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| OSDK version | `--sdkVersion` | `2.x`, the only version the React template supports. Not prompted unless the value is invalid. |","table":"table-2"},"1676":{"id":"/widgets-44","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt      | Flag           | Accepted values                                                            |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry URL | `--foundryUrl` | Must start with `https://`, such as `https://example.palantirfoundry.com`. |","table":"table-2"},"1677":{"id":"/widgets-45","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                     | Flag         | Accepted values                                                                                              |\n| -------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Will you be using an OSDK? | `--skipOsdk` | Passing `--osdkPackage` or `--osdkRegistryUrl` answers yes. `--skipOsdk` answers no and conflicts with both. |","table":"table-2"},"1678":{"id":"/widgets-46","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt            | Flag            | Accepted values                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| OSDK package name | `--osdkPackage` | Must match `@<scope>/sdk`, such as `@my-app/sdk`. |","table":"table-2"},"1679":{"id":"/widgets-47","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Flag                | Accepted values                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| npm registry URL | `--osdkRegistryUrl` | The Foundry Artifacts URL ending in `/contents/release/npm`. |","table":"table-2"},"1680":{"id":"/widgets-48","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt         | Flag          | Accepted values                       |\n| -------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Widget set RID | `--widgetSet` | `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. |","table":"table-2"},"1681":{"id":"/widgets-49","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt | Flag           | Accepted values                                                                             |\n| ------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| None   | `--repository` | Optional code repository RID, written to `foundry.config.json` for `osdk widgetset deploy`. |","table":"table-2"},"1682":{"id":"/widgets-50","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"To skip every prompt:"},"1683":{"id":"/widgets-51","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#install-dependencies","content":"The generated `.npmrc` sends `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` to your Foundry npm registry, so a `401` or `404` for your SDK package means the token is missing, expired, or lacks access."},"1684":{"id":"/widgets-52","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#start-developer-mode","content":"The terminal prints a setup URL. Open it to load your local widgets in Foundry, as described in Run locally."},"1685":{"id":"/widgets-53","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\".gitignore\" />"},"1686":{"id":"/widgets-54","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"1687":{"id":"/widgets-55","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"README.md\" />"},"1688":{"id":"/widgets-56","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"eslint.config.mjs\" />"},"1689":{"id":"/widgets-57","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"1690":{"id":"/widgets-58","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1691":{"id":"/widgets-59","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"1692":{"id":"/widgets-60","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"tsconfig.json\" />"},"1693":{"id":"/widgets-61","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"tsconfig.node.json\" />"},"1694":{"id":"/widgets-62","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1695":{"id":"/widgets-63","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"1696":{"id":"/widgets-64","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.config.ts\" />"},"1697":{"id":"/widgets-65","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.css\" />"},"1698":{"id":"/widgets-66","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1699":{"id":"/widgets-67","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"useDarkTheme.ts\" />"},"1700":{"id":"/widgets-68","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"vite-env.d.ts\" />"},"1701":{"id":"/widgets-69","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"Widget.module.css\" />"},"1702":{"id":"/widgets-70","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"Widget.tsx\" />"},"1703":{"id":"/widgets-71","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json` | The Foundry URL and widget set settings that the Vite plugin and `osdk widgetset deploy` read. See Build and publish. |","table":"table-3"},"1704":{"id":"/widgets-72","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File     | Purpose                                                                                                                          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.npmrc` | Points your SDK package's scope at your Foundry registry and authenticates with `${FOUNDRY_TOKEN}`. Only generated with an OSDK. |","table":"table-3"},"1705":{"id":"/widgets-73","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite.config.ts` | Adds `@vitejs/plugin-react` and `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin`, serves on port 8080 with CORS enabled, and lists `./index.html` as the build input. |","table":"table-3"},"1706":{"id":"/widgets-74","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File         | Purpose                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `index.html` | The widget's entrypoint. It loads `/src/main.tsx`. |","table":"table-3"},"1707":{"id":"/widgets-75","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                 | Purpose                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.config.ts` | The widget config: ID `widgetId`, a `greetingName` string parameter, a `counterValue` number parameter, and a `setCounterValue` event. |","table":"table-3"},"1708":{"id":"/widgets-76","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.tsx` | Renders `Widget` inside `FoundryWidget`, and inside `OsdkProvider` when you use an OSDK. Importing `main.config.ts` here is what lets the Vite plugin find it. |","table":"table-3"},"1709":{"id":"/widgets-77","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File            | Purpose                                               |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/client.ts` | Creates the OSDK client. Only generated with an OSDK. |","table":"table-3"},"1710":{"id":"/widgets-78","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/Widget.tsx` | Reads both parameters, increments the counter every second by emitting `setCounterValue`, and renders a reset button. |","table":"table-3"},"1711":{"id":"/widgets-79","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/useDarkTheme.ts` | Tracks `prefers-color-scheme: dark` so the widget can apply Blueprint's dark theme. |","table":"table-3"},"1712":{"id":"/widgets-80","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"Without an OSDK, the CLI omits `.npmrc` and `src/client.ts`, and `package.json` drops `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/react`, and the SDK package."},"1713":{"id":"/widgets-81","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"The `package.json` scripts:"},"1714":{"id":"/widgets-82","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command | Description                               |\n| ------ | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `dev`  | `vite`  | Starts the dev server and developer mode. |","table":"table-4"},"1715":{"id":"/widgets-83","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script  | Command             | Description                                                                     |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build` | `tsc && vite build` | Typechecks, builds to `dist/`, and writes `dist/.palantir/widgets.config.json`. |","table":"table-4"},"1716":{"id":"/widgets-84","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command                                                        | Description        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `lint` | `eslint . --report-unused-disable-directives --max-warnings 0` | Lints the project. |","table":"table-4"},"1717":{"id":"/widgets-85","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command                        | Description |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `test` | `vitest run --passWithNoTests` | Runs tests. |","table":"table-4"},"1718":{"id":"/widgets-86","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script    | Command        | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `preview` | `vite preview` | Serves the production build locally. |","table":"table-4"},"1719":{"id":"/widgets-87","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-locally","content":"Developer mode loads widget code from your dev server into Foundry, so you can preview changes against real host data without deploying a version."},"1720":{"id":"/widgets-88","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#start-the-dev-server","content":"Export `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` and run `npm run dev`. The plugin stops with `FOUNDRY_TOKEN environment variable not found` if the variable is missing. Instead of the usual local URL, Vite prints:"},"1721":{"id":"/widgets-89","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"The setup page loads each HTML entrypoint so Vite parses its widget config, then builds a development manifest whose scripts point at your dev server. It sends that manifest for the widget set in `foundry.config.json` to Foundry, enables developer mode, and redirects you to the widget set's preview page at `<foundryUrl>/workspace/custom-widgets/preview/<widgetSetRid>`."},"1722":{"id":"/widgets-90","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"If a widget's config is never found, the page gives up after 10 attempts with `Timed out waiting for widget config files to be parsed. Are you sure a widget config is imported?`."},"1723":{"id":"/widgets-91","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"Component changes reach the embedded widget through Vite hot module replacement. A change to a widget config file does not: the terminal warns that the config changed, and you open the setup URL again to send the new parameters and events to Foundry."},"1724":{"id":"/widgets-92","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"You do not need to publish a widget set before developing on it. To place the widget in a Workshop module, publish a version once so the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. See Build and publish."},"1725":{"id":"/widgets-93","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"In Foundry Code Workspaces, run Vite in the `code-workspaces` mode instead:"},"1726":{"id":"/widgets-94","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"In this mode the plugin reads the Foundry URL from `FOUNDRY_PROXY_URL`, the token from the file named by `FOUNDRY_PROXY_TOKEN`, and the dev server address from `DEV_SERVER_DOMAIN` and `DEV_SERVER_BASE_PATH`, all set by the workspace. Open the preview panel to enter developer mode, and refresh it after you change a widget config. The plugin warns when you run `npm run dev` inside a workspace, or the `code-workspaces` mode outside one."},"1727":{"id":"/widgets-95","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"Inside Foundry, a widget authenticates through the host instead of OAuth. Create the client against the page origin with the widget token provider:"},"1728":{"id":"/widgets-96","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"`createFoundryWidgetTokenProvider` resolves to a placeholder that Foundry replaces with real credentials on each request. Pass the client to `FoundryWidget`, which needs it to resolve object set parameters, and to `OsdkProvider` so `@osdk/react` hooks work inside the widget:"},"1729":{"id":"/widgets-97","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"From there, query with the hooks in Query objects or read object sets the host passes in, as shown in React widgets. At build time, the Vite plugin also lists every package reachable through `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`) whose `package.json` has an `osdk.packageRid` field, with its version, in the manifest's `inputSpec`."},"1730":{"id":"/widgets-98","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"`createFoundryWidgetClient` from `@osdk/widget.client` speaks the same protocol without a framework. Outside a Foundry host or developer mode, it throws `Invariant failed: [FoundryWidgetClient] Missing __PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__ in window` (production builds show only `Invariant failed`)."},"1731":{"id":"/widgets-99","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member        | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subscribe()` | Starts forwarding host messages to `hostEventTarget`. Call it before `ready()`. |","table":"table-5"},"1732":{"id":"/widgets-100","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member          | Description                     |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `unsubscribe()` | Stops forwarding host messages. |","table":"table-5"},"1733":{"id":"/widgets-101","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member    | Description                                                        |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ready()` | Sends `widget.ready` so the host sends the first parameter values. |","table":"table-5"},"1734":{"id":"/widgets-102","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                                     | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emitEvent(eventId, { parameterUpdates })` | Sends `widget.emit-event`. Typed against the events in your config. |","table":"table-5"},"1735":{"id":"/widgets-103","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                      | Description            |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `resize({ width, height })` | Sends `widget.resize`. |","table":"table-5"},"1736":{"id":"/widgets-104","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member     | Description            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `reload()` | Sends `widget.reload`. |","table":"table-5"},"1737":{"id":"/widgets-105","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member            | Description            |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `hotkey(payload)` | Sends `widget.hotkey`. |","table":"table-5"},"1738":{"id":"/widgets-106","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                 | Description                                         |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessage(message)` | Sends any widget message. Prefer the methods above. |","table":"table-5"},"1739":{"id":"/widgets-107","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member            | Description                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `hostEventTarget` | An `EventTarget` that dispatches `host.update-parameters`, `host.set-hotkeys`, and `host.set-theme`, with the message payload in `event.detail`. |","table":"table-5"},"1740":{"id":"/widgets-108","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Every parameter type, event, permission, and how they map to the manifest."},"1741":{"id":"/widgets-109","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Read parameters, emit events, and handle loading states with `FoundryWidget`."},"1742":{"id":"/widgets-110","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Configure the Vite plugin, build the manifest, and deploy versions."},"1743":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"page","content":"Parameters and events","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events"},"1744":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-0","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","content":"Declare a widget's parameters, events, and browser permissions with defineConfig, and see how each field maps to the widgets.config.json manifest."},"1745":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-1","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"Define a config"},"1746":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-2","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"Config fields"},"1747":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-3","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Parameter types"},"1748":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-4","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"Loading states"},"1749":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-5","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"Events"},"1750":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-6","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"1751":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-7","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"How the config maps to the manifest"},"1752":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-8","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","content":"A widget config declares what the host can pass into your widget and what the widget can send back. Write one per widget with `defineConfig` from `@osdk/widget.client`. The config also types your React hooks, and the Vite plugin turns it into the manifest Foundry reads."},"1753":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-9","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"Export the config as the file's default export, name the file `*.config.ts` (or `.js`, `.tsx`, `.jsx`), and import it from the widget's entrypoint script. The Vite plugin finds configs through that import; see Build and publish."},"1754":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-10","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"`defineConfig` returns its argument unchanged. Its `const` type parameter keeps parameter IDs, types, and `parameterUpdateIds` as literal types, which is what lets `useFoundryWidgetContext` and `emitEvent` type-check against your config."},"1755":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-11","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field | Type     | Default  | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ----- | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | Required | Unique within the widget set. camelCase: letters and digits only, starting with a lowercase letter. At most 100 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1756":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-12","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field  | Type     | Default  | Description                                         |\n| ------ | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `name` | `string` | Required | The name shown in the host. At most 100 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1757":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-13","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field         | Type     | Default | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `description` | `string` |         | Shown in the host. At most 250 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1758":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-14","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field  | Type         | Default  | Description                                                  |\n| ------ | ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `\"workshop\"` | Required | The host the widget targets. `\"workshop\"` is the only value. |","table":"table-0"},"1759":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-15","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field        | Type                                  | Default  | Description                                                          |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `Record<string, ParameterDefinition>` | Required | Values the host passes in, keyed by parameter ID. Use `{}` for none. |","table":"table-0"},"1760":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-16","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field    | Type                              | Default  | Description                                                       |\n| -------- | --------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `events` | `Record<string, EventDefinition>` | Required | Events the widget can emit, keyed by event ID. Use `{}` for none. |","table":"table-0"},"1761":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-17","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field         | Type                  | Default | Description                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions` | `BrowserPermission[]` |         | Extra browser capabilities the widget requests. See Permissions. |","table":"table-0"},"1762":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-18","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field                     | Type      | Default                    | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | --------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refreshHostDataOnAction` | `boolean` | Plugin default, else unset | Asks the host to refresh the Ontology data it passes in, currently object set parameters, when the widget is thought to have applied an action through the Ontology APIs. |","table":"table-0"},"1763":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-19","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"TypeScript cannot check ID formats and lengths, so the Vite plugin validates them when it loads the config and fails the build or developer mode with messages such as `Widget id \"my-widget\" does not match allowed pattern (must be camelCase)`."},"1764":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-20","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Every parameter needs a `type` and a `displayName`, the label shown in the host's setup panel. Parameter IDs follow the same camelCase rule and 100-character limit as widget IDs."},"1765":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-21","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`     | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ---------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"string\"` |              | `string`            |       |","table":"table-1"},"1766":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-22","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`     | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ---------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"number\"` |              | `number`            |       |","table":"table-1"},"1767":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-23","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`      | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ----------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"boolean\"` |              | `boolean`           |       |","table":"table-1"},"1768":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-24","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`   | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes                      |\n| -------- | ------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `\"date\"` |              | `string`            | An ISO date, `YYYY-MM-DD`. |","table":"table-1"},"1769":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-25","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`        | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes            |\n| ------------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `\"timestamp\"` |              | `string`            | An ISO datetime. |","table":"table-1"},"1770":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-26","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`       | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes           |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ------------------- | --------------- |\n| `\"scenario\"` |              | `string`            | A Scenario RID. |","table":"table-1"},"1771":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-27","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`    | Extra fields | Value in the widget             | Notes                                    |\n| --------- | ------------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `\"array\"` | `subType`    | An array of the `subType` value | `subType` is any of the six types above. |","table":"table-1"},"1772":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-28","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`        | Extra fields  | Value in the widget        | Notes                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"objectSet\"` | `allowedType` | `{ objectSetRid: string }` | `allowedType` is an object type or interface from your generated SDK, such as `Employee` or `Worker`. In React, the value also carries a hydrated `objectSet`; see React widgets. |","table":"table-1"},"1773":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-29","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`           | Extra fields | Value in the widget        | Notes                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------------ | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"mapTileLayer\"` |              | `{ tileSourceId: string }` | Read-only: a tile source ID for the Foundry Tiles APIs. Events cannot update it. |","table":"table-1"},"1774":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-30","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"An `objectSet` parameter needs the RID that generated SDKs embed in each type definition. If it is missing, the plugin fails with `ObjectSet parameter \"employees\" must have a valid rid in its metadata, make sure your OSDK was generated with a generator version >=2.6.2`. The older `objectType` field is deprecated; use `allowedType`."},"1775":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-31","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Dates and timestamps stay strings. Parse them with the date library your widget already uses."},"1776":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-32","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"The host sends each parameter as an async value, so your widget can show what is still loading. The `type` field moves through these states:"},"1777":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-33","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`          | `value` | `error` | Meaning                                     |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"not-started\"` |         |         | The host has not started loading the value. |","table":"table-2"},"1778":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-34","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`      | `value` | `error` | Meaning                        |\n| ----------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `\"loading\"` |         |         | The first load is in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"1779":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-35","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`     | `value`                   | `error` | Meaning                                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"loaded\"` | The value, or `undefined` |         | The value is ready. `undefined` means the host variable has no value. |","table":"table-2"},"1780":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-36","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`        | `value`            | `error` | Meaning                 |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| `\"reloading\"` | The previous value |         | A new value is loading. |","table":"table-2"},"1781":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-37","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`     | `value`                | `error` | Meaning         |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| `\"failed\"` | The last value, if any | `Error` | Loading failed. |","table":"table-2"},"1782":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-38","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"The types are exported from `@osdk/widget.client` as `AsyncValue`, `AsyncLoadedValue`, `AsyncFailedValue`, and so on. React widgets covers how `FoundryWidget` combines them."},"1783":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-39","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"An event tells the host to update one or more of the widget's parameters. Declare each event with a label and the parameters it updates:"},"1784":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-40","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | The event name shown in the host, where builders attach behavior to it. |","table":"table-3"},"1785":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-41","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"| Field                | Type       | Description                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterUpdateIds` | `string[]` | The parameter IDs the event sets. Each must be a parameter in the same config, and none can be a `mapTileLayer` parameter. |","table":"table-3"},"1786":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-42","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"When you emit the event, `parameterUpdates` must contain a value for every ID in `parameterUpdateIds`, typed like the parameter's value:"},"1787":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-43","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"To fire an event without updating anything, set `parameterUpdateIds: []` and emit `parameterUpdates: {}`. Listing a `mapTileLayer` parameter is a type error, and the plugin rejects it with `Event \"selectTile\" cannot update read-only map tile layer parameter \"tiles\"`."},"1788":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-44","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"A widget runs in a sandboxed frame. Request extra capabilities with `permissions`:"},"1789":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-45","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value      | Requests                         |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"camera\"` | The `camera` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1790":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-46","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value          | Requests                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `\"microphone\"` | The `microphone` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1791":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-47","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value        | Requests                           |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `\"autoplay\"` | The `autoplay` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1792":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-48","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value               | Requests                            |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-downloads\"` | The `allow-downloads` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1793":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-49","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value           | Requests                        |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-forms\"` | The `allow-forms` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1794":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-50","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value            | Requests                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-modals\"` | The `allow-modals` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1795":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-51","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value            | Requests                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-popups\"` | The `allow-popups` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1796":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-52","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"The same values are available as constants on `BrowserPermission` from `@osdk/widget.api`, such as `BrowserPermission.CAMERA`. A request does not guarantee access: the user may still need to accept a browser prompt, depending on the permission and browser settings."},"1797":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-53","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"`vite build` writes one manifest per widget set to `.palantir/widgets.config.json` in the build output. Each widget's config becomes an entry under `widgetSet.widgets`, keyed by widget ID. For the config at the top of this page, the manifest looks like this:"},"1798":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-54","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field  | Source                                    |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.rid` | `widgetSet.rid` in `foundry.config.json`. |","table":"table-5"},"1799":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-55","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field      | Source                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.version` | `widgetSet.autoVersion` in `foundry.config.json`; by default the `version` in `package.json`. See Versioning. |","table":"table-5"},"1800":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-56","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgets.<id>` | One entry per HTML entrypoint, keyed by the config's `id`. Two widgets with the same ID fail the build with `Duplicate widget ID`. |","table":"table-5"},"1801":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-57","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                                       | Source                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `id`, `name`, `description`, `events`, `permissions` | Copied from the config. |","table":"table-5"},"1802":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-58","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                     |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `type`         | `\"workshop\"` becomes `\"workshopWidgetV1\"`. |","table":"table-5"},"1803":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-59","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                  | Source                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entrypointJs`, `entrypointCss` | The script and stylesheet tags in the built HTML file, in order, with the leading `/` removed. |","table":"table-5"},"1804":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-60","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                                                                                                                                          |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters`   | Copied from the config, except `objectSet`: `allowedType` becomes the type's RID, and `objectTypeRids` holds the object type RID, or is empty for an interface. |","table":"table-5"},"1805":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-61","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field            | Source                                                                    |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refreshHostDataOnAction` | The config's value, else the plugin's `defaults.refreshHostDataOnAction`. |","table":"table-5"},"1806":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-62","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field              | Source                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `inputSpec.discovered.sdks` | The `rid` and `version` of every package reachable through `dependencies` whose `package.json` has an `osdk.packageRid`. |","table":"table-5"},"1807":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-63","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                        | Source                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inputSpec.discovered.authorizations` | `authorizations.read` and `authorizations.requiredRead` from `resources.json` in the project root, when that file exists. |","table":"table-5"},"1808":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-64","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"Fields without a value, such as an unset `permissions`, are left out of the JSON. In developer mode the plugin sends Foundry the same widget entries, but with `entrypointJs` pointing at your dev server."},"1809":{"id":"/widgets/publish","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"page","content":"Build and publish","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish"},"1810":{"id":"/widgets/publish-0","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish","content":"Configure @osdk/widget.vite-plugin, build a widget set and its manifest, deploy versions with osdk widgetset deploy, and manage them."},"1811":{"id":"/widgets/publish-1","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"Add the Vite plugin"},"1812":{"id":"/widgets/publish-2","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"How the plugin finds configs"},"1813":{"id":"/widgets/publish-3","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Build multiple widgets"},"1814":{"id":"/widgets/publish-4","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Build"},"1815":{"id":"/widgets/publish-5","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"`foundry.config.json`"},"1816":{"id":"/widgets/publish-6","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"Versioning"},"1817":{"id":"/widgets/publish-7","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#deploy","content":"Deploy"},"1818":{"id":"/widgets/publish-8","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build-1","content":"Build"},"1819":{"id":"/widgets/publish-9","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Deploy"},"1820":{"id":"/widgets/publish-10","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"Manage versions"},"1821":{"id":"/widgets/publish-11","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish","content":"Publishing a widget set takes two commands: `vite build` produces your widget files and a manifest, and `osdk widgetset deploy` uploads them to Foundry as a new version. This page covers the Vite plugin, `foundry.config.json`, versioning, and the CLI."},"1822":{"id":"/widgets/publish-12","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"`@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` writes the manifest during `vite build` and runs developer mode during `vite`. Projects from `@osdk/create-widget` already include it."},"1823":{"id":"/widgets/publish-13","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"The plugin supports Vite 6 and 7. It takes one optional argument:"},"1824":{"id":"/widgets/publish-14","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"| Option                             | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaults.refreshHostDataOnAction` | `boolean` |         | The `refreshHostDataOnAction` value for every widget whose config does not set it. See Config fields. |","table":"table-0"},"1825":{"id":"/widgets/publish-15","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"Each HTML file in `build.rollupOptions.input` is one widget. For each one, the plugin looks for a widget config among the modules its entry script imports:"},"1826":{"id":"/widgets/publish-16","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The file name, minus its extension, ends in `.config`, such as `main.config.ts`."},"1827":{"id":"/widgets/publish-17","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The file lives under `src/` and the entrypoint script imports it directly. Developer mode only tracks direct imports."},"1828":{"id":"/widgets/publish-18","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The default export is the config from `defineConfig`."},"1829":{"id":"/widgets/publish-19","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"If you do not need the config object at runtime, a side-effect import such as `import \"./main.config.js\";` is enough. Each entrypoint must import exactly one config."},"1830":{"id":"/widgets/publish-20","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Add an HTML file per widget, each loading its own script that imports its own config:"},"1831":{"id":"/widgets/publish-21","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1832":{"id":"/widgets/publish-22","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.html\" />"},"1833":{"id":"/widgets/publish-23","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1834":{"id":"/widgets/publish-24","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1835":{"id":"/widgets/publish-25","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"main.config.ts\" />"},"1836":{"id":"/widgets/publish-26","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.tsx\" />"},"1837":{"id":"/widgets/publish-27","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.config.ts\" />"},"1838":{"id":"/widgets/publish-28","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Then list every HTML file as a build input. Both the array and object forms of `input` work:"},"1839":{"id":"/widgets/publish-29","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"The build writes one manifest with an entry per widget, keyed by each config's `id`, so every widget in the set needs a different ID."},"1840":{"id":"/widgets/publish-30","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"The template's `build` script runs `tsc && vite build`. Vite writes your HTML, scripts, and styles to its output directory, `dist/` by default, and the plugin then adds the manifest:"},"1841":{"id":"/widgets/publish-31","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1842":{"id":"/widgets/publish-32","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index-[hash].js\" />"},"1843":{"id":"/widgets/publish-33","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index-[hash].css\" />"},"1844":{"id":"/widgets/publish-34","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"widgets.config.json\" />"},"1845":{"id":"/widgets/publish-35","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"To write the manifest, the plugin reads each built HTML file for its script and stylesheet tags, evaluates each widget config in a separate Vite server, computes the version, and scans `package.json` dependencies for SDK packages. Parameters and events shows the result field by field."},"1846":{"id":"/widgets/publish-36","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Build errors from the plugin:"},"1847":{"id":"/widgets/publish-37","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                 | Cause                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json file not found.` | No `foundry.config.json` in the working directory or any parent. |","table":"table-1"},"1848":{"id":"/widgets/publish-38","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                             | Cause                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `No widget config files found for entrypoint ...` | The entrypoint does not import a `*.config` module. |","table":"table-1"},"1849":{"id":"/widgets/publish-39","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                   | Cause                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Multiple widget config files found for entrypoint ...` | The entrypoint's bundle includes more than one `*.config` module. |","table":"table-1"},"1850":{"id":"/widgets/publish-40","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                            | Cause                                  |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `No default export found in ...` | The config file has no default export. |","table":"table-1"},"1851":{"id":"/widgets/publish-41","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                      | Cause                      |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `Duplicate widget ID: ...` | Two configs share an `id`. |","table":"table-1"},"1852":{"id":"/widgets/publish-42","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                                             | Cause                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Foundry serves widget files from the root path, so Vite's base must be \"/\". ...` | Vite's `base` is set to anything other than `/`, such as `./` or `/widgets/`. Remove `base` or set it to `/`. Developer mode is not affected. |","table":"table-1"},"1853":{"id":"/widgets/publish-43","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                            | Cause                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Entrypoint chunk not found for input file: ...` | The built HTML's script paths do not match a bundle entry chunk, for example when an entry `<script>` points outside the bundle. |","table":"table-1"},"1854":{"id":"/widgets/publish-44","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                 | Cause                                                                                      |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `Unexpected inline content found in Vite HTML output` | The built HTML has an inline `<script>` or `<link>` with content. Load scripts with `src`. |","table":"table-1"},"1855":{"id":"/widgets/publish-45","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                | Cause                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Unexpected ... attribute found in Vite HTML output` | A `<script>` has attributes other than `src`, `type`, and `crossorigin`, or a stylesheet `<link>` has attributes other than `rel`, `href`, and `crossorigin`. |","table":"table-1"},"1856":{"id":"/widgets/publish-46","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                          | Cause                                                         |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Invalid script type attribute found in Vite HTML output: ...` | A `<script>` `type` other than `module` or `text/javascript`. |","table":"table-1"},"1857":{"id":"/widgets/publish-47","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                             | Cause                                                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `The version string ... is not SemVer compliant.` | The computed version is not valid SemVer. See Versioning. |","table":"table-1"},"1858":{"id":"/widgets/publish-48","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Config validation errors, such as a widget ID that is not camelCase, are listed in Parameters and events."},"1859":{"id":"/widgets/publish-49","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"The plugin and `osdk widgetset` commands read `foundry.config.json` from the working directory or the nearest parent. `@osdk/create-widget` writes it for you:"},"1860":{"id":"/widgets/publish-50","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field        | Type     | Default  | Description                                                        |\n| ------------ | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `foundryUrl` | `string` | Required | Your Foundry stack. Developer mode and the CLI send requests here. |","table":"table-2"},"1861":{"id":"/widgets/publish-51","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field           | Type     | Default  | Description                                                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.rid` | `string` | Required | The widget set RID, written to the manifest and used as the deploy target. |","table":"table-2"},"1862":{"id":"/widgets/publish-52","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                 | Type     | Default  | Description                                              |\n| --------------------- | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.directory` | `string` | Required | The build output to deploy. Match Vite's `build.outDir`. |","table":"table-2"},"1863":{"id":"/widgets/publish-53","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                  | Type     | Default | Description                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.repository` | `string` |         | A code repository RID to publish through instead of the widget set. See Deploy. |","table":"table-2"},"1864":{"id":"/widgets/publish-54","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                   | Type                                                                         | Default        | Description                         |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.autoVersion` | `{ type: \"package-json\" }` or `{ type: \"git-describe\", tagPrefix?: string }` | `package-json` | How the build computes the version. |","table":"table-2"},"1865":{"id":"/widgets/publish-55","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"The file is validated on load. Unknown top-level fields fail with `does not match the expected schema`."},"1866":{"id":"/widgets/publish-56","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"Every deployed version needs a SemVer version string. The build computes it once and writes it to the manifest's `widgetSet.version`; `osdk widgetset deploy` reads it from there and has no version flag."},"1867":{"id":"/widgets/publish-57","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"The default. The version is the `version` field of the nearest `package.json`. Bump it, then rebuild before you deploy:"},"1868":{"id":"/widgets/publish-58","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"The version comes from `git describe --tags --first-parent --dirty`:"},"1869":{"id":"/widgets/publish-59","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"With an empty `tagPrefix`, the build uses the most recent tag reachable from `HEAD` and strips a leading `v`, so `v1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. With a prefix such as `widgets/`, it only matches tags that start with the prefix and strips it, so `widgets/1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. Commits after the tag and uncommitted changes add a suffix such as `1.4.0-3-g1a2b3c4-dirty`. The build fails if git is missing, the directory is not a repository, or no tag matches."},"1870":{"id":"/widgets/publish-60","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy","content":"`osdk widgetset deploy` from `@osdk/cli` zips the build output and publishes it as a new version."},"1871":{"id":"/widgets/publish-61","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"The CLI reads the version from `.palantir/widgets.config.json` in the directory, zips everything in the directory, and uploads it. When `repository` is set, it uploads to that code repository on behalf of the widget set, which works only if the repository is authorized to publish the widget set. It passes the current git branch along, unless HEAD is detached or the project is not a git repository."},"1872":{"id":"/widgets/publish-62","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Every option defaults to the matching `foundry.config.json` field where one exists:"},"1873":{"id":"/widgets/publish-63","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default         | Description         |\n| ------------- | --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `--widgetSet` | `widgetSet.rid` | The widget set RID. |","table":"table-3"},"1874":{"id":"/widgets/publish-64","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default      | Description                                  |\n| -------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `foundryUrl` | The Foundry URL. Must start with `https://`. |","table":"table-3"},"1875":{"id":"/widgets/publish-65","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default               | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--directory` | `widgetSet.directory` | The directory to upload. It must contain `.palantir/widgets.config.json`. |","table":"table-3"},"1876":{"id":"/widgets/publish-66","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default                | Description                               |\n| -------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--repository` | `widgetSet.repository` | A code repository RID to publish through. |","table":"table-3"},"1877":{"id":"/widgets/publish-67","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default                | Description                 |\n| -------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `--branchName` | The current git branch | The branch to publish from. |","table":"table-3"},"1878":{"id":"/widgets/publish-68","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option    | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--token` |         | A Foundry token. Conflicts with `--tokenFile`. |","table":"table-3"},"1879":{"id":"/widgets/publish-69","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default | Description                        |\n| ------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `--tokenFile` |         | A file containing a Foundry token. |","table":"table-3"},"1880":{"id":"/widgets/publish-70","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option            | Default | Description                       |\n| ----------------- | ------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `--verbose`, `-v` |         | Verbose logging. Repeat for more. |","table":"table-3"},"1881":{"id":"/widgets/publish-71","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Without `--token` or `--tokenFile`, the CLI reads `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`. The deprecated `FOUNDRY_SDK_AUTH_TOKEN` still works with a warning. The token must be a JWT."},"1882":{"id":"/widgets/publish-72","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"After the first version is published, the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. Until then you can still preview it with developer mode."},"1883":{"id":"/widgets/publish-73","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"The same options select the widget set and credentials:"},"1884":{"id":"/widgets/publish-74","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version list` | Lists published versions, newest first, for the current git branch or `--branchName`. |","table":"table-4"},"1885":{"id":"/widgets/publish-75","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                                 | Description                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `osdk widgetset version info <version>` | Prints the details of one version as JSON. |","table":"table-4"},"1886":{"id":"/widgets/publish-76","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                                   | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version delete <version>` | Deletes a version after a confirmation prompt. `--yes` or `-y` skips the prompt. Deletion cannot be undone. |","table":"table-4"},"1887":{"id":"/widgets/react","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"page","content":"React widgets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react"},"1888":{"id":"/widgets/react-0","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react","content":"Render a widget with FoundryWidget, read typed parameters and loading states with useFoundryWidgetContext, and emit events back to the host."},"1889":{"id":"/widgets/react-1","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"Install"},"1890":{"id":"/widgets/react-2","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Render `FoundryWidget`"},"1891":{"id":"/widgets/react-3","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"Read parameters"},"1892":{"id":"/widgets/react-4","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"Loading states"},"1893":{"id":"/widgets/react-5","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"Emit events"},"1894":{"id":"/widgets/react-6","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Object set parameters"},"1895":{"id":"/widgets/react-7","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#listen-to-host-messages","content":"Listen to host messages"},"1896":{"id":"/widgets/react-8","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"Render outside Foundry"},"1897":{"id":"/widgets/react-9","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react","content":"`@osdk/widget.client-react` connects a React tree to the Foundry host. `FoundryWidget` handles the message protocol, and `useFoundryWidgetContext` gives every component typed parameter values and an `emitEvent` function derived from your widget config."},"1898":{"id":"/widgets/react-10","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"Projects from `@osdk/create-widget` already include these packages. To add them to an existing Vite and React project:"},"1899":{"id":"/widgets/react-11","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"`@osdk/widget.client-react` supports React 18 and 19 and lists `@osdk/client` as a peer dependency. Add `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/react`, and your SDK package to call the Ontology."},"1900":{"id":"/widgets/react-12","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Wrap the widget's root in `FoundryWidget` and pass its config. Importing the config in the entrypoint is also what lets the Vite plugin find it."},"1901":{"id":"/widgets/react-13","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop     | Type                              | Default  | Description                                                                     |\n| -------- | --------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `config` | The return type of `defineConfig` | Required | The widget config. Every parameter and event type in the context comes from it. |","table":"table-0"},"1902":{"id":"/widgets/react-14","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop       | Type              | Default  | Description |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `children` | `React.ReactNode` | Required | The widget. |","table":"table-0"},"1903":{"id":"/widgets/react-15","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop     | Type                         | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `Client` from `@osdk/client` |         | An OSDK client, used to hydrate object set parameters and to serialize object sets you emit. Required by the types when the config has an `objectSet` parameter. |","table":"table-0"},"1904":{"id":"/widgets/react-16","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop            | Type                         | Default                       | Description                                                                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `initialValues` | Async value per parameter ID | Every parameter `not-started` | Starting values for `asyncParameterValues` before the host's first update. |","table":"table-0"},"1905":{"id":"/widgets/react-17","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"On mount, `FoundryWidget`:"},"1906":{"id":"/widgets/react-18","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Subscribes to host messages and sends `widget.ready`, so the host sends the first parameter values."},"1907":{"id":"/widgets/react-19","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Observes the size of `document.body` and sends `widget.resize` with its border-box width and height on every change."},"1908":{"id":"/widgets/react-20","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Sends `widget.reload` before a Vite full-page reload in development."},"1909":{"id":"/widgets/react-21","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Wraps `children` in an error boundary. An uncaught render error shows its stack trace, plus troubleshooting tips when `NODE_ENV` is not `production`. Add your own error boundary inside `FoundryWidget` to show a custom message instead."},"1910":{"id":"/widgets/react-22","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Render one `FoundryWidget` per widget, at the root. It creates the widget client once, when it mounts."},"1911":{"id":"/widgets/react-23","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"`useFoundryWidgetContext` returns the context for the nearest `FoundryWidget`. The context is not generic at runtime, so bind your config's type once with `withTypes` and import that hook everywhere:"},"1912":{"id":"/widgets/react-24","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"`useFoundryWidgetContext<typeof MainConfig>()` is equivalent. Outside a `FoundryWidget`, the hook returns a default context; see Render outside Foundry."},"1913":{"id":"/widgets/react-25","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field               | Type                                 | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `parameters.values` | Each parameter's value, all optional | The latest values, typed from the config: `headerText` is `string \\| undefined`, `todoItems` is `string[] \\| undefined`. |","table":"table-1"},"1914":{"id":"/widgets/react-26","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field              | Type                                                                | Description                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `parameters.state` | `\"not-started\" \\| \"loading\" \\| \"loaded\" \\| \"reloading\" \\| \"failed\"` | One loading state for the widget's parameters. See Loading states. |","table":"table-1"},"1915":{"id":"/widgets/react-27","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field                  | Type                                                                  | Description                                                                             |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `asyncParameterValues` | Per parameter ID: `{ type, value }`, where `value` is an `AsyncValue` | The individual state of each parameter, for widgets that load parameters independently. |","table":"table-1"},"1916":{"id":"/widgets/react-28","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field       | Type                                      | Description                                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emitEvent` | `(eventId, { parameterUpdates }) => void` | Sends one of the config's events. See Emit events. |","table":"table-1"},"1917":{"id":"/widgets/react-29","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field             | Type                     | Description                                                   |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hostEventTarget` | `FoundryHostEventTarget` | The raw stream of host messages. See Listen to host messages. |","table":"table-1"},"1918":{"id":"/widgets/react-30","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"`parameters.state` summarizes the parameters in the host's most recent update, in this order of precedence:"},"1919":{"id":"/widgets/react-31","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State      | When                                                                        |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"failed\"` | Any parameter failed. `parameters.values` keeps the values that did arrive. |","table":"table-2"},"1920":{"id":"/widgets/react-32","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State       | When                                         |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"loading\"` | Any parameter is loading for the first time. |","table":"table-2"},"1921":{"id":"/widgets/react-33","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State         | When                                                             |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"reloading\"` | Any parameter is reloading. Values keep their previous contents. |","table":"table-2"},"1922":{"id":"/widgets/react-34","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State           | When                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `\"not-started\"` | Any parameter has not started loading. |","table":"table-2"},"1923":{"id":"/widgets/react-35","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State      | When                    |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- |\n| `\"loaded\"` | Every parameter loaded. |","table":"table-2"},"1924":{"id":"/widgets/react-36","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"While the state is `not-started` or `loading`, `parameters.values` is `{}`, so give every read a fallback and keep rendering. Show progress next to the content instead of replacing it:"},"1925":{"id":"/widgets/react-37","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"To react to one parameter without waiting on the others, read `asyncParameterValues`:"},"1926":{"id":"/widgets/react-38","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"`emitEvent(eventId, { parameterUpdates })` sends a `widget.emit-event` message. TypeScript limits `eventId` to the config's events and requires a value for every ID in the event's `parameterUpdateIds`. The call returns nothing and does not report whether the host acted on the event."},"1927":{"id":"/widgets/react-39","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"In the example above, `handleAdd` emits `updateTodoItems` with the new list. The widget does not keep its own copy: when the host writes the update to the variable bound to `todoItems`, the new list arrives through `parameters.values` and the widget re-renders. The template's counter works the same way, reading `counterValue` and emitting `setCounterValue` with the next number."},"1928":{"id":"/widgets/react-40","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"For an `objectSet` parameter, the host sends an object set RID. Pass an OSDK `client` to `FoundryWidget`, and the value in `parameters.values` gains an `objectSet` you can query, typed by the parameter's `allowedType`."},"1929":{"id":"/widgets/react-41","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Query the set with `useObjectSet` from `@osdk/react`. Hydrated object sets are cached per parameter, so the `objectSet` reference only changes when the host sends a new RID, and it is safe to pass straight to hooks. To emit an object set, pass an `ObjectSet` from `@osdk/client`:"},"1930":{"id":"/widgets/react-42","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"`emitEvent` turns each `ObjectSet` into a temporary object set RID with an extra request before it sends the event. Because of that step:"},"1931":{"id":"/widgets/react-43","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"If you emit the same event again before the request finishes, only the last call is sent."},"1932":{"id":"/widgets/react-44","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Errors, such as a failed request, are not reported to the caller."},"1933":{"id":"/widgets/react-45","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Emitting an object set without a `client` on `FoundryWidget` fails, and so does receiving one."},"1934":{"id":"/widgets/react-46","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"See Work with object sets for filtering, pivoting, and combining the sets you receive."},"1935":{"id":"/widgets/react-47","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#listen-to-host-messages","content":"`hostEventTarget` dispatches every `host.update-parameters` message, with the raw payload in `event.detail`. Use it to log or react to updates beyond what `parameters` exposes:"},"1936":{"id":"/widgets/react-48","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"`FoundryWidget` needs the host API that Foundry injects. Outside Foundry and developer mode, it throws `Invariant failed: [FoundryWidgetClient] Missing __PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__ in window` when it renders (production builds show only `Invariant failed`)."},"1937":{"id":"/widgets/react-49","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"Components below it still render on their own: without a `FoundryWidget` ancestor, `useFoundryWidgetContext` returns a default context whose `parameters.state` is `not-started`, whose `parameters.values` is `{}`, and whose `emitEvent` does nothing. Because widget components already handle empty values, you can render them directly in unit tests and Storybook."},"1938":{"id":"/widgets/react-50","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"To start `asyncParameterValues` in a known state before the host's first update, pass `initialValues` to `FoundryWidget`. It does not affect `parameters.values` or `parameters.state`, which stay `{}` and `not-started` until the first `host.update-parameters` message."},"1939":{"id":"/ai/agents","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"page","content":"Agents","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents"},"1940":{"id":"/ai/agents-0","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"Converse with AIP Agents through the Platform SDK, start sessions for agents in your generated SDK, and read injected clients with @osdk/agents."},"1941":{"id":"/ai/agents-1","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"Chat with an AIP Agent"},"1942":{"id":"/ai/agents-2","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"Send a message"},"1943":{"id":"/ai/agents-3","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"Stream the answer"},"1944":{"id":"/ai/agents-4","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"Start a session for a generated agent"},"1945":{"id":"/ai/agents-5","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"Send events and read state"},"1946":{"id":"/ai/agents-6","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"Reach the clients from agent code"},"1947":{"id":"/ai/agents-7","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"An agent is configured in Foundry and runs its own model calls, tools, and retrieval; your app sends it input and reads its answers. Use this page to call an AIP Agent built in AIP Agent Studio, to start a session for an agent included in your generated SDK, or to reach the OSDK clients from code inside an agent."},"1948":{"id":"/ai/agents-8","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"Every API on this page is pre-release. The AIP Agents platform endpoints are marked beta, the generated-SDK session method is `experimental_createSession`, the Agents session endpoints are marked alpha, and `@osdk/agents` is at version 0.x with its client helpers under `/experimental`."},"1949":{"id":"/ai/agents-9","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                  | Use                                       |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Chat with an agent built in AIP Agent Studio | `Sessions` from `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` |","table":"table-0"},"1950":{"id":"/ai/agents-10","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                             | Use                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Start a session for an agent your generated SDK exports | `client(agent).experimental_createSession()` from `@osdk/client` |","table":"table-0"},"1951":{"id":"/ai/agents-11","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                           | Use                                            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Call the Ontology from code that runs inside an agent | `getClient()` from `@osdk/agents/experimental` |","table":"table-0"},"1952":{"id":"/ai/agents-12","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                           | Use                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Chat with a language model directly, without an agent | `generateText` or `useChat` |","table":"table-0"},"1953":{"id":"/ai/agents-13","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"The `AipAgentChat` component chats with a language model, not with an AIP Agent."},"1954":{"id":"/ai/agents-14","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"`@osdk/foundry.aipagents` is the Platform SDK package for AIP Agents. It works with the `Client` from `createClient` or a `PlatformClient`; see Platform SDK setup."},"1955":{"id":"/ai/agents-15","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                               | Required scope         | Description                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.create(client, agentRid, { agentVersion? })` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Starts a session. Omit `agentVersion` for the latest published version. |","table":"table-1"},"1956":{"id":"/ai/agents-16","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                        | Required scope         | Description                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.blockingContinue(client, agentRid, sessionRid, body)` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Sends a message and resolves with the full answer. |","table":"table-1"},"1957":{"id":"/ai/agents-17","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                         | Required scope         | Description                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.streamingContinue(client, agentRid, sessionRid, body)` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Sends a message and resolves with a `Response` whose body streams the answer as Markdown text. |","table":"table-1"},"1958":{"id":"/ai/agents-18","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                                  | Required scope         | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.cancel(client, agentRid, sessionRid, { messageId, response? })` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Cancels a streamed exchange, optionally replacing the answer. |","table":"table-1"},"1959":{"id":"/ai/agents-19","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                                        | Required scope        | Description                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.list(client, agentRid)`, `Sessions.get(client, agentRid, sessionRid)` | `api:aip-agents-read` | Reads sessions this client created. |","table":"table-1"},"1960":{"id":"/ai/agents-20","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"Each function takes query parameters as its last argument. Pass `{ preview: true }` while the endpoints are in beta. Find the agent RID in AIP Agent Studio."},"1961":{"id":"/ai/agents-21","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field | Type               | Description         |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `userInput`   | `{ text: string }` | The user's message. |","table":"table-2"},"1962":{"id":"/ai/agents-22","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field     | Type                             | Description                                                             |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterInputs` | `Record<string, ParameterValue>` | Values for the agent's application variables. Pass `{}` if it has none. |","table":"table-2"},"1963":{"id":"/ai/agents-23","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field      | Type                  | Description                                                     |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contextsOverride` | `Array<InputContext>` | Replaces the context the agent would retrieve for this message. |","table":"table-2"},"1964":{"id":"/ai/agents-24","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messageId`   | `string` | Streaming only. An id you choose, so you can cancel the exchange. |","table":"table-2"},"1965":{"id":"/ai/agents-25","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field    | Type     | Description                      |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `sessionTraceId` | `string` | An id for tracing this exchange. |","table":"table-2"},"1966":{"id":"/ai/agents-26","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"`blockingContinue` resolves with `agentMarkdownResponse`, `parameterUpdates`, `totalTokensUsed`, `interruptedOutput`, and `sessionTraceId`."},"1967":{"id":"/ai/agents-27","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"`streamingContinue` resolves with a `Response`. Read its body as text:"},"1968":{"id":"/ai/agents-28","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"A session handles one exchange at a time: wait for the answer, or cancel it with `Sessions.cancel` and the same `messageId`, before sending the next message. Cancelling does not close the stream, so also stop reading it."},"1969":{"id":"/ai/agents-29","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"When your generated SDK includes agents, it exports each one alongside your object types, and all of them as `$Agents`. Pass one to the client and call `experimental_createSession` with the agent's arguments:"},"1970":{"id":"/ai/agents-30","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior  | Details                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Arguments | A record keyed by argument name. OSDK objects and object sets are converted to the agent's argument types, including nested values. Omit the argument for agents that take none. |","table":"table-3"},"1971":{"id":"/ai/agents-31","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior     | Details                                                                                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Return value | An `AgentSession` with the session's `id`, `experimental_sendEvent`, and `experimental_getState`. |","table":"table-3"},"1972":{"id":"/ai/agents-32","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior | Details                                                                                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Version  | The version pinned in your generated SDK. Override it with `client({ ...employeeAssistant, version: \"2.0.0\" })`. |","table":"table-3"},"1973":{"id":"/ai/agents-33","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior            | Details                                                                       |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Unsupported clients | Throws before sending a request on branch, scenario, and transaction clients. |","table":"table-3"},"1974":{"id":"/ai/agents-34","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior | Details                                                                                      |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Scopes   | Loads the agent definition (`api:agents-read`) and creates the session (`api:agents-write`). |","table":"table-3"},"1975":{"id":"/ai/agents-35","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"Creating a session runs agent logic and can modify platform data."},"1976":{"id":"/ai/agents-36","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"Use the session that `experimental_createSession` returns, or reopen one by ID with `experimental_getSession`. `experimental_sendEvent` retries until the session accepts the event, and `experimental_getState` waits until the state reflects your last event."},"1977":{"id":"/ai/agents-37","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Method                               | Description                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `experimental_getSession(sessionId)` | Opens an existing session. Throws if it belongs to a different agent or Ontology. |","table":"table-4"},"1978":{"id":"/ai/agents-38","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Method                                    | Description                                                                          |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `experimental_sendEvent(event, options?)` | Sends one event, keyed by its event type. Generated agents type the key and payload. |","table":"table-4"},"1979":{"id":"/ai/agents-39","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Method                            | Description                                                                                                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `experimental_getState(options?)` | Resolves to the session's `status` (`\"live\"`, `\"completed\"`, `\"failed\"`, or `\"canceled\"`), `arguments`, `agentState`, and context items. |","table":"table-4"},"1980":{"id":"/ai/agents-40","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"Both methods take `$timeoutMs` (default 30 seconds) and `$pollIntervalMs` (default 1 second), and throw `AgentSendEventTimeoutError` or `AgentGetStateTimeoutError` from `@osdk/client/experimental` when they run out of time."},"1981":{"id":"/ai/agents-41","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"For an agent that is not in your generated SDK, call `AgentSessions` in `@osdk/foundry.agents` directly. These endpoints are alpha and take `{ preview: true }`, and you handle retries and the consistency key yourself."},"1982":{"id":"/ai/agents-42","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Function                                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendEvent(client, sessionId, { event })` | Sends an event of a type the agent declared when it was published. `result.type` is `\"accepted\"`, with a `consistencyKey`, or `\"sessionNotReady\"`; retry the latter after a short delay. |","table":"table-5"},"1983":{"id":"/ai/agents-43","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Function                                                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getSessionState(client, sessionId, { consistencyKey? })` | Reads the session. `type` is `\"available\"`, with `status`, `agentState`, `arguments`, and context items; `\"behind\"` when it has not yet caught up to `consistencyKey`; or `\"notReady\"`. |","table":"table-5"},"1984":{"id":"/ai/agents-44","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"| Function                 | Description                                |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `get(client, sessionId)` | Reads the session's agent RID and version. |","table":"table-5"},"1985":{"id":"/ai/agents-45","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-and-read-state","content":"The event types and payload shapes are defined by the agent, so check its published definition."},"1986":{"id":"/ai/agents-46","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"`@osdk/agents` is for code that runs inside a Foundry agent, not for apps that call one. Foundry injects an Ontology `Client` and a `PlatformClient` into each invocation; `@osdk/agents/experimental` reads them."},"1987":{"id":"/ai/agents-47","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export        | Description                                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getClient()` | The Ontology SDK `Client` for the current invocation. Throws if no Ontology is imported into the repository. |","table":"table-6"},"1988":{"id":"/ai/agents-48","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                | Description                                      |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getPlatformClient()` | The `PlatformClient` for the current invocation. |","table":"table-6"},"1989":{"id":"/ai/agents-49","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                      | Description                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `withClients(clients, run)` | Runs `run` with `clients` as the current clients. Use it in tests. |","table":"table-6"},"1990":{"id":"/ai/agents-50","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                                          | Description                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ScopeResources`, `ScopeAuthorization`, `Scope` | Resource and authorization scope declarations, re-exported from `@osdk/functions/experimental`. |","table":"table-6"},"1991":{"id":"/ai/agents-51","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"The `AgentConfig` type from `@osdk/agents` describes the `export const config` an agent declares alongside its code: `locator: string`, plus optional `apiName`, `sources: Array<string>`, and an experimental `scope`."},"1992":{"id":"/ai/agents-52","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"The clients exist only while an invocation runs. Call `getClient()` and `getPlatformClient()` inside your handlers, not at module load and not from work that outlives the invocation."},"1993":{"id":"/ai/agents-53","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"To call a language model from agent code, pass `getPlatformClient()` to `foundryModel`."},"1994":{"id":"/ai/chat","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"page","content":"Generate and stream text","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat"},"1995":{"id":"/ai/chat-0","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"Call Foundry-hosted language models with generateText and streamText from @osdk/aip-core, in Node.js or the browser."},"1996":{"id":"/ai/chat-1","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#install","content":"Install"},"1997":{"id":"/ai/chat-2","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Create a model"},"1998":{"id":"/ai/chat-3","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"Model identifiers"},"1999":{"id":"/ai/chat-4","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#generate-text","content":"Generate text"},"2000":{"id":"/ai/chat-5","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"Prompts, messages, and system instructions"},"2001":{"id":"/ai/chat-6","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"Stream text"},"2002":{"id":"/ai/chat-7","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"Stream result"},"2003":{"id":"/ai/chat-8","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"Sampling options"},"2004":{"id":"/ai/chat-9","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Cancel a request"},"2005":{"id":"/ai/chat-10","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"Usage and finish reason"},"2006":{"id":"/ai/chat-11","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Errors and warnings"},"2007":{"id":"/ai/chat-12","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"Use the AI SDK"},"2008":{"id":"/ai/chat-13","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"Call a provider SDK directly"},"2009":{"id":"/ai/chat-14","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2010":{"id":"/ai/chat-15","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` sends chat completions to the Foundry Language Model Service (LMS) with the same auth, governance, and usage tracking as the rest of your OSDK app. Use `generateText` for a complete answer and `streamText` to render tokens as they arrive."},"2011":{"id":"/ai/chat-16","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x, and its API can change in any minor release. The current release runs one model call per request: there is no built-in multi-step tool loop, no structured (JSON) output, and only text content parts are sent. Image and file parts are dropped with a warning."},"2012":{"id":"/ai/chat-17","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#install","content":"`@osdk/client` is a peer dependency. `@osdk/aip-core` brings in `@osdk/language-models` itself."},"2013":{"id":"/ai/chat-18","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Every call takes a model handle from `foundryModel`. It needs a `PlatformClient` from `createPlatformClient` and the model's LMS API name."},"2014":{"id":"/ai/chat-19","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Pass a client from `createPlatformClient`, not the `Client` from `createClient`: `foundryModel` uses the client's `baseUrl` and authenticated `fetch`, and an Ontology `Client` does not expose them. Reuse the same token provider for both clients so the user signs in once."},"2015":{"id":"/ai/chat-20","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"OAuth applications must request the `api:use-language-models-execute` scope. The default scopes of `createPublicOauthClient` do not include it, so list every scope your app needs. See Authentication for the other token providers."},"2016":{"id":"/ai/chat-21","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"`model` accepts an API name string or a `ModelIdentifier`:"},"2017":{"id":"/ai/chat-22","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value    | Example    | Use it for                                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `string` | `\"gpt-4o\"` | A built-in LMS model, by API name. Shorthand for `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName }`. |","table":"table-0"},"2018":{"id":"/ai/chat-23","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value                           | Example                                   | Use it for             |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName }` | `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName: \"gpt-4o\" }` | The same, spelled out. |","table":"table-0"},"2019":{"id":"/ai/chat-24","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value                                             | Example                                                                           | Use it for                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"registeredModel\", registeredModelRid }` | `{ type: \"registeredModel\", registeredModelRid: \"ri.language-model-service...\" }` | A model your organization registered in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"2020":{"id":"/ai/chat-25","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"Which models you can call depends on your enrollment. Look up API names in Model Catalog in Foundry. The handle's `modelId` is `foundry/<apiName or rid>`, useful for logging."},"2021":{"id":"/ai/chat-26","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#generate-text","content":"`generateText` sends one request and resolves with the full response."},"2022":{"id":"/ai/chat-27","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"Give the conversation as either `prompt` or `messages`. Passing both throws. At least one of `system`, `prompt`, or `messages` is required."},"2023":{"id":"/ai/chat-28","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option   | Type                            | Description                        |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `prompt` | `string \\| Array<ModelMessage>` | A string becomes one user message. |","table":"table-1"},"2024":{"id":"/ai/chat-29","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option     | Type                  | Description                    |\n| ---------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `messages` | `Array<ModelMessage>` | The full conversation history. |","table":"table-1"},"2025":{"id":"/ai/chat-30","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option   | Type                                                        | Description                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `system` | `string \\| SystemModelMessage \\| Array<SystemModelMessage>` | Instructions prepended before the conversation. An empty string is ignored. |","table":"table-1"},"2026":{"id":"/ai/chat-31","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"A `ModelMessage` is one of:"},"2027":{"id":"/ai/chat-32","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`     | `content` |\n| ---------- | --------- |\n| `\"system\"` | `string`  |","table":"table-2"},"2028":{"id":"/ai/chat-33","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`   | `content`                                                                                                           |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"user\"` | `string`, or an array of `{ type: \"text\", text }` parts. Image and file parts are accepted by the type but dropped. |","table":"table-2"},"2029":{"id":"/ai/chat-34","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`        | `content`                                            |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"assistant\"` | `string`, or an array of text and `tool-call` parts. |","table":"table-2"},"2030":{"id":"/ai/chat-35","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`   | `content`                                          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool\"` | An array of `tool-result` parts. See Tool calling. |","table":"table-2"},"2031":{"id":"/ai/chat-36","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"To hold a multi-turn conversation, keep the history and append each answer before the next question:"},"2032":{"id":"/ai/chat-37","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"`streamText` returns immediately and starts the request. Read tokens from `textStream`, or every event from `fullStream`. The other fields are promises that resolve when the stream ends."},"2033":{"id":"/ai/chat-38","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"Use `getReader()` in browsers: not every browser supports `for await` over a `ReadableStream`."},"2034":{"id":"/ai/chat-39","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field        | Type                     | Description       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------ | ----------------- |\n| `textStream` | `ReadableStream<string>` | Text deltas only. |","table":"table-3"},"2035":{"id":"/ai/chat-40","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field        | Type                              | Description                |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `fullStream` | `ReadableStream<TextStreamChunk>` | Every event, listed below. |","table":"table-3"},"2036":{"id":"/ai/chat-41","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field  | Type              | Description      |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ---------------- |\n| `text` | `Promise<string>` | The full answer. |","table":"table-3"},"2037":{"id":"/ai/chat-42","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field           | Type                           | Description                                |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `reasoningText` | `Promise<string \\| undefined>` | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-3"},"2038":{"id":"/ai/chat-43","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field       | Type                       | Description                        |\n| ----------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `toolCalls` | `Promise<Array<ToolCall>>` | Tool calls requested by the model. |","table":"table-3"},"2039":{"id":"/ai/chat-44","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field          | Type                    | Description             |\n| -------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `finishReason` | `Promise<FinishReason>` | Why generation stopped. |","table":"table-3"},"2040":{"id":"/ai/chat-45","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field                 | Type                          | Description                                               |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usage`, `totalUsage` | `Promise<LanguageModelUsage>` | Token counts. Identical while each call is a single step. |","table":"table-3"},"2041":{"id":"/ai/chat-46","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field      | Type                                   | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `warnings` | `Promise<Array<Warning> \\| undefined>` | Ignored inputs. Resolves even when the stream fails. |","table":"table-3"},"2042":{"id":"/ai/chat-47","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field                 | Type                                                                              | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `request`, `response` | `Promise<RequestMetadata \\| undefined>`, `Promise<ResponseMetadata \\| undefined>` | The request body sent, and the response id, model, timestamp, and assistant message. |","table":"table-3"},"2043":{"id":"/ai/chat-48","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"`fullStream` emits these `TextStreamChunk` events:"},"2044":{"id":"/ai/chat-49","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`         | Fields        | When                       |\n| -------------- | ------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `\"text-delta\"` | `id`, `delta` | Each piece of answer text. |","table":"table-4"},"2045":{"id":"/ai/chat-50","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`              | Fields        | When                          |\n| ------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `\"reasoning-delta\"` | `id`, `delta` | Each piece of reasoning text. |","table":"table-4"},"2046":{"id":"/ai/chat-51","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`        | Fields                            | When                                                                         |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool-call\"` | `toolCallId`, `toolName`, `input` | Once per tool call, after the model finishes, with `input` parsed from JSON. |","table":"table-4"},"2047":{"id":"/ai/chat-52","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`     | Fields                                     | When              |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------- |\n| `\"finish\"` | `finishReason`, `rawFinishReason`, `usage` | Once, at the end. |","table":"table-4"},"2048":{"id":"/ai/chat-53","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`    | Fields  | When                                                                        |\n| --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"error\"` | `error` | The request or stream failed. The stream then errors with the same `Error`. |","table":"table-4"},"2049":{"id":"/ai/chat-54","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"`streamText` also takes `onChunk`, `onError`, and `onFinish` callbacks. `onFinish` receives `finishReason`, `text`, `reasoningText`, `toolCalls`, `usage`, `totalUsage`, `warnings`, `request`, and `response`."},"2050":{"id":"/ai/chat-55","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"`generateText` and `streamText` share these options:"},"2051":{"id":"/ai/chat-56","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option            | Type     | Description                 |\n| ----------------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `maxOutputTokens` | `number` | Maximum tokens to generate. |","table":"table-5"},"2052":{"id":"/ai/chat-57","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `temperature` | `number` | Randomness. `0` is the most deterministic. |","table":"table-5"},"2053":{"id":"/ai/chat-58","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `topP` | `number` | Nucleus sampling threshold. |","table":"table-5"},"2054":{"id":"/ai/chat-59","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option            | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `presencePenalty` | `number` | Penalizes tokens that have appeared at all. |","table":"table-5"},"2055":{"id":"/ai/chat-60","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option             | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `frequencyPenalty` | `number` | Penalizes tokens by how often they have appeared. |","table":"table-5"},"2056":{"id":"/ai/chat-61","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option          | Type            | Description                               |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `stopSequences` | `Array<string>` | Stops generation at any of these strings. |","table":"table-5"},"2057":{"id":"/ai/chat-62","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seed` | `number` | Seed for repeatable sampling, where the model supports it. |","table":"table-5"},"2058":{"id":"/ai/chat-63","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option    | Type                                  | Description                        |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `headers` | `Record<string, string \\| undefined>` | Extra HTTP headers on the request. |","table":"table-5"},"2059":{"id":"/ai/chat-64","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option        | Type          | Description          |\n| ------------- | ------------- | -------------------- |\n| `abortSignal` | `AbortSignal` | Cancels the request. |","table":"table-5"},"2060":{"id":"/ai/chat-65","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"Models differ in which options they honor. The LMS proxy does not accept `topK`, so there is no such option."},"2061":{"id":"/ai/chat-66","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Pass an `AbortSignal`. `generateText` rejects, and `streamText` errors its streams and rejects its promises. `textStream` and `fullStream` share one source, so cancelling one of them does not abort the request; it is aborted only when both are cancelled."},"2062":{"id":"/ai/chat-67","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Check `signal.aborted` rather than `error.name`: the client's `fetch` wraps the abort in its own error type."},"2063":{"id":"/ai/chat-68","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`generateText` resolves with a `GenerateTextResult`:"},"2064":{"id":"/ai/chat-69","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field  | Type     | Description      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `text` | `string` | The answer text. |","table":"table-6"},"2065":{"id":"/ai/chat-70","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field           | Type                  | Description                                |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `reasoningText` | `string \\| undefined` | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-6"},"2066":{"id":"/ai/chat-71","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field     | Type                 | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `content` | `Array<ContentPart>` | Text, reasoning, and tool-call parts in order. |","table":"table-6"},"2067":{"id":"/ai/chat-72","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field       | Type              | Description                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `toolCalls` | `Array<ToolCall>` | Tool calls requested by the model. |","table":"table-6"},"2068":{"id":"/ai/chat-73","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field         | Type                | Description                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `toolResults` | `Array<ToolResult>` | Always empty: tools are not executed for you. |","table":"table-6"},"2069":{"id":"/ai/chat-74","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field          | Type           | Description             |\n| -------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `finishReason` | `FinishReason` | Normalized stop reason. |","table":"table-6"},"2070":{"id":"/ai/chat-75","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                       |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rawFinishReason` | `string \\| undefined` | The provider's own value, such as `\"tool_calls\"`. |","table":"table-6"},"2071":{"id":"/ai/chat-76","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                 |\n| ------- | -------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `usage` | `LanguageModelUsage` | Token counts for this call. |","table":"table-6"},"2072":{"id":"/ai/chat-77","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field        | Type                 | Description      |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `totalUsage` | `LanguageModelUsage` | Same as `usage`. |","table":"table-6"},"2073":{"id":"/ai/chat-78","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field   | Type                | Description                           |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `Array<StepResult>` | One entry per model call. Always one. |","table":"table-6"},"2074":{"id":"/ai/chat-79","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field      | Type                          | Description               |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `warnings` | `Array<Warning> \\| undefined` | Inputs that were ignored. |","table":"table-6"},"2075":{"id":"/ai/chat-80","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field                 | Type                                  | Description                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `request`, `response` | `RequestMetadata`, `ResponseMetadata` | The request body, plus response `id`, `modelId`, `timestamp`, `body`, and `messages`. |","table":"table-6"},"2076":{"id":"/ai/chat-81","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`FinishReason` is one of `\"stop\"`, `\"length\"` (hit `maxOutputTokens`), `\"tool-calls\"`, `\"content-filter\"`, `\"error\"`, or `\"other\"`."},"2077":{"id":"/ai/chat-82","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`LanguageModelUsage` has `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens`, each `number | undefined`, plus optional `reasoningTokens` and `cachedInputTokens`. Fields are `undefined` when the model does not report usage."},"2078":{"id":"/ai/chat-83","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`generateText` also accepts `onStepFinish(step)` and `onFinish(event)`, where `event` adds `steps` and `totalUsage` to the step result."},"2079":{"id":"/ai/chat-84","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Failed requests reject with `PalantirApiError` from `@osdk/client`, which carries `statusCode`, `errorName`, and `message`. A `403` usually means the token lacks `api:use-language-models-execute` or your user cannot use the model."},"2080":{"id":"/ai/chat-85","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Unsupported input does not throw. It is skipped and reported in `warnings`:"},"2081":{"id":"/ai/chat-86","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                 | Behavior |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| Image or file parts in a user message | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2082":{"id":"/ai/chat-87","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                           | Behavior |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| Reasoning or file parts in an assistant message | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2083":{"id":"/ai/chat-88","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                  | Behavior |\n| ---------------------- | -------- |\n| Media in a tool result | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2084":{"id":"/ai/chat-89","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                                  | Behavior                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------- |\n| A tool whose `inputSchema` is not a JSON Schema object | Sent with empty parameters. |","table":"table-7"},"2085":{"id":"/ai/chat-90","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                       | Behavior                          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Tool-call arguments that are not valid JSON | Passed through as the raw string. |","table":"table-7"},"2086":{"id":"/ai/chat-91","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"If your app already uses the AI SDK, `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` provides a Foundry provider for it. You get the AI SDK's own `generateText`, `streamText`, and `tool()` helpers, including its multi-step tool loop. The provider implements the v3 provider specification, so use `ai` version 6."},"2087":{"id":"/ai/chat-92","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"`foundry(model)` and `foundry.languageModel(model)` accept the same API name or `ModelIdentifier` as `foundryModel`. The provider also ignores `topK` and JSON response formats, and reports them as warnings."},"2088":{"id":"/ai/chat-93","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"`@osdk/language-models` is the lower-level package `@osdk/aip-core` is built on. It returns Foundry's provider-compatible proxy URLs, so you can point an OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google SDK at Foundry instead of the provider. Use it when you need a provider feature `@osdk/aip-core` does not cover yet, such as the OpenAI Responses API or embeddings."},"2089":{"id":"/ai/chat-94","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                   | Returns                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getOpenAiBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/openai/v1` |","table":"table-8"},"2090":{"id":"/ai/chat-95","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                      | Returns                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getAnthropicBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/anthropic` |","table":"table-8"},"2091":{"id":"/ai/chat-96","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                   | Returns                                |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `getGoogleBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/google` |","table":"table-8"},"2092":{"id":"/ai/chat-97","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function              | Returns                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createFetch(client)` | The client's `fetch`, which sets a fresh `Authorization` header on every request. |","table":"table-8"},"2093":{"id":"/ai/chat-98","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                  | Returns                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getFoundryToken(client)` | `Promise<string>` with the current token. |","table":"table-8"},"2094":{"id":"/ai/chat-99","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"Each function accepts an Ontology `Client` or a `PlatformClient`."},"2095":{"id":"/ai/chat-100","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"`createFetch` replaces the `Authorization` header on each request, so the client keeps working after the token from `getFoundryToken` expires. The proxy accepts each provider's native request format; Foundry's LLM-provider compatible APIs documentation lists the supported endpoints."},"2096":{"id":"/ai/chat-101","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"Tool calling: let the model query the Ontology and propose actions."},"2097":{"id":"/ai/chat-102","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"React chat UIs: stream into React with `useChat`."},"2098":{"id":"/ai","page_id":"/ai","type":"page","content":"AI overview","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai"},"2099":{"id":"/ai-0","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"Packages for adding LLM features to OSDK apps with Foundry's Language Model Service, what each one does, and what you need before you start."},"2100":{"id":"/ai-1","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#packages","content":"Packages"},"2101":{"id":"/ai-2","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"Which to use"},"2102":{"id":"/ai-3","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"2103":{"id":"/ai-4","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"Current limits"},"2104":{"id":"/ai-5","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"Add text generation, tool calling, chat UIs, and agents to an OSDK app using models hosted by Foundry's Language Model Service (LMS). Requests run with the signed-in user's permissions and Foundry's governance and usage tracking, so you never ship a provider API key."},"2105":{"id":"/ai-6","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"These packages are pre-release. `@osdk/aip-core`, `@osdk/language-models`, and `@osdk/agents` are at version 0.x, and the React APIs ship from `/experimental` entry points. Expect breaking changes in minor releases."},"2106":{"id":"/ai-7","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package          | Import           | What it does                                                                                               | Maturity |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/aip-core` | `@osdk/aip-core` | `foundryModel`, `generateText`, `streamText`, tool definitions, and the `LmsChatTransport` chat transport. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2107":{"id":"/ai-8","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package          | Import                  | What it does                                                    | Maturity |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/aip-core` | `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` | `createFoundryAI`, a Foundry provider for the AI SDK version 6. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2108":{"id":"/ai-9","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                 | Import                  | What it does                                                                                                              | Maturity |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/language-models` | `@osdk/language-models` | Proxy base URLs and an authenticated `fetch` for the OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google SDKs. `@osdk/aip-core` is built on it. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2109":{"id":"/ai-10","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package       | Import                         | What it does                                                    | Maturity     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `@osdk/react` | `@osdk/react/experimental/aip` | `useChat`, a hook that streams a conversation into React state. | Experimental |","table":"table-0"},"2110":{"id":"/ai-11","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                  | Import                                               | What it does                                              | Maturity     |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | `@osdk/react-components/experimental/aip-agent-chat` | `AipAgentChat`, a prebuilt chat panel built on `useChat`. | Experimental |","table":"table-0"},"2111":{"id":"/ai-12","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                   | Import                    | What it does                                                                                 | Maturity       |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` | `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` | Platform SDK for agents built in AIP Agent Studio: sessions, blocking and streaming replies. | Beta endpoints |","table":"table-0"},"2112":{"id":"/ai-13","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package        | Import                                      | What it does                                                                                           | Maturity |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| `@osdk/agents` | `@osdk/agents`, `@osdk/agents/experimental` | `AgentConfig` and the injected `getClient` and `getPlatformClient` for code that runs inside an agent. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2113":{"id":"/ai-14","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                       | Start with                |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Summarize, classify, or draft text from a script or server | `generateText` in Node.js |","table":"table-1"},"2114":{"id":"/ai-15","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                          | Start with   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Show an answer token by token | `streamText` |","table":"table-1"},"2115":{"id":"/ai-16","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                   | Start with   |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |\n| Let the model look up Ontology data or propose actions | Tool calling |","table":"table-1"},"2116":{"id":"/ai-17","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                              | Start with     |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Add a chat panel to a React app with no custom UI | `AipAgentChat` |","table":"table-1"},"2117":{"id":"/ai-18","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                   | Start with |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| Build your own chat UI | `useChat`  |","table":"table-1"},"2118":{"id":"/ai-19","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                     | Start with              |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Use the AI SDK's helpers, Zod tools, and multi-step loop | `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` |","table":"table-1"},"2119":{"id":"/ai-20","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                                         | Start with              |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Call an OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google SDK feature that `@osdk/aip-core` lacks | `@osdk/language-models` |","table":"table-1"},"2120":{"id":"/ai-21","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                            | Start with |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Talk to an agent configured in AIP Agent Studio | Agents     |","table":"table-1"},"2121":{"id":"/ai-22","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"`@osdk/language-models` is not superseded: `@osdk/aip-core` depends on it for the proxy URL. Use `@osdk/aip-core` for a provider-neutral API, and `@osdk/language-models` when you want a provider's own SDK."},"2122":{"id":"/ai-23","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement            | Details                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| AIP on your enrollment | AIP must be enabled, and your users need permission to use AIP builder capabilities. |","table":"table-2"},"2123":{"id":"/ai-24","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| OAuth scope | Third-party applications must request `api:use-language-models-execute`. The default scopes of `createPublicOauthClient` do not include it. Agents need `api:aip-agents-read` and `api:aip-agents-write`, or `api:agents-read` and `api:agents-write` for generated agents. |","table":"table-2"},"2124":{"id":"/ai-25","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement        | Details                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A `PlatformClient` | `foundryModel`, `createFoundryAI`, and `AipAgentChat` take a client from `createPlatformClient`, not the Ontology `Client`. Create it with the same token provider. |","table":"table-2"},"2125":{"id":"/ai-26","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A model     | Use a model API name, such as `\"gpt-4o\"`, or a registered model RID. Available models vary by enrollment; look them up in Model Catalog. |","table":"table-2"},"2126":{"id":"/ai-27","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                       | Applies to                   |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| One model call per request; you run the tool loop yourself. | `generateText`, `streamText` |","table":"table-3"},"2127":{"id":"/ai-28","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                                  | Applies to                   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Tool `inputSchema` must be JSON Schema; Zod schemas are not converted. | `generateText`, `streamText` |","table":"table-3"},"2128":{"id":"/ai-29","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                                                                      | Applies to                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Text only: image and file parts are dropped, with a warning in `@osdk/aip-core` and silently in `useChat`. | `@osdk/aip-core`, `useChat` |","table":"table-3"},"2129":{"id":"/ai-30","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                 | Applies to                                |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| No structured JSON output, no `topK`. | `@osdk/aip-core`, `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` |","table":"table-3"},"2130":{"id":"/ai-31","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                         | Applies to                |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| No tools, multi-step loops, or stream resume. | `useChat`, `AipAgentChat` |","table":"table-3"},"2131":{"id":"/ai-32","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"The AI SDK provider lifts the first two: the AI SDK runs the loop and converts Zod schemas."},"2132":{"id":"/ai-33","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`generateText`, `streamText`, models, messages, and usage."},"2133":{"id":"/ai-34","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"Query the Ontology and propose actions from model tool calls."},"2134":{"id":"/ai-35","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`useChat`, custom transports, and streaming rendering."},"2135":{"id":"/ai-36","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"AIP Agents, generated agent sessions, and `@osdk/agents`."},"2136":{"id":"/ai-37","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"A prebuilt chat panel for React."},"2137":{"id":"/ai-38","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`llms.txt`, per-page Markdown, and AGENTS.md for coding assistants."},"2138":{"id":"/ai/llms","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"page","content":"Use these docs with AI","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","AI-assisted development"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms"},"2139":{"id":"/ai/llms-0","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms","content":"Give coding assistants accurate OSDK context with llms.txt, per-page Markdown, and the package AGENTS.md files."},"2140":{"id":"/ai/llms-1","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"From any page"},"2141":{"id":"/ai/llms-2","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#markdown-for-every-url","content":"Markdown for every URL"},"2142":{"id":"/ai/llms-3","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"llms.txt"},"2143":{"id":"/ai/llms-4","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"Docs inside your node_modules"},"2144":{"id":"/ai/llms-5","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms","content":"Every page on this site is also published as plain Markdown, so you can hand OSDK documentation to ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, or your own agent without scraping HTML."},"2145":{"id":"/ai/llms-6","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"Each page header has two controls:"},"2146":{"id":"/ai/llms-7","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"| Control           | What it does                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Copy Markdown** | Copies the page as Markdown, ready to paste into a chat or prompt. |","table":"table-0"},"2147":{"id":"/ai/llms-8","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"| Control       | What it does                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Open** menu | Opens the page in ChatGPT, Claude, or Cursor with a prompt that points at the Markdown version, or opens the source on GitHub. |","table":"table-0"},"2148":{"id":"/ai/llms-9","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#markdown-for-every-url","content":"Append `.md` to any docs URL to get the Markdown version:"},"2149":{"id":"/ai/llms-10","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"The site follows the llms.txt convention:"},"2150":{"id":"/ai/llms-11","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"| File        | Contents                                                                                        | Use it when                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `/llms.txt` | An index of every page, grouped by section, with a one-line summary and a link to its Markdown. | Your tool fetches pages on demand. |","table":"table-1"},"2151":{"id":"/ai/llms-12","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"| File             | Contents                  | Use it when                                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/llms-full.txt` | Every page, concatenated. | You want the whole SDK in a single context window. |","table":"table-1"},"2152":{"id":"/ai/llms-13","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"In chat, type `@Docs`, choose **Add new doc**, and enter `https://palantir.github.io/osdk-ts/llms-full.txt`. Mention it with `@Docs` in later prompts."},"2153":{"id":"/ai/llms-14","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"Add the index to your project's `CLAUDE.md` so Claude fetches the pages it needs:"},"2154":{"id":"/ai/llms-15","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"Fetch `https://palantir.github.io/osdk-ts/llms.txt`, pick the relevant pages, then fetch their `.md` links. Use `llms-full.txt` when the agent can't make follow-up requests."},"2155":{"id":"/ai/llms-16","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"The React packages ship agent instructions and documentation in their npm tarballs, so assistants working in your repository can read docs that match your installed version:"},"2156":{"id":"/ai/llms-17","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"| Package       | Files                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react` | `AGENTS.md` (install rules, version matching, correct and incorrect patterns) and `docs/` (the React guides on this site) |","table":"table-2"},"2157":{"id":"/ai/llms-18","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"| Package                  | Files                                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` (one page per component, including generated prop tables) |","table":"table-2"},"2158":{"id":"/ai/llms-19","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"Point your assistant at them directly:"},"2159":{"id":"/ai/llms-20","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"The files in `node_modules` match the version you have installed. This site always documents the latest release."},"2160":{"id":"/ai/react","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"page","content":"React chat UIs","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/react"},"2161":{"id":"/ai/react-0","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"Build streaming chat interfaces with useChat from @osdk/react/experimental/aip, custom chat transports, or the prebuilt AipAgentChat component."},"2162":{"id":"/ai/react-1","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"Choose an approach"},"2163":{"id":"/ai/react-2","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#install","content":"Install"},"2164":{"id":"/ai/react-3","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"Create the model once"},"2165":{"id":"/ai/react-4","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#build-a-chat-with-usechat","content":"Build a chat with `useChat`"},"2166":{"id":"/ai/react-5","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"How streaming renders"},"2167":{"id":"/ai/react-6","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#options","content":"Options"},"2168":{"id":"/ai/react-7","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"Return value"},"2169":{"id":"/ai/react-8","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"Messages"},"2170":{"id":"/ai/react-9","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"Custom transports"},"2171":{"id":"/ai/react-10","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"Stream chunks"},"2172":{"id":"/ai/react-11","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"Use the prebuilt component"},"2173":{"id":"/ai/react-12","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"`useChat` streams a conversation with a Foundry-hosted model into React state: you render `messages` and call `sendMessage`. For a finished UI, drop in the `AipAgentChat` component instead."},"2174":{"id":"/ai/react-13","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"`useChat` is exported from the experimental entry point `@osdk/react/experimental/aip`, and `AipAgentChat` from `@osdk/react-components/experimental/aip-agent-chat`. Both can change in any minor release. The current version is text-only: it does not send tools, run multi-step loops, or resume a dropped stream, and it does not render reasoning text."},"2175":{"id":"/ai/react-14","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach       | You write   | Use it when                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `AipAgentChat` | One element | You want a complete chat panel with a composer, message list, and optional model picker. |","table":"table-0"},"2176":{"id":"/ai/react-15","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach  | You write | Use it when                                               |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useChat` | The UI    | You need your own layout, message rendering, or controls. |","table":"table-0"},"2177":{"id":"/ai/react-16","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach                            | You write                | Use it when                                                              |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `useChat` with a custom `transport` | The UI and the transport | You need to observe or change the stream, such as recording token usage. |","table":"table-0"},"2178":{"id":"/ai/react-17","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#install","content":"`@osdk/react` already depends on `@osdk/aip-core`; install it directly because your code imports `foundryModel` from it. `useChat` does not read from `OsdkProvider`, so it works inside or outside one."},"2179":{"id":"/ai/react-18","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"`useChat` needs a model from `foundryModel`, which takes a `PlatformClient` and the model's LMS API name. Create it at module scope so it stays the same object across renders. A new model object rebuilds the hook's transport."},"2180":{"id":"/ai/react-19","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"If your app already has an Ontology client, pass the same `auth` to `createClient` so the user signs in once. Model selection and scopes are covered in Generate and stream text."},"2181":{"id":"/ai/react-20","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#build-a-chat-with-usechat","content":"The list keeps rendering while a reply streams and after an error, so earlier messages never disappear."},"2182":{"id":"/ai/react-21","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"`sendMessage` appends the user message and sets `status` to `\"submitted\"`."},"2183":{"id":"/ai/react-22","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"On the first text token, an assistant message is added and `status` becomes `\"streaming\"`. Its single text part grows as tokens arrive."},"2184":{"id":"/ai/react-23","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"Updates are batched every 50 ms by default, so a fast stream does not render once per token. Change it with `experimentalThrottle`."},"2185":{"id":"/ai/react-24","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"When the stream ends, `status` returns to `\"ready\"` and `onFinish` fires with the final message."},"2186":{"id":"/ai/react-25","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"`stop()` aborts the request and keeps the partial reply; `status` returns to `\"ready\"` with no error. A failed request sets `status` to `\"error\"`, fills `error`, and calls `onError`. `sendMessage` resolves in every case; it does not reject."},"2187":{"id":"/ai/react-26","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option  | Type            | Default | Description                                                          |\n| ------- | --------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `model` | `LanguageModel` |         | The model from `foundryModel`. Required unless you pass `transport`. |","table":"table-1"},"2188":{"id":"/ai/react-27","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option   | Type     | Default | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `system` | `string` |         | System prompt sent with every request. Replaces any system messages in `messages`. |","table":"table-1"},"2189":{"id":"/ai/react-28","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                   | Type | Default | Description                             |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `temperature`, `maxOutputTokens`, `topP`, `presencePenalty`, `frequencyPenalty`, `stopSequences`, `seed` |      |         | Sampling options, as in `generateText`. |","table":"table-1"},"2190":{"id":"/ai/react-29","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option    | Type                                  | Default | Description                         |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `headers` | `Record<string, string \\| undefined>` |         | Extra HTTP headers on each request. |","table":"table-1"},"2191":{"id":"/ai/react-30","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option | Type     | Default   | Description                                                            |\n| ------ | -------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`   | `string` | Generated | Chat id. Changing it starts a new, empty store seeded from `messages`. |","table":"table-1"},"2192":{"id":"/ai/react-31","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option     | Type                       | Default | Description                           |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `ReadonlyArray<UIMessage>` | `[]`    | Initial messages. Read once per `id`. |","table":"table-1"},"2193":{"id":"/ai/react-32","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option      | Type                       | Default                     | Description                                                                                               |\n| ----------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transport` | `ChatTransport<UIMessage>` | `new LmsChatTransport(...)` | Replaces the default transport. When set, `model`, `system`, sampling options, and `headers` are ignored. |","table":"table-1"},"2194":{"id":"/ai/react-33","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option                 | Type     | Default | Description                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `experimentalThrottle` | `number` | `50`    | Minimum milliseconds between re-renders while streaming. |","table":"table-1"},"2195":{"id":"/ai/react-34","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option    | Type                     | Default | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onError` | `(error: Error) => void` |         | Called when a request or stream fails. Not called for `stop()`. |","table":"table-1"},"2196":{"id":"/ai/react-35","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option     | Type                                     | Default | Description                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onFinish` | `(event: { message, messages }) => void` |         | Called once after a reply completes. |","table":"table-1"},"2197":{"id":"/ai/react-36","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"Changing `model` or a sampling option takes effect on the next message and keeps the conversation, which is how a model picker works."},"2198":{"id":"/ai/react-37","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field | Type     | Description  |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------ |\n| `id`  | `string` | The chat id. |","table":"table-2"},"2199":{"id":"/ai/react-38","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field      | Type                       | Description                                        |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `ReadonlyArray<UIMessage>` | The conversation, including the reply in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"2200":{"id":"/ai/react-39","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field    | Type         | Description                                            |\n| -------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `status` | `ChatStatus` | `\"ready\"`, `\"submitted\"`, `\"streaming\"`, or `\"error\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2201":{"id":"/ai/react-40","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                                    |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | The last failure, while `status` is `\"error\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2202":{"id":"/ai/react-41","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field         | Type                                         | Description                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessage` | `(input: SendMessageInput) => Promise<void>` | Sends `{ text }`, or `{ role: \"user\", parts }`. |","table":"table-2"},"2203":{"id":"/ai/react-42","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field        | Type                                                  | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `regenerate` | `(options?: { messageId?: string }) => Promise<void>` | Removes the last assistant message, or the one with `messageId` and everything after it, and generates again. |","table":"table-2"},"2204":{"id":"/ai/react-43","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field  | Type         | Description                   |\n| ------ | ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Aborts the reply in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"2205":{"id":"/ai/react-44","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field         | Type                                       | Description                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `setMessages` | `(messages \\| (prev) => messages) => void` | Replaces the conversation. Ignored while `status` is `\"submitted\"` or `\"streaming\"`; call `stop()` first. |","table":"table-2"},"2206":{"id":"/ai/react-45","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field        | Type         | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `clearError` | `() => void` | Resets `status` from `\"error\"` to `\"ready\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2207":{"id":"/ai/react-46","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field          | Type                  | Description                                                                               |\n| -------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resumeStream` | `() => Promise<void>` | Reconnects to a dropped stream. The LMS transport cannot reconnect, so this does nothing. |","table":"table-2"},"2208":{"id":"/ai/react-47","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"Clear the conversation with `setMessages([])`, or render a new chat by changing `id`."},"2209":{"id":"/ai/react-48","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"A `UIMessage` is what the UI renders:"},"2210":{"id":"/ai/react-49","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field | Type     | Description                           |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | Stable id. Use it as the React `key`. |","table":"table-3"},"2211":{"id":"/ai/react-50","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field  | Type                                | Description   |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `role` | `\"system\" \\| \"user\" \\| \"assistant\"` | Who wrote it. |","table":"table-3"},"2212":{"id":"/ai/react-51","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field   | Type                   | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parts` | `Array<UIMessagePart>` | `{ type: \"text\", text }`, `{ type: \"reasoning\", text }`, or `{ type: \"file\", url, mediaType }`. |","table":"table-3"},"2213":{"id":"/ai/react-52","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field      | Type                      | Description        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Optional app data. |","table":"table-3"},"2214":{"id":"/ai/react-53","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"Only text parts reach the model. `getUIMessageText(message)` from `@osdk/aip-core` joins a message's text parts. To restore a saved conversation, pass it as `messages` with a stable `id`, and persist the final list from `onFinish`."},"2215":{"id":"/ai/react-54","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"A transport turns the conversation into a stream of `UIMessageChunk` events. The default, `LmsChatTransport` from `@osdk/aip-core`, calls `streamText` and takes the same model, `system`, sampling, and `headers` options as `useChat`. Write your own to observe or change the stream."},"2216":{"id":"/ai/react-55","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"A `ChatTransport` has two methods:"},"2217":{"id":"/ai/react-56","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"| Method                                                                         | Description                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessages({ trigger, chatId, messageId, messages, abortSignal, headers })` | Returns `Promise<ReadableStream<UIMessageChunk>>`. `trigger` is `\"submit-message\"` or `\"regenerate-message\"`; `messageId` is the id for the assistant reply. Honor `abortSignal` so `stop()` works. |","table":"table-4"},"2218":{"id":"/ai/react-57","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"| Method                          | Description                            |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `reconnectToStream({ chatId })` | Returns a stream to resume, or `null`. |","table":"table-4"},"2219":{"id":"/ai/react-58","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"This transport wraps `LmsChatTransport` and reports token usage from the `\"finish\"` chunk:"},"2220":{"id":"/ai/react-59","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"Keep the transport stable with `useMemo` or module scope, for the same reason as the model."},"2221":{"id":"/ai/react-60","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"`LmsChatTransport` emits these chunks in order. `useChat` reads `\"text-delta\"` and `\"error\"`; the others are there for custom transports and consumers."},"2222":{"id":"/ai/react-61","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`    | Fields      | Meaning            |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------ |\n| `\"start\"` | `messageId` | The reply started. |","table":"table-5"},"2223":{"id":"/ai/react-62","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                          | Fields | Meaning                 |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------- |\n| `\"start-step\"`, `\"finish-step\"` |        | Bracket the model call. |","table":"table-5"},"2224":{"id":"/ai/react-63","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                                       | Fields                       | Meaning      |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `\"text-start\"`, `\"text-delta\"`, `\"text-end\"` | `id`, plus `delta` on deltas | Answer text. |","table":"table-5"},"2225":{"id":"/ai/react-64","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                                                      | Fields                       | Meaning                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `\"reasoning-start\"`, `\"reasoning-delta\"`, `\"reasoning-end\"` | `id`, plus `delta` on deltas | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-5"},"2226":{"id":"/ai/react-65","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                   | Fields                            | Meaning                                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool-input-available\"` | `toolCallId`, `toolName`, `input` | A tool call. `useChat` sends no tools, so this appears only from custom transports. |","table":"table-5"},"2227":{"id":"/ai/react-66","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`     | Fields                                        | Meaning             |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `\"finish\"` | `messageMetadata?: { finishReason?, usage? }` | The reply finished. |","table":"table-5"},"2228":{"id":"/ai/react-67","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`    | Fields      | Meaning            |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------ |\n| `\"error\"` | `errorText` | The stream failed. |","table":"table-5"},"2229":{"id":"/ai/react-68","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"`AipAgentChat` wraps `useChat` in a styled chat panel. It takes the `PlatformClient` and model API names and builds the model itself:"},"2230":{"id":"/ai/react-69","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"Despite the name, it chats with a language model through the Language Model Service, not with an agent built in AIP Agent Studio. For props, render slots, `BaseAipAgentChat`, and theming, see AipAgentChat; for the stylesheet setup, see Prerequisites. To call AIP Agents, see Agents."},"2231":{"id":"/ai/tools","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"page","content":"Tool calling","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools"},"2232":{"id":"/ai/tools-0","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Let a Foundry-hosted model call your code to query the Ontology and propose actions, with JSON Schema tools and a confirm-before-apply loop."},"2233":{"id":"/ai/tools-1","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"Set up the clients"},"2234":{"id":"/ai/tools-2","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"Define tools"},"2235":{"id":"/ai/tools-3","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"Control tool choice"},"2236":{"id":"/ai/tools-4","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"Read tool calls"},"2237":{"id":"/ai/tools-5","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"Run the loop"},"2238":{"id":"/ai/tools-6","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Keep tool results small"},"2239":{"id":"/ai/tools-7","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"Propose actions, then confirm"},"2240":{"id":"/ai/tools-8","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#stream-with-tools","content":"Stream with tools"},"2241":{"id":"/ai/tools-9","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"Use the AI SDK"},"2242":{"id":"/ai/tools-10","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Safety checklist"},"2243":{"id":"/ai/tools-11","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Tools let the model ask your app to run code, such as an Ontology query, and then answer from the result. With `@osdk/aip-core`, the model returns tool calls and your code runs them, so you decide what executes and when."},"2244":{"id":"/ai/tools-12","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x and its API can change in any minor release. Two limits shape this page:"},"2245":{"id":"/ai/tools-13","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Each `generateText` or `streamText` call is one model step. Tools are never executed for you; you run them and loop."},"2246":{"id":"/ai/tools-14","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"`inputSchema` must be a plain JSON Schema object. A Zod schema is not converted: the tool is sent with empty parameters and a warning. For Zod schemas and an automatic loop, use the AI SDK provider."},"2247":{"id":"/ai/tools-15","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"Tool code needs two clients: the Ontology `Client` to run queries and actions, and a model built on a `PlatformClient`. Create both from one token provider. This Node.js setup uses a service user; the scopes must include `api:use-language-models-execute`."},"2248":{"id":"/ai/tools-16","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"In a browser, use `createPublicOauthClient` with the same scopes, as shown in Generate and stream text."},"2249":{"id":"/ai/tools-17","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"A `ToolSet` maps tool names to definitions. The name is what the model calls, so make it descriptive."},"2250":{"id":"/ai/tools-18","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` | When and why to use the tool. The model reads this to decide. |","table":"table-0"},"2251":{"id":"/ai/tools-19","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field         | Type               | Description                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inputSchema` | JSON Schema object | The arguments, as `{ type: \"object\", properties, required }`. |","table":"table-0"},"2252":{"id":"/ai/tools-20","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field             | Type                                      | Description                |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `providerOptions` | `Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>` | Provider-specific options. |","table":"table-0"},"2253":{"id":"/ai/tools-21","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"`satisfies ToolSet` keeps the literal tool names, so `toolName` on each returned call is typed as `\"searchEmployees\"`."},"2254":{"id":"/ai/tools-22","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                                                                      |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"auto\"`     | The model decides whether to call a tool. The default when tools are present. |","table":"table-1"},"2255":{"id":"/ai/tools-23","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                               |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `\"required\"` | The model must call at least one tool. |","table":"table-1"},"2256":{"id":"/ai/tools-24","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `\"none\"`     | The model must answer in text. |","table":"table-1"},"2257":{"id":"/ai/tools-25","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice`                                    | Behavior                       |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"tool\", toolName: \"searchEmployees\" }` | The model must call that tool. |","table":"table-1"},"2258":{"id":"/ai/tools-26","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"When the model wants a tool, `finishReason` is `\"tool-calls\"` and `toolCalls` lists each call:"},"2259":{"id":"/ai/tools-27","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type     | Description                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `toolCallId`     | `string` | Pass it back with the result. |","table":"table-2"},"2260":{"id":"/ai/tools-28","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type     | Description      |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `toolName`       | `string` | The tool to run. |","table":"table-2"},"2261":{"id":"/ai/tools-29","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type      | Description                                                                                     |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `input`          | `unknown` | Arguments parsed from the model's JSON. If the JSON is invalid, the raw string, with a warning. |","table":"table-2"},"2262":{"id":"/ai/tools-30","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"`input` is whatever the model produced. It is not validated against `inputSchema`, so check it before use."},"2263":{"id":"/ai/tools-31","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"To finish the answer, append the model's message and a `tool` message with your results, then call the model again. Stop when it answers without tool calls, or after a step limit."},"2264":{"id":"/ai/tools-32","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"`result.response.messages` holds the assistant message, including its tool-call parts. Each `tool-result` part must use the `toolCallId` of the call it answers."},"2265":{"id":"/ai/tools-33","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"A tool result `output` is one of:"},"2266":{"id":"/ai/tools-34","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`   | `value`  | Sent to the model as |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `\"text\"` | `string` | The string.          |","table":"table-3"},"2267":{"id":"/ai/tools-35","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`   | `value`   | Sent to the model as     |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------------ |\n| `\"json\"` | `unknown` | `JSON.stringify(value)`. |","table":"table-3"},"2268":{"id":"/ai/tools-36","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`         | `value`  | Sent to the model as                                        |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"error-text\"` | `string` | The string. Use it so the model can recover from bad input. |","table":"table-3"},"2269":{"id":"/ai/tools-37","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`         | `value`   | Sent to the model as     |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------ |\n| `\"error-json\"` | `unknown` | `JSON.stringify(value)`. |","table":"table-3"},"2270":{"id":"/ai/tools-38","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`      | `value`                                           | Sent to the model as                                 |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"content\"` | Array of `{ type: \"text\", text }` and media parts | The text parts joined by newlines. Media is dropped. |","table":"table-3"},"2271":{"id":"/ai/tools-39","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Every tool result is sent back as input tokens on the next step."},"2272":{"id":"/ai/tools-40","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Pass `$select` so the query loads only the properties the model needs. See Load objects."},"2273":{"id":"/ai/tools-41","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Set a small `$pageSize` and say the limit in the tool description."},"2274":{"id":"/ai/tools-42","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Map OSDK objects to plain fields, as above, instead of returning whole instances."},"2275":{"id":"/ai/tools-43","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Filter on the server with `where` instead of asking the model to filter a long list. See Filter objects."},"2276":{"id":"/ai/tools-44","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"A model can misread a request or be steered by text in the data it reads. Do not apply an action from inside a tool. Have the tool record a proposal, show it to the user, and apply it only after they confirm."},"2277":{"id":"/ai/tools-45","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"Call `runProposalTool` from your loop's `runTool` for `proposeJobTitleChange`, and pass `{ ...tools, ...actionTools }` to `generateText`. `$validateOnly: true` checks the parameters against the action's rules without applying it, so the model learns about invalid input while it can still correct it. Show `proposals` in your UI and call `applyProposal` from the user's confirm button. See Apply actions for the validation result and errors."},"2278":{"id":"/ai/tools-46","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#stream-with-tools","content":"`streamText` takes the same `tools` and `toolChoice`. Tool calls arrive on `fullStream` as `\"tool-call\"` chunks after the text, once the model finishes, and `toolCalls` resolves to the same list. Run them and call `streamText` again with the extended `messages`. `(await result.response)?.messages` holds the assistant message to append."},"2279":{"id":"/ai/tools-47","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"The AI SDK provider in `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` accepts Zod schemas, runs each tool's `execute` for you, and loops until a stop condition. It needs `ai` version 6."},"2280":{"id":"/ai/tools-48","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"`execute` runs without asking anyone, so keep action tools on the propose-then-confirm pattern above: `execute` records the proposal and your UI applies it."},"2281":{"id":"/ai/tools-49","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Treat tool `input` as untrusted. Check types and ranges before you query or write."},"2282":{"id":"/ai/tools-50","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Tool calls run with the signed-in user's permissions, or the service user's in Node. Give a service user only the scopes and data access the feature needs."},"2283":{"id":"/ai/tools-51","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Never apply an action, send a message, or delete data without an explicit user confirmation."},"2284":{"id":"/ai/tools-52","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Limit the number of steps so a confused model cannot loop forever."},"2285":{"id":"/ai/tools-53","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Text in Ontology data can contain instructions. Do not let tool results grant the model new permissions."},"2286":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"page","content":"Call platform APIs","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis"},"2287":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-0","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis","content":"The calling convention for @osdk/foundry functions, including argument order, pagination, errors, binary responses, and preview endpoints."},"2288":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-1","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Import a namespace"},"2289":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-2","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"Argument order"},"2290":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-3","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Responses"},"2291":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-4","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Paginate"},"2292":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-5","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#batch-requests","content":"Batch requests"},"2293":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-6","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Handle errors"},"2294":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-7","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Preview endpoints"},"2295":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-8","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2296":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-9","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis","content":"Every Platform SDK function takes the client first, then the endpoint's path, body, query, and header arguments, in that order. This page covers that convention and how to handle pagination, errors, binary content, and preview endpoints."},"2297":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-10","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Each package exports one namespace per resource, named in the plural: `Users`, `Groups`, `Datasets`, `Files`, `MediaSets`. Each function in a namespace maps to one REST endpoint."},"2298":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-11","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Request and response types, such as `User`, `Group`, and `ListUsersResponse`, are exported by name from the same package. Identifier types such as `UserId` and `PageToken` are strings, so plain string values work wherever they are expected."},"2299":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-12","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"After the client, a function takes up to four groups of arguments, always in this order:"},"2300":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-13","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument   | Example  |\n| -------- | ---------- | -------- |\n| 1        | The client | `client` |","table":"table-0"},"2301":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-14","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                                                    | Example                  |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| 2        | Path parameters, one positional argument each, in URL order | `datasetRid`, `filePath` |","table":"table-0"},"2302":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-15","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                                         | Example                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| 3        | The request body, for `POST` and `PUT` endpoints | `{ where: { type: \"queryString\", value: \"jane\" } }` |","table":"table-0"},"2303":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-16","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                        | Example                            |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| 4        | Query parameters, as one object | `{ pageSize: 100, preview: true }` |","table":"table-0"},"2304":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-17","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                         | Example                |\n| -------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| 5        | Header parameters, as one object | `{ ReadToken: token }` |","table":"table-0"},"2305":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-18","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"A function only takes the groups its endpoint has:"},"2306":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-19","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"When a function has optional query parameters and you need to pass headers, pass `undefined` or an object for the query parameters first. Your editor shows the parameter names, such as `$queryParams` and `$headerParams`, on hover."},"2307":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-20","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns | The function resolves to                                        |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| JSON             | The parsed body, typed, such as `User` or `ListGroupsResponse`. |","table":"table-1"},"2308":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-21","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns   | The function resolves to                         |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| No content (`204`) | `undefined`. The return type is `Promise<void>`. |","table":"table-1"},"2309":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-22","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns | The function resolves to                                                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Binary content   | The `Response`. Read it with `.blob()`, `.arrayBuffer()`, `.text()`, or `.body`. |","table":"table-1"},"2310":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-23","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Binary endpoints include `Files.content`, `Datasets.readTable`, `MediaSets.read`, and `Users.profilePicture`. Their return type is `Promise<Response>`:"},"2311":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-24","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Call `URL.revokeObjectURL` when you no longer show the image."},"2312":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-25","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Upload endpoints such as `Files.upload` and `MediaSets.upload` take the bytes as a `Blob`. A `File` from an `<input type=\"file\">` is a `Blob`, so you can pass it directly."},"2313":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-26","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Most list and search endpoints return one page at a time as `{ data, nextPageToken }`. A few, such as `Groups.listCurrent` and `OntologiesV2.list`, return every result in `data` with no token. Pass `nextPageToken` back as `pageToken` to get the next page. The last page has no `nextPageToken`."},"2314":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-27","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"| Parameter  | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `pageSize` | `number` | Preferred page size. The server can return more or fewer items, and some endpoints cap it. |","table":"table-2"},"2315":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-28","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"| Parameter   | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pageToken` | `string` | Token from the previous page. Omit it for the first page. |","table":"table-2"},"2316":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-29","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"For `GET` endpoints, such as `Users.list`, these are query parameters. For `POST` endpoints, such as `Users.search`, they go in the body."},"2317":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-30","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"A small async generator turns any paged endpoint into a stream of items:"},"2318":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-31","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Use it with query-parameter and body pagination alike:"},"2319":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-32","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Breaking out of the loop stops further requests."},"2320":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-33","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#batch-requests","content":"Resources with many lookups have a `getBatch` function that takes an array of request elements and returns a `data` map keyed by ID. Each documents its maximum batch size in JSDoc; `Users.getBatch` accepts up to 500:"},"2321":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-34","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"A failed call rejects with a `PalantirApiError`, exported from `@osdk/client`. This includes network failures and error responses that are not JSON; those have no `errorName`, and `cause` is an `UnknownError` whose `originalError` holds the underlying error. If the token provider itself throws, the call rejects with a plain `Error`."},"2322":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-35","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field     | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | The server's message, or `Failed to fetch <status> <statusText>`. |","table":"table-3"},"2323":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-36","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `errorName` | `string \\| undefined` | Stable identifier, such as `UserNotFound` or `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly`. Switch on this. |","table":"table-3"},"2324":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-37","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                            |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorCode` | `string \\| undefined` | Category, such as `NOT_FOUND`, `PERMISSION_DENIED`, `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, or `CONFLICT`. |","table":"table-3"},"2325":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-38","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field              | Type                  | Description                 |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `errorDescription` | `string \\| undefined` | Human-readable description. |","table":"table-3"},"2326":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-39","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description  |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ------------ |\n| `statusCode` | `number \\| undefined` | HTTP status. |","table":"table-3"},"2327":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-40","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorInstanceId` | `string \\| undefined` | Server-side ID for this occurrence. Include it in support requests. |","table":"table-3"},"2328":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-41","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `object \\| undefined` | Context for the error, such as `{ userId }`. |","table":"table-3"},"2329":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-42","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Each package exports a type for every error it can return, with the exact `errorName`, `errorCode`, and `parameters`. Import them to see what to expect:"},"2330":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-43","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Shared errors, such as `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly`, `InvalidPageToken`, and `ApiUsageDenied`, are exported from `@osdk/foundry.core`."},"2331":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-44","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"The client retries `429` and `503` responses up to three times before rejecting. Other errors reject immediately."},"2332":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-45","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Functions tagged `@beta` or `@alpha` in JSDoc call preview endpoints. They take a `preview` query parameter, and the server rejects the call with `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly` unless you set it to `true`:"},"2333":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-46","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"`preview` always goes in the query-parameter object, after any body:"},"2334":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-47","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Preview endpoints can change shape between package versions. Pin the package version, and check the changelog when you upgrade."},"2335":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-48","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Users and groups"},"2336":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-49","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Datasets"},"2337":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-50","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Media sets"},"2338":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-51","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Ontology metadata"},"2339":{"id":"/platform/datasets","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"page","content":"Datasets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK","Recipes"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets"},"2340":{"id":"/platform/datasets-0","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"Read dataset files and tables, upload files in transactions, and manage branches with @osdk/foundry.datasets."},"2341":{"id":"/platform/datasets-1","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"Get a dataset"},"2342":{"id":"/platform/datasets-2","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"Read a table"},"2343":{"id":"/platform/datasets-3","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"List and download files"},"2344":{"id":"/platform/datasets-4","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"Upload a single file"},"2345":{"id":"/platform/datasets-5","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Upload in a transaction"},"2346":{"id":"/platform/datasets-6","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#delete-a-file","content":"Delete a file"},"2347":{"id":"/platform/datasets-7","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"Work with branches"},"2348":{"id":"/platform/datasets-8","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#create-a-dataset","content":"Create a dataset"},"2349":{"id":"/platform/datasets-9","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"Reference"},"2350":{"id":"/platform/datasets-10","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"`@osdk/foundry.datasets` reads and writes Foundry datasets. Use it to download a file, export a table as CSV or Arrow, upload files, and group several uploads into one transaction."},"2351":{"id":"/platform/datasets-11","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"Every sample takes a `client` from `createClient` or `createPlatformClient`; see Set up. Reads need the `api:datasets-read` scope and writes need `api:datasets-write`. A dataset is identified by its RID, such as `ri.foundry.main.dataset.<id>`."},"2352":{"id":"/platform/datasets-12","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"This page describes version 2.87 of `@osdk/foundry.datasets`. In older versions, such as 2.5, `Files.content` and `Datasets.readTable` resolve to a `Blob` instead of a `Response`."},"2353":{"id":"/platform/datasets-13","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.get` returns the dataset's `rid`, `name`, and `parentFolderRid`. `Datasets.getSchema` returns its column schema:"},"2354":{"id":"/platform/datasets-14","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.getSchema` reads the latest committed version of the default branch. Pass `{ branchName }` or `{ endTransactionRid }` to read another."},"2355":{"id":"/platform/datasets-15","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"`Datasets.readTable` exports a tabular dataset as CSV or Apache Arrow and resolves to a `Response`:"},"2356":{"id":"/platform/datasets-16","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option   | Type               | Description                  |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| `format` | `\"CSV\" \\| \"ARROW\"` | Required. The export format. |","table":"table-0"},"2357":{"id":"/platform/datasets-17","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option    | Type       | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `columns` | `string[]` | Required. The columns to include. Pass `[]` for all columns. |","table":"table-0"},"2358":{"id":"/platform/datasets-18","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option     | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rowLimit` | `number` | The maximum number of rows. Row order is not deterministic. |","table":"table-0"},"2359":{"id":"/platform/datasets-19","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | `string` | The branch to read. Defaults to the dataset's default branch. |","table":"table-0"},"2360":{"id":"/platform/datasets-20","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option                                     | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startTransactionRid`, `endTransactionRid` | `string` | Read the view at, or between, specific transactions. |","table":"table-0"},"2361":{"id":"/platform/datasets-21","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"For `\"ARROW\"`, read the body with `response.arrayBuffer()` and decode it with an Arrow library such as `apache-arrow`. `readTable` does not support views."},"2362":{"id":"/platform/datasets-22","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"`Files.list` lists the files in the latest view of the default branch, one page at a time. `Files.content` downloads one file:"},"2363":{"id":"/platform/datasets-23","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"Each `File` has `path`, `transactionRid`, `sizeBytes` (a string, when known), and `updatedTime`. `Files.get` returns the same metadata for one path."},"2364":{"id":"/platform/datasets-24","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"`Files.list`, `Files.get`, and `Files.content` take the same view options:"},"2365":{"id":"/platform/datasets-25","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option | Reads                                  |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| None   | The latest view of the default branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2366":{"id":"/platform/datasets-26","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option       | Reads                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | The latest view of that branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2367":{"id":"/platform/datasets-27","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option              | Reads                            |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `endTransactionRid` | The view as of that transaction. |","table":"table-1"},"2368":{"id":"/platform/datasets-28","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option                                        | Reads                                                                                                      |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startTransactionRid` and `endTransactionRid` | Files changed between the two transactions. Set both to the same RID to see only that transaction's files. |","table":"table-1"},"2369":{"id":"/platform/datasets-29","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"To read every page of `Files.list`, use the `paginate` helper from Call platform APIs."},"2370":{"id":"/platform/datasets-30","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"`Files.upload` takes the dataset RID, the file path, and the content as a `Blob`. Without options, it uploads in a new transaction on the default branch and commits it:"},"2371":{"id":"/platform/datasets-31","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"It resolves to the new `File`. If a file already exists at that path, only the newest version is visible afterwards."},"2372":{"id":"/platform/datasets-32","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | `string` | Upload to this branch in a new transaction, which is committed. |","table":"table-2"},"2373":{"id":"/platform/datasets-33","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option            | Type                                             | Description                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transactionType` | `\"APPEND\" \\| \"UPDATE\" \\| \"SNAPSHOT\" \\| \"DELETE\"` | With `branchName`, the type of the new transaction. Defaults to `\"UPDATE\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2374":{"id":"/platform/datasets-34","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option           | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transactionRid` | `string` | Upload into an open transaction that you commit yourself. |","table":"table-2"},"2375":{"id":"/platform/datasets-35","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"In a browser, a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">` is a `Blob`, so you can pass it as the content."},"2376":{"id":"/platform/datasets-36","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"To upload several files atomically, open a transaction, upload into it, then commit. If anything fails, abort it so no partial upload becomes visible:"},"2377":{"id":"/platform/datasets-37","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Create a transaction with `Transactions.create`. Pass the branch as a query parameter, or omit it for the default branch."},"2378":{"id":"/platform/datasets-38","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Upload each file with `Files.upload`, passing `transactionRid`."},"2379":{"id":"/platform/datasets-39","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Call `Transactions.commit`, or `Transactions.abort` on failure."},"2380":{"id":"/platform/datasets-40","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"The transaction type decides what the committed view contains:"},"2381":{"id":"/platform/datasets-41","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type       | Effect on the view                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `SNAPSHOT` | Replaces every file. The view contains only files from this transaction. |","table":"table-3"},"2382":{"id":"/platform/datasets-42","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                 |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UPDATE` | Adds files and overwrites files at the same paths. |","table":"table-3"},"2383":{"id":"/platform/datasets-43","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                  |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `APPEND` | Adds new files. It cannot overwrite existing files. |","table":"table-3"},"2384":{"id":"/platform/datasets-44","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `DELETE` | Removes files. Use it with `Files.deleteFile` and `transactionRid`. |","table":"table-3"},"2385":{"id":"/platform/datasets-45","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"A `Transaction` has `rid`, `transactionType`, `status` (`\"OPEN\"`, `\"COMMITTED\"`, or `\"ABORTED\"`), `createdTime`, and `closedTime`. Check a transaction later with `Transactions.get`."},"2386":{"id":"/platform/datasets-46","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#delete-a-file","content":"`Files.deleteFile` removes a file in a new `DELETE` transaction on the default branch, which it commits. The file stays visible in historical views. Pass `branchName` for another branch, or `transactionRid` to delete several files in one open `DELETE` transaction:"},"2387":{"id":"/platform/datasets-47","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"`Branches` creates, reads, lists, and deletes dataset branches. A new branch can point at a committed transaction:"},"2388":{"id":"/platform/datasets-48","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"Each `Branch` has a `name` and the `transactionRid` it points to, if any. Delete one with `Branches.deleteBranch(client, datasetRid, branchName)`. The default branch is `master` on most stacks."},"2389":{"id":"/platform/datasets-49","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#create-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.create` creates an empty dataset in a folder, with a default branch:"},"2390":{"id":"/platform/datasets-50","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type"