cts the browser to Foundry to sign in. After the redirect back to `redirectUrl`, the client exchanges the code, stores the refresh token per `tokenStorage`, and refreshes the access token one minute before it expires."},"3790":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-7","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","content":"An older overload takes `useHistory`, `loginPage`, `postLoginPage`, `scopes`, `fetchFn`, and `ctxPath` as positional arguments. Prefer `options`, which also accepts `refreshTokenMarker`, `tokenStorage`, and `logger`."},"3791":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-8","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter  | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `clientId` | `string` | The client ID of your Developer Console application. |","table":"table-0"},"3792":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-9","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type     | Description                         |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `url`     | `string` | The base URL of your Foundry stack. |","table":"table-0"},"3793":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-10","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter     | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `redirectUrl` | `string` | The redirect URL registered on the application. It must be a route of your app. |","table":"table-0"},"3794":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-11","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type                       | Description |\n| --------- | -------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `options` | `PublicOauthClientOptions` | See below.  |","table":"table-0"},"3795":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-12","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-realmId","content":"| `realmId?` | `string` | Realm of the authentication provider to use when the user needs to log in, sent as the `_realm` authorize parameter. Users who already have a Foundry session keep that session's identity. Takes precedence over the domain's default authentication provider. If it does not match an enabled provider, Foundry shows the provider picker. To ignore stored refresh tokens when `realmId` changes, also pass it as `refreshTokenMarker`. |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3796":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-13","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-useHistory","content":"| `useHistory?` | `boolean` | If true, uses `history.replaceState()`, otherwise uses `window.location.assign()` (defaults to true) |\n| ------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3797":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-14","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-loginPage","content":"| `loginPage?` | `string` | Custom landing page URL prior to logging in |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3798":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-15","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-postLoginPage","content":"| `postLoginPage?` | `string` | URL to return to after completed authentication cycle (defaults to `window.location.toString()`) |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3799":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-16","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-scopes","content":"| `scopes?` | `string[]` | OAuth scopes to request. Defaults to `[\"api:read-data\", \"api:write-data\", \"api:use-ontologies-read\", \"api:use-ontologies-write\"]`. |\n| --------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3800":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-17","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-fetchFn","content":"| `fetchFn?` | `((input: RequestInfo \\| URL, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>)` | Custom fetch function to use for requests (defaults to `globalThis.fetch`) |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3801":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-18","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-ctxPath","content":"| `ctxPath?` | `string` | Context path for the authorization server (defaults to \"multipass\") |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3802":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-19","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-refreshTokenMarker","content":"| `refreshTokenMarker?` | `string` | Value stored with the refresh token. A stored refresh token is only reused when its marker matches this value, so changing it (for example when the SDK version or `realmId` changes) forces a new authorization. |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3803":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-20","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-tokenStorage","content":"| `tokenStorage?` | `TokenStorageType` | Controls how refresh tokens are stored. Affects security vs. convenience tradeoff. - `'localStorage'` (default): Tokens persist across browser sessions. Best UX but vulnerable on shared devices. - `'sessionStorage'`: Tokens cleared when browser/tab closes. Recommended for shared devices. Users re-authenticate each browser session. - `'none'`: Tokens never stored. Users re-authenticate on every page load. Most secure but worst UX. Does not request `offline_access` scope. Default: `'localStorage'` |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3804":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-21","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-logger","content":"| `logger?` | `OauthLogger` | Optional logger for warning messages. If not provided, warnings are silently dropped. Structurally compatible with `@osdk/api`'s `Logger`. |\n| --------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3805":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-22","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#options","content":"When `scopes` is omitted, the client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write`. Unless `tokenStorage` is `\"none\"`, it also requests `offline_access` to get a refresh token."},"3806":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-23","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"`PublicOauthClient`. The interface has no JSDoc, so this table is written by hand."},"3807":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-24","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member | Type                    | Description                                                             |\n| ------ | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `()`   | `() => Promise<string>` | Returns a valid access token, signing in or refreshing first if needed. |","table":"table-1"},"3808":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-25","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member                | Type                        | Description                                                  |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getTokenOrUndefined` | `() => string \\| undefined` | The current access token without signing in, or `undefined`. |","table":"table-1"},"3809":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-26","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member   | Type                   | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `signIn` | `() => Promise<Token>` | Signs in: uses the stored refresh token, completes a pending redirect, or redirects to Foundry. Concurrent calls share one attempt. |","table":"table-1"},"3810":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-27","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member    | Type                  | Description                                                                               |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `signOut` | `() => Promise<void>` | Revokes the access token and removes the stored refresh token. Throws when not signed in. |","table":"table-1"},"3811":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-28","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member    | Type                                | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refresh` | `() => Promise<Token \\| undefined>` | Refreshes the access token with the stored refresh token. Throws when none is stored or the refresh fails. |","table":"table-1"},"3812":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-29","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member             | Type                                 | Description                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `addEventListener` | `(type, listener, options?) => void` | Listens for `\"signIn\"`, `\"signOut\"`, or `\"refresh\"`. `signIn` and `refresh` events carry the `Token` in `detail`. |","table":"table-1"},"3813":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-30","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member                | Type                                 | Description         |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `removeEventListener` | `(type, listener, options?) => void` | Removes a listener. |","table":"table-1"},"3814":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-31","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"`Token` is `{ access_token: string; expires_in: number; refresh_token?: string; expires_at: number }`."},"3815":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-32","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#see-also","content":"Authentication"},"3816":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-33","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#see-also","content":"createClient"},"3817":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"page","content":"OsdkProvider","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider"},"3818":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-0","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","content":"React context provider that shares an OSDK client and its normalized cache with every hook below it."},"3819":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-1","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"Props"},"3820":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-2","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#devmode-fields","content":"`devMode` fields"},"3821":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-3","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#example","content":"Example"},"3822":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-4","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"Share an observable client"},"3823":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-5","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#see-also","content":"See also"},"3824":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-6","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","content":"Wraps your app so `@osdk/react` hooks can reach the client. Given a `Client`, the provider builds an `ObservableClient` from it, which holds the shared cache, and rebuilds it whenever `client` changes. Given an `ObservableClient`, the provider uses it and its cache as is."},"3825":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-7","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"The props type is not exported, so this table is written by hand."},"3826":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-8","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"| Prop     | Type                         | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `Client \\| ObservableClient` |         | The client from `createClient` in `@osdk/client`, or an observable client from `createObservableClient` in `@osdk/client/observable`. Create it once at module scope; a new instance starts a new, empty cache. |","table":"table-0"},"3827":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-9","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"| Prop       | Type              | Default | Description                    |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `children` | `React.ReactNode` |         | The tree that uses OSDK hooks. |","table":"table-0"},"3828":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-10","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"| Prop             | Type      | Default                             | Description                                                             |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableDevTools` | `boolean` | `true` when devtools are registered | Turns the devtools integration on or off. Ignored in production builds. |","table":"table-0"},"3829":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-11","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#props","content":"| Prop      | Type                                 | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `devMode` | `ObservableClientOptions[\"devMode\"]` |         | Development-only behavior of the observable client. Ignored in production builds. Only accepted with a plain `Client`; pass it to `createObservableClient` instead when you supply an observable client. See the fields below. |","table":"table-0"},"3830":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-12","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#devmode-fields","content":"| Field           | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actionDelayMs` | `number` | Delay, in milliseconds, applied to the result of an action that has an optimistic update, so the optimistic state stays visible. Defaults to `1000`; pass `0` to disable it. |","table":"table-1"},"3831":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-13","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#devmode-fields","content":"| Field      | Type                                                           | Description                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `logLevel` | `\"trace\" \\| \"debug\" \\| \"info\" \\| \"warn\" \\| \"error\" \\| \"fatal\"` | Log level of the observable client. Defaults to `\"error\"`; pass `\"debug\"` to see its tracing. |","table":"table-1"},"3832":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-14","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#devmode-fields","content":"| Field             | Type      | Description                                                                              |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `debug.refCounts` | `boolean` | Logs the reference-count lifecycle of cache entries and shortens their retention window. |","table":"table-1"},"3833":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-15","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#devmode-fields","content":"| Field             | Type      | Description             |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ----------------------- |\n| `debug.cacheKeys` | `boolean` | Logs cache-key lookups. |","table":"table-1"},"3834":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-16","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"To share a cache with code outside React, create an observable client and pass it to `OsdkProvider`:"},"3835":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-17","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"`useOsdkClient()` returns the underlying client used by the observable client's store."},"3836":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-18","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"Keep the observable client stable across renders. Replace it when the ontology, branch, or authentication context changes."},"3837":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-19","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"The provider does not clear the shared cache when it unmounts. Each consumer must unsubscribe from its own observations."},"3838":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-20","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#share-an-observable-client","content":"Multiple providers can use the same observable client, and they share its user-agent registrations. Code outside React must use the observable client's APIs to share the cache; plain client fetches do not populate it."},"3839":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-21","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#see-also","content":"Create a client"},"3840":{"id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider-22","page_id":"/reference/react/osdk-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/osdk-provider#see-also","content":"Devtools"},"3841":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"page","content":"@osdk/react/platform-apis","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react/platform-apis"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis"},"3842":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-0","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"Hooks for Foundry users, markings, and CBAC banners and restrictions, built on @osdk/foundry.admin."},"3843":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-1","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usecurrentfoundryuser","content":"useCurrentFoundryUser"},"3844":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-2","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usefoundryuser","content":"useFoundryUser"},"3845":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-3","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usefoundryuserslist","content":"useFoundryUsersList"},"3846":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-4","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usemarkings","content":"useMarkings"},"3847":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-5","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usemarkingcategories","content":"useMarkingCategories"},"3848":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-6","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#useuserviewmarkings","content":"useUserViewMarkings"},"3849":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-7","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usecbacbanner","content":"useCbacBanner"},"3850":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-8","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usecbacmarkingrestrictions","content":"useCbacMarkingRestrictions"},"3851":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-9","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#example","content":"Example"},"3852":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-10","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#see-also","content":"See also"},"3853":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-11","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"These hooks call Foundry platform APIs with the client from `OsdkProvider`. Install the optional peer dependencies first:"},"3854":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-12","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"All hooks share these behaviors:"},"3855":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-13","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"Each hook instance fetches on mount and keeps its result in component state. Results are not shared through the OSDK cache, so two components that call the same hook make two requests."},"3856":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-14","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"`isLoading` is `true` while enabled and no successful response has arrived. If the request fails, `isLoading` stays `true` alongside `error`, so check `error` first. When `enabled` is `false`, the hook does not fetch and `isLoading` is `false`."},"3857":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-15","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"`refetch()` reruns the request. The data field is `undefined` until the new response arrives."},"3858":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-16","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis","content":"`error` holds the request error, if any."},"3859":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-17","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usecurrentfoundryuser","content":"Gets the signed-in user."},"3860":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-18","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#type-table-useCurrentFoundryUser.ts-UseCurrentFoundryUserOptions-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Enable or disable the query. When `false`, the query will not automatically execute. This is useful for: - Lazy/on-demand queries that should wait for user interaction - Dependent queries that need data from another query first - Conditional queries based on component state Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useCurrentFoundryUser.ts-UseCurrentFoundryUserOptions"},"3861":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-19","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usecurrentfoundryuser","content":"Returns `{ currentUser, isLoading, error, refetch }`, where `currentUser` is a `User` from `@osdk/foundry.admin`."},"3862":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-20","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usefoundryuser","content":"Gets one user by ID."},"3863":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-21","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#type-table-useFoundryUser.ts-UseFoundryUserOptions-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Enable or disable the query. When `false`, the query will not automatically execute. This is useful for: - Lazy/on-demand queries that should wait for user interaction - Dependent queries that need data from another query first - Conditional queries based on component state Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useFoundryUser.ts-UseFoundryUserOptions"},"3864":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-22","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#type-table-useFoundryUser.ts-UseFoundryUserOptions-status","content":"| `status?` | `UserStatus` | The status filter applied when fetching the user. Default: `\"ACTIVE\"` |\n| --------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useFoundryUser.ts-UseFoundryUserOptions"},"3865":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-apis-23","page_id":"/reference/react/platform-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/platform-apis#usefoundryuser","content":"Returns `{ user, isLoading, error, refetch }`, where `user` is a `User`."},"3866":{"id":"/reference/react/platform-a