thout specificity issues."},"5942":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1153","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#theme-architecture-best-practices","content":"**Override at the right level**:"},"5943":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1154","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#theme-architecture-best-practices","content":"Override OSDK component tokens (`--osdk-*`) for component-specific changes"},"5944":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1155","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#theme-architecture-best-practices","content":"Override Blueprint tokens (`--bp-*`) for system-wide design changes"},"5945":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1156","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#theme-architecture-best-practices","content":"**Leverage the mapping**: Since OSDK tokens map to Blueprint tokens, changing a Blueprint token will automatically affect all OSDK tokens that reference it."},"5946":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1157","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#dark-mode","content":"`@osdk/react-components` ships built-in dark-theme overrides that activate when `[data-bp-color-scheme=\"dark\"]` is set on an ancestor element (typically `<html>`) — matching Blueprint's own convention so the OSDK + Blueprint tokens flip together. The supported way to set the attribute is `<OsdkThemeProvider>` from `@osdk/react-components/experimental/theme`; see OsdkThemeProvider for the full reference, including `defaultTheme=\"system\"` (the default, follows `prefers-color-scheme`), runtime toggles via `useOsdkTheme`, and controlled mode for integrating with an external theme store."},"5947":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1158","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#dark-mode","content":"Under `[data-bp-color-scheme=\"dark\"]` Blueprint flips its own `--bp-*` tokens, so `dark.css` only re-maps the subset of `--osdk-*` tokens that have no `--bp-*` counterpart or that intentionally diverge from Blueprint's value."},"5948":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1159","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#adding-your-own-dark-overrides","content":"To customize dark-mode tokens beyond the defaults, declare your overrides in a higher layer using the same selector:"},"5949":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1160","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables#tokens-flipped-in-dark-mode","content":"The package overrides only `--osdk-*` tokens in dark mode. `--bp-*` tokens flip independently via Blueprint's own dark block. Tokens with identical light/dark values (primary/danger/success intents, sizes, weights, spacing, focus width) are not overridden. See `src/tokens/base-tokens/dark.css` for the full list."},"5950":{"id":"/components/cbac-picker","page_id":"/components/cbac-picker","type":"page","content":"CbacPicker","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Experimental"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/cbac-picker"},"5951":{"id":"/components/cbac-picker-0","page_id":"/components/cbac-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/cbac-picker","content":"CbacPicker lets users select classification-based access control (CBAC) markings grouped by category, while the server decides which combinations are valid."},"5952":{"id":"/components/cbac-picker-1","page_id":"/components/cbac-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/cbac-picker#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"5953":{"id":"/components/cbac-picker-2","page_id":"/components/cbac-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/cbac-picker#import","content":"Import"},"5954":{"id":"/components/cbac-picker-3","page_id":"/components/cbac-pi