onents/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type                           | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderValue` | `(value: string) => ReactNode` | Custom display function for filter values. Replaces the default string display in dropdown items, chips, and listogram rows. When the function returns a string, that string is also used for search matching within filter dropdowns. When it returns a non-string `ReactNode`, search falls back to the raw value. |","table":"table-8"},"6312":{"id":"/components/filter-list-159","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showCount` | `boolean` | Show aggregation counts next to filter option values. Applies to LISTOGRAM, SINGLE_SELECT, and MULTI_SELECT components. Defaults to `true for LISTOGRAM and MULTI_SELECT, false for SINGLE_SELECT`. |","table":"table-8"},"6313":{"id":"/components/filter-list-160","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name       | Type                     | Description                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `colorMap` | `Record<string, string>` | Maps filter values to colors for visual differentiation. Used by LISTOGRAM (per-row bar colors). |","table":"table-8"},"6314":{"id":"/components/filter-list-161","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name              | Type                                                                          | Description                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `listogramConfig` | `{ displayMode?: \"full\" \\| \"count\" \\| \"minimal\"; maxVisibleItems?: number; }` | Configuration for LISTOGRAM display mode. Only applies when filterComponent is \"LISTOGRAM\". |","table":"table-8"},"6315":{"id":"/components/filter-list-162","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name            | Type                                                  | Description                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toWhereClause` | `(state: FilterState) => WhereClause<Q> \\| undefined` | Optional custom WHERE clause generator. When provided, this is used instead of auto-generating a WHERE clause from the `key` and filter state. |","table":"table-8"},"6316":{"id":"/components/filter-list-163","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"When using `type: \"PROPERTY\"` or `type: \"LINKED_PROPERTY\"`, specify a `filterComponent`:"},"6317":{"id":"/components/filter-list-164","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component   | Best For                        | State Type    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `LISTOGRAM` | Categorical data with bar chart | `EXACT_MATCH` |","table":"table-9"},"6318":{"id":"/components/filter-list-165","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component       | Best For              | State Type |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ---------- |\n| `SINGLE_SELECT` | Single value dropdown | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6319":{"id":"/components/filter-list-166","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component      | Best For                          | State Type |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `MULTI_SELECT` | Multi-select dropdown with search | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6320":{"id":"/components/filter-list-167","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component   | Best For                         | State Type    |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `TEXT_TAGS` | Tag-based input with suggestions | `EXACT_MATCH` |","table":"table-9"},"6321":{"id":"/components/filter-list-168","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component       | Best For                       | State Type      |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| `CONTAINS_TEXT` | Free-text search on a property | `CONTAINS_TEXT` |","table":"table-9"},"6322":{"id":"/components/filter-list-169","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component      | Best For                         | State Type     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `NUMBER_RANGE` | Min/max range slider for numbers | `NUMBER_RANGE` |","table":"table-9"},"6323":{"id":"/components/filter-list-170","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component    | Best For          | State Type   |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `DATE_RANGE` | Date range picker | `DATE_RANGE` |","table":"table-9"},"6324":{"id":"/components/filter-list-171","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component | Best For              | State Type |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ---------- |\n| `TOGGLE`  | Boolean on/off toggle | `TOGGLE`   |","table":"table-9"},"6325":{"id":"/components/filter-list-172","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component     | Best For           | State Type |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ---------- |\n| `SINGLE_DATE` | Single date picker | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6326":{"id":"/components/filter-list-173","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component    | Best For             | State Type |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `MULTI_DATE` | Multiple date picker | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6327":{"id":"/components/filter-list-174","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component  | Best For                  | State Type |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `TIMELINE` | Date range with start/end | `TIMELINE` |","table":"table-9"},"6328":{"id":"/components/filter-list-175","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#combining-with-objecttable","content":"FilterList owns its filter state. Read the clause out with `onFilterClauseChanged` and pass it to `ObjectTable`:"},"6329":{"id":"/components/filter-list-176","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`onFilterListChanged` reports the state the list mounted with and every change\nafter it — a filter set, a filter removed, or a reset — as an event with a\n`reason` (what happened) and a `snapshot` (everything derived from the resulting\nstate), so you don't need to wire up `onFilterStateChanged`,\n`onFilterClauseChanged` and `onEffectiveObjectSet` separately and reconcile\ntheir firings:"},"6330":{"id":"/components/filter-list-177","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`         | Extra fields | Fires when                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_LIST_INITIALIZED\"` | —            | The list mounted, once, before any interaction |","table":"table-10"},"6331":{"id":"/components/filter-list-178","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`      | Extra fields            | Fires when                        |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_STATE_CHANGED\"` | `filterKey`, `newState` | The user changed a filter's value |","table":"table-10"},"6332":{"id":"/components/filter-list-179","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type` | Extra fields | Fires when                         |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_REMOVED\"`  | `filterKey`  | A filter was removed from the list |","table":"table-10"},"6333":{"id":"/components/filter-list-180","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`   | Extra fields | Fires when                                |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_LIST_RESET\"` | —            | The reset button restored the mount state |","table":"table-10"},"6334":{"id":"/components/filter-list-181","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`filteredObjectSet` is `undefined` when no `objectSet` prop is supplied."},"6335":{"id":"/components/filter-list-182","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`\"FILTER_LIST_INITIALIZED\"` reports the state seeded from `defaultFilterStates`\nand from each definition's `defaultFilterState`, so the initial clause and\nfiltered `ObjectSet` arrive without waiting for a first interaction. If you only\ncare about the current state and not what caused it, ignore `reason` — every\n`snapshot` carries the full `filterClause` and `filteredObjectSet`:"},"6336":{"id":"/components/filter-list-183","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"Changes are reported as they happen, with no debounce, so an analytics handler\nsees every distinct interaction. Free-text and range inputs debounce their own\nkeystrokes, so typing reports once per pause rather than once per character. If\nyou need coarser batching than that — one network request per burst, say —\ndebounce your own handler."},"6337":{"id":"/components/filter-list-184","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#addremove-filters-uncontrolled-mode","content":"Use `addFilterMode=\"uncontrolled\"` with `isVisible: false` on some filters to let users add and remove filters dynamically:"},"6338":{"id":"/components/filter-list-185","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#addremove-filters-uncontrolled-mode","content":"Filters marked `isVisible: false` appear in the \"Add filter\" popover. Users can add them to the list and remove visible filters via the close button. Reset restores the original visibility."},"6339":{"id":"/components/filter-list-186","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#removable-filters-controlled-mode","content":"When `addFilterMode=\"controlled\"` and `onFilterRemoved` is provided, each filter shows a remove button on hover. The consumer manages the definitions array:"},"6340":{"id":"/components/filter-list-187","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#prefiltered-objectset","content":"Pass a `.where()` objectSet to scope filter dropdown values. For example, to only show Engineering employees:"},"6341":{"id":"/components/filter-list-188","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#prefiltered-objectset","content":"The filter dropdowns will only show job titles and locations that exist within the Engineering department."},"6342":{"id":"/components/filter-list-189","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#keyword-search-filter","content":"Add a full-text search filter that searches across multiple properties:"},"6343":{"id":"/components/filter-list-190","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-listogram-colors","content":"Assign colors to specific values in a listogram:"},"6344":{"id":"/components/filter-list-191","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"Use `renderValue` to customize how filter values are displayed and searched. The returned string replaces the raw value for both display and search matching. This is useful for showing human-readable names instead of IDs:"},"6345":{"id":"/components/filter-list-192","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"`renderValue` works with `LISTOGRAM`, `SINGLE_SELECT`, and `MULTI_SELECT` filter components. For `MULTI_SELECT`, it applies to both dropdown items and selected chips. Searching within a filter dropdown matches against the `renderValue` output."},"6346":{"id":"/components/filter-list-193","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"For best performance, memoize `renderValue` with `useCallback` to avoid unnecessary re-renders:"},"6347":{"id":"/components/filter-list-194","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#listogram-display-modes","content":"Control how much detail each listogram row shows:"},"6348":{"id":"/components/filter-list-195","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#limiting-visible-items","content":"By default, LISTOGRAM filters show at most 5 items with a \"View all\" link. Override with `maxVisibleItems`:"},"6349":{"id":"/components/filter-list-196","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"The collapse control is available by default and `FilterList` owns the collapsed\nstate, so collapsing works with no wiring at all:"},"6350":{"id":"/components/filter-list-197","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"Start collapsed with `defaultCollapsed`. `onCollapsedChange` fires in both\nmodes; in uncontrolled mode it is purely a listener on top of the built-in\nbehavior, so the panel keeps collapsing and expanding on its own. Use it when\nthe surrounding layout needs to react:"},"6351":{"id":"/components/filter-list-198","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"To own the state yourself, pass `collapsed` instead of `defaultCollapsed`. That\nswitches the feature into controlled mode: the prop is the source of truth, the\ncomponent keeps no internal state, and the panel only moves when you re-render\nwith a new value in response to `onCollapsedChange`. If both are supplied,\n`collapsed` wins."},"6352":{"id":"/components/filter-list-199","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"`onCollapsedChange` is only an event listener — it never enables the control and\nnever takes over the state. Availability is governed by `enableCollapse` alone."},"6353":{"id":"/components/filter-list-200","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"Pass `enableCollapse={false}` to pin the panel open and remove the control\nentirely; `collapsed` and `defaultCollapsed` are then ignored."},"6354":{"id":"/components/filter-list-201","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#drag-and-drop-sorting","content":"Enable reordering of filters via drag and drop:"},"6355":{"id":"/components/filter-list-202","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#exclude-toggle","content":"LISTOGRAM and TEXT_TAGS filters support an exclude/include toggle. Hover a filter item and click the three-dot menu to toggle between \"Keeping\" and \"Excluding\" modes. When excluding, selected values are excluded from results and appear with a strikethrough."},"6356":{"id":"/components/filter-list-203","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"FilterList uses CSS custom properties included in `@osdk/react-components/styles.css` for theming. Override `--osdk-*` tokens to customize FilterList without affecting other components, or override `--bp-*` tokens for global theming."},"6357":{"id":"/components/filter-list-204","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"Use the `className` prop for scoped styling:"},"6358":{"id":"/components/filter-list-205","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"For a full reference of CSS tokens, see the CSS Variables documentation."},"6359":{"id":"/components/filter-list-206","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#best-practices","content":"**Memoize filterDefinitions** -- define the array outside the component or wrap in `useMemo` to avoid unnecessary re-renders"},"6360":{"id":"/components/filter-list-207","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#best-practices","content":"**Persist filter state with `defaultFilterStates`** -- read changes out via `onFilterStateChanged`, key them with the exported `getFilterKey(definition)`, and pass them back through `defaultFilterStates` to rehydrate after navigation. `serializeFilterStates` / `deserializeFilterStates` handle the `Date` round-trip for you"},"6361":{"id":"/components/filter-list-208","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#best-practices","content":"**Use objectSet constraints to scope filter values** -- pass a prefiltered objectSet (e.g. `client(Employee).where(...)`) so filter dropdowns only show relevant values"},"6362":{"id":"/components/filter-list-209","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#best-practices","content":"**Keep filter lists focused** -- show 3-8 filters; too many filters overwhelm users"},"6363":{"id":"/components/filter-list-210","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#best-practices","content":"**Use `addFilterMode=\"uncontrolled\"` for progressive disclosure** -- start with a few visible filters and let users add more as needed"},"6364":{"id":"/components/image-viewer","page_id":"/components/image-viewer","type":"page","content":"ImageViewer","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Media"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/image-viewer"},"6365":{"id":"/components/image-viewer-0","page_id":"/components/image-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/image-viewer","content":"ImageViewer renders an image from an OSDK Media object, and BaseImageViewer renders an image from a URL you provide."},"6366":{"id":"/components/image-viewer-1","page_id":"/components/image-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/image-viewer#import","content":"Import"},"6367":{"id":