                 |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `--osdk-table-border` | `var(--osdk-table-border-width) solid var(--osdk-table-border-color)` | Base table border (outermost edges). |","table":"table-20"},"6766":{"id":"/components/object-table-350","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#shared-border-tokens","content":"See CSSVariables.md for the canonical reference of every `--osdk-table-*` token."},"6767":{"id":"/components/object-table-351","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#override-examples","content":"Each example below scopes overrides under a `className` passed to `<ObjectTable className=\"my-table\" />` so other tables on the page are unaffected. Drop the class selector to apply globally via `:root` in the `user.theme` layer."},"6768":{"id":"/components/object-table-352","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editable-cell-background","content":"Use the `data-editable` attribute that the table sets on every editable `<td>` to highlight only the cells the user can actually change. Pair it with `--osdk-table-cell-editable-border` to outline the cell in edit mode and `--osdk-table-cell-edited-border` to mark cells with pending changes."},"6769":{"id":"/components/object-table-353","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-for-conditional-row-styling","content":"Attach custom `data-*` attributes per row with the `getRowAttributes` prop and drive row styling in CSS using attribute selectors. Row background comes from `--osdk-table-row-bg-default` and `--osdk-table-row-bg-alternate` — overriding both ensures the override wins regardless of zebra parity."},"6770":{"id":"/components/object-table-354","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-for-conditional-row-styling","content":"Notes:"},"6771":{"id":"/components/object-table-355","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-for-conditional-row-styling","content":"Entries whose value is `undefined` are skipped, so attributes can be conditional without emitting empty values."},"6772":{"id":"/components/object-table-356","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-for-conditional-row-styling","content":"The table reserves `data-selected`, `data-focused`, `data-row-parity`, and `data-pinned` on rows and cells — don't return those names from `getRowAttributes`."},"6773":{"id":"/components/object-table-357","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-for-conditional-row-styling","content":"See Row Attributes and Conditional Row Styling for the full pattern walkthrough."},"6774":{"id":"/components/object-table-358","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#additional-resources","content":"ObjectTable API Reference"},"6775":{"id":"/components/object-table-359","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#additional-resources","content":"ObjectTable Implementation"},"6776":{"id":"/components/object-table-360","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#additional-resources","content":"PeopleApp Examples"},"6777":{"id":"/components/object-table-361","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#additional-resources","content":"@osdk/react documentation"},"6778":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"page","content":"OsdkThemeProvider","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Theming"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider"},"6779":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-0","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","content":"OsdkThemeProvider manages light and dark theme state and sets the data-bp-color-scheme attribute that switches the OSDK and Blueprint design tokens."},"6780":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-1","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"6781":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-2","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#import","content":"Import"},"6782":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-3","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"6783":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-4","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"Props reference"},"6784":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-5","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#defaulttheme-modes","content":"`defaultTheme` modes"},"6785":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-6","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#useosdktheme-hook","content":"`useOsdkTheme` hook"},"6786":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-7","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#examples","content":"Examples"},"6787":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-8","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#default-follow-the-os-preference","content":"Default: follow the OS preference"},"6788":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-9","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#force-light-or-dark-with-defaulttheme","content":"Force light or dark with `defaultTheme`"},"6789":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-10","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#build-a-themetoggle","content":"Build a `ThemeToggle`"},"6790":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-11","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#drive-the-theme-from-an-external-store-controlled-mode","content":"Drive the theme from an external store (controlled mode)"},"6791":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-12","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#scope-theming-to-a-subtree","content":"Scope theming to a subtree"},"6792":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-13","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#branching-on-the-resolved-theme-in-js","content":"Branching on the resolved theme in JS"},"6793":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-14","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","content":"Components inside the provider re-render when the resolved theme changes."},"6794":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-15","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#prerequisites","content":"Before using `OsdkThemeProvider`, complete the library setup described in Prerequisites, in particular the CSS layer imports - the provider only flips an attribute; the OSDK token CSS does the rest."},"6795":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-16","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#quick-start","content":"With no props the provider follows `prefers-color-scheme` and re-renders when the OS preference changes. To override the OS at runtime, descendants call `setTheme` from `useOsdkTheme`."},"6796":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-17","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#quick-start","content":"[!IMPORTANT]\n**Always render the provider somewhere above OSDK components.** OSDK components stay in light mode without it — the CSS only flips when `data-bp-color-scheme=\"dark\"` is on an ancestor, and the provider is the supported way to manage that attribute. If an external store already owns your theme value, use controlled mode instead of skipping the provider — that way descendants can still call `useOsdkTheme`."},"6797":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-18","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"| Prop    | Type                                         | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `theme` | `\"light\" \\| \"dark\" \\| \"system\"` _(optional)_ | —       | Controlled theme. When provided, the provider does not maintain its own state — the parent must respond to `onThemeChanged` (or update its own external store) and re-render with the new value. See Drive the theme from an external store. |","table":"table-0"},"6798":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-19","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"| Prop           | Type                            | Default    | Description                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultTheme` | `\"light\" \\| \"dark\" \\| \"system\"` | `\"system\"` | Initial theme when uncontrolled. Ignored when `theme` is provided. The provider owns the state from then on; descendants change it at runtime via `useOsdkTheme().setTheme`. |","table":"table-0"},"6799":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-20","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"| Prop             | Type                                          | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onThemeChanged` | `(theme: OsdkThemeMode) => void` _(optional)_ | —       | Fires whenever a descendant calls `setTheme`. Use this to layer side effects (persistence, analytics) on top of the default state update, or to drive an external store in controlled mode. |","table":"table-0"},"6800":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-21","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"| Prop     | Type                               | Default                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `target` | `HTMLElement \\| null` _(optional)_ | `document.documentElement` | Element to write `data-bp-color-scheme` onto. Defaults to `<html>` so Blueprint portals (popovers, dialogs, tooltips) — which render outside the React tree — also receive the theme. See Scope theming to a subtree. |","table":"table-0"},"6801":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-22","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#props-reference","content":"| Prop       | Type              | Default | Description                                               |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `children` | `React.ReactNode` | —       | Subtree that should resolve the theme via `useOsdkTheme`. |","table":"table-0"},"6802":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-23","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#defaulttheme-modes","content":"| Mode       | Behavior                                                                                |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"system\"` | Follows the OS `prefers-color-scheme` setting and re-renders when it changes (default). |","table":"table-1"},"6803":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-24","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#defaulttheme-modes","content":"| Mode      | Behavior                                              |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"light\"` | Starts in light mode regardless of the OS preference. |","table":"table-1"},"6804":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-25","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#defaulttheme-modes","content":"| Mode     | Behavior                                             |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"dark\"` | Starts in dark mode regardless of the OS preference. |","table":"table-1"},"6805":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-26","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#defaulttheme-modes","content":"`\"system\"` is the only mode where the resolved theme can change without anyone calling `setTheme` — it reacts to the OS preference flipping while your app is open."},"6806":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-27","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#useosdktheme-hook","content":"| Field   | Type                            | Description                               |\n| ------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `theme` | `\"light\" \\| \"dark\" \\| \"system\"` | The requested mode, including `\"system\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"6807":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-28","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#useosdktheme-hook","content":"| Field           | Type                | Description                                                                                               |\n| --------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolvedTheme` | `\"light\" \\| \"dark\"` | The concrete theme actually applied to the DOM. When `theme === \"system\"`, tracks `prefers-color-scheme`. |","table":"table-2"},"6808":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-29","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#useosdktheme-hook","content":"| Field      | Type                            | Description                           |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `setTheme` | `(next: OsdkThemeMode) => void` | Switch the requested mode at runtime. |","table":"table-2"},"6809":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-30","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#useosdktheme-hook","content":"Must be called from a descendant of `<OsdkThemeProvider>`; throws otherwise."},"6810":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-31","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#default-follow-the-os-preference","content":"The simplest setup — no props needed. The provider starts in `\"system\"` mode, listens to `prefers-color-scheme`, and flips automatically when the user toggles their OS appearance."},"6811":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-32","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#default-follow-the-os-preference","content":"To verify this in development, open Chrome DevTools → `⌘⇧P` → \"Show Rendering\" → set \"Emulate CSS media feature prefers-color-scheme\" to `light` or `dark`."},"6812":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-33","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#force-light-or-dark-with-defaulttheme","content":"Pin the initial mode if your app intentionally ships in light or dark regardless of the OS:"},"6813":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-34","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#force-light-or-dark-with-defaulttheme","content":"Users can still switch at runtime via `useOsdkTheme().setTheme`; `defaultTheme` only seeds the initial value."},"6814":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-35","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#build-a-themetoggle","content":"A typical settings-bar control that lets the user pick light/dark/system:"},"6815":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-36","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#build-a-themetoggle","content":"Render it anywhere inside the provider:"},"6816":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-37","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#drive-the-theme-from-an-external-store-controlled-mode","content":"If the theme value already lives outside the OSDK tree (e.g. in a parent design-system provider), pass it in via the `theme` prop. The provider stops owning state; you re-render it with the new value when the store changes, and the provider rewrites `data-bp-color-scheme` accordingly."},"6817":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-38","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#drive-the-theme-from-an-external-store-controlled-mode","content":"If descendants call `setTheme` from `useOsdkTheme()`, controlled mode does **not** update the provider's state — it fires `onThemeChanged` so you can route the change back into your store."},"6818":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-39","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#drive-the-theme-from-an-external-store-controlled-mode","content":"Use controlled mode whenever an external source of truth exists. Use uncontrolled (just `defaultTheme`) when the provider can own the state itself."},"6819":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-40","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#scope-theming-to-a-subtree","content":"By default the provider writes `data-bp-color-scheme` onto `<html>` so portaled overlays (popovers, dialogs, tooltips) inherit the theme. To theme only a slice of the page — for example, embedding an OSDK dashboard inside a host app that already manages its own theme — pass a `target`:"},"6820":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-41","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#scope-theming-to-a-subtree","content":"Trade-off: portals from `@base-ui/react` / Blueprint render in a portal container that is **not** a descendant of `scopeRef`, so dropdowns and tooltips opened from inside the scoped subtree will follow the document-level theme, not the scoped one. Use the default (`<html>`) target unless you specifically need per-region theming."},"6821":{"id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider-42","page_id":"/components/osdk-theme-provider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/osdk-theme-provider#branching-on-the-resolved-theme-in-js","content":"If you need to swap an asset or change a non-CSS value based on theme, read `resolvedTheme` — not `theme` — so the `\"system\"` mode resolves to a concrete `\"light\"` or `\"dark\"` for you:"},"6822":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"page","content":"PdfViewer","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Media"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer"},"6823":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-0","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer","content":"PdfViewer renders a PDF from an OSDK Media object with text selection, custom annotations, sidebar navigation, and in-document search."},"6824":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-1","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#import","content":"Import"},"6825":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-2","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#usage","content":"Usage"},"6826":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-3","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#with-osdk-media","content":"With OSDK Media"},"6827":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-4","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#with-a-url-arraybuffer-uint8array-or-blob","content":"With a URL, ArrayBuffer, Uint8Array, or Blob"},"6828":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-5","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#with-annotations-and-sidebar","content":"With annotations and sidebar"},"6829":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-6","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#props","content":"Props"},"6830":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-7","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#pdfviewerprops","content":"PdfViewerProps"},"6831":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-8","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"BasePdfViewerProps"},"6832":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-9","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#features","content":"Features"},"6833":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-10","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#text-selection-and-copy","content":"Text selection and copy"},"6834":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-11","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#sidebar","content":"Sidebar"},"6835":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-12","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"Annotations"},"6836":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-13","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"Search (Ctrl+F / Cmd+F)"},"6837":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-14","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"Toolbar"},"6838":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-15","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#lazy-page-rendering","content":"Lazy page rendering"},"6839":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-16","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#high-dpi-rendering","content":"High-DPI rendering"},"6840":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-17","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#architecture-three-tiers","content":"Architecture: three tiers"},"6841":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-18","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"Building blocks"},"6842":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-19","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#example-content-only-viewer","content":"Example: content-only viewer"},"6843":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-20","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#hooks","content":"Hooks"},"6844":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-21","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#composition-hooks","content":"Composition hooks"},"6845":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-22","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"Primitive hooks"},"6846":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-23","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#example-custom-viewer-with-usepdfviewerstate","content":"Example: custom viewer with `usePdfViewerState`"},"6847":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-24","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#example-minimal-viewer-with-usepdfviewercore","content":"Example: minimal viewer with `usePdfViewerCore`"},"6848":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-25","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#types","content":"Types"},"6849":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-26","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/pdf-viewer#theming","content":"Theming"},"6850":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-27","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#import","content":"**`PdfViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the PDF contents, and renders the viewer."},"6851":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-28","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#import","content":"**`BasePdfViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts the PDF source directly as a URL string, `ArrayBuffer`, `Uint8Array`, or `Blob`. Use this when you already have the PDF source."},"6852":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-29","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#import","content":"`src` follows the convention shared by every viewer in this package: it names the\nbinary source to render from, in whatever forms that renderer supports.\n`BasePdfViewer` supports all of them, so it is the reference for `src`. Viewers\nwhose input is already-decoded text or a parsed object take `content` instead."},"6853":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-30","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#pdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop    | Type    | Required | Description                                  |\n| ------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `media` | `Media` | Yes      | OSDK Media object to fetch PDF contents from |","table":"table-0"},"6854":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-31","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#pdfviewerprops","content":"Plus all props from `BasePdfViewerProps` except `src`."},"6855":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-32","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop  | Type                                          | Default | Description                                          |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src` | `string \\| ArrayBuffer \\| Uint8Array \\| Blob` | —       | PDF source: URL string or in-memory bytes (required) |","table":"table-1"},"6856":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-33","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop          | Type              | Default | Description                                                                         |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `annotations` | `PdfAnnotation[]` | `[]`    | Annotations to overlay on the PDF. Each annotation carries its own 1-indexed `page` |","table":"table-1"},"6857":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-34","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop                | Type                                  | Default | Description                            |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onAnnotationClick` | `(annotation: PdfAnnotation) => void` | —       | Callback when an annotation is clicked |","table":"table-1"},"6858":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-35","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop         | Type                                  | Default | Description                                       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDownload` | `(result: PdfDownloadResult) => void` | —       | Callback fired when a download completes or fails |","table":"table-1"},"6859":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-36","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop              | Type      | Default | Description                                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableHighlight` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether the highlight toggle button is shown in the toolbar |","table":"table-1"},"6860":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-37","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop              | Type                                     | Default | Description                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onTextHighlight` | `(event: PdfTextHighlightEvent) => void` | —       | Callback fired when the user creates a text highlight. Only fires while highlight mode is active |","table":"table-1"},"6861":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-38","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop                | Type                                     | Default | Description                                                               |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onHighlightDelete` | `(event: PdfTextHighlightEvent) => void` | —       | Callback fired when the user deletes a highlight via the PDF.js editor UI |","table":"table-1"},"6862":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-39","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop          | Type     | Default | Description               |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------- |\n| `defaultPage` | `number` | `1`     | Initial uncontrolled page |","table":"table-1"},"6863":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-40","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop           | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `defaultScale` | `number` | `1.0`   | Initial uncontrolled zoom level |","table":"table-1"},"6864":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-41","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop              | Type      | Default | Description                                                                |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultAutoSize` | `boolean` | `false` | Initial uncontrolled auto-size state. Takes precedence over `defaultScale` |","table":"table-1"},"6865":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-42","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop                 | Type      | Default | Description                        |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `defaultSidebarOpen` | `boolean` | `false` | Initial uncontrolled sidebar state |","table":"table-1"},"6866":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-43","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop             | Type      | Default | Description                                         |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableDownload` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether the download button is shown in the toolbar |","table":"table-1"},"6867":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-44","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop               | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `downloadFileName` | `string` | —       | Filename used by the toolbar download button. Derived from the `src` URL when omitted, falling back to `document.pdf` |","table":"table-1"},"6868":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-45","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop          | Type          | Default        | Description                                                |\n| ------------- | ------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sidebarMode` | `SidebarMode` | `\"thumbnails\"` | Which sidebar panel to show: `\"thumbnails\"` or `\"outline\"` |","table":"table-1"},"6869":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-46","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop           | Type                                           | Default | Description                                                                                         |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `outlineIcons` | `Partial<Record<number, React.ComponentType>>` | —       | Custom icon components for each outline depth level (0-indexed). No icons are rendered when omitted |","table":"table-1"},"6870":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-47","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop       | Type                                | Default | Description                                                                    |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `formData` | `Record<string, PdfFormFieldValue>` | —       | Initial form field values keyed by field name, applied when the document loads |","table":"table-1"},"6871":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-48","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop           | Type                                                | Default | Description                                                                                |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onFormSubmit` | `(data: Record<string, PdfFormFieldValue>) => void` | —       | Callback fired when the user clicks the toolbar save button, with all current field values |","table":"table-1"},"6872":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-49","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop           | Type                                                    | Default | Description                                      |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onFormChange` | `(fieldName: string, value: PdfFormFieldValue) => void` | —       | Callback fired when any form field value changes |","table":"table-1"},"6873":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-50","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#basepdfviewerprops","content":"| Prop        | Type     | Default | Description                           |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `className` | `string` | —       | CSS class applied to the root element |","table":"table-1"},"6874":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-51","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#text-selection-and-copy","content":"The component renders an invisible text layer on top of each PDF page using the pdf.js `TextLayer` API. This enables native browser text selection — users can click and drag to select text, then copy it with Ctrl+C / Cmd+C."},"6875":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-52","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#sidebar","content":"The sidebar supports two modes controlled by the `sidebarMode` prop:"},"6876":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-53","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#sidebar","content":"**Thumbnails** (`\"thumbnails\"`) — Renders page thumbnails. Click a thumbnail to jump to that page."},"6877":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-54","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#sidebar","content":"**Outline** (`\"outline\"`) — Shows the document's table of contents. If the PDF has embedded bookmarks, those are displayed with their original nesting and bold/italic styling. If no bookmarks exist, headings are automatically extracted from the text content based on font size."},"6878":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-55","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"Annotations are positioned using PDF coordinate space (origin at bottom-left of the page). The component transforms these to CSS positioning automatically. Four built-in annotation types are supported:"},"6879":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-56","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"| Type        | Visual                             |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `highlight` | Semi-transparent colored rectangle |","table":"table-2"},"6880":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-57","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"| Type        | Visual                |\n| ----------- | --------------------- |\n| `underline` | Colored bottom border |","table":"table-2"},"6881":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-58","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"| Type      | Visual                |\n| --------- | --------------------- |\n| `comment` | Small circular marker |","table":"table-2"},"6882":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-59","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"| Type  | Visual                  |\n| ----- | ----------------------- |\n| `pin` | Rotated teardrop marker |","table":"table-2"},"6883":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-60","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"A fifth type, `custom`, renders whatever its `render` callback returns instead of a built-in visual. See `PdfCustomAnnotation` and `PdfAnnotationRenderProps`."},"6884":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-61","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#annotations","content":"Each annotation accepts an optional `color` CSS value to override the default theme color, and a `label` string shown as a tooltip on hover. Annotations are keyboard-accessible (focusable and activatable with Enter/Space)."},"6885":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-62","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"Pressing Ctrl+F (or Cmd+F on macOS) opens a search bar that finds text across all pages. Matches are highlighted in the text layer, and the current match is visually distinguished. Navigation between matches:"},"6886":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-63","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"**Enter** — next match"},"6887":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-64","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"**Shift+Enter** — previous match"},"6888":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-65","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"**Escape** — close search bar"},"6889":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-66","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#search-ctrlf--cmdf","content":"The search bar shows a match counter (e.g. \"3 of 12\"). The toolbar includes a search button as an alternative to the keyboard shortcut."},"6890":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-67","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"The built-in toolbar provides:"},"6891":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-68","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Page navigation** — previous/next buttons and a page number input"},"6892":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-69","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Zoom controls** — zoom in/out in 25% steps (range: 25%–500%)"},"6893":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-70","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Rotate controls** — rotate all pages left (counter-clockwise) or right (clockwise) in 90° increments"},"6894":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-71","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Sidebar toggle** — open/close the sidebar panel"},"6895":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-72","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Search button** — opens the search bar"},"6896":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-73","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#toolbar","content":"**Download button** — downloads the PDF (hidden by default, enable with `enableDownload`)"},"6897":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-74","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#lazy-page-rendering","content":"Pages are rendered lazily by the pdf.js `PDFViewer` — only pages in or near the viewport are mounted. This keeps memory usage and render cost low for large documents."},"6898":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-75","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#high-dpi-rendering","content":"The canvas renderer accounts for `window.devicePixelRatio` to produce sharp text on Retina and other high-DPI displays."},"6899":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-76","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#architecture-three-tiers","content":"The PDF viewer is designed as a three-tier API so you can choose the right level of abstraction:"},"6900":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-77","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#architecture-three-tiers","content":"**Components** (`PdfViewer` / `BasePdfViewer`) — Drop-in viewers with full UI out of the box."},"6901":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-78","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#architecture-three-tiers","content":"**Building block components** — Assemble a custom layout using `PdfViewerContent`, `PdfViewerToolbar`, etc."},"6902":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-79","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#architecture-three-tiers","content":"**Hooks** — Build entirely custom components. The hooks do all the heavy lifting."},"6903":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-80","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"All building blocks are exported from `@osdk/react-components/pdf-viewer` for composing custom PDF viewer layouts. Use `PdfViewerContent` as the foundation and add whichever chrome you need."},"6904":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-81","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component          | Description                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PdfViewerContent` | Core PDF renderer (scroll area + annotations). No toolbar/sidebar. |","table":"table-3"},"6905":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-82","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component          | Description                                                    |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PdfViewerToolbar` | Page navigation, zoom, rotation, search, and download controls |","table":"table-3"},"6906":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-83","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component            | Description                                            |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PdfViewerSearchBar` | Search input with match count and prev/next navigation |","table":"table-3"},"6907":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-84","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component          | Description                             |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------- |\n| `PdfViewerSidebar` | Thumbnail sidebar showing page previews |","table":"table-3"},"6908":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-85","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component                 | Description                                                |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PdfViewerOutlineSidebar` | Document outline sidebar (bookmarks or extracted headings) |","table":"table-3"},"6909":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-86","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#building-blocks","content":"| Component                  | Description                              |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `PdfViewerAnnotationLayer` | Annotation overlay for a single PDF page |","table":"table-3"},"6910":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-87","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#hooks","content":"The hooks are the backbone of the PDF viewer. They handle all state management, pdfjs initialization, event synchronization, and feature logic — so you can build custom components without re-implementing any of it."},"6911":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-88","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#composition-hooks","content":"These compose the primitive hooks and manage all UI state for you."},"6912":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-89","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#composition-hooks","content":"| Hook                | Description                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfViewerState` | Full-featured hook. Includes everything from `usePdfViewerCore` plus zoom helpers, rotation, sidebar, search, outline, download, and keyboard shortcuts. |","table":"table-4"},"6913":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-90","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#composition-hooks","content":"| Hook               | Description                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfViewerCore` | Minimal hook to render and navigate a PDF. Handles document loading, pdfjs viewer init, scale/page sync, and annotation portals. |","table":"table-4"},"6914":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-91","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"For maximum control, use the primitive hooks directly."},"6915":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-92","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook             | Description                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfDocument` | Loads a `PDFDocumentProxy` from a URL, `ArrayBuffer`, `Uint8Array`, or `Blob` using pdf.js. Manages the web worker lifecycle. |","table":"table-5"},"6916":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-93","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook           | Description                                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfViewer` | Initializes the pdfjs `PDFViewer`, `EventBus`, `PDFLinkService`, and `PDFFindController`. |","table":"table-5"},"6917":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-94","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook               | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfViewerSync` | Bidirectional sync between React state and the pdfjs viewer (scale + page). Returns `scrollToPage`. |","table":"table-5"},"6918":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-95","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook                 | Description                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfViewerSearch` | Full-text search across the PDF. Manages query, match count, navigation, and the search open/close state. |","table":"table-5"},"6919":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-96","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook                      | Description                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfAnnotationPortals` | Listens for page render events and provides portal targets for overlaying React annotation components on each page. |","table":"table-5"},"6920":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-97","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/pdf-viewer#primitive-hooks","content":"| Hook            | Description                                                                                                           |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usePdfOutline` | Extracts outline items from a PDF document. Uses embedded bookmarks when available, falls back to heading extraction. |","table":"table-5"},"6921":{"id":"/components/pdf-viewer-98","page_id":"/components/pdf-viewer","tags":[],"type":"