architecture","content":"Blueprint is a React UI toolkit built by Palantir.\nOSDK components use Blueprint's design tokens as the foundation layer so they\nintegrate seamlessly with other Palantir applications and components that\nalready use Blueprint."},"7015":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-13","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#layer-1-blueprint-tokens","content":"The foundation. Blueprint design tokens (`--bp-*`) define the raw visual\nprimitives — colors, typography, spacing, and intent states. These are\ninherited from `@blueprintjs/core`."},"7016":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-14","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#layer-2-osdk-tokens","content":"Most OSDK tokens (`--osdk-*`) map to Blueprint tokens by default; a few hold\nraw values instead (e.g. opacities and cursors). Override these to theme OSDK\ncomponents **without** affecting other Blueprint components in your app."},"7017":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-15","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#layer-3-component-tokens","content":"Per-component CSS variables (e.g. `--osdk-table-*`, `--osdk-form-*`) control\nspecific UI elements. Each component documents its available variables."},"7018":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-16","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#css-layers","content":"Styles are organized using CSS `@layer` for predictable cascade ordering:"},"7019":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-17","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#css-layers","content":"Later layers always win, regardless of selector specificity. This means your\nbrand overrides will always take precedence over OSDK defaults."},"7020":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-18","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#dark-mode","content":"Wrap your app with `OsdkThemeProvider` to control the color scheme:"},"7021":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-19","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#theme-modes","content":"| Mode       | Behavior                                                    |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"system\"` | Follows the OS `prefers-color-scheme` and updates on change |","table":"table-0"},"7022":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-20","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#theme-modes","content":"| Mode      | Behavior                                    |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"light\"` | Forces light theme regardless of OS setting |","table":"table-0"},"7023":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-21","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#theme-modes","content":"| Mode     | Behavior                                   |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `\"dark\"` | Forces dark theme regardless of OS setting |","table":"table-0"},"7024":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-22","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#theme-modes","content":"The provider sets `data-bp-color-scheme` on the document element, which\nthe CSS token layer uses to flip both `--bp-*` and `--osdk-*` tokens."},"7025":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-23","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#switching-at-runtime","content":"Use the `useOsdkTheme` hook from a descendant to switch modes:"},"7026":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-24","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#controlled-mode","content":"If an external store already owns the theme (e.g. Redux, a parent\ndesign-system provider), pass `theme` instead of `defaultTheme`:"},"7027":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-25","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#when-to-override---bp--vs---osdk-","content":"| Prefix   | Override when you want to...                          |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--bp-*` | Theme both Blueprint and OSDK components consistently |","table":"table-1"},"7028":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-26","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#when-to-override---bp--vs---osdk-","content":"| Prefix     | Override when you want to...                          |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--osdk-*` | Theme only OSDK components, leave Blueprint unchanged |","table":"table-1"},"7029":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-27","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#when-to-override---bp--vs---osdk-","content":"| Prefix                 | Override when you want to... |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `--osdk-<component>-*` | Customize a single component |","table":"table-1"},"7030":{"id":"/components/styling-overview-28","page_id":"/components/styling-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/styling-overview#when-to-override---bp--vs---osdk-","content":"Most `--osdk-*` tokens map to a `--bp-*` token by default (a handful — e.g.\n`--osdk-disabled-opacity`, `--osdk-drag-handle-cursor` — hold raw values\ninstead). If your app uses Blueprint components alongside OSDK components and\nyou want a consistent look, override the `--bp-*` tokens; for `--osdk-*` tokens\nwith no `--bp-*` backing, overr