e form padding variables on the form or a wrapper element:"],[4702,"`ActionForm` fetches action metadata, renders fields for the action parameters, runs client-side validation, validates the action with Foundry, and calls the OSDK action when the user submits. The form title is hidden by default. Pass `showFormTitle={true}` to show it; the title uses `formTitle` when provided, otherwise the action display name, otherwise the action API name."],[4703,"`ActionForm` is a discriminated union: provide both `formState` and `onFormStateChange` for controlled mode, or omit both for uncontrolled mode."],[4733,"`ActionForm` is a lightweight OSDK component and does not yet match the full ActionForm in Foundry. The table below lists the main gaps to account for when adopting it."],[4757,"`ActionForm` is built on `BaseForm`, so the form layout and field styling use the same CSS variables documented in CSSVariables.md."],[1292,"`actionLevelValidation` is a list of rules that must all pass before a user can submit. `displayMetadata.failureMessage` is shown when a rule fails."],[2560,"`ActionTypesV2.list` returns one page of action types, and `ActionTypesV2.get` returns one by API name:"],[265,"`ActionValidationError.message` is `\"Validation Error: \"` followed by the validation response as JSON. It is useful in logs, not in UI. Read `.validation` instead:"],[3584,"`ActionValidationError`"],[4295,"`ActionValidationError`"],[4222,"`aggregate` computes counts and metrics over an object set on the server and returns only the numbers. It loads no objects, so it is the right tool for totals, averages, and breakdowns, however large the set."],[3121,"`aggregate` takes `\"$count\"` or a `\"property:metric\"` string:"],[4266,"`aggregate` takes `$count` or `\"<property>:<metric>\"`:"],[4223,"`aggregate` takes `$select`, the metrics to compute, and an optional `$groupBy`. Filter first with `where`; every object set method that returns an object set, such as `pivotTo` or `intersect`, can come