onParams<Q>` is the action's parameters plus:"],[4609,"`asyncIter` accepts `$select`, `$orderBy`, `$includeRid`, and `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties`. It requests pages of 10,000 objects and always requests a snapshot."],[836,"`asyncIter` fetches page after page until every matching object has loaded. It reads from a consistent snapshot, so each object arrives once even when data changes during the loop. Page size is chosen by the client; `asyncIter` has no `$pageSize` option."],[4608,"`asyncIter` loads page after page until it has every object in the set, and yields them one at a time:"],[3217,"`autoFetchMore: true` on a large object type can take a long time and hold every object in memory. Prefer a number, or `fetchMore` on demand. For counts, sums, and group-bys, use `useOsdkAggregation` instead of loading objects."],[4781,"`availableModels` + `onModelChange` — render a model picker in the\ncomposer footer."],[4778,"`BaseAipAgentChat` is OSDK-agnostic — the consumer drives the chat by\npassing the current `messages`, `status`, `error`, and an `onSendMessage`\ncallback that resolves once the user's message has been forwarded.\nUse it for non-OSDK backends, custom transports, or unit tests."],[7039,"`BaseTiffViewerProps`"],[7119,"`BaseWorkshopModule` accepts an explicit `branchRid`. When no branch is supplied, it opens on main, including when Workshop previously remembered another branch in the browser session."],[841,"`batchApplyAction` applies an array of parameter objects in one request, which is faster than one request per object. It does not support `$validateOnly`. Send the edits in chunks:"],[4317,"`batchApplyAction` does not throw it. A batch that fails validation rejects with a `PalantirApiError`."],[4207,"`batchApplyAction` takes an array of parameter objects for the same action and applies them in one request:"],[1966,"`blockingContinue` resolves with `agentMarkdownResponse`, `parameterUpdates`, `totalTokensUsed`, `interruptedOutput`, and `sessionTrace