perties, options?)` returns an object instance with `$apiName`, `$objectType`, `$primaryKey`, `$rid`, `$clone`, and `$link`. The primary key property must be in `properties`. Pass `options.links` to stub linked objects, and `options.titlePropertyApiName` to set `$title`."],[954,"`createObservableClient` from `@osdk/client/observable` is the cache that powers `@osdk/react`. It deduplicates requests, shares objects between subscribers, and refetches affected lists after an action you apply through it. Wrap it in a composable:"],[102,"`createPlatformClient(baseUrl, tokenProvider, options?, fetchFn?)` creates a client for Foundry Platform APIs, such as `@osdk/foundry.admin`, without an Ontology. Use it in apps that have no generated SDK. A client from `createClient` also works with the `@osdk/foundry.*` Platform SDK functions, so most apps need only one client. The exception is the AI helpers in `@osdk/aip-core`, such as `foundryModel`, which require a client from `createPlatformClient` (see Chat and streaming):"],[22,"`createPublicOauthClient` runs the OAuth authorization code flow with PKCE against Foundry. Create it once, at module scope, next to your client."],[668,"`createSeedWithMetadata` from `@osdk/seed-helpers` builds seed data without a server, and returns it with whatever your function returns. `create` returns a reference with the object's properties, `$apiName`, and `$primaryKey`; `link` connects two references by link name."],[3178,"`data` is `undefined` until the first page arrives. After that, `isLoading` can be `true` while `data` still holds the previous result, for example while the hook revalidates after an action. Keep rendering `data` during those refreshes instead of replacing the list with a spinner. Loading and errors covers the pattern in depth."],[2706,"`data` is an `ActionEditResponse`: a summary of what the action changed, not a value returned by the action's logic."],[2389,"`Datasets.create` creates an empty dataset in a folder, with a default branch:"],[2353,"`Datasets.get` returns the dataset's `rid`, `name`, and `parentFolderRid`. `Datasets.getSchema` returns its column schema:"],[2354,"`Datasets.getSchema` reads the latest committed version of the default branch. Pass `{ branchName }` or `{ endTransactionRid }` to read another."],[2355,"`Datasets.readTable` exports a tabular dataset as CSV or Apache Arrow and resolves to a `Response`:"],[1429,"`datasources` says where property values come from. Without it, a dataset backs every property. Give an object type one base datasource (`dataset`, `stream`, `restrictedView`, or `direct`) plus any number of `derived` datasources; `defineObject` throws if you list more than one `dataset`, `stream`, or `restrictedView`. Properties not mapped by a `derived` datasource come from the base datasource."],[3926,"`DebouncedCallback<TArgs>`, a function with the same arguments as `callback` and two methods:"],[176,"`dedupeIntervalMs` defaults to `2000` on `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, `useLinks`, `useOsdkAggregation`, and `useOsdkFunction`. If two components mount the same query within that window, the second one reuses the first request."],[6784,"`defaultTheme` modes"],[1301,"`defineAction` takes the parameters and logic rules directly, for actions the helpers do not cover. The rules use the Ontology IR rule types, such as `addObjectRule`, `modifyObjectRule`, `deleteObjectRule`, `addOrModifyObjectRuleV2`, and `addInterfaceRule`."],[1302,"`defineAction` throws when there are no rules, when parameter IDs repeat, when a rule or section references a parameter that is not defined, or when a parameter condition refers to the same parameter or to one that comes later in the parameter order."],[1754,"`defineConfig` returns its argument unchanged. Its `const` type parameter keeps parameter IDs, types, and `parameterUpdateIds` as literal types, which is what lets `useFoundryWidgetContext` and `emitEvent` type-check against your config."],[1270,"`defineDeleteObjectAction` r