82,"`system` — system prompt prepended to every request."],[667,"`test.extend` creates the server, seed client, and integration client once per worker and passes them to each test. `stop()` runs in `finally`, so a server that fails to start does not leave its process or `.test-run-*` directory behind."],[3385,"`TestOsdkProvider` and `fakeObservableClient` ship in `@osdk/react` under `@osdk/react/testing`, so they need no extra install."],[3391,"`TestOsdkProvider` from `@osdk/react/testing` puts a `client` and an `observableClient` of your choice into context, without the devtools and user-agent setup of `OsdkProvider`. Use it when the code under test calls `useOsdkClient`, `useObservableClient`, or a platform API hook."],[3906,"`TestOsdkProvider` props"],[3910,"`TestOsdkProvider` puts a `client` and an `observableClient` of your choice into context, skipping the devtools and user-agent setup of `OsdkProvider`. Use it only in tests; in production, `OsdkProvider` derives the observable client from `client` so the two cannot diverge."],[3489,"`TextStreamChunk`"],[7040,"`TiffViewerProps`"],[3814,"`Token` is `{ access_token: string; expires_in: number; refresh_token?: string; expires_at: number }`."],[3212,"`totalCount` is a string because the count can exceed `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`. It is `undefined` when the server does not report it."],[2503,"`transformation.type` selects the conversion, such as `\"image\"`, `\"documentToImage\"`, `\"documentToText\"`, `\"audioToText\"`, or `\"videoToImage\"`. Each type has its own options; your editor lists them from the `Transformation` type. To transform an item you can only read through a read token, pass it as the `Token` header parameter."],[893,"`tsc` does not rewrite import paths. Write relative imports with the `.js` extension, as above, so `dist/` also loads in Node.js without a bundler. Create a client lists the client methods you can call."],[1427,"`type.type` is a type name (`boolean`, `binary`, `byte`, `short`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `double`, `decimal`, `string`, `date`, or `timestamp`) or an object for a composite type: `{ type: \"array\", elementType }`, `{ type: \"map\", keyType, valueType }`, `{ type: \"optional\", wrappedType }`, or `{ type: \"struct\", fields: [{ identifier, baseType }] }`. Each entry in `constraints` has a `constraint` for that base type and an optional `failureMessage`. String constraints are `regex`, `oneOf`, `length`, `isUuid`, and `isRid`:"],[1404,"`type` takes a string for most types and an object for types with options."],[1134,"`type`, `array`, `reducers`, `description`, `visibility`, `nullability`, `typeClasses`, and `baseFormatter` work as they do on object type properties. The other options:"],[3106,"`union`, `intersect`, and `subtract` are methods on every object set. Each takes one or more sets of the same type and returns a new set:"],[4533,"`union`, `intersect`, and `subtract` take one or more object sets of the same type and return a new object set. Nothing loads until you call a load method:"],[3349,"`useCbacMarkingRestrictions` checks a proposed set of marking IDs before you apply it, for example in a marking picker:"],[2174,"`useChat` is exported from the experimental entry point `@osdk/react/experimental/aip`, and `AipAgentChat` from `@osdk/react-components/experimental/aip-agent-chat`. Both can change in any minor release. The current version is text-only: it does not send tools, run multi-step loops, or resume a dropped stream, and it does not render reasoning text."],[2179,"`useChat` needs a model from `foundryModel`, which takes a `PlatformClient` and the model's LMS API name. Create it at module scope so it stays the same object across renders. A new model object rebuilds the hook's transport."],[2173,"`useChat` streams a conversation with a Foundry-hosted model into React state: you render `messages` and call `sendMessage`. For a finished UI, drop in the `AipAgentChat` component instead."],[2134,"`useChat`, custom transports