re visible to the next read. Edits in Object Storage V1 are eventually consistent and can take a moment to appear."],[6560,"When `editable` is a function, the column is still considered \"potentially editable\" at the table level — the bottom edit-mode bar is shown so users can enter and exit edit mode. The per-row predicate decides whether each cell renders the editor or the read-only value."],[6561,"When `editable` is truthy, columns default to a text or number input (auto-detected from the property type). Use `editFieldConfig` to specify a different editor component."],[4722,"When `formFieldDefinitions` is omitted, `ActionForm` derives one field per action parameter from action metadata."],[6602,"When `isAllSelected` is `true`, the table shows all rows as selected regardless of the `selectedRows` array content"],[6626,"When `onSubmitEdits` is provided, a \"Submit Edits\" button appears"],[3805,"When `scopes` is omitted, the client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write`. Unless `tokenStorage` is `\"none\"`, it also requests `offline_access` to get a refresh token."],[2997,"When a call fails, `error` holds the `Error` and `data` becomes `undefined`. The error stays until a later call succeeds, so render it next to the rest of the component rather than in place of it. `refetch` doubles as a retry:"],[3224,"When a component receives an object from a list, pass the instance itself. The hook does not fetch; it subscribes to the cached copy, so the component re-renders when an action or optimistic update changes that object, and `isOptimistic` tells you whether the change is confirmed."],[2306,"When a function has optional query parameters and you need to pass headers, pass `undefined` or an object for the query parameters first. Your editor shows the parameter names, such as `$queryParams` and `$headerParams`, on hover."],[258,"When a request fails before reaching Foundry, or the response is not JSON, the error is a `PalantirApiError` with no `errorCode` or `errorName`, and the original error on `cause`. `statusCode` is set if a response arrived."],[3360,"When a request fails, `isLoading` stays `true` next to `error`. Check `error` before `isLoading`, as the examples on this page do."],[139,"When hooks fetch"],[4313,"When no object matches, `fetchOne` and `$link.<link>.fetchOne` reject with a `PalantirApiError` that carries only a message, `Expected a single result but got 0 instead`, and no `statusCode`, `errorCode`, or `errorName`."],[6970,"When overriding theme tokens, keep the result accessible:"],[177,"When several mounted hooks share an entry, the smallest non-zero `dedupeIntervalMs` among them applies. In-flight requests are always shared, whatever the interval."],[1567,"When the action succeeds, the list updates without a refetch call: the action response tells the cache which objects changed. See Apply actions for validation, batches, and optimistic updates."],[2791,"When the cache updates itself"],[2258,"When the model wants a tool, `finishReason` is `\"tool-calls\"` and `toolCalls` lists each call:"],[3105,"When the options change, `useObjectSet` keeps returning the previous `data` while the new query loads, with `isLoading` set to `true`. Changing to an object set that starts from a different object type clears it. A set pivoted from the same starting type does not count as a different type."],[4312,"When the request never got a response, `statusCode` is `undefined`. The low-level error is on `error.cause`, and its `originalError` holds the `TypeError` from the failed `fetch`."],[2185,"When the stream ends, `status` returns to `\"ready\"` and `onFinish` fires with the final message."],[2792,"When to invalidate"],[7012,"When to Override `--bp-*` vs `--osdk-*`"],[3088,"When to use `useObjectSet`"],[851,"When to use it"],[2523,"When to use the OSDK instead"],[138,"When two hooks share an entry"],[6285,"When using `type: \"CUSTOM\"`, the definition supports:"],[6253,"When using `type: \"HAS_LINK\"`, the definition supports:"],[6243,"When using `type: \"KEYWORD_SEARCH\"`, the definition supports:"],[6265,"When using `type: \"LINKED_PROPERTY\"`, the definition supports:"],[6316,"When using `type: \"PROPERTY\"` or `type: \"LINKED_PROPERTY\"`, specify a `filterComponent`:"],[6225,"When using `type: \"PROPERTY\"`, the definition supports:"],[6299,"When using `type: \"STATIC_VALUES\"`, the definition supports:"],[4198,"When you apply an action whose validation fails, `applyAction` throws an `ActionValidationError` from `@osdk/client`. Its `validation` field holds the same validation result:"],[179,"When you apply an action with `useOsdkAction`, the client requests the action's edits from the server and updates the cache from them. You do not need to invalidate anything."],[2821,"When you apply an action with the `Client`, invalidate what it edited. Ask for the edits with `$returnEdits` and invalidate by type:"],[1449,"When you compile with `--apiNamespace`, the string reference must include the namespace, such as `\"com.example.Office\"`."],[1786,"When you emit the event, `parameterUpdates` must contain a value for every ID in `parameterUpdateIds`, typed like the parameter's value:"],[147,"When you need to invalidate"],[2478,"When you only have the item's path in the set, look up its RID with `getRidByPath`. It is a preview endpoint:"],[3208,"When you pass an interface instead of an object type, each object only exposes the interface's properties. Two options change that:"],[1159,"When you use a shared property type, its key must be the shared property type's API name: `properties: { name }` works, and `properties: { fullName: name }` throws. `primaryKeyConstraint` is `\"MUST_BE_PK\"`, `\"CANNOT_BE_PK\"`, or `\"NO_RESTRICTION\"`."],[1969,"When your generated SDK includes agents, it exports each one alongside your object types, and all of them as `$Agents`. Pass one to the client and call `experimental_createSession` with the agent's arguments:"],[3673,"WhereClause"],[2020,"Which models you can call depends on your enrollment. Look up API names in Model Catalog in Foundry. The handle's `modelId` is `foundry/<apiName or rid>`, useful for logging."],[2101,"Which to use"],[2996,"While `enabled` is `false`, `isLoading` is `false` and `data` is `undefined`."],[3985,"While a new query loads, `data` keeps the last completed result for the same object type, so the list does not flash empty between filters."],[3359,"While a request runs, the previous result is cleared and the data field is `undefined`."],[1924,"While the state is `not-started` or `loading`, `parameters.values` is `{}`, so give every read a fallback and keep rendering. Show progress next to the content instead of replacing it:"],[1204,"Who can submit"],[276,"Why `client(Employee)`"],[1455,"Why use `@osdk/react`"],[1649,"Widgets ship in a **widget set**, a Foundry resource with a RID such as `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. One project builds one widget set, and each HTML entrypoint in its Vite config becomes one widget in the set. You deploy the set as numbered versions, and the host loads the scripts and stylesheets that the version's manifest lists."],[840,"With `{ $validateOnly: true }`, `applyAction` returns the validation result instead of applying the action. Its `result` is `\"VALID\"` or `\"INVALID\"`."],[4247,"With `$exact: { $includeNullValue: true }`, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."],[4232,"With `$groupBy`, the result is an array with one entry per group. Each entry has the group's values under `$group`, plus the same metric fields:"],[2775,"With `enabled: false`, the hook does not fetch and returns `data: undefined`, `isLoading: false`, and `error: undefined`. `refetch` does nothing while disabled."],[4630,"With `fetchPage`, include each `$orderBy` key in `$select`. An `$orderBy` that names no selected property does not typecheck."],[609,"With `git-describe`, the CLI strips `tagPrefix` from the result, or a leading `v` when there is no prefix. The result depends on where you are relative to the newest tag:"],[3059,"With `useObjectSet`, call `pivotTo` on the object set you pass in. The result is then typed as the linked type, which the hook's own `pivotTo` option does not do:"],[4619,"With a snapshot, every page of a non-stream-backed object type reflects the same point in time, so a completed traversal returns each object exactly once. This does not hold with `$orderBy: \"relevance\"`: relevance-ordered pages can repeat or skip objects, so use a single `fetchPage` for relevance results. Paging fails if the snapshot expires or the server detects a paging inconsistency (`PagingInconsistencyDetected`). Stream-backed object types do not keep a snapshot across pages: changes during a traversal can make it fail, and exactly-once traversal is not guaranteed."],[6391,"With a string"],[7143,"With a string"],[6369,"With a URL"],[7060,"With a URL"],[6827,"With a URL, ArrayBuffer, Uint8Array, or Blob"],[1869,"With an empty `tagPrefix`, the build uses the most recent tag reachable from `HEAD` and strips a leading `v`, so `v1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. With a prefix such as `widgets/`, it only matches tags that start with the prefix and strips it, so `widgets/1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. Commits after the tag and uncommitted changes add a suffix such as `1.4.0-3-g1a2b3c4-dirty`. The build fails if git is missing, the directory is not a repository, or no tag matches."],[6828,"With annotations and sidebar"],[6099,"With MIME type override"],[4766,"With model picker (controlled)"],[4767,"With model picker (uncontrolled)"],[4246,"With more than one `$groupBy` property, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."],[6795,"With no props the provider follows `prefers-color-scheme` and re-renders when the OS preference changes. To override the OS at runtime, descendants call `setTheme` from `useOsdkTheme`."],[6128,"With OSDK Media"],[6368,"With OSDK Media"],[6390,"With OSDK Media"],[6826,"