u provide, in a styled monospace <pre><code> block."],[7146,"XmlViewerProps"],[714,"Yes, with `@osdk/client` and a confidential OAuth client. `createConfidentialOauthClient` from `@osdk/oauth` uses the client credentials grant, so requests act as the application's service user, not a signed-in person:"],[709,"Yes. `@osdk/client` has no UI dependency and works in any browser or JavaScript runtime with `fetch`. Create a client with `createClient` and call `client(Employee).fetchPage()`, `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction()`, and so on. See Use the client without React."],[716,"Yes. `@osdk/create-app` has React, Vue, and Expo templates, plus a React template for public apps without sign-in. Choose one at the prompt, or pass it directly:"],[2986,"you call `refetch`, or invalidate it through the observable client (see Invalidate the cache),"],[221,"You call `refetch`, or something invalidates the entry."],[2734,"You can also apply an action with the `Client` from `useOsdkClient`. This bypasses the cache: components do not update until you invalidate the affected data yourself (see Invalidate the cache). Prefer `useOsdkAction` in components."],[6729,"You can also attach custom `data-*` attributes per row with the `getRowAttributes` prop — see Row Attributes and Conditional Row Styling."],[3191,"You can also filter on `$primaryKey`, for example `{ $primaryKey: { $in: [101, 102] } }`, without knowing the name of the primary key property."],[1477,"You can call `@osdk/client` from any data layer, including TanStack Query. `@osdk/react` adds behavior that a generic request cache cannot reproduce because it understands Ontology objects:"],[6599,"You can filter by object properties and derived properties by including them in the `WhereClause`:"],[622,"You cannot delete the live version. To take the site offline, clear the live version with `osdk site version unset`; the site is unreachable until you set one again."],[4178,"You cannot set both on one call; the types reject it."],[3100,"You combined sets with `union`, `intersect`, or `subtract`."],[2905,"You do not add any JSX. During `vite dev`, the plugin injects two scripts into `index.html`: one that installs a React Fiber hook, and one that imports the panel:"],[2803,"You do not need to invalidate after:"],[1724,"You do not need to publish a widget set before developing on it. To place the widget in a Workshop module, publish a version once so the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. See Build and publish."],[1594,"You might also see the same error for `unstable-do-not-use.js` or a path in `@osdk/api`. `@osdk/react` imports its runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, and your installed `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` comes from a different release than your `@osdk/react`."],[462,"You must pass `--version` or `--autoVersion`, or set `site.autoVersion` in `foundry.config.json`. When the deploy succeeds, the CLI prints the live URL, `https://<subdomain>`. With `--uploadOnly`, it prints `https://<subdomain>/.system/preview?previewVersion=<version>` instead."],[1502,"You need Node.js and an application in Foundry Developer Console. The CLI asks for these values, so collect them first:"],[1458,"You pick the Ontology resources your app needs in Developer Console, and Foundry generates an npm package for them, such as `@my-app/sdk`. The generated package contains typed definitions only. The runtime that sends requests, pages results, and applies actions lives in `@osdk/client`, and you pass definitions to it:"],[3101,"You pivoted across several links."],[2810,"Your code applies an action with the `Client` directly, as in `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction(...)`, instead of through `useOsdkAction`."],[200,"Your code edits data with `@osdk/client` directly, a REST call, or a background job."],[3288,"Your edits go into a separate layer on top of the cached server data. Every component that reads an edited object, or a list that contains one, re-renders with the edits."],[2534,"Your